window.ZGCLAB_DETAILS["news-9"]=[{"id":"news-1587","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"国土安全部发言人特里西娅·麦克劳克林将离开特朗普政府","title_en":"DHS spokesperson Tricia McLaughlin leaving Trump administration","summary_cn":"美国国土安全部公共事务助理部长特里西娅·麦克劳克林即将离开特朗普政府。她一直是特朗普移民政策的主要辩护者之一，担任国土安全部部长克里斯蒂·诺姆的发言人。其离职之际，国土安全部正因部分政府停摆面临资金中断，民主党和共和党就移民与海关执法局改革存在争议。据Axios报道，其副手劳伦·比斯将升任公共事务助理部长。","summary_en":"Department of Homeland Security Assistant Secretary for Public Affairs Tricia McLaughlin is leaving the Trump administration. She has been one of the administration's top defenders of President Donald Trump's immigration policies, serving as a spokesperson for DHS Secretary Kristi Noem. Her departure comes as DHS deals with a funding lapse amid a partial government shutdown, with Democrats and Republicans debating Immigration and Customs Enforcement reforms. Axios reports that her deputy, Lauren Bis, will be promoted to Assistant Secretary of Public Affairs.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:14:06.784142+00:00","url":"https://foxbaltimore.com/news/nation-world/dhs-spokesperson-tricia-mclaughlin-leaving-trump-administration-immigration-ice-minnesota-alex-pretti-renee-good-replacement-lauren-bis-deputy","content":"DHS spokesperson Tricia McLaughlin leaving Trump administrationby CAITLYN FROLO | The National News DeskTue, February 17, 2026 at 12:28 PMUpdated Wed, February 18, 2026 at 1:23 PMPatricia McLaughlin Official Portrait at DHS Headquarters (Photo by Mikaela McGee)1CommentSharetopics: Tricia McLaughlinDepartment of Homeland SecurityTrump administrationImmigration policiesGovernment shutdownPublic affairsLauren BisPolitical communicationsWASHINGTON (TNND) — Department of Homeland Security Assistant Secretary for Public Affairs Tricia McLaughlin is leaving the administration.Politico first reported McLaughlin's plans to depart the Trump team next week, citing DHS officials.McLaughlin is one of the administration's top defenders of President Donald Trump's immigration policies, serving as a spokesperson for DHS Secretary Kristi Noem. The sources told the outlet that McLaughlin plans to inform her coworkers on Tuesday of next week's departure. Secretary Noem wished McLaughlin well on Monday afternoon in a post on X. \"Tricia McLaughlin has served with exceptional dedication, tenacity, and professionalism as Assistant Secretary for Public Affairs at the Department of Homeland Security,\" Noem wrote. \"She has played an instrumental role in advancing our mission to secure the homeland and keep Americans safe.\"While we are sad to see her leave, we are grateful for her service and wish Tricia nothing but success.\"View post on XHer departure comes as DHS deals with a funding lapse amid a partial government shutdown, as Democrats debate Republicans over Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) reforms.Politico reports that McLaughlin started making plans to leave the administration in December, but delayed her departure after the fatal shooting of Renee Good and Alex Pretti in Minneapolis.View post on XAs for who will replace McLaughlin, Axios reports that Lauren Bis, a deputy of McLaughlin's, will be promoted to Assistant Secretary of Public Affairs.McLaughlin is from Ohio and previously served as political communications director for Ohio Gov. Mike DeWine and as a senior adviser on Vivek Ramaswamy’s 2024 Republican presidential campaign, the DHS website reads.She also served in the first Trump administration at the Treasury Department under then-Secretary Steven Mnuchin as Acting Deputy Assistant Secretary focused on economic sanctions. She also served at the State Department as Chief of Staff for Nuclear Arms Control.TrendingMother of 3-year-old hit-and-run victim says teen’s sentence falls shortA Baltimore mother whose 3-year-old daughter was killed in a hit-and-run says she is frustrated and disappointed with the sentence a 14-year-old boy received inMaryland state trooper injured in I-695 crashMultiple ambulances were sent to a crash site on I-695 after a Maryland State Police trooper was reportedly involved in a collision on Thursday.Harford Co. man convicted in wife's 2025 murder charged in 1986 cold case rape, murderA Harford County man recently convicted of his wife’s murder is now under investigation for two, 40-year-old cold cases, including a 1986 rape and murder in BalOceans Calling cancels Friday events as weather, beach erosion halt buildOceans Calling has canceled all planned events for Friday due to inclement weather and beach erosion over the past week, which have unsafe the festival site unsOIG pushes back on City's compliance cost claim as hundreds of complaints pile upBaltimore’s Office of Inspector General is pushing back against the Scott administration’s effort to pause a court order restoring the watchdog’s access to CityNEWS IN PHOTOS:\"Local\"6NEWWoman identified in deadly Maryland multi-county police chase crash12NEWTeen hurt in targeted shooting at Prince George’s Community College3Committee votes in favor of Harford Road Overlay bill4Oceans Calling cancels Friday events as weather, beach erosion halt build","content_cn":"国土安全部发言人特里西娅·麦克劳克林离开特朗普政府\n作者：CAITLYN FROLO | The National News Desk\n2026年2月17日，星期二，下午12:28\n更新于2026年2月18日，星期三，下午1:23\n\n帕特里夏·麦克劳克林在国土安全部总部的官方肖像（摄影：Mikaela McGee）\n1条评论\n分享\n\n话题：特里西娅·麦克劳克林；国土安全部；特朗普政府；移民政策；政府停摆；公共事务；劳伦·比斯；政治传播\n\n华盛顿（TNND）——国土安全部公共事务助理部长特里西娅·麦克劳克林将离开本届政府。\n\nPolitico援引国土安全部官员的话首先报道了麦克劳克林计划于下周离开特朗普团队的消息。\n\n麦克劳克林是本届政府为唐纳德·特朗普总统移民政策辩护的主要人物之一，担任国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆的发言人。消息人士告诉该媒体，麦克劳克林计划于周二通知同事她将在下周离职。诺姆部长周一下午在X上发帖祝愿麦克劳克林一切顺利。\n\n诺姆写道：“特里西娅·麦克劳克林作为国土安全部公共事务助理部长，以非凡的奉献精神、坚韧毅力和专业素养履职。”“她在推进我们保卫国土、保障美国人安全的使命中发挥了不可或缺的作用。”\n\n“尽管她的离开令我们难过，但我们感谢她的服务，并祝愿特里西娅取得一切成功。”\n\n在X上查看帖子\n\n她离职之际，国土安全部正因部分政府停摆而面临资金中断，民主党人和共和党人正就移民与海关执法局（ICE）改革展开辩论。\n\nPolitico报道称，麦克劳克林从12月起就开始计划离开本届政府，但在明尼阿波利斯发生蕾妮·古德和亚历克斯·普雷蒂遭枪击身亡事件后推迟了离职。\n\n在X上查看帖子\n\n至于谁将接替麦克劳克林，Axios报道称，麦克劳克林的副手劳伦·比斯将被晋升为公共事务助理部长。\n\n国土安全部网站显示，麦克劳克林来自俄亥俄州，此前曾担任俄亥俄州州长迈克·德怀恩的政治传播主任，并在维韦克·拉马斯瓦米2024年共和党总统竞选中担任高级顾问。\n\n她还曾在首届特朗普政府中，于时任部长史蒂文·姆努钦领导下的财政部担任代理副助理部长，重点负责经济制裁事务。她还曾在国务院担任核军备控制办公厅主任。\n\n热门\n\n3岁肇事逃逸受害者母亲称，少年刑期不足\n一名巴尔的摩母亲的3岁女儿在一次肇事逃逸中死亡，她称自己对一名14岁男孩被判处的刑罚感到沮丧和失望。\n\n马里兰州警在I-695事故中受伤\n据报道，一名马里兰州警察周四发生碰撞事故后，多辆救护车被派往I-695事故现场。\n\n哈福德县男子因谋杀妻子于2025年被定罪，如今又被控与1986年悬案中的强奸和谋杀有关\n一名哈福德县男子最近因谋杀妻子被定罪，目前正因两起40年前的悬案接受调查，其中包括1986年发生在巴尔的摩的强奸和谋杀案。\n\n因天气和海滩侵蚀阻碍搭建，Oceans Calling取消周五活动\n由于恶劣天气以及过去一周的海滩侵蚀使音乐节场地不安全，Oceans Calling取消了周五所有计划活动。\n\n数百起投诉不断累积，监察长办公室反驳市政府关于合规成本的说法\n巴尔的摩市监察长办公室正反驳斯科特政府试图暂停一项法院命令的做法；该命令将恢复监察机构对市政府的访问权限。\n\n图片新闻：\n“Local”\n6条新消息\n一名女子在马里兰州致命的跨县警方追捕事故中被确认身份\n12条新消息\n一名青少年在乔治王子社区学院遭针对性枪击中受伤\n3条新消息\n委员会投票支持哈福德路铺设法案\n4条新消息\n因天气和海滩侵蚀阻碍搭建，Oceans Calling取消周五活动","publish_source":"foxbaltimore.com","publish_time":"2026-02-17T17:28:26+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2390","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"联邦调查局解密更多指控乔·拜登腐败的文件","title_en":"FBI declassifies more documents alleging corruption by Joe Biden","summary_cn":"美国联邦调查局继续解密涉及拜登家族的文件，内容包含机密线人关于亨特·拜登为外国公司工作及其父亲可能角色的说法。参议院司法委员会主席格拉斯利称已有三名FBI线人提供相关信息，并强调并非断言指控属实，而是要求查明FBI调查情况。报道也提到其中一名线人斯米尔诺夫因撒谎被定罪。","summary_en":"The FBI is continuing to declassify documents involving the Biden family, including confidential source claims about Hunter Biden's foreign business work and his father's possible role. Senate Judiciary Chairman Chuck Grassley said three FBI sources have provided information, stressing the allegations are not asserted as true but that the FBI's investigation should be examined. The report notes one source, Alexander Smirnov, was convicted of lying.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:42:58.525090+00:00","url":"https://foxbaltimore.com/news/nation-world/fbi-declassifies-more-documents-alleging-corruption-by-joe-biden-chuck-grassley-barack-obama","content":"FBI declassifies more documents alleging corruption by Joe Bidenby KRISTINE FRAZAO | The National News DeskWed, September 17, 2025 at 4:43 PM3VIEW ALL PHOTOSWASHINGTON, DC - SEPTEMBER 16: Ranking Member Sen. Richard Durbin (D-IL) (R) questions Federal Bureau of Investigation Director Kash Patel as Chairman Sen. Chuck Grassley (R-IA) looks on during a hearing with the Senate Judiciary Committee in the Hart Senate Office Building on Capitol Hill on September 16, 2025 in Washington, DC. Patel was questioned about last week’s assassination of Turning Point USA founder Charlie Kirk and his social media posts related to the FBI’s investigation of the shooting, as well as a lawsuit filed by former senior FBI officials who were terminated by Patel for what they claim are political reasons. (Photo by Andrew Harnik/Getty Images)0CommentSharetopics: FBIJoe BidenHunter BidenCorruptionDeclassified documentsAllegationsBurismaSenate Judiciary CommitteeWASHINGTON (TNND) — The Federal Bureau of Investigation is continuing on its quest to release more and more documents that, up until now, have been hidden from the public eye.They include what confidential sources said about Hunter Biden’s work for foreign companies, as well as the role his father may have played while he was still serving as Vice President under President Barack Obama. (TNND)They include what confidential sources said about Hunter Biden’s work for foreign companies, as well as the role his father may have played while he was still serving as Vice President under President Barack Obama.The latest round of declassified documents centers on allegations of potential wrongdoing by former President Joe Biden and his son, Hunter.Speaking at a Senate Judiciary Committee hearing Tuesday, Sen. Chuck Grassley, R-Iowa, the Chairman, said, “In total, we now have three different FBI confidential human sources providing information about the Biden family and potential criminal conduct.\"His committee has been investigating alleged corruption by the Biden family for years and released a report on their findings in September 2020.\"This report not only details examples of extensive and complex financial transactions involving the Bidens, it also describes the quandary other U.S. governmental officials faced as they attempted to guide and support Ukraine’s anticorruption efforts.\"On Tuesday, Grassley released the newly declassified documents, in which one FBI source alleges that while he was Vice President, Joe Biden met directly with then Ukrainian President Petro Poroshenko, \"to protect the business interests\" of his son Hunter, and would \"take care of the Burisma holding issues,\" and Poroshenko would protect Zlochevsky.Mykola Zlochevsky was the owner of Burisma, the Ukrainian gas company paying Hunter Biden about a million dollars a year to serve on its board.Republicans for years have questioned the position he held while his father was overseeing policy related to Ukraine, alleging corruption and calling the FBI’s decision not to pursue the case a partisan weaponization of the federal government.Still,. at least one of the FBI’s sources, Alexander Smirnov, was convicted of lying about former President Joe Biden and his son taking bribes from Burisma - a case now under review by Trump’s Justice Department.According to the Associated Press, \"While Smirnov’s identity wasn’t publicly known before the indictment, his claims played a major part in the Republican effort in Congress to investigate the president and his family, and helped spark a House impeachment inquiry into Biden.\"At Tuesday's hearing, Grassley added, \"We aren’t saying the allegations are true. We wanna know what the FBI did to fully investigate their veracity or lack of and what they concluded,\" he said.In September 2024, Hunter Biden pleaded guilty to federal tax charges, a crime for which he was later pardoned by his father. But it seems clear that President Donald Trump has no interest in letting the matter go, especially as it pertains to any role Joe Biden may have had.TrendingMother of 3-year-old hit-and-run victim says teen’s sentence falls shortA Baltimore mother whose 3-year-old daughter was killed in a hit-and-run says she is frustrated and disappointed with the sentence a 14-year-old boy received inMaryland state trooper injured in I-695 crashMultiple ambulances were sent to a crash site on I-695 after a Maryland State Police trooper was reportedly involved in a collision on Thursday.Oceans Calling cancels Friday events as weather, beach erosion halt buildOceans Calling has canceled all planned events for Friday due to inclement weather and beach erosion over the past week, which have unsafe the festival site unsHarford Co. man convicted in wife's 2025 murder charged in 1986 cold case rape, murderA Harford County man recently convicted of his wife’s murder is now under investigation for two, 40-year-old cold cases, including a 1986 rape and murder in BalOIG pushes back on City's compliance cost claim as hundreds of complaints pile upBaltimore’s Office of Inspector General is pushing back against the Scott administration’s effort to pause a court order restoring the watchdog’s access to CityNEWS IN PHOTOS:\"Local\"7NEWPHOTOS: FOX45 fights hunger at the Maryland Food Bank616 people taken to hospital after crash with stolen vehicle driven by juveniles & MTA bus6Woman identified in deadly Maryland multi-county police chase crash12Teen hurt in targeted shooting at Prince George’s Community College","content_cn":"FBI解密更多指控乔·拜登腐败的文件by KRISTINE FRAZAO | The National News Desk\n2025年9月17日，星期三，下午4:43\n3查看所有照片\n华盛顿特区——9月16日：2025年9月16日，在华盛顿特区国会山哈特参议院办公大楼举行的参议院司法委员会听证会上，资深成员理查德·德宾参议员（伊利诺伊州民主党）（右）向联邦调查局局长卡什·帕特尔提问，委员会主席查克·格拉斯利参议员（爱荷华州共和党）在一旁观看。帕特尔被问及上周美国转折点组织创始人查理·柯克遇刺一事、他与FBI调查枪击案相关的社交媒体帖子，以及前FBI高级官员提起的一起诉讼；这些官员被帕特尔解雇，并声称解雇出于政治原因。（摄影：Andrew Harnik/Getty Images）\n0评论 分享\n主题：FBI\n乔·拜登\n亨特·拜登\n腐败\n解密文件\n指控\nBurisma\n参议院司法委员会\n华盛顿（TNND）——联邦调查局正继续努力，发布越来越多迄今为止一直不为公众所见的文件。\n这些文件包括机密消息人士所说的亨特·拜登为外国公司工作的情况，以及他的父亲在巴拉克·奥巴马总统任内担任副总统期间可能发挥的作用。（TNND）\n这些文件包括机密消息人士所说的亨特·拜登为外国公司工作的情况，以及他的父亲在巴拉克·奥巴马总统任内担任副总统期间可能发挥的作用。\n最新一批解密文件集中于对前总统乔·拜登及其儿子亨特可能存在不当行为的指控。\n周二在参议院司法委员会听证会上，委员会主席、爱荷华州共和党参议员查克·格拉斯利说：“总的来说，我们现在有三名不同的FBI机密人类消息来源，提供有关拜登家族及潜在犯罪行为的信息。”\n他的委员会多年来一直在调查有关拜登家族腐败的指控，并于2020年9月发布了一份调查报告。\n“这份报告不仅详细列举了涉及拜登家族的大量复杂金融交易实例，还描述了其他美国政府官员在试图指导和支持乌克兰反腐败工作时所面临的困境。”\n周二，格拉斯利公布了新解密的文件。其中一名FBI消息人士指称，乔·拜登担任副总统期间，曾直接会见时任乌克兰总统彼得罗·波罗申科，“以保护”其儿子亨特的“商业利益”，并会“处理Burisma控股方面的问题”，而波罗申科则会保护兹洛切夫斯基。\nMykola Zlochevsky是Burisma这家乌克兰天然气公司的所有者，该公司每年向亨特·拜登支付约100万美元，让他担任董事会成员。\n多年来，共和党人一直质疑亨特在其父亲负责乌克兰相关政策期间所担任的职务，指称其中存在腐败，并称FBI决定不继续调查此案，是联邦政府被党派化武器化的表现。\n不过，至少有一名FBI消息人士亚历山大·斯米尔诺夫因谎称前总统乔·拜登及其儿子从Burisma收受贿赂而被定罪——此案目前正由特朗普司法部重新审查。\n据美联社报道，“在被起诉前，斯米尔诺夫的身份并不为公众所知，但他的说法在国会共和党调查拜登家族的努力中发挥了重要作用，调查了\n总统及其家人，并帮助引发了众议院对拜登的弹劾调查。\"在周二的听证会上，格拉斯利补充说：\"我们不是在说这些指控属实。我们想知道联邦调查局做了什么，以彻底调查这些指控的真实性或不实之处，以及他们得出了什么结论，\"他说。\n\n2024年9月，亨特·拜登承认犯有联邦税务罪，而他后来因这一罪行被父亲赦免。但很明显，总统唐纳德·特朗普无意让此事过去，尤其是涉及乔·拜登可能扮演的任何角色时。\n\n热门新闻\n\n3岁肇事逃逸受害者的母亲称，涉事青少年的判决远远不够\n一名巴尔的摩母亲的3岁女儿在一起肇事逃逸事故中死亡，她表示对马里兰州一名14岁男孩所获刑罚感到沮丧和失望\n\n马里兰州一名州警在I-695公路事故中受伤\n据报道，一名马里兰州警方的州警周四卷入一起碰撞事故后，多辆救护车被派往I-695公路事故现场。\n\n天气和海滩侵蚀导致活动场地受损，Oceans Calling取消周五活动\n由于恶劣天气以及过去一周的海滩侵蚀导致音乐节场地不安全，Oceans Calling取消了周五所有原定活动。\n\n哈福德县男子因谋杀妻子被定罪后，又因1986年悬案强奸、谋杀案被起诉\n一名最近因谋杀妻子而被定罪的哈福德县男子，目前正因两起40年前的悬案接受调查，其中包括1986年的一起强奸和谋杀案\n\n投诉数量不断增加，监察长办公室反驳市政府关于合规成本的说法\n巴尔的摩监察长办公室反驳斯科特政府暂停执行恢复监察机构获取城市新闻权限的法院命令的努力\n\n图片新闻：\n\"本地\"7\n新图片：FOX45在马里兰州食品银行开展抗击饥饿活动\n16\n7人因一辆由未成年人驾驶的被盗车辆与MTA公交车相撞而被送往医院\n6\n在马里兰州多县警方追捕事故中，一名死者身份得到确认\n12\n乔治王子社区学院发生有针对性的枪击，一名青少年受伤","publish_source":"foxbaltimore.com","publish_time":"2025-09-17T20:43:02+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2079","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI加大对国际“764”儿童剥削网络的打击力度","title_en":"FBI intensifies crackdown on international '764' child exploitation network","summary_cn":"美国联邦调查局正加大力度打击名为“764”的国际网络犯罪组织，该组织被指针对儿童，胁迫其自残、遭受性虐待甚至自杀。FBI局长卡什·帕特尔称此类犯罪为“美国现代恐怖主义”。FBI副局长邦吉诺确认正积极追捕相关成员，巴尔的摩和亚利桑那已有嫌疑人被捕，全国约300项调查与该网络有关。","summary_en":"The FBI is escalating efforts to dismantle an international online network known as \"764,\" which authorities say targets children and coerces them into self-harm, sexual abuse and even suicide. FBI Director Kash Patel described such crimes as \"modern-day terrorism in America.\" Deputy Director Dan Bongino confirmed agents are actively pursuing members, with arrests in Baltimore and Arizona, and roughly 300 active investigations nationwide linked to the network.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:30:06.071272+00:00","url":"https://foxbaltimore.com/news/nation-world/fbi-intensifies-crackdown-on-international-764-child-exploitation-network-crimes-kash-patel-children-federal-authorities","content":"FBI intensifies crackdown on international '764' child exploitation networkby KAYLA GASKINS | The National News DeskThu, November 20, 2025 at 4:36 PM3VIEW ALL PHOTOSWASHINGTON, DC - NOVEMBER 19: FBI Director Kash Patel (R), accompanied by Attorney General Pam Bondi (L), speaks at a news conference to announce the indictment of a former Olympic snowboarder Ryan Wedding, charging him with murder and money laundering in connection to a drug trafficking organization at the Justice Department on November 19, 2025 in Washington, DC. The Justice Department announced a fifteen-million-dollar reward for information leading to the arrest of Ryan James Wedding, the leader of a criminal drug organization who smuggled large quantities of cocaine through Colombia and Mexico for distribution in the United States and Canada. (Photo by Andrew Harnik/Getty Images)0CommentSharetopics: FBIChild exploitation764 networkOnline predatorsChild abuseCybercrimeLaw enforcementChild safety WASHINGTON (TNND) — The FBI is escalating its efforts to dismantle a violent online network known as “764,” an international group authorities say targets children and coerces them into acts of self-harm, sexual abuse, and even suicide.Experts say the level of brutality stands out even among extremist movements. (TNND)Federal officials describe the organization as one of the most horrific child-exploitation networks they have encountered. The group operates largely in the shadows of the internet, where predators, often posing as peers, manipulate minors into performing violent acts—sometimes live on camera.“What I refer to as modern-day terrorism in America,” FBI Director Kash Patel said in September, describing crimes linked to the group. “These are crimes that involve harming our children by going after them online—causing self-mutilation, suicide, sexual abuse.”Experts say the level of brutality stands out even among extremist movements.Seamus Hughes, a researcher at the University of Nebraska Omaha’s National Counterterrorism Innovation, Technology, and Education Center (NCITE), told an audience at the Eradicate Hate Global Summit that the network is unlike any he has seen in his two decades studying extremist groups.“I’ve interviewed people involved with ISIS, al-Qaeda, al-Shabaab,” Hughes said. “764 is probably the worst group I've studied in 20 years. Full stop.”ABC’s Nightline recently interviewed the parents of a 13-year-old victim who died by suicide after being coerced and encouraged by members of the 764 network. The child was manipulated into livestreaming the act while individuals online watched and goaded him on.“It’s one thing to learn your child has died,” the boy’s mother said. “It’s another to learn people were watching. And egging him on.”Authorities say an Australian teenager alerted the family after witnessing the livestream, prompting an international investigation into the group’s role.FBI Deputy Director Dan Bongino announced new developments on Wednesday, calling 764 a “heinous child-exploitation ring” and confirming that federal agents are actively pursuing members tied to the network.The FBI’s Baltimore Field Office recently arrested a suspect accused of targeting five minors, including one as young as 13.In Arizona, another alleged member was taken into custody on charges involving nine victims between the ages of 11 and 15. According to federal authorities, the allegations include distributing child pornography, cyberstalking, animal torture content, and “conspiring to provide material support to terrorists.”The scope of the FBI’s inquiry is vast. National correspondence indicates that around 300 active investigations are currently linked to the 764 network nationwide, underscoring the reach of the group and the urgency of the bureau’s response.The FBI continues to warn parents to remain vigilant about their children’s online activity, emphasizing that many of the predators operate anonymously and target vulnerable teens on mainstream platforms.TrendingMother of 3-year-old hit-and-run victim says teen’s sentence falls shortA Baltimore mother whose 3-year-old daughter was killed in a hit-and-run says she is frustrated and disappointed with the sentence a 14-year-old boy received inMaryland state trooper injured in I-695 crashMultiple ambulances were sent to a crash site on I-695 after a Maryland State Police trooper was reportedly involved in a collision on Thursday.Oceans Calling cancels Friday events as weather, beach erosion halt buildOceans Calling has canceled all planned events for Friday due to inclement weather and beach erosion over the past week, which have unsafe the festival site unsHarford Co. man convicted in wife's 2025 murder charged in 1986 cold case rape, murderA Harford County man recently convicted of his wife’s murder is now under investigation for two, 40-year-old cold cases, including a 1986 rape and murder in BalOIG pushes back on City's compliance cost claim as hundreds of complaints pile upBaltimore’s Office of Inspector General is pushing back against the Scott administration’s effort to pause a court order restoring the watchdog’s access to CityNEWS IN PHOTOS:\"Local\"7NEWPHOTOS: FOX45 fights hunger at the Maryland Food Bank616 people taken to hospital after crash with stolen vehicle driven by juveniles & MTA bus6Woman identified in deadly Maryland multi-county police chase crash12Teen hurt in targeted shooting at Prince George’s Community College","content_cn":"FBI加大打击国际“764”儿童剥削网络的力度\n作者：KAYLA GASKINS | The National News Desk\n2025年11月20日，星期四，下午4:36\n3\n查看全部照片\n\n华盛顿特区——11月19日：2025年11月19日，在华盛顿特区司法部，FBI局长卡什·帕特尔（右）在司法部长帕姆·邦迪（左）陪同下，于新闻发布会上宣布起诉前奥运单板滑雪运动员瑞安·韦丁，指控其与一个贩毒组织有关联的谋杀和洗钱罪。司法部宣布，悬赏1500万美元征集可导致逮捕瑞安·詹姆斯·韦丁的信息；他是一个犯罪贩毒组织的头目，该组织通过哥伦比亚和墨西哥走私大量可卡因，供在美国和加拿大分销。（Andrew Harnik/Getty Images 摄）\n0\n评论\n分享\n\n话题：FBI\n儿童剥削\n764网络\n网络掠食者\n虐待儿童\n网络犯罪\n执法\n儿童安全\n\n华盛顿（TNND）——FBI正在加大努力，瓦解一个名为“764”的暴力网络组织；当局称，这是一个国际团体，专门锁定儿童并胁迫他们实施自残、性虐待，甚至自杀。\n\n专家称，即便在极端主义运动中，其残忍程度也格外突出。（TNND）\n\n联邦官员称，该组织是他们遇到过的最令人发指的儿童剥削网络之一。该团体主要在互联网的阴影中活动，掠食者常常伪装成同龄人，操纵未成年人实施暴力行为——有时还会在镜头前直播。\n\n“我称之为美国的现代恐怖主义，”FBI局长卡什·帕特尔9月在描述与该团体相关的犯罪时说，“这些犯罪涉及通过网络侵害我们的孩子——导致自残、自杀、性虐待。”\n\n专家称，即便在极端主义运动中，其残忍程度也格外突出。\n\n内布拉斯加大学奥马哈分校国家反恐创新、技术与教育中心（NCITE）的研究员西默斯·休斯在“根除仇恨全球峰会”上告诉听众，该网络与他在研究极端主义组织的二十年里见过的任何组织都不同。\n\n“我采访过参与ISIS、基地组织、青年党的人，”休斯说，“764可能是我20年来研究过的最糟糕的组织。毫无疑问。”\n\nABC的《夜线》最近采访了一名13岁受害者的父母；这名受害者在遭764网络成员胁迫和怂恿后死于自杀。该儿童被操纵着直播这一行为，而网上的人观看并煽动他继续下去。\n\n“得知自己的孩子去世是一回事，”男孩的母亲说，“得知有人在观看，又是另一回事。而且他们还在怂恿他。”\n\n当局称，一名澳大利亚青少年在目睹直播后提醒了这家人，从而引发了对该团体所扮演角色的国际调查。\n\nFBI副局长丹·邦吉诺周三宣布了新进展，称764是一个“令人发指的儿童剥削团伙”，并确认联邦探员正在积极追捕与该网络有关联的成员。\n\nFBI巴尔的摩办事处最近逮捕了一名嫌疑人，其被指控锁定了5名未成年人，其中一人年仅13岁。\n\n在亚利桑那州，另一名据称的成员因涉及9名年龄在11至15岁之间受害者的指控被拘留。联邦当局称，相关指控包括传播儿童色情制品、网络跟踪、虐待动物\n内容，以及“密谋向恐怖分子提供物质支持”。FBI调查的范围十分广泛。全国通信显示，目前全国约有300项正在进行的调查与764网络有关，这凸显了该组织的影响范围以及该局回应的紧迫性。FBI继续警告家长密切关注孩子的网络活动，强调许多掠食者匿名活动，并在主流平台上针对脆弱的青少年。\n热门\n3岁肇事逃逸受害者的母亲称青少年判决过轻\n巴尔的摩一名母亲的3岁女儿在一次肇事逃逸事故中死亡，她表示自己对一名14岁男孩所获判决感到沮丧和失望\n马里兰州警在I-695事故中受伤\n据报道，一名马里兰州警察周四在碰撞事故中涉入后，多辆救护车被派往I-695的事故现场。\n由于天气和海滩侵蚀阻碍搭建，Oceans Calling取消周五活动\n由于恶劣天气及过去一周的海滩侵蚀使音乐节场地不安全，Oceans Calling已取消周五所有计划活动\n哈福德县男子因妻子2025年被杀案被定罪，又被控1986年悬案强奸、谋杀\n一名近期因谋杀妻子被定罪的哈福德县男子，目前正因两起40年前的悬案接受调查，其中包括1986年发生在巴尔的摩的一起强奸和谋杀案\n随着数百起投诉堆积，监察长办公室反驳市政府关于合规成本的说法\n巴尔的摩监察长办公室正在反驳斯科特政府暂停一项法院命令的努力，该命令旨在恢复监督机构对市政府的访问权限\n图片新闻：\n“本地”7\n新\n图片：FOX45在马里兰食品银行抗击饥饿\n6\n由青少年驾驶的被盗车辆与MTA公交车相撞后，16人被送往医院\n6\n马里兰州致命多县警察追捕事故中一名女子身份已确认\n12\n普林斯乔治社区学院针对性枪击事件中一名青少年受伤","publish_source":"foxbaltimore.com","publish_time":"2025-11-20T21:36:40+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2194","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"美国国土安全部：ICE执法人员面临的死亡威胁激增8000%","title_en":"ICE officers face 8,000% increase in death threats, DHS shares","summary_cn":"美国国土安全部公布新数据称，移民和海关执法局（ICE）执法人员遭遇的死亡威胁增加了8000%。助理部长特里西娅·麦克劳克林表示，执法人员及其家人面临悬赏、跟踪和人肉搜索等暴力威胁，并指责“庇护政客”的妖魔化言论。国土安全部长诺姆承诺将依法严惩伤害执法人员者。报道还提到一名墨西哥籍男子因在TikTok悬赏杀害ICE人员被捕。","summary_en":"New data from the Department of Homeland Security shows an 8,000% increase in death threats targeting U.S. Immigration and Customs Enforcement officers. Assistant DHS Secretary Tricia McLaughlin said officers and their families face bounties, stalking and doxxing, blaming \"sanctuary politicians\" for vilification. DHS Secretary Kristi Noem vowed to prosecute those who harm law enforcement. The report also noted a Mexican national arrested in Dallas for allegedly offering $10,000 bounties on TikTok for the murder of ICE agents.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:36:05.996085+00:00","url":"https://foxbaltimore.com/news/nation-world/ice-officers-face-8000-rise-in-death-threats-dhs-shares-homeland-security-safety-violence-tricia-mclaughlin-arrests-illegal-migrant-phone-calls-doxxing","content":"ICE officers face 8,000% increase in death threats, DHS sharesby CAITLYN FROLO | The National News DeskThu, October 30, 2025 at 10:31 AMUpdated Thu, October 30, 2025 at 10:34 AM6VIEW ALL PHOTOSPedestrians chant, \"ICE go home!\" as federal immigration agents walk along North Clark Street in the River North neighborhood, Sunday, Sept. 28, 2025, in Chicago. (Ashlee Rezin/Chicago Sun-Times via AP)1CommentSharetopics: ICEDeath threatsDHSViolenceImmigrationLaw enforcementBountiesSanctuary politicsWASHINGTON (TNND) — U.S. Immigration and Customs Enforcement officers are facing an unprecedented surge in death threats and violent attacks, new data from the Department of Homeland Security reveals. New statistics released Wednesday from the agency say ICE officers are experiencing an 8,000% increase in death threats targeting ICE officers. In a statement released to Fox News, Assistant DHS Secretary Tricia McLaughlin said the threats come as officers risk their lives to \"remove the worst of the worst.\"\"From bounties placed on their heads for their murders, threats to their families, stalking, and doxxing online, our officers are experiencing an unprecedented level of violence and threats against them and their families,\" McLaughlin said. McLaughlin said \"sanctuary politicians\" are contributing to the surge in violent threats, writing, \"their repeated vilification and demonization tactics, including gross comparisons to the Nazi Gestapo. This violence against law enforcement must end.\"DHS Secretary Kristi Noem has promised to prosecute those who harm law enforcement officers to \"the fullest extent of the law.\"Eduardo Aguilar, a Mexican national, was arrested earlier this month in Dallas for allegedly offering $10,000 bounties on TikTok for the murder of ICE agents. \"We are thankful this criminal who had a firearm in his possession was arrested before he could kill one of our law enforcement officers,\" DHS wrote. \"The Trump administration will not back down from these threats, and every criminal, terrorist, and illegal alien will face American justice.\"View post on XIn another instance in Texas, an ICE officer's spouse was threatened over the phone, Fox News reports.\"I don’t know how you let your husband work for ICE, and you sleep at night. F--- you, f--- your family. I hope your kids get deported by accident. How do you sleep? F--- you. Did you hear what happened to the Nazis after World War II? Because it’s what’s going to happen to your family,\" the caller said, according to DHS.TrendingOceans Calling cancels Friday events as weather, beach erosion halt buildOceans Calling has canceled all planned events for Friday due to inclement weather and beach erosion over the past week, which have unsafe the festival site uns16 people taken to hospital after crash with stolen vehicle driven by juveniles & MTA bus16 people were taken to the hospital after a crash involving a stolen vehicle driven by juveniles and an MTA bus in east Baltimore on Thursday afternoon.Police 25 people evacuated after Amtrak train catches fire in EssexTwenty-five people were evacuated from an Amtrak train that caught fire in Essex Thursday evening.Woman identified in deadly Maryland multi-county police chase crashMaryland State Police identified the woman seen in body-camera and dash-camera video released Wednesday following last month’s multi-county chase as 34-year-oldSix indicted in Baltimore federal drug case; cocaine hidden in steel cratesSix people were indicted in connection with a federal investigation into an alleged Baltimore drug-trafficking organization that authorities say moved large shiNEWS IN PHOTOS:\"Local\"3Maryland pharmacies close as drug reimbursements squeeze stores3Data center triggers a small-town makeover as big cities fight to keep them out5State lawmaker cited after Spotlight on Maryland investigation325 people evacuated after Amtrak train catches fire in Essex","content_cn":"ICE官员面临的死亡威胁增加8,000%，DHS分享数据\n作者：CAITLYN FROLO | The National News Desk\n2025年10月30日星期四上午10:31\n更新于2025年10月30日星期四上午10:34\n查看全部照片\n2025年9月28日星期日，芝加哥River North社区，联邦移民执法人员沿北克拉克街行走时，行人高喊“ICE回家！”（Ashlee Rezin/Chicago Sun-Times，经美联社提供）\n1条评论\n分享\n主题：ICE\n死亡威胁\nDHS\n暴力\n移民\n执法\n悬赏\n庇护城市政治\n华盛顿（TNND）——国土安全部公布的新数据显示，美国移民与海关执法局（ICE）官员正面临前所未有的死亡威胁和暴力袭击激增。该机构周三发布的新统计数据显示，针对ICE官员的死亡威胁增加了8,000%。DHS助理部长特里西娅·麦克劳克林在给福克斯新闻的一份声明中说，官员们冒着生命危险去“清除最坏的那批人”，因此遭到这些威胁。\n“有人悬赏要杀害我们的官员，威胁他们的家人，跟踪他们，并在网上人肉曝光；我们的官员正经历前所未有的暴力和针对他们及其家人的威胁，”麦克劳克林说。麦克劳克林说，“庇护城市政治人物”正在助长暴力威胁激增，并写道：“他们一再采取诋毁和妖魔化手段，包括把我们的官员与纳粹盖世太保进行恶劣的比较。这种针对执法部门的暴力必须停止。”DHS部长克里斯蒂·诺姆承诺，将对伤害执法人员的人“依法追究到底”。\n本月早些时候，墨西哥籍公民爱德华多·阿吉拉尔在达拉斯被捕，他涉嫌在TikTok上悬赏1万美元，要求杀害ICE特工。“我们感谢这名持有枪支的罪犯在杀害我们的一名执法人员之前被捕，”DHS写道。“特朗普政府不会向这些威胁退缩，每一名罪犯、恐怖分子和非法外国人都将面对美国的司法制裁。”\n查看X上的帖子\n福克斯新闻报道，在得克萨斯州的另一起事件中，一名ICE官员的配偶接到电话威胁。\n据DHS称，来电者说：“我不知道你怎么能让你的丈夫为ICE工作，还能安睡。去你的，去你全家。我希望你的孩子被意外驱逐。你怎么睡得着？去你的。你听说过二战后纳粹的下场吗？因为你的家人也会遭遇同样的事情。”\n热门\nOceans Calling因天气和海滩侵蚀取消周五活动\n由于恶劣天气以及过去一周的海滩侵蚀使音乐节场地变得不安全，Oceans Calling取消了周五所有计划中的活动\n16人在一辆被盗车辆与MTA公交车相撞后被送医，该被盗车辆由未成年人驾驶\n周四下午，巴尔的摩东部一辆由未成年人驾驶的被盗车辆与一辆MTA公交车相撞，造成16人被送往医院。\n警方\nAmtrak列车在埃塞克斯起火，25人撤离\n周四晚间，一列在埃塞克斯起火的Amtrak列车上有25人被疏散。\n马里兰州多县警方追车致命车祸中的女性身份确认\n马里兰州警方确认了周三公布的随身摄像机和车载摄像机视频中出现的女性身份；这些视频来自上月的一场涉及多个县的追捕行动，该女性现年34岁\n六人因巴尔的摩联邦毒品案件被起诉；可卡因藏在钢制箱子里\n六人因一项联邦调查而被起诉。调查涉及一个涉嫌在巴尔的摩贩毒的组织，当局称该组织转运了大量……\n图片新闻：“本地”\n3家马里兰药店因药品报销挤压商家而关闭\n数据中心促成小城改造，大城市则努力阻止其进入\n州议员在《聚焦马里兰》调查后被传唤\n325人在埃塞克斯Amtrak列车起火后撤离","publish_source":"foxbaltimore.com","publish_time":"2025-10-30T14:31:41+00:00"}},{"id":"news-555","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI局长帕特尔称世界杯期间未发生重大犯罪袭击","title_en":"FBI Director Patel celebrates no major criminal attacks during the World Cup","summary_cn":"美国联邦调查局局长卡什·帕特尔在社交平台X上表示，2026年世界杯期间美国未发生重大犯罪袭击或重大安全事件。他称本届世界杯共有650万人观看78场比赛，联邦调查局投入近5000名人员，覆盖16个主办城市，是FBI历史上为单一活动投入资源最多的一次，并感谢联邦、州及地方合作伙伴。","summary_en":"FBI Director Kash Patel said on X that there were no significant criminal attacks or major security incidents during the 2026 FIFA World Cup hosted in the United States. He noted 6.5 million attendees across 78 matches in 11 venues, and said the FBI dedicated nearly 5,000 personnel across 16 host cities, calling it the largest resource dedication the FBI has ever made for any event.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:25:12.936008+00:00","url":"https://foxchattanooga.com/news/nation-world/fbi-director-patel-celebrates-no-major-criminal-attacks-during-the-world-cup-fifa-spain-argentina-donald-trump","content":"FBI Director Patel celebrates no major criminal attacks during the World Cupby CHARLOTTE HAZARD | The National News DeskMon, July 20, 2026 at 11:12 AM3VIEW ALL PHOTOSWASHINGTON, D.C. - JULY 16: FBI Director Kash Patel attends an address to the nation by U.S. President Donald Trump in the East Room of the White House on July 16, 2026 in Washington, DC. Trump was expected to speak on election security. (Photo by Saul Loeb/Pool - Getty Images)0CommentSharetopics: FBIKash PatelWorld CupFIFASecurityTrumpTask ForceNew JerseyWASHINGTON (TNND) — FBI Director Kash Patel celebrated there being no major attacks during the World Cup.“We’re proud to report that, thank God, and thankfully to the men and women of the FBI and our partners, we had no significant criminal attacks during this World Cup,” he wrote on the social media platform, X. “To put that in perspective, we had 6.5 million people attend the 78 matches in the U.S. across 11 venues.”View post on XThe U.S. hosted the FIFA World Cup for the past few weeks. The final tournament was held in New Jersey where Spain defeated Argentina.Patel also said that there were no major security incidents.View post on X“The 2026 FIFA World Cup was the largest sporting event in the history of the world, shattering previous attendance record by double digits,” he said. “America- we got it done, ZERO major security incidents across our nation while we hosted the equivalent of 78 super bowls in 38 days, along with 40 base camps, endless fan zones, and celebrations in nearly every state.”He said that President Donald Trump established a White House FIFA Task Force for security.“This FBI led the charge dedicating nearly 5,000 personnel to the effort out of HQ, field, and international offices - across 16 host cities,” Patel wrote on X. “And, none of what we accomplished is possible without our federal, state and local partners who all put in the same relentless effort. It’s the largest resource dedication the FBI has EVER made for any event.”TrendingFather, son arrested in Chattanooga after woman found confined to chair in homeTwo Chattanooga men face aggravated neglect charges after an arrest report says police they found an elderly woman in severe pain and living in unsafe conditionFamily of child who drowned at Chattanooga apartment pool files wrongful death lawsuitThe family of a 4-year-old boy who drowned at a Chattanooga apartment complex pool last month has filed a wrongful death lawsuit, claiming the pool's gate couldNames released after Dalton-area spa raids, but no sex trafficking charges listedAuthorities have now released the names and charges of people arrested in Tuesday's raids at seven Dalton-area massage parlors.But despite initially describing Christa Pike Execution: 'Dead Woman Walking' documentary examines Tennessee death row caseA case that has haunted Tennessee for more than 30 years is coming back into the spotlight.Christa Gail Pike was just 18 years old when she was convicted in theBroken thermometer sends 14 students, 2 teachers to hospital before hazmat scare clearedFourteen students and two teachers were taken to the hospital Wednesday after a broken thermometer prompted fears of a mercury exposure at Dalewood Middle SchooNEWS IN PHOTOS:\"Local\"4Tennessee-Texas game: Enhanced security, traffic changes planned for Trump visit10Dollywood Harvest Festival returns through Oct. 31, honoring Dolly Parton with music4$3.25 million WBE Champions bass tournament gambles on fans to pay the bills3Chattanooga groups sound alarm over voter registration ahead of Oct. 5 deadline","content_cn":"FBI局长帕特尔称赞世界杯期间未发生重大犯罪袭击\n作者：CHARLOTTE HAZARD | The National News Desk\n2026年7月20日，星期一，美国东部时间上午11:12\n3\n查看所有照片\n2026年7月16日，华盛顿特区——FBI局长卡什·帕特尔于2026年7月16日在华盛顿特区白宫东厅出席美国总统唐纳德·特朗普的全国讲话。特朗普预计将就选举安全发表讲话。（照片：Saul Loeb/Pool - Getty Images）\n0条评论\n分享\n主题：FBI、卡什·帕特尔、世界杯、FIFA、安全、特朗普、特别工作组、新泽西州\n华盛顿（TNND）——FBI局长卡什·帕特尔称赞世界杯期间没有发生重大袭击。\n他在社交媒体平台X上写道：“我们很自豪地报告，感谢上天，也感谢FBI的男女工作人员及我们的合作伙伴，本届世界杯期间没有发生重大犯罪袭击。作为参考，美国11个场地举行的78场比赛共有650万人到场。”\n在X上查看帖子\n过去几周，美国举办了FIFA世界杯。决赛在新泽西州举行，西班牙击败阿根廷。\n帕特尔还表示，没有发生重大安全事件。\n在X上查看帖子\n他说：“2026年FIFA世界杯是世界历史上规模最大的体育赛事，出席人数以两位数百分比打破此前纪录。美国——我们做到了，在全国举办相当于38天内78场超级碗的赛事期间，连同40个大本营、数不尽的球迷区，以及几乎每个州的庆祝活动，发生的重大安全事件为零。”\n他说，总统唐纳德·特朗普成立了白宫FIFA特别工作组以负责安全事务。\n帕特尔在X上写道：“这届FBI牵头行动，来自总部、外地办事处和国际办事处的近5,000名人员投入这项工作，覆盖16个主办城市。我们取得的一切成就，都离不开联邦、州和地方合作伙伴；他们都付出了同样不懈的努力。这是FBI为任何活动作出的最大规模资源投入。”\n热门内容\n查塔努加一名女子被发现被困在家中椅子上后，父子被捕\n两名查塔努加男子面临严重疏于照料指控，逮捕报告称，警方发现一名老年女子疼痛严重，且生活在不安全的环境中。\n在查塔努加公寓泳池溺亡儿童的家属提起过失致死诉讼\n一名4岁男孩上月在查塔努加一处公寓综合体泳池溺亡，其家人已提起过失致死诉讼，称泳池大门可能……\n道尔顿地区水疗中心突袭后姓名公布，但未列出性交易指控\n当局现已公布周二对道尔顿地区7家按摩店突袭中被捕人员的姓名及指控。但尽管最初描述……\n克里斯塔·派克被处决：《死去女人的行走》纪录片审视田纳西州死囚案\n一个困扰人们逾30年的案件再次成为焦点。克里斯塔·盖尔·派克年仅18岁时被判……\n温度计破裂引发危险品恐慌后解除，14名学生、2名教师送医\n周三，一支破裂的温度计引发对戴尔伍德中学汞暴露的担忧后，14名学生和两名教师被送往医院。\n图片新闻：\n“本地”\n4\n田纳西州—得克萨斯州比赛：为特朗普到访计划加强安保、调整交通\n10\n多莉山丰收节回归，持续至10月31日，以音乐致敬多莉·帕顿\n4\n325万美元WBE Champions鲈鱼锦标赛押注由粉丝买单\n3\n查塔努加团体在10月5日截止日前就选民登记发出警告","publish_source":"foxchattanooga.com","publish_time":"2026-07-20T15:12:20+00:00"}},{"id":"news-486","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI与雷诺-斯帕克斯印第安殖民地警方在安娜·斯科特遇害案中再逮捕一人","title_en":"FBI, Reno-Sparks Indian Colony police make another arrest in Anna Scott killing","summary_cn":"美国联邦调查局与雷诺-斯帕克斯印第安殖民地警察局于7月27日在雷诺逮捕了该殖民地成员乔尔·克里斯蒂，联邦指控为事后从犯及协助教唆。此案涉及2022年派拉蒙湖派尤特部落成员安娜·斯科特遭枪杀后被焚尸的案件。警方表示调查仍在进行，将继续与联邦、州、地方及部落执法机构合作，确保所有涉案人员被绳之以法。","summary_en":"The FBI, working with the Reno-Sparks Indian Colony Police Department, arrested colony member Joel Christy in Reno on July 27 on federal charges of accessory after the fact and aiding and abetting in the 2022 homicide of Anna Scott, a Pyramid Lake Paiute Tribe member who was shot and killed and whose body was placed in a car and set on fire. Authorities said the investigation remains active and ongoing, with federal, state, local and tribal agencies continuing to work together to identify and bring to justice everyone involved.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-25T10:42:11.344117+00:00","url":"https://foxreno.com/news/local/fbi-reno-sparks-indian-colony-police-make-another-arrest-in-anna-scott-killing","content":"FBI, Reno-Sparks Indian Colony police make another arrest in Anna Scott killingby Kaylynn PerezMon, July 27, 2026 at 2:37 PMPhotos of Anna Scott (Courtesy of Scott's family)0CommentSharetopics: FBIAnna ScottReno-SparksIndian ColonyJoel ChristyAccessoryAidingHomicideFederal investigators have made another arrest in the homicide investigation into the death of Anna Scott, a member of the Pyramid Lake Paiute Tribe who was shot and killed before her body was placed inside a car and set on fire back in 2022. RELATED: Delshay Astor appears in federal court for Anna Scott killing, jury trial set for Aug. 4The Federal Bureau of Investigation, working with the Reno-Sparks Indian Colony Police Department, arrested Reno-Sparks Indian Colony member Joel Christy on July 27, in Reno on federal charges of accessory after the fact and aiding and abetting.A federal indictment was obtained, and Christy was taken into custody without incident.The investigation remains active and ongoing, with federal, state, local and tribal law enforcement agencies continuing to work together.“I want to commend the outstanding work of the FBI, the Washoe County Sheriff’s Office, and all of our law enforcement partners for their continued dedication to this investigation,” RSIC Chief of Police Jarrod J. Nunes said. “Today’s arrest represents another significant step forward, but our work is not finished. We remain committed to ensuring that everyone involved is identified and brought to justice.”RELATED: Four years later, suspect arrested in the death of Anna Marie Scott“Our hearts remain with Anna Scott’s family as they continue to endure the unimaginable pain of losing their loved one,” RSIC Chairman Daryl D. Gardipe said. “This tragedy has also weighed heavily on the Reno-Sparks Indian Colony community. It is deeply alarming when members of our community are connected to acts of violence, and these events affect us all. We hope today’s arrest brings Anna’s family one step closer to the justice they deserve and provides a path toward healing for everyone affected by this tragedy.”Watch the full press conference on Delshay Astor's indictment here: Because it is an active federal criminal investigation, the Reno-Sparks Indian Colony said it will not respond to media inquiries or provide additional comment beyond the release, and directed requests for information to the FBI.Trending323 grams of fentanyl, guns and $60,000 cash seized in Sparks drug bust323 grams of fentanyl, guns and $60,000 cash seized in Sparks drug bustCarson City Sheriff’s Office K-9Carson City Sheriff’s Office K-9 Camper is trained to use his nose to detect scents that can be difficult for people to find.Deputy Derrick Kepler and K-9 CampeEmergency landing near Spring Creek: Plane rolls 50 feet before ditch stopEmergency landing near Spring Creek: Plane rolls 50 feet before ditch stopReno parents appear in court in death of their daughter Izabella LovingNicholas and Andrea Loving appeared in Washoe County District Court Wednesday for a status hearing in the case involving the death of their 5-year-old daughter,Details and footage from Sparks officer-involved-shooting on Kleppe Lane released The Sparks Police Department is releasing details and footage regarding the September 15 officer-involved-shooting that happened on Kleppe Lane.NEWS IN PHOTOS:\"Local\"5Details and footage from Sparks officer-involved-shooting on Kleppe Lane released 4Two men sentenced for 2022 Sparks shooting death of Joel Undercoffer4Steve Alford to retire as Nevada men's basketball coach after 2026-27 season4Dump truck overturns on southbound I-580 in Reno, driver hurt","content_cn":"FBI、里诺-斯帕克斯印第安殖民地警方在安娜·斯科特遇害案中再次实施逮捕\n作者：Kaylynn Perez\n2026年7月27日，星期一，下午2:37\n安娜·斯科特的照片（由斯科特家人提供）\n0条评论\n分享\n主题：FBI、安娜·斯科特、里诺-斯帕克斯、印第安殖民地、乔尔·克里斯蒂、事后从犯、协助、杀人\n联邦调查人员在对安娜·斯科特死亡案的凶杀调查中再次实施逮捕。斯科特是金字塔湖派尤特部落成员，她于2022年遭枪击身亡，随后其遗体被放入一辆汽车并被纵火焚烧。\n相关报道：德尔谢·阿斯特就安娜·斯科特遇害案出庭联邦法院，陪审团审判定于8月4日举行\n联邦调查局与里诺-斯帕克斯印第安殖民地警察局合作，于7月27日在里诺逮捕了里诺-斯帕克斯印第安殖民地成员乔尔·克里斯蒂；他面临联邦事后从犯及协助和教唆罪名指控。\n已取得联邦起诉书，克里斯蒂在未发生意外的情况下被拘押。\n调查仍在积极进行中，联邦、州、地方和部落执法机构继续协作。\n“我要赞扬FBI、沃肖县警长办公室以及我们所有执法合作伙伴在这项调查中持续展现的出色工作和奉献精神，”RSIC警察局长Jarrod J. Nunes说。“今天的逮捕是又一个重要的进展，但我们的工作尚未完成。我们仍致力于确保所有涉案人员都被识别出来并被绳之以法。”\n相关报道：四年后，安娜·玛丽·斯科特死亡案嫌疑人被捕\n“当安娜·斯科特的家人仍在承受失去亲人的难以想象的痛苦时，我们的心始终与他们同在，”RSIC主席Daryl D. Gardipe说。“这场悲剧也令里诺-斯帕克斯印第安殖民地社区深感沉重。我们社区成员与暴力行为产生关联令人深感不安，而这些事件影响着我们所有人。我们希望今天的逮捕能让安娜的家人离他们应得的正义更近一步，并为所有受这场悲剧影响的人提供一条通往愈合的道路。”\n在此观看有关德尔谢·阿斯特被起诉的完整新闻发布会：\n里诺-斯帕克斯印第安殖民地表示，由于这是一起正在进行的联邦刑事调查，其不会回应媒体问询，也不会在新闻稿之外提供进一步评论，并将信息请求转交给FBI。\n热门\n在斯帕克斯缉毒行动中缴获323克芬太尼、枪支和6万美元现金\n在斯帕克斯缉毒行动中缴获323克芬太尼、枪支和6万美元现金\n卡森城警长办公室警犬\n卡森城警长办公室警犬 Camper 经过训练，能用鼻子探测人们难以发现的气味。\n副警长Derrick Kepler与警犬Campe\n斯普林克里克附近紧急降落：飞机滑行50英尺后在沟渠中停下\n斯普林克里克附近紧急降落：飞机滑行50英尺后在沟渠中停下\n里诺父母就女儿伊莎贝拉·洛文死亡案出庭\n尼古拉斯和安德里亚·洛文周三在沃肖县地区法院出席了有关其5岁女儿死亡案件的状态听证会，\n公布斯帕克斯警员在Kleppe Lane涉枪事件的细节和录像\n斯帕克斯警察局正在公布9月15日发生在Kleppe Lane的警员涉枪事件的细节和录像。\n图片新闻：\n“本地”\n5\n公布斯帕克斯警员在Kleppe Lane涉枪事件的细节和录像\n4\n两名男子因2022年斯帕克斯枪杀Joel Undercoffer案被判刑\n4\nSteve Alford将在2026-27赛季后从内华达大学男子篮球队教练职位退休\n4\n里诺I-580南向路段一辆翻斗车侧翻，司机受伤","publish_source":"foxreno.com","publish_time":"2026-07-27T21:37:50+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2495","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"国土安全部公布华盛顿特区被捕“最恶劣”移民嫌犯照片","title_en":"DHS shares the mugshots of the 'worst of the worst' migrants arrested in DC","summary_cn":"美国国土安全部公布了在华盛顿特区被捕的所谓“最恶劣”移民嫌犯照片，称这些人有绑架、袭击、贩毒等前科，其中两人分别为MS-13和18街帮派成员。报道称特朗普联邦接管特区警察后已有200多名非法移民被捕，助理部长麦克劳克林发表声明，FBI、缉毒局、移民及海关执法局等机构参与巡逻和抓捕。","summary_en":"The Department of Homeland Security released mugshots of migrants it called the 'worst of the worst' arrested in Washington, D.C., citing prior convictions for kidnapping, assault and drug trafficking, including two alleged MS-13 and 18th Street gang members. The report says over 200 illegal immigrants were arrested after Trump's federal takeover of D.C. policing, with FBI, DEA and ICE agents assisting patrols and arrests.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:18:36.851461+00:00","url":"https://foxsanantonio.com/news/nation-world/dhs-shares-the-mugshots-of-the-worst-of-the-worst-migrants-arrested-in-dc","content":"DHS shares the mugshots of the 'worst of the worst' migrants arrested in DCby ELAINE MALLON | The National News Desk Wed, August 20, 2025 at 12:32 PMUpdated Wed, August 20, 2025 at 1:22 PM16VIEW ALL PHOTOSOn Tuesday, August 19, the Department of Homeland Security highlighted some of the worst of the worst arrested in President Trump’s efforts to crack down on violent crime in Washington, D.C., over the past week. (DHS)0CommentSharetopics: MugshotsMigrantsDHSArrestsGang membersTrumpPublic safetyD.C.WASHINGTON (TNND) — Since President Donald Trump's federal takeover of the D.C. police force, authorities have apprehended more than 200 illegal immigrants, including several known gang members. The Department of Homeland Security released the mugshots of those it called the \"worst of the worst,\" previously convicted criminals, who were nabbed off the streets by law enforcement officers over the past week. Their combined rap sheet includes kidnapping, assault, smuggling heroin, larceny, commercialized sexual offenses, and \"dangerous drugs.\" Two of the men arrested — Cristian Salmeron-Osorio and Jossue Garcia-Portillo both from El Salvador — were known members of MS-13 and the 18th street gang, respectively.\"President Trump was clear: he will make DC safe and beautiful again, ”Assistant Secretary Tricia McLaughlin said in a statement. “In less than a week, ICE and CBP arrested gang members, kidnappers, drug traffickers, and other violent thugs. We will support the re-establishment of law and order and public safety, so Americans can feel safe in our nation’s capital.”Over the course of the past week, federal law enforcement agents from the FBI, Drug Enforcement Administration, Department of Homeland Security, Immigration and Customs Enforcement and several others have been seen all throughout D.C. patrolling the streets and assisting the Metropolitan Police Department in arrests. The National News Desk previously reported that following Trump's deployment of the National Guard and federal law enforcement agents, crime in D.C. has dropped by 8%, according to the D.C. Police Union. The D.C. Police Union reported on its Facebook page that violent crime is down by 22% and property crime is down by 6%. Carjackings saw the biggest drop — down by 83%. Robberies were down by 46% and car theft down by 21%.Have questions, concerns or tips? Send them to Elaine at emallon@sbgtv.com and follow here on X @MallonElaine Trending\"A tremendous loss\": Grieving coach remembers 15-year-old boxing studentJesse Balderrama, better known as \"Boogie\", strapped up his gloves at Top Dog Boxing on the south side.Biggest drug bust in Gonzales County history: 60 felonies, 40 suspectsA sweeping nine-month drug investigation in Gonzales County led to dozens of felony cases and the largest narcotics operation in county history.Gregg Popovich re-marries, ties the knot with Mary Barth BudenholzerThe longtime leader of the San Antonio Spurs has made headlines off the court.Six arrested after gambling raid at Far Southeast Side homeSAN ANTONIO &mdash; Six people were arrested Wednesday morning after Bexar County Sheriff's deputies carried out a search warrant at a home in Far Southeast Bexar County.The raid took place at a home off Esma Street near SoutMotorcycle rider critically injured after crashing into vehicle on Northwest SideSAN ANTONIO - A man was critically injured after crashing his motorcycle into a car early Thursday morning.The crash happened just before 4 a.m. at Wurzbach Road and Live Oak Road on the Northwest Side.Police said the 37NEWS IN PHOTOS:\"Local\"4Appeals court rejects finding that Texas death row inmate Melissa Lucio is innocent4Terrorism charge against San Antonio mother accused in school attack plot dismissed12Motorcycle rider critically injured after crashing into vehicle on Northwest Side10Driver still unidentified after 62-year-old man killed in Southeast Side hit-and-run","content_cn":"国土安全部分享了在华盛顿特区被捕的“最坏中的最坏”移民的嫌犯照片\n作者：ELAINE MALLON | The National News Desk\n2025年8月20日，星期三，下午12:32\n更新于2025年8月20日，星期三，下午1:22\n16\n查看全部照片\n8月19日，星期二，国土安全部重点介绍了在特朗普总统过去一周打击华盛顿哥伦比亚特区暴力犯罪的行动中被捕的一些“最坏中的最坏”人员。（DHS）\n0\n评论\n分享\n话题：嫌犯照片 移民 DHS 逮捕 帮派成员 特朗普 公共安全 华盛顿特区\n华盛顿（TNND）——自唐纳德·特朗普总统联邦接管华盛顿特区警察部门以来，当局已逮捕超过200名非法移民，其中包括数名已知的帮派成员。国土安全部公布了其称为“最坏中的最坏”的人员的嫌犯照片；这些此前被定罪的罪犯是在过去一周被执法人员从街头抓获的。\n\n他们合计的犯罪记录包括绑架、袭击、走私海洛因、盗窃、商业化性犯罪以及“危险药物”。被捕者中有两人——均来自萨尔瓦多的Cristian Salmeron-Osorio和Jossue Garcia-Portillo——分别是MS-13和第18街帮派的已知成员。\n\n“特朗普总统说得很清楚：他将让华盛顿特区再次安全、美丽，”助理部长Tricia McLaughlin在一份声明中说。“不到一周，ICE和CBP就逮捕了帮派成员、绑架犯、毒贩和其他暴力恶徒。我们将支持重建法治和公共安全，让美国人在我国首都感到安全。”\n\n在过去一周中，来自联邦调查局、缉毒局、国土安全部、移民与海关执法局以及其他若干机构的联邦执法人员一直在华盛顿特区各处巡逻街道，并协助大都会警察局实施逮捕。The National News Desk此前报道，根据华盛顿特区警察工会的数据，特朗普部署国民警卫队和联邦执法人员后，华盛顿特区犯罪率下降了8%。华盛顿特区警察工会在其Facebook页面称，暴力犯罪下降22%，财产犯罪下降6%。劫车案降幅最大——下降83%。抢劫案下降46%，汽车盗窃案下降21%。\n\n有问题、担忧或线索？请发送给Elaine：emallon@sbgtv.com，并在X上关注@MallonElaine。\n\n热门\n\n“巨大的损失”：悲痛的教练追忆15岁的拳击学生\nJesse Balderrama，更广为人知的名字是“Boogie”，曾在南区的Top Dog Boxing戴上拳击手套。\n\n冈萨雷斯县史上最大缉毒行动：60项重罪，40名嫌疑人\n在冈萨雷斯县开展的一项历时九个月的大规模毒品调查导致数十起重罪案件，成为该县历史上最大规模的毒品行动。\n\nGregg Popovich再婚，与Mary Barth Budenholzer结为连理\n这位圣安东尼奥马刺队长期领导者因场外消息登上新闻。\n\n远东南区一住宅赌博突袭后6人被捕\n圣安东尼奥——贝克萨县警长办公室的警员周三上午在贝克萨县远东南区一所住宅执行搜查令后，6人被捕。突袭发生在Esma街附近、靠近Sout……的一处住宅。\n\n西北区摩托车骑手撞上车辆后重伤\n圣安东尼奥——周四清晨，一名男子骑摩托车撞上一辆汽车后重伤。事故发生在凌晨4点前不久，地点位于西北区Wurzbach路与Live Oak路交叉口。警方称，这名37……\n\n图片新闻：\n“本地”\n4\n上诉法院驳回德州死囚Melissa Lucio无罪的认定\n4\n针对被控策划校园袭击的圣安东尼奥母亲的恐怖主义指控被撤销\n12\n西北区摩托车骑手撞上车辆后重伤\n10\n东南区一名62岁男子在肇事逃逸事故中死亡，司机身份仍未确定","publish_source":"foxsanantonio.com","publish_time":"2025-08-20T17:32:38+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1292","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"弗兰克尔关于众议院待议国土安全部法案的声明","title_en":"Frankel Statement on Pending House Department of Homeland Security Bill | U.S. Representative Lois Frankel","summary_cn":"2026年3月27日，美国众议员洛伊丝·弗兰克尔发表声明，批评共和党众议院领导层拒绝审议参议院已通过的两党法案。该法案旨在重新开放国土安全部大部分机构，并确保运输安全管理局官员等必要工作人员获得薪酬。弗兰克尔指出，这些员工已超过六周未领薪水却仍坚守岗位，而众议院共和党人却推进参议院已宣布无望通过的法案，纯属政治作秀，无法重开政府或支付工资。","summary_en":"On March 27, 2026, U.S. Rep. Lois Frankel issued a statement criticizing Republican House leadership for refusing to take up a bipartisan Senate-passed bill to reopen most of the Department of Homeland Security and ensure TSA officers and other essential workers are paid. She noted these workers have gone over six weeks without pay while continuing to keep Americans safe, and called the House Republican alternative political theater that will not reopen the government, pay workers, or advance real negotiations.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:29:14.549288+00:00","url":"https://frankel.house.gov/news/documentsingle.aspx?DocumentID=4990","content":"Press Releases\nFrankel Statement on Pending House Department of Homeland Security Bill\nShare on Facebook\nShare on X\nPrint this Page\nShare by Email\nWashington, DC,\nMarch 27, 2026\nToday, Rep. Lois Frankel released the following statement after Republican House leadership refused to take up a bipartisan Senate-passed bill to reopen the majority of the Department of Homeland Security.\n“I am appalled that Republican House leadership is refusing to take up the bipartisan Senate-passed bill, which would reopen most of the Department of Homeland Security and ensure TSA officers and other essential workers are paid,” said Rep. Frankel. “For more than six weeks, these hardworking Americans have gone without a paycheck while continuing to keep us safe. Instead, House Republicans are bringing up a bill that the Senate has already declared dead on arrival, which is nothing more than political theater. It won’t reopen the government, it won’t pay workers, and it won’t move us toward a real solution. Congress should act now to pay these workers and get back to serious negotiations on reining in ICE immigration enforcement.”","content_cn":"新闻稿\n弗兰克尔就待审议的众议院国土安全部法案发表声明\n分享到 Facebook\n分享到 X\n打印本页\n通过电子邮件分享\n华盛顿特区，\n2026年3月27日\n今天，在共和党众议院领导层拒绝审议一项已获参议院通过、旨在恢复国土安全部大部分机构运作的两党法案后，联邦众议员洛伊丝·弗兰克尔发表以下声明。\n“共和党众议院领导层拒绝审议这项获参议院通过的两党法案，我对此感到震惊。该法案将恢复国土安全部大部分机构的运作，并确保运输安全管理局人员和其他必要工作人员获得薪酬，”弗兰克尔众议员表示。“六个多星期以来，这些勤劳的美国人一直在继续保障我们的安全，却没有领到薪水。相反，众议院共和党人正在提出一项参议院已经宣布注定无法通过的法案，这不过是一场政治作秀。它不会让政府恢复运作，不会给工作人员发薪，也不会推动我们迈向真正的解决方案。国会应当立即采取行动，为这些工作人员发薪，并回到严肃的谈判中，以遏制移民与海关执法局的移民执法。”","publish_source":"frankel.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-03-27T00:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3604","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"警惕冒充CrowdStrike的欺诈邮件","title_en":"Beware fraudulent CrowdStrike emails","summary_cn":"2024年7月，CrowdStrike的一次缺陷更新导致全球计算机系统宕机。随后，美国网络安全和基础设施局警告称出现冒充CrowdStrike客服的网络钓鱼邮件，攻击者利用错拼域名伪装公司网站，邮件可能包含声称修复受影响电脑的附件或链接，实则可能擦除数据或窃取登录凭证。CrowdStrike情报部门已列出宕机后注册的潜在错拼域名。文章建议用户直接访问官网而非点击邮件链接，警惕意外附件，并识别错拼域名。","summary_en":"In July 2024, a defective CrowdStrike update caused a global computer outage. The U.S. Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Agency subsequently warned of phishing emails impersonating CrowdStrike customer support, with attackers using typosquatting domains to mimic the company's website. The emails may contain attachments or links claiming to fix affected computers but could erase data or steal login credentials. CrowdStrike Intelligence listed potential typosquatting domains registered after the outage. The article advises navigating directly to official websites, being wary of unexpected attachments, and spotting typosquatting domains.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:59:54.498924+00:00","url":"https://freedom.press/digisec/blog/beware-fraudulent-crowdstrike-emails","content":"Share\nCopy link\nEmail\nBluesky\nX/Twitter\nWhatsApp\nTelegram\nReddit\nMastodon\nLinkedIn\nFacebook\nPrint\nMore options\nBeware fraudulent CrowdStrike emails\nPublished\nJuly 24, 2024\nUpdated Nov. 8, 2024\n/\nFreedom of the Press Foundation\nTorkild Retvedt (CC BY-SA 2.0)\nIt’s the Digital Security Training team at Freedom of the Press Foundation (FPF), with security news that keeps you, your sources, and your devices safe. If someone has shared this newsletter with you, please subscribe here.\nIn the newsLast Friday, computer systems worldwide were taken down by a defective update from enterprise cybersecurity vendor CrowdStrike. In the wake of the outage, the U.S. Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Agency is warning of phishing emails, with attackers posing as CrowdStrike customer support. These emails may include file attachments or website links claiming to fix affected computers. Victims would believe that they are downloading an official patch. Instead, the attacks could completely erase computer data or steal login credentials. In its security blog, CrowdStrike Intelligence reports that these threat actors utilize typosquatting — intentionally misspelled or similar website domains — to impersonate the company’s website. CrowdStrike Intelligence has created a list of potential typosquatting domains registered after the outage. Read more here.\nGet Weekly Tips & Advice\nSubscribe for easy and actionable tips that improve your digital security awareness.\nFull Name\nEmail Address\nSubscribe\nSee all newsletters\nThanks for subscribing to Freedom of the Press Foundation’s digital security mailing list. We’ll send you easy and actionable tips that improve your digital security awareness.\nWhat you can doWe regularly advise our readers about targeted phishing attempts. If your newsroom was impacted by this outage, CrowdStrike has already released a self-mediation guide for your IT administrator to follow. But much of the advice on spotting phishing attempts applies to everyone in the newsroom, not just the IT team. You should also consider these actions to avoid future phishing attempts:If you receive emails claiming to be from customer support, navigate directly to the website yourself, rather than using the link from someone claiming to be from customer support. Read more about phishing here.Be wary of downloading or opening unexpected file attachments in emails. Some file types, like those ending in .exe and .pdf, are especially common for delivering malware. If you receive a suspicious PDF, you could use Dangerzone to convert it into a safe file.Finally, look for signs of typosquatting websites. They might be misspelled, or have additional words and letters before the domain name. For example, “fakewebsites[.]com” and “fakewebsitepatch[.]com” are typosquatting on “fakewebsite[.]com.”Our team is always ready to assist journalists with digital security concerns. Reach out here, and stay safe and secure out there.Best,Kevin–Kevin PhamDigital Security Training InternFreedom of the Press Foundation","content_cn":"分享\n复制链接\n电子邮件\nBluesky\nX/Twitter\nWhatsApp\nTelegram\nReddit\nMastodon\nLinkedIn\nFacebook\n打印\n更多选项\n\n警惕欺诈性CrowdStrike电子邮件\n\n发布时间\n2024年7月24日\n更新时间：2024年11月8日\n/\n新闻自由基金会\nTorkild Retvedt（CC BY-SA 2.0）\n\n这里是新闻自由基金会（FPF）的数字安全培训团队，为你带来安全资讯，帮助保护你、你的消息来源和你的设备安全。如果有人将这份新闻通讯分享给你，请在此订阅。\n\n新闻动态\n上周五，全球计算机系统因企业网络安全供应商CrowdStrike发布的一次有缺陷更新而瘫痪。此次中断发生后，美国网络安全与基础设施局警告称，出现了网络钓鱼电子邮件，攻击者冒充CrowdStrike客户支持人员。这些电子邮件可能包含文件附件或网站链接，声称可以修复受影响的计算机。受害者会以为自己正在下载官方补丁，实际上，这些攻击可能彻底删除计算机数据或窃取登录凭据。在其安全博客中，CrowdStrike Intelligence报告称，这些威胁行为者利用“域名仿冒”——故意拼写错误或使用相似的网站域名——来冒充该公司的网站。CrowdStrike Intelligence已创建一份中断发生后注册的潜在仿冒域名列表。点击此处阅读更多内容。\n\n每周提示与建议\n订阅即可获取简单、可操作的建议，帮助提升你的数字安全意识。\n\n姓名\n电子邮件地址\n订阅\n查看所有新闻通讯\n\n感谢你订阅新闻自由基金会的数字安全邮件列表。我们将发送简单、可操作的建议，帮助提升你的数字安全意识。\n\n你可以采取的措施\n我们会定期向读者提供有关针对性网络钓鱼企图的建议。如果你的新闻编辑部受到此次中断影响，CrowdStrike已经发布了一份自助修复指南，供你的IT管理员遵循。但识别网络钓鱼企图的大部分建议适用于编辑部所有人，而不仅仅是IT团队。你还应考虑采取以下措施，避免未来遭遇网络钓鱼企图：\n\n如果你收到声称来自客户支持的电子邮件，请自行直接访问该网站，而不要使用自称客户支持人员的人发来的链接。点击此处阅读更多关于网络钓鱼的信息。\n\n警惕下载或打开电子邮件中意外出现的文件附件。某些文件类型（例如以.exe和.pdf结尾的文件）尤其常被用于传播恶意软件。如果你收到可疑的PDF，可以使用Dangerzone将其转换为安全文件。\n\n最后，留意仿冒网站的迹象。它们可能存在拼写错误，或在域名前添加额外的单词和字母。例如，“fakewebsites[.]com”和“fakewebsitepatch[.]com”都是对“fakewebsite[.]com”的域名仿冒。\n\n我们的团队随时准备协助记者处理数字安全问题。请在此联系我们，并在网络环境中保持安全。\n\n此致\nKevin——Kevin Pham\n数字安全培训实习生\n新闻自由基金会","publish_source":"freedom.press","publish_time":"2024-07-24T13:00:00-07:00"}},{"id":"news-1841","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI无视联邦法律突袭记者住所","title_en":"FBI ignores federal law to raid journalist’s home","summary_cn":"自由新闻基金会（FPF）发布声明，谴责FBI突袭《华盛顿邮报》记者汉娜·纳坦森的住所。FPF倡导主任塞思·斯特恩指出，司法部及批准搜查令的法官无视或曲解了《隐私保护法》，该法禁止执法部门为寻找他人犯罪证据而突袭新闻编辑室和记者。政府表示纳坦森并非调查对象，但FPF担心记者与消息来源的保密性将受到侵犯。","summary_en":"The Freedom of the Press Foundation (FPF) issued a statement condemning the FBI's raid on the home of Washington Post reporter Hannah Natanson. FPF Advocacy Director Seth Stern said the Department of Justice and the judge who approved the warrant ignored or distorted the Privacy Protection Act, which bars law enforcement from raiding newsrooms and reporters to search for evidence of alleged crimes by others. The government said Natanson is not under investigation, but FPF fears journalist-source confidentiality will be compromised.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:32:24.129642+00:00","url":"https://freedom.press/issues/fbi-ignores-federal-law-to-raid-journalists-home","content":"Search & Seizure\nShare\nCopy link\nEmail\nBluesky\nX/Twitter\nWhatsApp\nTelegram\nReddit\nMastodon\nLinkedIn\nFacebook\nPrint\nMore options\nFBI ignores federal law to raid journalist’s home\nJan. 14, 2026\n/\nFreedom of the Press Foundation\nAn FBI agent pictured during an operation in 2025.\nAP Photo/David Zalubowski\nFOR IMMEDIATE RELEASE: This morning, the FBI raided the home of Washington Post reporter Hannah Natanson, reportedly in connection with an investigation of a system administrator accused of accessing and taking home classified intelligence reports. The following can be attributed to Seth Stern, chief of advocacy at Freedom of the Press Foundation (FPF).\n“This is an alarming escalation in the Trump administration’s multipronged war on press freedom. The Department of Justice (and the judge who approved this outrageous warrant) is either ignoring or distorting the Privacy Protection Act, which bars law enforcement from raiding newsrooms and reporters to search for evidence of alleged crimes by others, with very few inapplicable exceptions.“The government has said that Natanson is not under investigation, nor should she be for simply reporting information provided to her by sources. Even the Trump DOJ’s guidelines on searching reporters’ source materials (which were weakened from prior guidelines based on the administration’s proven lies about “fake news”) make clear that it’s a last resort for rare emergencies only. The administration may now be in possession of volumes of journalist communications having nothing to do with any pending investigation and, if investigators are able to access them, we have zero faith that they will respect journalist-source confidentiality.”\nPlease contact us if you would like further comment.\nRelated Posts\nICE wants to scare you out of sharing the news\nICE•Newsletter\nDisciplinary office ignores complaints over journalist raid\nSearch & Seizure•Article\nPPE protects your right to know\nProtests•Newsletter","content_cn":"搜查与扣押\n分享\n复制链接\n电子邮件\nBluesky\nX/Twitter\nWhatsApp\nTelegram\nReddit\nMastodon\nLinkedIn\nFacebook\n打印\n更多选项\n\nFBI无视联邦法律，搜查记者住所\n2026年1月14日\n/\n新闻自由基金会\n\n2025年一次行动中的FBI特工。\n美联社照片/David Zalubowski\n\n立即发布：今天上午，FBI搜查了《华盛顿邮报》记者汉娜·纳坦森的住所，据报道，此次行动与调查一名系统管理员有关，该管理员被指控访问并带回家机密情报报告。以下声明可归于新闻自由基金会（FPF）倡导负责人塞思·斯特恩。\n\n“这是特朗普政府对新闻自由发动多线战争的令人震惊的升级。司法部（以及批准这份离谱搜查令的法官）要么无视、要么歪曲《隐私保护法》；该法禁止执法部门搜查新闻编辑部和记者，以寻找他人涉嫌犯罪的证据，只有极少数不适用的例外情况。\n\n“政府表示纳坦森并未受到调查，而且她只是报道消息来源提供的信息，本不应受到调查。即使是特朗普司法部关于搜查记者消息来源材料的指导方针（该方针因政府被证实有关‘假新闻’的谎言而较以往版本削弱）也明确指出，这只能是罕见紧急情况下的最后手段。政府现在可能掌握大量与任何正在进行的调查毫无关系的记者通信；如果调查人员能够访问这些通信，我们完全不相信他们会尊重记者与消息来源之间的保密关系。”\n\n如需进一步评论，请联系我们。\n\n相关文章\nICE想吓得你不敢分享新闻\nICE•通讯\n\n纪律办公室无视有关搜查记者住所的投诉\n搜查与扣押•文章\n\nPPE保护你的知情权\n抗议•通讯","publish_source":"freedom.press","publish_time":"2026-01-14T11:37:00-08:00"}},{"id":"news-406","ktid":1056587,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1056587","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"英特尔Gamer Days 2026促销活动启动","title_en":"Dawn of the Deals: Gamer Days 2026 | Intel Gaming Access","summary_cn":"英特尔游戏官方博客介绍2026年Gamer Days活动，自8月10日启动，持续至9月13日的零售捆绑促销允许购买符合条件的英特尔酷睿、酷睿Ultra或Arc显卡产品的玩家获得《古墓丽影：亚特兰蒂斯遗产》和《星球大战：银河赛车》数字版。英特尔是两款游戏的官方发布合作伙伴，提供XeSS 3支持，并联合Fuse Games与Crystal Dynamics优化。文章还列出参与零售商及抽奖活动细节。","summary_en":"Intel's gaming blog announces Gamer Days 2026, running from August 10, with a retail bundle through September 13 letting buyers of qualifying Intel Core, Core Ultra, or Arc graphics products obtain digital copies of Tomb Raider: Legacy of Atlantis and STAR WARS: Galactic Racer. Intel is the official launch partner for both titles, providing XeSS 3 support and working with Fuse Games and Crystal Dynamics on optimization. The post also lists participating retailers and giveaway details.","tag":"other","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:59:18.192316+00:00","url":"https://game.intel.com/us/stories/dawn-of-the-deals-gamer-days-2026/","content":"< News\nBy Intel Gaming |\nAugust 9, 2026\nDawn of the Deals: Gamer Days 2026\nThe 2026 iteration of Intel’s annual Gamer Days celebration begins today, August 10, and this is your invitation to participate to the fullest. There are giveaways to be had, content collaborations to enjoy, promotions galore, and don’t forget the headline act—the Intel retail bundle. The bundle offer runs from August 10 through September 13 and with it gamers can secure their own digital copies of the upcoming titles Tomb Raider: Legacy of Atlantis and STAR WARS: Galactic Racer™ when they make a qualifying Intel Core, Intel Core Ultra, or Intel Arc™ Graphics purchase from one of Intel’s participating partners.\nThese two epic titles also feature in the Intel Gaming Access giveaway—but in collector’s editions! Now that you want them even more, enter from August 10 to September 10 for a chance to win Tomb Raider: Legacy of Atlantis Collector’s Edition and/or STAR WARS: Galactic Racer™ Collector’s Edition. Try for both, see what happens—you can never have too many collector’s editions.\nIntel is the official launch partner for both Tomb Raider: Legacy of Atlantis (on general release from February 12, 2027) and STAR WARS: Galactic Racer™ (releases October 6, 2026). Intel has worked closely with Fuse Games and Crystal Dynamics to optimize both games for Intel gaming platforms—that includes XeSS 3 support at launch—to ensure that gamers get the best possible experience on their Intel-powered systems with these titles. On launch day, expect enablement for the full suite of XeSS 3 technologies in both titles, which means XeSS Super Resolution (SR), XeSS Frame Generation (FG), Xe Low Latency (LL), and Xe Multi-Frame Generation. All ensure a smooth, high-fidelity gaming experience. And it’s not just Intel who’s excited.\nMatt Webster, founder and CEO of Fuse Games, says: “From the outset we wanted to create an experience that delights players, and making sure the game runs brilliantly on PC is an important part of that vision. We’ve worked closely with the team at Intel to help us fine-tune performance and deliver enhancements like XeSS 3, giving players the best possible experience when they jump in on October 6.”\nAnd this from Scot Amos, Head of Studio, Crystal Dynamics: “We’re excited for players to discover Tomb Raider: Legacy of Atlantis on February 12, 2027. Intel has been an incredible partner throughout development, working closely with our team to ensure players enjoy an optimized and immersive experience when they step into our reimagining of Lara Croft’s debut adventure.”\nSo, where to get the bundle? To get Tomb Raider: Legacy of Atlantis and/or STAR WARS: Galactic Racer™, choose from the following products and enjoy the very best gaming experience—there is of course a range to suit. The Intel Gamer Days retail bundle featuring Tomb Raider: Legacy of Atlantis and STAR WARS: Galactic Racer™ includes purchases of the following qualifying Intel products from participating retail and OEM partners.\nLooking for a new desktop? These are your qualifying products: IntelⓇ CoreTM Ultra 5 and 7 Plus processors (Series 2); Intel Core Ultra 5, 7, and 9 processors (Series 2); Intel Core 14th Gen processors. For mobile, look for Intel Core Ultra 5, 7, and 9 processors (Series 3); Intel Core Ultra 5 and 7 Plus processors (Series 2); select mobile systems with Intel Core Ultra 5, 7, and 9 processors (Series 2); Intel Core processors (Series 2); IntelⓇ ArcTM G-series powered handheld devices. Qualifying Intel Arc Graphics products are: Intel Arc B-series discrete graphics cards and Intel Arc A-series discrete graphics cards. Gamers please take note that with each qualifying purchase, you get access to Tomb Raider: Legacy of Atlantis and STAR WARS: Galactic Racer™ download links on each title’s respective launch date. However, you need to redeem the bundle offers by October 31, 2026, to receive the relevant download links. To get up to speed on all that Intel-powered PC gaming makes possible, from ultimate AI performance and power efficiency to needle-sharp visuals and effortless multi-tasking, just click here.\nOK, where to buy? This is important because not every retailer out there is involved with the Gamer Days promotion and you don’t want to miss out on optimizing your purchase. In no order of merit because we are pretty pleased to partner with them all, here are the places to fulfil your Gamer Days needs. You can check out the promotion at Microcenter here. Go to iBUYPOWER for their custom PCs and laptops. CyberpowerPC adds Gamer Days to its deals. Assemble your battle station at ABS. Get a PC that’s built to be seen at NZXT. Razer reckons they have all you need for your dream setup. Save up to USD$260 on a new gaming PC at BuildRedux. For excellent AV, head to B&H photo and video. MAINGEAR, the boutique PC integrator, is involved. Find days of deals at Nimo, here. Access Corsair’s promotion here. Don’t skip Origin PC and their offers. Build your way to a deal at Skytech Gaming. Find your PC at Stormcraft. Join the party with Thermaltake. Access Amazon’s deals here. And last but not least, check out Yeyian Gaming. Whatever you’re looking for, there’s a retailer ready to take your gaming experience to the next level.\nNow you know where to go, make the most of these precious days before they’re done.\n< News","content_cn":"< 新闻\n作者：Intel Gaming |\n2026年8月9日\n优惠盛宴开启：Gamer Days 2026\n英特尔年度 Gamer Days 庆典的 2026 年活动将于今天（8 月 10 日）开始，这是邀请你尽情参与的时刻。这里有赠品可领取、内容合作可欣赏、各种促销活动，当然也别忘了重头戏——英特尔零售捆绑包。捆绑包优惠从 8 月 10 日持续至 9 月 13 日，届时玩家从英特尔参与合作伙伴处购买符合条件的 Intel Core、Intel Core Ultra 或 Intel Arc™ 显卡产品，即可获得即将推出的《古墓丽影：亚特兰蒂斯遗产》和《星球大战：银河赛车™》数字版游戏。\n这两款史诗级游戏也会出现在 Intel Gaming Access 赠品活动中——不过是收藏版！现在是不是更想要了？8 月 10 日至 9 月 10 日期间报名，就有机会赢取《古墓丽影：亚特兰蒂斯遗产》收藏版和/或《星球大战：银河赛车™》收藏版。两款都试试，看看会发生什么——收藏版永远不会嫌多。\n英特尔是《古墓丽影：亚特兰蒂斯遗产》（2027 年 2 月 12 日正式发售）和《星球大战：银河赛车™》（2026 年 10 月 6 日发售）的官方发布合作伙伴。英特尔与 Fuse Games 和 Crystal Dynamics 密切合作，针对英特尔游戏平台优化了这两款游戏——包括在发售时支持 XeSS 3——确保玩家在搭载英特尔技术的系统上游玩这些作品时获得最佳体验。发售当天，预计两款游戏都将支持完整的 XeSS 3 技术套件，这意味着 XeSS 超级分辨率（SR）、XeSS 帧生成（FG）、Xe 低延迟（LL）以及 Xe 多帧生成。所有这些都将带来流畅且高保真的游戏体验。而且，感到兴奋的可不只是英特尔。\nFuse Games 创始人兼首席执行官 Matt Webster 表示：“从一开始，我们就希望打造让玩家喜爱的体验，而确保游戏在 PC 上出色运行是这一愿景的重要组成部分。我们与英特尔团队密切合作，帮助我们微调性能并交付 XeSS 3 等增强功能，让玩家在 10 月 6 日进入游戏时获得最佳体验。”\nCrystal Dynamics 工作室负责人 Scot Amos 这样说道：“我们很期待玩家在 2027 年 2 月 12 日探索《古墓丽影：亚特兰蒂斯遗产》。在整个开发过程中，英特尔一直是令人难以置信的合作伙伴，与我们的团队密切合作，确保玩家踏入我们重新构想的劳拉·克劳馥初次冒险时，能够享受经过优化且沉浸感十足的体验。”\n那么，去哪里获得捆绑包呢？要获得《古墓丽影：亚特兰蒂斯遗产》和/或《星球大战：银河赛车™》，请从以下产品中进行选择，享受最出色的游戏体验——当然，这里有适合各种需求的产品。包含《古墓丽影：亚特兰蒂斯遗产》和《星球大战：银河赛车™》的 Intel Gamer Days 零售捆绑包，适用于从参与的零售和 OEM 合作伙伴处购买以下符合条件的英特尔产品。\n想买一台新台式机？符合条件的产品包括：IntelⓇ CoreTM Ultra 5 和 7 Plus 处理器（第 2 系列）；Intel Core Ultra 5、7 和 9 处理器（第 2 系列）；Intel Core 第 14 代处理器。对于移动设备，请寻找 Intel Core Ultra 5、7 和 9 处理器（第 3 系列）；Intel Core Ultra 5 和 7 Plus 处理器（第 2 系列）；搭载 Intel Core Ultra 5、7 和 9 处理器（第 2 系列）的指定移动系统；Intel Core 处理器（第 2 系列）；搭载 IntelⓇ ArcTM G 系列\n手持设备。符合条件的 Intel Arc Graphics 产品包括：Intel Arc B 系列独立显卡和 Intel Arc A 系列独立显卡。玩家请注意，每购买一件符合条件的产品，您都可在《Tomb Raider: Legacy of Atlantis》和《STAR WARS: Galactic Racer™》各自的发行日期获得相应游戏的下载链接。不过，您需要在 2026 年 10 月 31 日之前兑换套装优惠，才能获取相关下载链接。想全面了解 Intel 驱动的 PC 游戏能实现的一切，从极致的 AI 性能和能效，到锐利如针的画面和轻松的多任务处理，只需点击此处。\n\n好了，去哪里买？这一点很重要，因为并非所有零售商都参与 Gamer Days 促销，而您肯定不想错过优化购买的机会。排名不分先后，因为我们很高兴与所有合作伙伴携手合作，以下就是满足您 Gamer Days 需求的购买渠道。您可以在此查看 Microcenter 的促销活动。前往 iBUYPOWER 购买其定制 PC 和笔记本电脑。CyberpowerPC 将 Gamer Days 加入其优惠活动。在 ABS 组装您的战斗基地。在 NZXT 购买一台专为展示而打造的 PC。Razer 认为，他们拥有打造梦想装备所需的一切。在 BuildRedux 购买全新的游戏 PC，最高可节省 260 美元。想要出色的音视频产品，请前往 B&H photo and video。精品 PC 整合商 MAINGEAR 也参与其中。在此查看 Nimo 的多日优惠。在此访问 Corsair 的促销页面。别错过 Origin PC 及其优惠。在 Skytech Gaming 以优惠价格组装您的设备。在 Stormcraft 找到您的 PC。加入 Thermaltake 的派对。在此查看 Amazon 的优惠。最后但同样重要的是，别忘了看看 Yeyian Gaming。无论您在寻找什么，都有一家零售商准备好将您的游戏体验提升到新的高度。\n\n现在您知道该去哪里了，请在这些珍贵的日子结束之前充分利用它们。\n< 新闻","publish_source":"game.intel.com","publish_time":"2026-08-09T23:55:06+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3535","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"国会议员卡洛斯·希门尼斯在众议院国土安全委员会听证会上质询证人","title_en":"CONGRESSMAN CARLOS GIMENEZ GRILLS RACIST DEMOCRAT WITNESS AT HOUSE HOMELAND SECURITY COMMITTEE HEARING | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez","summary_cn":"美国众议员卡洛斯·希门尼斯办公室发布的新闻稿称，希门尼斯在众议院国土安全委员会关于美国边境安全的听证会上质询证人、亚利桑那州警长大卫·哈撒韦，后者指责其立场种族主义。新闻稿强调希门尼斯作为古巴出生移民支持加强边境安全、结束非法移民，并介绍其担任国土安全部交通与海事安全小组委员会主席等职务。","summary_en":"A press release from Congressman Carlos Gimenez's office states that during a House Homeland Security Committee hearing on U.S. border security, Gimenez questioned witness Arizona Sheriff David Hathaway, who accused the congressman of racism over his border stance. The release stresses that Gimenez, the only Cuban-born member of Congress and an immigrant himself, supports comprehensive border security and ending illegal immigration, and notes his role as Chairman of the Homeland Security Subcommittee on Transportation and Maritime Security.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T22:32:13.564542+00:00","url":"https://gimenez.house.gov/2024/9/congressman-carlos-gimenez-grills-racist-democrat-witness-at-house-homeland-security-committee-hearing","content":"Press Releases\nHome\nMedia\nPress Releases\nPrint\nCONGRESSMAN CARLOS GIMENEZ GRILLS RACIST DEMOCRAT WITNESS AT HOUSE HOMELAND SECURITY COMMITTEE HEARING\nSeptember 18, 2024\nWashington, D.C. - Today, Congressman Carlos Gimenez joined the House Homeland Security Committee hearing on U.S. border security. During Rep. Gimenez's line of questioning, Arizona Sheriff, David Hathaway, attempted to intimidate the Congressman and accused Rep. Gimenez of being a racist for his stance on the border crisis.\nCongressman Carlos Gimenez will not be intimidated by socialist Democrats who call supporting the border and legal immigration racist. As the only Cuban-born Member of Congress and an immigrant himself, Rep. Gimenez supports ending the border crisis by implementing comprehensive border security and ending the illegal immigration that continues to plague and undermine the security of our community and nation.\nWatch the fiery exchange HERE.\n###\nCongressman Carlos Giménez represents Miami-Dade County and the beautiful Florida Keys. He is the only Cuban-born Member of the 118th Congress, having fled his homeland shortly after the Communist takeover of the island. He is the first career firefighter paramedic elected to the House of Representatives and served as the former Fire Chief of the City of Miami and Mayor of Miami-Dade County. He serves as the Chairman of the Homeland Security Subcommittee on Transportation and Maritime Security, the Armed Services Committee, and the Select Committee on the Chinese Communist Party.\nPermalink: https://gimenez.house.gov/2024/9/congressman-carlos-gimenez-grills-racist-democrat-witness-at-house-homeland-security-committee-hearing\nMedia Kit\nPress Releases\nIn The News\nNewsletters\nYoutube\nPositive People in FL28","content_cn":"新闻稿\n首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n打印\n国会议员Carlos Gimenez在众议院国土安全委员会听证会上严厉质问种族主义民主党证人\n2024年9月18日\n华盛顿特区——今天，国会议员Carlos Gimenez参加了众议院国土安全委员会关于美国边境安全的听证会。在Gimenez议员的质询过程中，亚利桑那州警长David Hathaway试图恐吓这位国会议员，并指责Gimenez议员因其对边境危机的立场而具有种族主义。\n国会议员Carlos Gimenez不会被那些把支持边境安全和合法移民称为种族主义的社会主义民主党人吓倒。作为国会唯一一名古巴出生的议员、也是一名移民，Gimenez议员支持通过实施全面的边境安全措施，并结束持续困扰和削弱我们社区及国家安全的非法移民，来终结边境危机。\n观看这场激烈交锋，请点击这里。\n###\n国会议员Carlos Giménez代表迈阿密-戴德县和美丽的佛罗里达群岛。他是第118届国会唯一一名古巴出生的议员，在该岛被共产党接管后不久逃离祖国。他是第一位当选众议院议员的职业消防员兼急救医护人员，曾任迈阿密市消防局局长和迈阿密-戴德县县长。他担任国土安全委员会运输与海事安全小组委员会主席、军事委员会委员以及中国共产党特别委员会委员。\n永久链接：https://gimenez.house.gov/2024/9/congressman-carlos-gimenez-grills-racist-democrat-witness-at-house-homeland-security-committee-hearing\n媒体资料包\n新闻稿\n新闻报道\n新闻通讯\nYouTube\n佛罗里达州第28选区的积极人士","publish_source":"gimenez.house.gov","publish_time":"2024-09-18T00:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3052","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"国会议员卡洛斯·希门尼斯请愿国土安全部驱逐卡斯特罗政权特工","title_en":"CONGRESSMAN CARLOS GIMENEZ PETITIONS DHS TO DEPORT CASTRO REGIME AGENTS | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez","summary_cn":"2025年3月20日，美国众议员卡洛斯·希门尼斯致信国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆，敦促其立即调查并驱逐卡斯特罗政权特工，并附上与该政权镇压机构有直接关联的人员名单。文中提到3月14日ICE逮捕了居住在南佛罗里达的古巴情报人员托马斯·埃米利奥·埃尔南德斯·克鲁兹。希门尼斯表示将继续与国土安全部合作，识别并遣返此类人员。","summary_en":"On March 20, 2025, U.S. Congressman Carlos Gimenez sent a letter to Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem urging her to immediately investigate and deport agents of the Castro regime, providing a list of individuals with direct ties to the regime's repressive apparatus. The release notes that on March 14, 2025, ICE arrested Tomas Emilio Hernandez Cruz, a Cuban intelligence agent residing in South Florida. Gimenez said he will continue working with DHS to identify and repatriate such agents.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:58:19.526121+00:00","url":"https://gimenez.house.gov/2025/3/congressman-carlos-gimenez-petitions-dhs-to-deport-castro-regime-agents","content":"Press Releases\nHome\nMedia\nPress Releases\nPrint\nCONGRESSMAN CARLOS GIMENEZ PETITIONS DHS TO DEPORT CASTRO REGIME AGENTS\nMarch 20, 2025\nWASHINGTON, D.C. - Today, Congressman Carlos Gimenez (R-FL) sent a letter to Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem urging her to immediately investigate and deport agents of the Castro regime. Congressman Gimenez has provided the Secretary with a list of individuals with direct ties to the regime’s repressive apparatus.\nCurrently, regime agents who previously upheld the Castro dictatorship’s brutal policies have exploited U.S. immigration laws to gain entry into our country. These Cuban regime agents must immediately be identified, investigated, and deported\nOn March 14, 2025, U.S. Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) arrested Tomas Emilio Hernandez Cruz, an agent of the Castro intelligence sphere residing in South Florida. Cruz is in ICE custody pending deportation orders.\nCongressman Carlos Gimenez will continue to work closely with the Department of Homeland Security to further identify regime agents of terrorist regimes like Castro's Cuba, Maduro's Venezuela, and Ortega's Nicaragua, that have defrauded U.S. immigration laws and that are residing in our communities.\n“Like so many in our community, I was forced from my native homeland of Cuba shortly after the Communist Revolution & it is absolutely reprehensible how agents of the murderous Castro regime have gamed our immigration laws to infiltrate our country,” said Congressman Carlos Gimenez. “I applaud President Trump and his Administration for the swift action in recently apprehending an intelligence agent of the Cuban dictatorship living in South Florida and I look forward to continuing working closely together to identify, detain, and repatriate these despicable fraudsters living in our country.”\nRead the full letter to Secretary Noem HERE.\nRead the list of Castro regime agents residing in the U.S. HERE.\nRead the Fox News exclusive HERE.\n###\nCongressman Carlos Giménez represents Miami-Dade County and the beautiful Florida Keys. He is the only Cuban-born Member of the 119th Congress, having fled his homeland shortly after the Communist takeover of the island. He is the first career firefighter paramedic elected to the House of Representatives and served as the former Fire Chief of the City of Miami and Mayor of Miami-Dade County. Rep. Gimenez was appointed by Speaker Mike Johnson to the Smithsonian Institution’s Board of Regents and serves as Vice-Chairman of the Republican Governance Group. He serves as the Chairman of the Homeland Security Subcommittee on Transportation and Maritime Security, the Armed Services Committee, and the Select Committee on the Chinese Communist Party.\nPermalink: https://gimenez.house.gov/2025/3/congressman-carlos-gimenez-petitions-dhs-to-deport-castro-regime-agents\nMedia Kit\nPress Releases\nIn The News\nNewsletters\nYoutube\nPositive People in FL28","content_cn":"新闻稿\n首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n打印\n国会议员卡洛斯·希门尼斯请愿国土安全部驱逐卡斯特罗政权特工\n2025年3月20日\n华盛顿特区——今天，国会议员卡洛斯·希门尼斯（佛罗里达州共和党）致函国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆，敦促她立即调查并驱逐卡斯特罗政权的特工。国会议员希门尼斯已向部长提供了一份与该政权镇压机器有直接关联人员的名单。\n目前，曾执行卡斯特罗独裁政权残暴政策的政权特工，利用美国移民法进入了我国。这些古巴政权特工必须立即被识别、调查和驱逐。\n2025年3月14日，美国移民与海关执法局（ICE）逮捕了居住在南佛罗里达、属于卡斯特罗情报体系的特工托马斯·埃米利奥·埃尔南德斯·克鲁斯。克鲁斯目前被ICE拘押，等待驱逐令。\n国会议员卡洛斯·希门尼斯将继续与国土安全部密切合作，进一步识别卡斯特罗统治下的古巴、马杜罗统治下的委内瑞拉和奥尔特加统治下的尼加拉瓜等恐怖主义政权的特工；这些人欺骗美国移民法，并居住在我们的社区中。\n“和我们社区中的许多人一样，在共产主义革命后不久，我被迫离开了出生地古巴；卡斯特罗杀人政权的特工操弄我们的移民法、渗透我们的国家，绝对令人愤慨，”国会议员卡洛斯·希门尼斯表示。“我赞扬特朗普总统及其政府近期迅速采取行动，逮捕了一名居住在南佛罗里达的古巴独裁政权情报特工；我期待继续紧密合作，识别、拘留并遣返居住在我国的这些可鄙骗子。”\n在此阅读致诺姆部长的完整信函。\n在此阅读居住在美国的卡斯特罗政权特工名单。\n在此阅读福克斯新闻独家报道。\n###\n国会议员卡洛斯·希门尼斯代表迈阿密-戴德县和美丽的佛罗里达群岛。他是第119届国会中唯一出生于古巴的议员，在共产主义接管该岛后不久逃离故土。他是首位当选众议院的职业消防员兼急救医疗人员，曾担任迈阿密市消防局局长及迈阿密-戴德县县长。希门尼斯议员获议长迈克·约翰逊任命为史密森学会董事会成员，并担任共和党治理小组副主席。他担任国土安全委员会运输与海事安全小组委员会主席、军队委员会成员，以及中国共产党问题特别委员会成员。\n永久链接：https://gimenez.house.gov/2025/3/congressman-carlos-gimenez-petitions-dhs-to-deport-castro-regime-agents\n媒体资料包\n新闻稿\n新闻报道\n新闻通讯\nYouTube\n佛罗里达州第28选区的积极人士","publish_source":"gimenez.house.gov","publish_time":"2025-03-20T00:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2428","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"国会议员卡洛斯·希门尼斯要求国土安全部调查在美的卡斯特罗政权特工","title_en":"CONGRESSMAN CARLOS GIMENEZ REQUESTS DHS INVESTIGATE CASTRO REGIME AGENTS IN THE U.S. | Press Releases | Congressman Carlos Gimenez","summary_cn":"2025年9月9日，美国众议员卡洛斯·希门尼斯致信国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆，要求就居住在美国境内的卡斯特罗政权特工的调查与驱逐进展提供最新情况。信中他再次向诺姆提供了一份与古巴政权镇压机构直接相关的人员名单，并重申将与国土安全部合作，识别并清除那些欺诈美国移民法、潜伏于社区中的恐怖政权特工。","summary_en":"On September 9, 2025, U.S. Congressman Carlos Gimenez sent a letter to Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem requesting an update on the investigation and deportation of Castro regime agents residing in the United States. In the letter, he again provided Secretary Noem with a list of individuals directly linked to the Cuban regime's repressive apparatus, reiterating his commitment to working with DHS to identify and remove agents of terrorist regimes who defrauded U.S. immigration laws and embedded themselves in communities.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:12:41.329782+00:00","url":"https://gimenez.house.gov/2025/9/congressman-carlos-gimenez-requests-dhs-investigate-castro-regime-agents-in-the-u-s","content":"Press Releases\nHome\nMedia\nPress Releases\nPrint\nCONGRESSMAN CARLOS GIMENEZ REQUESTS DHS INVESTIGATE CASTRO REGIME AGENTS IN THE U.S.\nSeptember 9, 2025\nWASHINGTON, D.C. - Congressman Carlos Gimenez (R-FL) sent a letter to Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem requesting an update on the investigation and deportation of agents of the Castro regime residing in the United States.\nIn his letter, Congressman Gimenez provided Secretary Noem with a list of individuals directly linked to the Cuban regime’s repressive apparatus. He reiterated his commitment to working with the Department of Homeland Security to identify and remove agents of terrorist regimes who have defrauded U.S. immigration laws and embedded themselves in our communities.\nRead the Fox News exclusive HERE.\nRead the full letter HERE:\n###\nCongressman Carlos Giménez represents Miami-Dade County and the beautiful Florida Keys. He is the only Cuban-born Member of the 119th Congress, having fled his homeland shortly after the Communist takeover of the island. He is the first career firefighter-paramedic elected to the House of Representatives and served as the former Fire Chief of the City of Miami and Mayor of Miami-Dade County. Rep. Gimenez serves as the Chairman of the Homeland Security Subcommittee on Transportation and Maritime Security, the Armed Services Committee, and the Select Committee on the Chinese Communist Party. He was appointed by Speaker Mike Johnson to the Smithsonian Institution’s Board of Regents and the Mexico–United States Interparliamentary Group. Further, he serves as Vice-Chairman of the Republican Governance Group (RG2) and Vice Chair of Community Outreach for the Congressional Hispanic Conference.\nPermalink: https://gimenez.house.gov/2025/9/congressman-carlos-gimenez-requests-dhs-investigate-castro-regime-agents-in-the-u-s\nMedia Kit\nPress Releases\nIn The News\nNewsletters\nYoutube\nPositive People in FL28","content_cn":"新闻稿\n首页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n打印\n国会议员卡洛斯·希门尼斯要求国土安全部调查在美卡斯特罗政权特工\n2025年9月9日\n华盛顿特区——国会议员卡洛斯·希门尼斯（佛罗里达州共和党）致函国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆，请求就调查和驱逐居住在美国的卡斯特罗政权特工一事提供最新情况。\n希门尼斯议员在信中向诺姆部长提供了一份与古巴政权镇压机构有直接联系人员的名单。他重申，自己致力于与国土安全部合作，查明并驱逐那些欺骗美国移民法律、潜入我们社区的恐怖政权特工。\n阅读《福克斯新闻》独家报道，请点击这里。\n阅读完整信件，请点击这里：\n###\n国会议员卡洛斯·希门尼斯代表迈阿密-戴德县和美丽的佛罗里达群岛。他是第119届国会唯一一位出生于古巴的议员，在共产党接管该岛后不久逃离祖国。他是首位当选众议院议员的职业消防员兼急救医护员，曾任迈阿密市消防局局长和迈阿密-戴德县县长。希门尼斯议员担任国土安全委员会运输与海事安全小组委员会主席、军事委员会委员以及中国共产党特别委员会委员。他由议长迈克·约翰逊任命为史密森学会董事会董事以及墨西哥—美国议会间小组成员。此外，他还担任共和党治理小组（RG2）副主席和国会西语裔会议社区联络副主席。\n永久链接：https://gimenez.house.gov/2025/9/congressman-carlos-gimenez-requests-dhs-investigate-castro-regime-agents-in-the-u-s\n媒体资料包\n新闻稿\n媒体报道\n新闻通讯\nYouTube\n佛罗里达州第28国会选区积极人士","publish_source":"gimenez.house.gov","publish_time":"2025-09-09T00:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2732","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI局长再指温哥华为芬太尼危机源头，美国数据却显示相反","title_en":"FBI director again blames Vancouver for fentanyl crisis, but U.S. data says otherwise | Globalnews.ca","summary_cn":"美国联邦调查局(FBI)局长卡什·帕特尔在播客中再次指责温哥华在芬太尼危机中的角色，称贩运者将芬太尼飞入温哥华、在加拿大制造并全球分销。加拿大皇家骑警太平洋地区助理指挥官特布尔表示，加拿大向美国大量出口芬太尼的说法不准确，美国缉毒局和海关与边境保护局的数据也不支持。美国数据显示，2024财年美墨边境查获芬太尼逾1.8万磅，而美加边境仅约10磅。","summary_en":"FBI Director Kash Patel again blamed Vancouver for the fentanyl crisis, telling podcaster Joe Rogan that traffickers fly fentanyl into Vancouver, manufacture in Canada and distribute globally. RCMP Pacific region Assistant Commander David Teboul said claims that Canada exports significant quantities of fentanyl to the U.S. are inaccurate and not corroborated by U.S. agencies. U.S. data shows over 18,213 pounds seized at the U.S.-Mexico border in fiscal 2024 versus just over 10 pounds at the Canada-U.S. border.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T22:15:10.423540+00:00","url":"https://globalnews.ca/news/11246670/fbi-director-blames-vancouver-fentanyl-crisis-us-data","content":"Crime\nFBI director again blames Vancouver for fentanyl crisis, but U.S. data says otherwise\nBy\nAmy Judd &\nAngela Jung\nGlobal News\nPosted June 17, 2025 8:49 pm\nUpdated June 18, 2025 12:20 am\n3 min read\nIf you get Global News from Instagram or Facebook - that will be changing. Find out how you can still connect with us.\nHide message bar\n1:54\nRCMP defends fentanyl enforcement efforts against U.S. claims\nCanadian law enforcement continues to dispute U.S. claims about how much fentanyl is being smuggled across the border into the United States. It follows the latest allegation by the head of the FBI who specifically mentions Vancouver as a source of the problem. Angela Jung explains – Jun 17, 2025\nLeave a comment\nShare this item on Facebook\nShare this item via WhatsApp\nShare this item on X\nSend this page to someone via email\nSee more sharing options\nShare\nClose\nShare this item on Facebook\nfacebook\nShare this item on X\nx\nSend this page to someone via email\nemail\nShare this item via WhatsApp\nwhatsapp\nShare this item via Telegram\ntelegram\nShare this item on Reddit\nreddit\nShare this item on BlueSky\nbluesky\nCopy article link\nCopy link\nDescrease article font size\nIncrease article font size\nCanadian law enforcement continues to dispute claims from the U.S. administration about how much fentanyl is being smuggled across the border.\nIt follows the latest allegation by the head of the FBI who specifically mentions Vancouver as the source of the problem.In a recent appearance with podcaster Joe Rogan, FBI Director Kash Patel once again blamed Vancouver for its role in the fentanyl crisis.“They’re flying it into Vancouver, they’re taking the precursors to Canada, manufacturing up there, and doing their global distribution routes up there because we’ve been so effective down south,” Patel told Rogan.He also said that stricter enforcement at the Mexican border has resulted in cartels increasingly using Canada as a northern entry point for fentanyl.However, David Teboul, Assistant Commander of the RCMP, Pacific region, said the assertion that Canada is exporting fentanyl in “significant quantities into the U.S. is not accurate.” Story continues below advertisement\n“It is certainly not reflected by Canadian law enforcement agencies’ data, nor is it corroborated either by U. S. agencies, from the DEA (Drug Enforcement Administration), to the CBP (Customs and Border Protection), to all the partner agencies that we have very good relationships with,” Teboul said.\nGet breaking National news\nGet breaking Canada news delivered to your inbox as it happens so you won't miss a trending story.\nSign up for breaking National newsletter\nGet Started\nBy providing your email address, you have read and agree to Global News' Terms and Conditions and Privacy Policy.\n“They also don’t corroborate that. It’s been stated many times.”He did agree that most precursors are coming from China into Canada, but did not agree with the rest of Patel’s statement.\n2:10\nTrump’s FBI head criticizes Canadian drug enforcement\nData from the U.S. provided to Global News also showed that in the 2024 fiscal year, more than 18,213 pounds of fentanyl were seized at the U.S.-Mexico border.At the Canada-U.S. border, just over 10 pounds of fentanyl was seized in 2024. Story continues below advertisement\nSo far this year, more than 7,277 pounds of fentanyl from Mexico were confiscated compared to just over one pound from Canada.\nMore on Crime\nMore videos\nBelleville synagogue shooting a ‘hate-motivated attack,’ police say\nOttawa orders Appeal Court to review Saskatchewan sisters’ murder convictions\nNova Scotia teacher faces multiple sexual offense and assault charges\nPublic cautioned of high-risk sex offender who moved to Saskatoon: police\nTwo people killed in wrong way highway crash\nMore than $1M in drugs seized at Nova Scotia prison\nQuebec woman killed while on a Zoom call\nPolice say Martindale shooting was a targeted incident.\nHowever, one organized crime expert said it is critical not to be distracted by the data.“The drugs themselves don’t move by themselves, don’t get produced by themselves,” Calvin Chrustie, a senior partner and critical risk consultant with the Critical Risk Team said.“So let’s have the serious conversation about who are the threat actors, i.e., the criminal organizations. What type of support and enabling do they get from foreign states?”Chrustie said that B.C. has long been a convergence zone for organized crime groups and Vancouver is a popular choice due to its marine access.“I don’t think we should be listening to, and I never have, you know, in my career, post my career, to what the political assessment was, because I found it, you know, whether it was south of the border, north of the border, not the most informed historically, this whole issue got politicized,” he added.“I don’t think you know in terms of calculating the threat and calculating the severity of the problem, how much goes across a border.”Teboul said B.C. has a coordinated approach to drug trafficking and has had many successes getting drugs off the streets. Story continues below advertisement\n“British Columbia is also in a particular predicament, of course, with our very vast, beautiful ocean, but it’s permeable, of course, into the coast of British Columbia, and we need to dedicate some resources and investments at all three levels of government to secure our ports as well,” he added.\nStick to the Facts\nAdd Global News as a Preferred Source on Google to see more of our stories in your search results.\nJournalistic standards\nReport an error\n© 2025 Global News, a division of Corus Entertainment Inc.\nSponsored content\nMore from Global News\nBelleville synagogue shooting a ‘hate-motivated attack,’ police say\nQuebec man accused of chemical weapon plot faces terrorism charges\nAdvertisement\nStay in the loop\nThe email you need for the day’s top news stories from Canada and around the world.\nSign up for National newsletter\nSign Up\nTrending\nCarney says he studied risk of U.S.-led military action in NYT interview\n44,645\nRead\nDoctors urge women to remove fallopian tubes to reduce ovarian cancer risk\n25,084\nRead\nFormer soldier who shot at synagogue was suing military for $1M over vaccination policy\n24,674\nRead\nAs Trump mulls diesel export ban, what would it mean for Canada?\n18,845\nRead\n$11.5M from Sturgeon Lake trust helped fund Rath firm’s Tallcree payment: receiver\n15,347\nRead\nStarbucks to close 250 more stores in Canada and the U.S.\n15,276\nRead\nTop Videos\nWatermain break displaces 1,100 Trent University residence students in Peterborough\nPeterborough rowers selected for RBC Training Ground national final\nPeterborough city council divided on consultant’s report with ideas to save city up to $30 million\nOne City Peterborough cleanup team pilot project focuses on downtown streets\nWatermain break forces closure of Trent University’s Symons campus in Peterborough\nProject examines graveyards to reveal history of Peterborough County\nShredded plastic found across parks in Peterborough\nPeterborough area entrepreneurs learning how to implement AI into their businesses\nGlobal Peterborough’s Business Beat Sept. 21\nCity of Peterborough services review suggests zoo fees, airport transfer, garbage collection changes, sidewalk snowclearing cuts\nMore Videos\nStay in the loop\nThe email you need for the day’s top news stories from Canada and around the world.\nSign up for National newsletter\nSign Up\nAdvertisement\nReport an Error\nSubscribe here","content_cn":"犯罪\nFBI局长再次将芬太尼危机归咎于温哥华，但美国数据并非如此\n作者\nAmy Judd 和\nAngela Jung\n环球新闻\n发表于2025年6月17日晚上8:49\n更新于2025年6月18日凌晨12:20\n阅读需时3分钟\n如果你通过Instagram或Facebook获取环球新闻——这种情况将会改变。了解你仍可如何与我们保持联系。\n隐藏消息栏\n1:54\n加拿大皇家骑警为芬太尼执法行动辩护，回应美国方面的说法\n加拿大执法部门继续对美国关于有多少芬太尼被走私越境进入美国的说法提出异议。这是在FBI负责人最新指控之后发生的，他特别提到温哥华是问题的来源。Angela Jung报道——2025年6月17日\n发表评论\n在Facebook上分享此项目\n通过WhatsApp分享此项目\n在X上分享此项目\n通过电子邮件将此页面发送给某人\n查看更多分享选项\n分享\n关闭\n在Facebook上分享此项目\nfacebook\n在X上分享此项目\nx\n通过电子邮件将此页面发送给某人\nemail\n通过WhatsApp分享此项目\nwhatsapp\n通过Telegram分享此项目\ntelegram\n在Reddit上分享此项目\nreddit\n在BlueSky上分享此项目\nbluesky\n复制文章链接\n复制链接\n减小文章字体大小\n增大文章字体大小\n加拿大执法部门继续对美国政府关于有多少芬太尼被走私越境的说法提出异议。\n这是在FBI负责人最新指控之后发生的，他特别提到温哥华是问题的来源。近日，FBI局长Kash Patel与播客主持人Joe Rogan一同露面时，再次将芬太尼危机归咎于温哥华。“他们把芬太尼空运到温哥华，把前体运到加拿大，在那里制造，然后在那里进行全球分销，因为我们在南部的执法一直非常有效，”Patel对Rogan说。他还表示，墨西哥边境加强执法后，导致贩毒集团越来越多地利用加拿大作为芬太尼进入美国的北方入口。然而，加拿大皇家骑警太平洋地区助理指挥官David Teboul表示，称加拿大正以“数量巨大”的规模向美国出口芬太尼的说法并不准确。广告下方继续正文\n“加拿大执法机构的数据当然没有反映出这一点，美国机构也没有证实这一点——从缉毒局（DEA）到海关与边境保护局（CBP），再到我们与之保持良好关系的所有合作机构，”Teboul说。\n获取突发全国新闻\n突发加拿大新闻发生时直接发送到你的收件箱，这样你不会错过热门报道。\n注册突发全国新闻通讯\n开始\n提供电子邮件地址即表示你已阅读并同意环球新闻的条款与条件以及隐私政策。\n“他们也没有证实这一点。这已经被多次说明。”他确实同意，大多数前体是从中国运入加拿大的，但不同意Patel声明的其余部分。\n2:10\n特朗普的FBI负责人批评加拿大的毒品执法\n美国提供给环球新闻的数据还显示，在2024财政年度，美国与墨西哥边境查获了超过18,213磅芬太尼。在加美边境，2024年仅查获略多于10磅芬太尼。广告下方继续正文\n今年截至目前，从墨西哥查获的芬太尼超过7,277磅，而从加拿大查获的仅略多于1磅。\n更多犯罪新闻\n更多视频\n贝尔维尔犹太教堂枪击案是一起“出于仇恨动机的\n袭击”，警方称\n渥太华下令上诉法院复核萨斯喀彻温省姐妹谋杀案定罪\n新斯科舍省教师面临多项性犯罪和袭击指控\n警方提醒公众注意一名已搬到萨斯卡通的高风险性犯罪者\n两人在高速公路逆向行驶事故中丧生\n新斯科舍省监狱查获价值超过100万加元的毒品\n魁北克女子在进行Zoom通话时遇害\n警方称，马丁代尔枪击事件是有针对性的事件。\n然而，一位有组织犯罪专家表示，关键是不要被数据分散注意力。“毒品不会自行移动，也不会自行生产，”Critical Risk Team高级合伙人兼关键风险顾问Calvin Chrustie说。“所以，让我们认真讨论一下谁是威胁行为者，也就是犯罪组织。他们从外国政府那里获得了什么类型的支持和便利？”Chrustie说，不列颠哥伦比亚省长期以来一直是有组织犯罪团伙的汇聚区，而温哥华因其海运通道而成为热门选择。“我认为我们不应该听信——在我的职业生涯中，以及离职之后，我从来都没有听信过——那些政治评估，因为我发现，无论是在边境以南还是以北，从历史上看，对这一整件事的了解都并不充分，它已经被政治化了，”他补充道。“我不认为，在计算威胁和问题严重程度时，你知道有多少东西跨越了边境。”Teboul说，不列颠哥伦比亚省对毒品贩运采取了协调一致的方式，并且在将毒品清出街头方面取得了许多成功。广告下方继续\n“当然，不列颠哥伦比亚省也处于一个特殊困境中，我们拥有非常广阔而美丽的海洋，但它当然可以渗透到不列颠哥伦比亚省的海岸，我们也需要在三级政府层面投入一些资源和资金，以确保我们的港口安全，”他补充道。\n坚持事实\n在Google上将Global News添加为首选来源，以便在搜索结果中查看更多我们的报道。\n新闻标准\n报告错误\n© 2025 Global News，Corus Entertainment Inc.旗下部门。\n赞助内容\nGlobal News更多内容\n警方称贝尔维尔犹太教堂枪击事件是“出于仇恨的袭击”\n被控策划化学武器阴谋的魁北克男子面临恐怖主义指控\n广告\n保持关注\n为您提供加拿大及世界各地当天头条新闻所需的电子邮件。\n注册《National》新闻简报\n注册\n热门\n卡尼在接受《纽约时报》采访时称，他研究过美国主导军事行动的风险\n44,645\n阅读\n医生敦促女性切除输卵管以降低卵巢癌风险\n25,084\n阅读\n曾向犹太教堂开枪的前士兵因疫苗接种政策向军方索赔100万加元\n24,674\n阅读\n特朗普考虑禁止柴油出口，这对加拿大意味着什么？\n18,845\n阅读\n接管人：斯特金湖信托基金的1150万加元帮助资助了Rath公司向Tallcree支付款项\n15,347\n阅读\n星巴克将在加拿大和美国再关闭250家门店\n15,276\n阅读\n热门视频\n供水管破裂导致彼得伯勒特伦特大学宿舍1100名学生搬离\n彼得伯勒赛艇运动员入选RBC Training Ground全国决赛\n彼得伯勒市议会因一份提出可为城市节省高达3000万加元方案的顾问报告而意见分歧\nOne City Peterborough清洁团队试点项目聚焦市中心街道\n供水管破裂迫使彼得伯勒特伦特大学Symons校区关闭\n项目通过研究墓地揭示彼得伯勒县的历史\n撕碎的塑料\n在 Peterborough 各地的公园发现\nPeterborough 地区的企业家学习如何在自己的企业中实施人工智能\nGlobal Peterborough 的商业动态，9月21日\nPeterborough 市服务审查建议调整动物园收费、机场接送、垃圾收集，并削减人行道除雪服务\n更多视频\n掌握最新动态\n您每天需要的加拿大及世界各地头条新闻电子邮件。\n注册 National 新闻通讯\n注册\n广告\n报告错误\n在此订阅","publish_source":"globalnews.ca","publish_time":"2025-06-17T20:49:17-04:00"}},{"id":"news-1843","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"众议员戈麦斯联署对国土安全部长诺姆的弹劾条款","title_en":"Rep. Gomez Cosponsors Articles of Impeachment Against DHS Secretary Kristi Noem | U.S. Representative Jimmy Gomez","summary_cn":"2026年1月14日，美国众议员Jimmy Gomez（加州第34选区）联署由众议员Robin Kelly提出的三项针对国土安全部长Kristi Noem的弹劾条款。第一项指控其妨碍国会监督，DHS要求国会议员视察移民拘留设施须提前通知，法院曾初步叫停该政策，但在一名ICE官员枪杀美国公民后，诺姆又悄然签署新备忘录恢复七天通知要求。第二项指控其违反《移民与国籍法》及宪法第一、第四修正案，指示ICE进行无证逮捕并对公民使用暴力。第三项指控其自我交易，绕过竞标程序将2亿美元ICE招募广告合同授予与DHS高官关系密切的公司。","summary_en":"On January 14, 2026, U.S. Rep. Jimmy Gomez (CA-34) co-sponsored three articles of impeachment against Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem, filed with Rep. Robin Kelly. The first alleges obstruction of Congress: DHS required lawmakers to give advance notice before oversight visits to immigration detention facilities; a court preliminarily halted the policy, but after an ICE officer shot and killed a U.S. citizen, Noem quietly signed a memo reinstating the seven-day notice requirement. The second alleges violation of public trust through breaches of the Immigration and Nationality Act and the First and Fourth Amendments, including warrantless arrests and violence against citizens. The third alleges self-dealing via a $200 million ICE recruitment ad contract awarded without competitive bidding to a firm tied to a senior DHS official's husband.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:44:17.869363+00:00","url":"https://gomez.house.gov/news/documentsingle.aspx?DocumentID=5927","content":"Press Releases\nRep. Gomez Cosponsors Articles of Impeachment Against DHS Secretary Kristi Noem\nShare on Facebook\nShare on X\nPrint this Page\nShare by Email\nWashington,\nJanuary 14, 2026\nWASHINGTON, D.C. – Today, U.S. Rep. Jimmy Gomez (CA-34) co-sponsored articles of impeachment against Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem. Gomez joined Congresswoman Robin Kelly (D-IL) in filing three articles of impeachment against Secretary of Homeland Security Kristi Noem:\n1. Obstruction of Congress: DHS unlawfully imposed a policy requiring Members of Congress to give advance notice before conducting oversight visits at immigration detention facilities, interfering with Congress’s constitutional oversight authority, and preventing lawmakers from examining conditions and government conduct as incidents of violence against detainees was on the rise. Last month, the court preliminarily stopped DHS’s policy, affirming the rights of Members to conduct unannounced visits. However, after an ICE officer shot and killed a U.S. citizen last week, U.S. Secretary of Homeland Security Kristi Noem quietly signed a new memorandum reinstating the same seven-day notice requirement.\n2. Violation of Public Trust: Secretary Noem has repeatedly violated the Immigration and Nationality Act, the First and Fourth Amendments of the United States Constitution. She’s also broken due process by directing ICE to conduct warrantless arrests and use violence against U.S. citizens and lawful individuals. These dangerous actions have continued in cities across the country, including in Minneapolis, where Renee Nicole Good was shot and killed without justification.\n3. Self-Dealing: Secretary Noem has misused her position for personal gain while inappropriately using $200 million taxpayer dollars to fund an ad campaign for ICE recruitment. She bypassed the normal competitive bidding process to award a contract to a firm called Strategy Group. Strategy Group was formed just days before the award and is run by the husband of senior DHS official Tricia McClaughlin, a close friend of Secretary Noem.\nClick here to view the text of the impeachment articles.\nFollow Us Online\nplay video\nHappy Hispanic Heritage Month ✊🏽\nplay video\n🥺👉👈\nYoutube\nJimmy Gomez\nFacebook\nView this profile on Instagram Jimmy Gomez (@RepJimmyGomez) • Instagram photos and videos\nInstagram","content_cn":"新闻稿\nGomez众议员共同提出针对国土安全部长Kristi Noem的弹劾条款\n分享到Facebook\n分享到X\n打印此页面\n通过电子邮件分享\n华盛顿，\n2026年1月14日\n华盛顿特区——今天，美国众议员Jimmy Gomez（加州第34选区）共同提出了针对国土安全部长Kristi Noem的弹劾条款。Gomez与众议员Robin Kelly（伊利诺伊州民主党）共同提交了针对国土安全部长Kristi Noem的三项弹劾条款：\n1. 妨碍国会：国土安全部非法实施了一项政策，要求国会议员在对移民拘留设施进行监督访问前提前通知，从而干涉国会的宪法监督权，并阻止立法者检查拘留人员遭受暴力事件不断增加期间的设施状况和政府行为。上个月，法院初步叫停了国土安全部的这项政策，确认议员有权进行不预先通知的访问。然而，在上周一名ICE官员开枪打死一名美国公民后，美国国土安全部长Kristi Noem悄然签署了一份新备忘录，恢复了同样的七天提前通知要求。\n2. 违反公众信任：Noem部长一再违反《移民与国籍法》以及美国宪法第一和第四修正案。她还破坏正当程序，指示ICE在没有逮捕令的情况下进行逮捕，并对美国公民和合法人士使用暴力。这些危险行为持续发生在全国各地的城市，包括明尼阿波利斯；Renee Nicole Good在那里毫无正当理由地遭枪击身亡。\n3. 以权谋私：Noem部长利用职务谋取个人利益，同时不当使用2亿美元纳税人资金为ICE招募人员投放广告。她绕过正常的竞争性招标程序，将合同授予一家名为Strategy Group的公司。Strategy Group在合同授予前仅数日成立，由国土安全部高级官员Tricia McClaughlin的丈夫经营，而Tricia McClaughlin是Noem部长的密友。\n点击此处查看弹劾条款全文。\n在线关注我们\n播放视频\n西班牙裔传统月快乐 ✊🏽\n播放视频\n🥺👉👈\nYouTube\nJimmy Gomez\nFacebook\n在Instagram上查看此个人资料 Jimmy Gomez（@RepJimmyGomez）• Instagram照片和视频\nInstagram","publish_source":"gomez.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-01-14T00:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1821","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"密歇根州众议员弗里斯比请求审查影响缅甸TPS持有者的DHS命令","title_en":"Rep. Frisbie requests review of DHS order affecting Burmese TPS holders - MI House Republicans","summary_cn":"密歇根州众议员Steve Frisbie（共和党，巴特尔克里克）致信美国国土安全部长Kristi Noem，请求联邦政府考虑暂停执行一项影响缅甸国民临时保护身份（TPS）的DHS命令。弗里斯比指出，受影响者是社区的长期成员，努力工作、养家并贡献地方经济，若被遣返缅甸可能面临严重危险。他呼吁DHS采取平衡审慎的方式，兼顾执法优先事项与人道因素，尤其考虑快速实施可能给相关家庭带来的不确定性。","summary_en":"Michigan State Rep. Steve Frisbie (R-Battle Creek) sent a letter to U.S. Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem requesting that the federal government consider a temporary pause in implementing a DHS order affecting Burmese nationals under Temporary Protected Status (TPS). Frisbie noted that those affected are long-standing community members who work hard, raise families, and contribute to the local economy, and that returning them to Myanmar could put them in serious danger. He urged DHS to take a balanced and deliberate approach weighing enforcement priorities against humanitarian factors, particularly the uncertainty rapid implementation could create for affected families.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:43:16.661087+00:00","url":"https://gophouse.org/posts/rep-frisbie-requests-review-of-dhs-order-affecting-burmese-tps-holders","content":"<HomeHome>ReleaseShare This PageRep. Frisbie requests review of DHS order affecting Burmese TPS holdersRELEASE|January 15, 2026Contact: Steve Frisbie\nState Rep. Steve Frisbie (R-Battle Creek) is requesting that the federal government consider a temporary pause in the implementation of a Department of Homeland Security order that would affect Burmese nationals currently protected under Temporary Protected Status (TPS).\nFrisbie sent a letter this week to U.S. Department of Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem encouraging a careful review of the order before it takes effect, noting potential impacts on families, workers, and communities in Battle Creek and Springfield Michigan.\n“The individuals affected by this decision are long-standing members of our communities,” said Frisbie. “They work hard, raise their families, and contribute to our local economy. Sending them back to Myanmar could put them in serious danger and tear apart the lives they’ve built here.”\nTPS was granted to Burmese nationals due to ongoing instability and humanitarian concerns in Myanmar, and these conditions remain uncertain.\nIn his letter, Frisbie encouraged the Department of Homeland Security to take a balanced and deliberate approach that considers both enforcement priorities and humanitarian factors, particularly the uncertainty rapid implementation could create for affected families.\n“These are families who are established members of our community,” said Frisbie. I respectfully ask federal officials to review the available information and consider the real-life circumstances these families face.”\nRELATED POSTSOp-Ed: Michigan’s budget invests in working familiesSteve FrisbiePOSTS|8.24.26As published in The Detroit News on Aug. 19:\nFor many Michigan families with young children, daycare can cost as much as a second mortgage.\nIn some cases, parents are making difficult decisions about whether it makes financial sense to work at all. That is not the kind of choice any parent should have to make.\nRep. Frisbie secures state funding to improve Washington Heights homesSteve FrisbiePOSTS|7.31.26Retired paramedic serving in Legislature says home maintenance makes neighborhoods safer State Rep. Steve Frisbie, of Pennfield, is celebrating the inclusion of his $750,000 legislative spending request in the fiscal year 2027 state budget to help rehabilitate homes in Battle Creek’s Washington Heights neighborhood, improving safety, preserving homeownership, and strengthening the community for years to […]\nRetired paramedic Rep. Frisbie secures funding for victim servicesSteve FrisbiePOSTS|8.21.26State Rep. Steve Frisbie has successfully secured $85,000 in the fiscal year 2027 state budget to support the Michigan Sheriff’s Victim Services Unit, providing critical support to victims and their families during some of their most difficult moments. The Victim Services Unit works alongside law enforcement, fire and emergency services to provide critical support to […]\nRep. Frisbie secures funding for Haven of Rest recovery programsSteve FrisbiePOSTS|7.29.26Haven of Rest Ministries Men’s and Women’s Life Recovery Programs will receive $300,000 from the state’s fiscal year 2027 state budget to support its work helping people overcome homelessness and substance abuse addiction in the Battle Creek area thanks to a legislative spending request made by state Rep. Steve Frisbie. The one-time funding will help […]\nUSEFUL LINKSMIHR Member DirectoryMichigan House of RepresentativesMichigan Secretary of StateMichigan SenateMichigan Voter InformationState of MichiganMichigan Veterans InformationAccessibilityFOLLOW US© 2009 - 2026 Michigan House Republicans. All Rights Reserved.This site is protected by reCAPTCHA and the Google Privacy Policy and Terms of Service apply.","content_cn":"无法翻译","publish_source":"gophouse.org","publish_time":"2026-01-15T18:37:55+00:00"}},{"id":"news-154","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"蒂斯德尔：国土安全部针对锡克教社区的帖子是错误的","title_en":"Tisdel: DHS post targeting Sikh community was wrong - MI House Republicans","summary_cn":"密歇根州众议员马克·蒂斯德尔就美国国土安全部发布针对锡克教社区的AI生成图片一事发表声明。该图片描绘一名被标注为“辛格先生”的南亚裔男子，配文称其不会开车，引发锡克教和印度裔美国人组织批评，DHS随后删除该帖。蒂斯德尔表示该帖是错误的，锡克教社区有卓越的贡献记录，不应将整个社区与危险驾驶和移民违规挂钩，政府应解决问题而非制造替罪羊。","summary_en":"Michigan State Rep. Mark Tisdel issued a statement regarding a U.S. Department of Homeland Security AI-generated image targeting the Sikh community. The image depicted a bearded South Asian man labeled 'Mr. Singh' with a message saying he doesn't know how to drive, drawing criticism from Sikh and Indian American organizations; DHS later removed the post. Tisdel said the post was wrong, noting the Sikh community's extraordinary record of contribution, and argued an entire community should not be linked to dangerous driving and immigration violations, urging government to solve problems rather than create scapegoats.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T13:27:03.504333+00:00","url":"https://gophouse.org/posts/tisdel-dhs-post-targeting-sikh-community-was-wrong","content":"<HomeHome>ReleaseShare This PageTisdel: DHS post targeting Sikh community was wrongRELEASE|September 16, 2026Contact: Mark Tisdel\nCommercial-driver safety has become part of a growing national debate following fatal crashes that raised questions about licensing, driver training and English-language proficiency requirements. Federal officials have responded with increased scrutiny of immigrant commercial drivers and state licensing practices. The U.S. Department of Homeland Security recently posted  an AI-generated image depicting a bearded South Asian man identified as “Mr. Singh” facing a character resembling Optimus Prime with a DHS insignia. The image included the message “Get off our roads; you don’t know how to drive Mr. Singh.” The post drew criticism from Sikh and Indian American organizations that said it unfairly associated an entire community with dangerous driving and immigration violations. DHS later removed the post. State Rep. Mark Tisdel released the following statement:\n“The DHS post was wrong. The Sikh community has an extraordinary record of success, entrepreneurship, service and contribution in this country. These are our neighbors, business owners, professionals, workers and community leaders. To single them out and suggest that an entire community should somehow be viewed with suspicion is not only offensive, it is the epitome of ignorance and a waste of government time and resources.\n“There are legitimate safety standards that apply to commercial drivers, and those standards should be enforced fairly and consistently for everyone. But a broader challenge should never be reduced to a stereotype about one community. If there are gaps in language proficiency, literacy, education or training, then we should address those problems directly and help people meet the standard.\n“Government should be solving problems, not creating scapegoats.”\nRELATED POSTSRep. Tisdel marks 25th anniversary of Sept. 11 attacksMark TisdelPOSTS|9.15.26State Rep. Mark Tisdel today welcomed Amanda Reed to the Michigan Capitol as his special guest for the House of Representatives’ annual ceremony commemorating the anniversary of the 2001 terrorist attacks. This year marks 25 years since terrorists attacked the World Trade Center and the Pentagon and passengers aboard Flight 93 fought back against their […]\nTisdel stands with Michigan voters to get money out of politicsMark TisdelPOSTS|8.25.26State Rep. Mark Tisdel today voted to reduce the influence of powerful special interests in Michigan politics and strengthen public confidence that decisions in Lansing are made on behalf of taxpayers, patients and ratepayers, not major corporations seeking political influence. “The people of Michigan have been clear: They want money out of politics and accountability […]\n(WATCH) Mark Tisdel speech on getting money out of politicsMark TisdelPOSTS|8.26.26Rep. Mark Tisdel’s revolving door reform signed into lawMark TisdelPOSTS|7.28.26State Rep. Mark Tisdel today welcomed the signing of his legislation to close the revolving door between lawmakers and lobbyists, establishing new ethics safeguards to help ensure public officials serve the people of Michigan, not their future employers. House Bill 4062 creates a two-year cooling-off period before former state representatives and senators may register as […]\nUSEFUL LINKSMIHR Member DirectoryMichigan House of RepresentativesMichigan Secretary of StateMichigan SenateMichigan Voter InformationState of MichiganMichigan Veterans InformationAccessibilityFOLLOW US© 2009 - 2026 Michigan House Republicans. All Rights Reserved.This site is protected by reCAPTCHA and the Google Privacy Policy and Terms of Service apply.","content_cn":"无法翻译","publish_source":"gophouse.org","publish_time":"2026-09-16T15:26:37+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1713","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"发布：戈特海默宣布《ICE标准法案》，为国土安全设立明确、常识性的护栏","title_en":"RELEASE: Gottheimer Announces “ICE Standards Act” for Clear, Commonsense Guardrails for Homeland Security","summary_cn":"美国众议员乔什·戈特海默（新泽西州第五选区）宣布《ICE标准法案》，为联邦国土安全和移民执法设立专业、符合宪法的护栏。法案内容包括：建立强制性移民执法培训标准，涵盖降级冲突、宪法搜查扣押等；要求执法时使用随身及车载摄像头；设定统一制服与身份识别标准；确保风险最小化与降级；在拘留前尽力核实公民身份，禁止骚扰或驱逐美国公民；保护学校、医院、宗教场所和投票站等敏感地点；要求联邦执法行动提前通知州和地方执法部门。戈特海默批评国土安全部及ICE训练不足、逮捕配额武断，并呼吁国土安全部长诺姆辞职。","summary_en":"U.S. Congressman Josh Gottheimer (NJ-5) announced the ICE Standards Act, legislation establishing professional, constitutional guardrails for federal homeland security and immigration enforcement. The bill would set mandatory immigration enforcement training standards covering de-escalation and constitutional search and seizure; require body-worn and vehicle dashboard cameras; set uniform and identification standards; ensure risk-minimization and de-escalation; require every reasonable effort to verify citizenship before detention and prohibit harassment or deportation of U.S. citizens; protect sensitive locations such as schools, hospitals, places of worship and voting sites; and require advance notification to state and local law enforcement. Gottheimer criticised inadequate ICE training and arbitrary arrest quotas, and called for Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem to resign or be replaced.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:20:12.789313+00:00","url":"https://gottheimer.house.gov/posts/release-gottheimer-announces-ice-standards-act-for-clear-commonsense-guardrails-for-homeland-security","content":"Resources/PressShare onRELEASE: Gottheimer Announces “ICE Standards Act” for Clear, Commonsense Guardrails for Homeland SecurityJan 28, 2026Press\nAbove: Gottheimer announces new legislation to hold ICE and DHS accountable.\nPALISADES PARK, NJ — Today, January 28, 2026, U.S. Congressman Josh Gottheimer (NJ-5) announced the ICE Standards Act, commonsense legislation to establish professional, constitutional guardrails for federal homeland security and immigration enforcement.\nGottheimer’s new ICE Standards Act will:\nEstablish mandatory immigration enforcement training standards, including initial and annual training in de-escalation, constitutional search and seizure, and conducting operations appropriately in public and protest settings; as well as an immediate report to Congress detailing the training agents are receiving.\nRequire the use of body-worn and vehicle dashboard cameras during enforcement operations, ensuring transparency and accountability.\nSet clear uniform and identification standards, ensuring ICE agents are clearly identifiable unless formally approved for undercover work.\nEnsure risk-minimization and de-escalation during encounters, requiring agents to make every effort to reduce risk and defuse situations, which is critical as ICE and CBP increasingly encounter the public during enforcement activities.\nDraw a firm constitutional line protecting American citizens, requiring every reasonable effort to verify citizenship before detention and prohibiting harassment or deportation of U.S. citizens, which is already federal law.\nProtect sensitive locations, by prohibiting enforcement at locations including schools, hospitals, places of worship, and voting locations without an exigent circumstance.\nRequire advance notification and transparency with state and local law enforcement during federal immigration operations within a jurisdiction or municipality.\n“I believe that you can have tough borders, keep the gang members, terrorists, and other criminals out — and still live up to our values. But, we certainly don’t need inadequately trained ICE agents, with zero guardrails, roaming the streets,” said Congressman Josh Gottheimer (NJ-5). “That’s why I’m announcing new legislation, the ICE Standards Act, to put clear, enforceable standards in place for the Department of Homeland Security and its ICE immigration officers — standards that will protect the public, protect officers, and uphold the rule of law.”\nVideo of Gottheimer’s announcement can be found here.\nThis legislation comes in the wake of deeply troubling incidents, including the fatal shootings of two American citizens — Renee Good and Alex Pretti — in Minneapolis by federal immigration agents.\nCurrently, federal immigration enforcement agents are reportedly receiving only eight weeks of training, compared to NJ State Trooper academy training that lasts approximately six months. Reports also indicate that hundreds of American citizens have been wrongly arrested during immigration raids. Arbitrary arrest quotas put in place by DHS and this Administration — some 3,000 a day — have driven immigration enforcement to focus their energy on law-abiding, tax-paying residents, rather than hardened criminals who are the true dangers to local communities. More than half of the people ICE has arrested have no criminal convictions.\nGottheimer was joined by Palisades Park Mayor Chong “Paul” Kim, Palisades Park Councilman Christopher Kwak, Palisades Park Councilman Suk “John” Min, Palisades Park Councilwoman Christine Won-Yoon, Bergenfield Councilman Marc Pascual, Palisades Park Police Director Mike Gardner, and Steve Kuhn, First Vice President of the State Troopers Fraternal Association of New Jersey (STFA).\nBelow: Gottheimer announcing new legislation for commonsense guardrails for homeland security and immigration enforcement.\nGottheimer’s remarks as prepared for delivery are below:\nGood afternoon, everyone. Thank you for being here.\nI believe strongly that you can have secure, tough borders and a smart, legal immigration policy. We are a nation of laws and a nation of immigrants — and that’s how we built our great country — like my great-grandparents and my wife’s dad and grandparents, who came here after escaping the Holocaust. And it’s how it still grows stronger today. In the United States, our diversity, assembled over many generations, remains our greatest strength. They looked up at Lady Liberty, after passing through Ellis Island, and saw the inscription of the words we’ve all learned, “Give me your tired, your poor, your huddled masses yearning to breathe free.”\nI believe that you can have tough borders, keep the gang members, terrorists, and other criminals out — and still live up to our values, offering the promise of our democracy to newcomers looking to achieve that same American dream our families did – to breathe free. We can do both.\nBut we need to know who is in our country and who is not. And, so, immigration enforcement must be carried out professionally, lawfully, and with fact-driven accountability — because no individual and no government agency is above the Constitution.\nIn too many towns and cities right now, we’ve lost control of that sacred responsibility to our citizens and to many people who have a legal right to be here – to feel safe and protected in your community. But, instead, we are seeing too many instances of recklessness that endanger our neighbors and our law enforcement officers. As one Republican Senator said this week, “We’re at a situation where this just isn’t safe … It’s not safe for bystanders. It’s not safe for law enforcement.”\nThat’s just not okay in the greatest country the world has ever known.\nOver recent weeks, the country witnessed disturbing videos out of Minneapolis showing federal immigration agents shooting and killing two American citizens — Renee Good and Alex Pretti.\nThat is disturbing, it’s tragic, and it demands answers, so that we can work to restore public trust. And that just added to months of incidents of unidentified masked officers aggressively rounding people up, including yanking American citizens right out of their homes, barging into churches, schools, and roaming Home Depot, Target, and school parking lots as parents drop off their kids.  They’re going after people with U.S. passports, acting like thugs.\nWhat’s also troubling is that after the shooting of Alex Pretti, DHS officials blocked state investigators from accessing the scene and removed evidence — prompting a federal judge to order that the evidence not be destroyed or altered. In the case of Renee Good, state officials said they have been barred from participating in the investigation.  Also in the Alex Pretti case, the investigation was taken out of the FBI’s hands and given to DHS to investigate.\nThat is not how immigration enforcement should operate in this country, and not how our state and federal officials should work together.\nAcross the nation, immigration enforcement has sharply ramped up in non-border states, with more aggressive arrests in homes, workplaces, and public spaces. They said they were going to go after the “worst of the worst,” but, according to reporting, more than half of the people ICE is arresting have no criminal convictions whatsoever. This includes that 5-year-old boy and a corrections officer from Maine. Earlier this month in Minnesota, a U.S. citizen was detained at gunpoint in his home by federal agents without a warrant, forced to walk outside into freezing conditions in his underwear.\nAnother 5-year-old U.S. citizen was deported to Honduras earlier this month. And, a Maryland mother was detained for 25 days in ICE custody despite having documentation proving that she is a U.S. citizen.\nAs I said, I believe in keeping out gang members, criminals, and terrorists, but we certainly don’t need inadequately trained ICE agents, with zero guardrails, roaming the streets. And let me be clear about the training. I’m a huge supporter of law enforcement. I am beyond grateful for all they do. And you know why we have the best here in Jersey? Not just because they are committed to our communities, but because they’re well-trained.\nIn Jersey, state troopers spend six months at the academy and another six months riding along with a more senior partner.  Our local and county departments hold their cadets to a similar standard. They learn how to handle tough situations. How to respond and de-escalate a tough situation. How to protect themselves and the community.  According to reporting, most ICE officers receive eight weeks of training. Compare that to six months. You can understand why they might not be the best trained for the task they’ve been given.\nAnd DHS is hiring more officers from wherever they can find them right now – just to get them onto the streets and start piling up arrests. So, you can understand why they might not be best trained and prepared for the situations they are thrown into.\nReporting indicates that hundreds of American citizens have been wrongly arrested during immigration raids, and many have been wrongly deported — something that should never happen to American citizens.\nA big reason for these aggressive immigration pushes — arbitrary arrest quotas put in place by DHS and this Administration, some 3,000 a day, forcing immigration enforcement to focus their energy on law-abiding, tax-paying residents, rather than hardened criminals who are the true dangers to our community. ICE has conducted operations right here in North Jersey — including in Teaneck, Palisades Park, Bergenfield, and Hackensack.\nThat is absolutely inexcusable, and it should alarm every American.\nLet’s not forget, the buck stops with leadership — in this case, that’s Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem. After all that’s happened on her watch, she’s got to resign or be replaced.\nBut her leaving — while necessary — won’t solve the problem on its own. We actually need to fix and improve the system at DHS.\nThat’s why today, I’m announcing new legislation, the ICE Standards Act, to put clear, enforceable standards in place for the Department of Homeland Security and its ICE immigration officers — standards that will protect the public, protect officers, and uphold the rule of law.\nThese are policies that should be put into place immediately, and, frankly, should have been in the Homeland Security funding package we voted on in Congress last week.\nThis legislation is not about defunding immigration enforcement or making it harder for officers to do their jobs. I’m completely opposed to that. It’s just the opposite. It’s about making immigration enforcement better, more transparent, and more accountable, and making the right investments in the Department and officers. It’s also about getting the right guardrails in place, so that we have the rules of the road to protect everyone, and keep our communities safer.\nFirst, this bill sets much-needed training standards for federal immigration enforcement officers.\nRight now, as I mentioned, reporting suggests some officers receive as little as eight weeks of training — compared to approximately six months for New Jersey State Troopers. That gap puts civilians at risk, and it puts state and local officers at risk.\nThis lack of training and the horrific incidents that have ensued have done a massive disservice to our well-trained, effective immigration enforcement officers. We do not want untrained thugs doing damage to that reputation with their recklessness.\nAs a former state trooper said to me, “These guys wearing bandanas and gleefully pulling Americans from their cars make all officers with a badge look bad.”\nMy bill requires DHS to immediately tell Congress what training its officers are receiving, and it mandates officers to be trained upon hiring and annually on de-escalation, constitutional search and seizures, and operating appropriately with protestors present.\nThat matters — especially when immigration enforcement officers are increasingly operating in community settings and environments they are not traditionally trained for.\nSecond, the bill requires the use of body-worn cameras and vehicle dashboard cameras during enforcement operations.\nThese cameras protect the public — and they protect officers. Ask police here in Jersey – those cameras are key. This bill explicitly preserves an officer’s right to review footage, which our cops know is critical. The footage also ensures full transparency for the public.\nRight now, the Homeland funding bill in Congress includes funding for cameras — but no mandate to actually use them. This bill closes that gap, ensuring transparency and accountability.\nThird, the bill establishes clear standards for uniforms and identification.\nOfficers must clearly display their agency with an appropriate uniform or identification, unless they receive written supervisory approval for undercover operations. The goal is transparency, so communities know exactly who is operating in their streets.\nI’m always for protecting officers, and we must do everything to keep them safe from doxing or other attacks. But, people also deserve to know who is operating in their communities – and who’s approaching them. There is a way to handle both, and we should do it.\nFourth, the bill establishes clear risk-minimization and de-escalation standards, requiring officers to make every effort to reduce risk and defuse situations.\nFifth — and this is critical and key to our Constitutional rights — the bill draws a firm line when it comes to American citizens.\nEvery single reasonable effort must be made to verify citizenship status before they’re put under arrest or randomly rounded up and thrown into the back of a vehicle. U.S. citizens may not be deported, and American citizens may not be harassed during enforcement operations. Full stop.\nSixth, the bill protects sensitive locations.\nImmigration enforcement will be prohibited at schools, hospitals, places of worship, and voting locations. Kids in schools shouldn’t have to worry about anything except learning. Families should be able to worship. People should be able to seek medical care without fear that they’ll never return home.\nFor more than 30 years, federal policy restricted immigration enforcement at sensitive locations, including houses of worship. This should be the law.\nThat is common sense, and that lives up to our values.\nAnd, finally, my legislation requires notification and transparency with state and local law enforcement when federal immigration enforcement operations occur in their jurisdictions.\nLocal law enforcement should not be left in the dark — especially as detention and deportation activity accelerates. Proper notification and communication improves transparency, protects officers, and makes everyone safer. The FBI should also be allowed to do its job and investigate – not be pushed aside, as they have been in Minnesota and elsewhere.\nThese are not crazy ideas. They are commonsense ideas — many of which already have bipartisan support.\nI’m encouraged that members of both parties have expressed serious concerns about recent ICE tragedies, because this shouldn’t be a partisan issue.\nI was also pleased to see that Homeland Security Chairman Andrew Garbarino will call he Acting ICE Director, CBP Commissioner, and  U.S. Citizenship and Immigration Services Director before his committee to testify next month and get all the facts.\nFacts matter.  The Constitution matters. Due process matters. Rule of law matters. And human life matters.\nThose are all things we all agree on.\nWe can and should fund the government. We should not shut it down. And I’m ready to go back this week to vote again on a new package, if that’s what’s necessary. But that funding for DHS has to come with basic, smart guardrails that ensure transparency, professionalism, and accountability. It can be a revised DHS bill, or a separate vote. Either is fine by me.\nBut unchecked power undermines public safety, puts officers in impossible situations, and erodes trust in institutions we depend on.\nThis legislation is about the rule of law — and making sure homeland security actions reflect our values as Americans.\nAnd, ultimately, I believe it should be followed by comprehensive immigration reform, something that many of us have been working on for years. Too many of my colleagues on the far right, though, have opted to use immigration as a political weapon in elections, instead of fixing the problem. Last Congress, there was a thoughtful bipartisan bill that was killed at the last minute because the presidential nominee wanted to use the issue for politics. Well, it appears that the chickens have come home to roost. So, maybe it’s time to finally fix these issues.\nI look forward to working with colleagues on both sides of the aisle to move this legislation forward and then taking on the bigger issues, helping us live up to our values as a country.\nWe need to lower the temperature and work together to make the changes and improvements we need — that way, we can ensure our best days are ahead of us.\nThank you. God bless you, God bless our first responders, and God bless the United States of America.\n###\nShare on","content_cn":"资源/新闻稿分享\n新闻稿\n戈特海默宣布《ICE标准法案》，为国土安全设立明确、常识性的 guardrails\n2026年1月28日\n新闻\n上图：戈特海默宣布新立法，以追究ICE和国土安全部的责任。\n\n新泽西州帕利塞兹公园——今天，即2026年1月28日，美国众议员乔什·戈特海默（新泽西州第5选区）宣布《ICE标准法案》，这是一项常识性立法，旨在为联邦国土安全和移民执法建立专业且符合宪法的规范。\n\n戈特海默的新《ICE标准法案》将：\n\n建立强制性的移民执法培训标准，包括初始培训和年度培训，内容涵盖降级冲突、符合宪法的搜查与扣押，以及在公共场所和抗议活动环境中适当开展行动；同时要求立即向国会提交报告，详细说明执法人员正在接受的培训。\n\n要求在执法行动期间使用随身摄像机和车辆仪表盘摄像机，确保透明度和问责制。\n\n制定明确统一的制服和身份识别标准，确保ICE特工身份清晰可辨，除非正式获批从事卧底工作。\n\n确保在接触过程中将风险降至最低并进行降级处理，要求特工尽一切努力降低风险、缓和局势；随着ICE和海关与边境保护局（CBP）在执法活动中越来越多地接触公众，这一点至关重要。\n\n划定一条坚定的宪法界线保护美国公民，要求在拘留前尽一切合理努力核实公民身份，并禁止骚扰或驱逐美国公民——这本已是联邦法律规定。\n\n保护敏感地点，禁止在学校、医院、礼拜场所和投票地点等地点执法，除非存在紧急情况。\n\n要求在某一辖区或市镇内开展联邦移民行动期间，提前通知州和地方执法部门并保持透明。\n\n“我相信，你可以拥有严密的边境，把帮派成员、恐怖分子和其他罪犯挡在外面——同时仍然恪守我们的价值观。但我们当然不需要培训不足、毫无规范约束的ICE特工在街头游荡，”美国众议员乔什·戈特海默（新泽西州第5选区）说。“这就是我宣布新立法《ICE标准法案》的原因：为国土安全部及其ICE移民执法人员制定明确且可执行的标准——这些标准将保护公众、保护执法人员，并维护法治。”\n\n戈特海默宣布这一消息的视频可在此处找到。\n\n这项立法出台之际，正值一系列令人深感不安的事件发生之后，其中包括两名美国公民——蕾妮·古德和亚历克斯·普雷蒂——在明尼阿波利斯被联邦移民执法人员枪杀身亡。\n\n据报道，目前联邦移民执法人员只接受八周培训，而新泽西州警察学院的培训则持续约六个月。报告还显示，数百名美国公民在移民突袭行动中被错误逮捕。国土安全部和本届政府设立的任意逮捕配额——有时每天高达3,000人——促使移民执法部门将精力集中于守法、纳税的居民，而非那些真正威胁当地社区的惯犯。ICE逮捕的人中，超过一半没有任何犯罪定罪记录。\n\n戈特海默与帕利塞兹公园市市长钟“保罗”·金、帕利塞兹公园市议员克里斯托弗·郭、帕利塞兹公园市议员苏克“约翰”·闵、\n帕利塞兹公园市议员克里斯蒂娜·Won-Yoon，卑尔根菲尔德市议员马克·Pascual，帕利塞兹公园警察局长迈克·Gardner，以及新泽西州警察兄弟会（STFA）第一副主席史蒂夫·Kuhn。\n下图：Gottheimer宣布新立法，为国土安全和移民执法制定常识性的约束措施。\n以下是Gottheimer准备发表的讲话：\n大家下午好。感谢各位到场。\n我坚信，你可以拥有安全、强硬的边境和明智、合法的移民政策。我们是一个法治国家，也是一个移民国家——我们伟大的国家正是这样建立起来的——就像我的曾祖父母，以及我妻子的父亲和祖父母，他们在逃离大屠杀后来到这里。这也是我们的国家今天仍在不断壮大的方式。在美国，我们历经许多代人汇聚而成的多元性，依然是我们最大的力量。他们经过埃利斯岛后，抬头仰望自由女神像，看到了我们都学过的铭文：“把你疲惫的、贫穷的、渴望自由呼吸的、蜷缩在一起的群众交给我。”\n我相信，你可以拥有强硬的边境，把帮派成员、恐怖分子和其他罪犯挡在外面——同时仍然恪守我们的价值观，向那些希望实现与我们家人相同的美国梦、渴望自由呼吸的新来者提供民主的希望。两者我们都可以做到。\n但我们需要知道谁在我们的国家，谁不在。因此，移民执法必须以专业、合法的方式开展，并接受基于事实的问责——因为没有任何个人、也没有任何政府机构可以凌驾于宪法之上。\n眼下，在太多城镇和城市，我们已经失去了对这项神圣责任的掌控——这项责任关乎我们的公民，也关乎许多依法有权留在这里、在自己社区中感到安全并受到保护的人。但相反，我们看到太多鲁莽行径，危及邻居和执法人员。正如一名共和党参议员本周所说：“我们现在的情况就是，这根本不安全……对旁观者来说不安全。对执法人员来说也不安全。”\n在这个世界有史以来最伟大的国家里，这绝对不可接受。\n最近几周，全国目睹了从明尼阿波利斯传出的令人不安的视频：联邦移民执法人员开枪打死了两名美国公民——Renee Good和Alex Pretti。\n这令人不安，也是一场悲剧，并且需要给出答案，以便我们努力恢复公众信任。而这又叠加在数月来发生的一系列事件之上：身份不明、戴着面具的警员强行抓捕人员，包括直接把美国公民从家中拽走，闯入教堂、学校，并在家长送孩子时游荡于Home Depot、Target和学校停车场。他们甚至追捕持有美国护照的人，行事如同暴徒。\n同样令人担忧的是，在Alex Pretti遭枪击后，国土安全部官员阻止州调查人员进入现场，并移走证据——促使一名联邦法官下令不得销毁或篡改证据。在Renee Good一案中，州官员表示，他们被禁止参与调查。此外，在Alex Pretti一案中，调查被移出联邦调查局（FBI）的管辖范围，交由国土安全部调查。\n这不是移民执法在这个国家应有的运作方式，也不是我们的州和联邦官员应有的合作方式。\n在全国各地，移民执法\n在非边境州大幅加大了行动力度，在住宅、工作场所和公共场所进行更具侵略性的逮捕。他们说将要针对“最恶劣的罪犯”，但据报道，ICE逮捕的人中有一半以上根本没有任何刑事定罪记录。其中包括那个5岁的男孩和一名来自缅因州的惩教官。本月早些时候在明尼苏达州，一名美国公民在家中被联邦特工持枪扣留，且没有搜查令；他被迫只穿着内衣走到室外，面对严寒天气。\n本月早些时候，另一名5岁的美国公民被驱逐到洪都拉斯。此外，马里兰州一名母亲尽管持有证明自己是美国公民的文件，仍被拘留在ICE羁押中长达25天。\n正如我所说，我支持阻止帮派成员、罪犯和恐怖分子入境，但我们当然不需要训练不足、毫无约束的ICE特工在街头游荡。让我明确说明一下培训问题。我是执法部门的大力支持者。对于他们所做的一切，我感激不尽。你知道为什么我们新泽西州拥有最优秀的执法人员吗？不仅因为他们致力于服务我们的社区，还因为他们训练有素。\n在新泽西州，州警要在警察学院学习六个月，然后再与一名资深搭档随行执勤六个月。我们的地方和县级部门也要求学员达到类似标准。他们学习如何处理棘手局面，如何应对并缓和紧张局势，如何保护自己和社区。据报道，大多数ICE官员只接受八周培训。把这与六个月相比，你就能理解为什么他们可能不是应对所赋予任务的最佳训练人选。\n而国土安全部目前正在尽可能从各处招聘更多官员——只是为了让他们上街并开始堆积逮捕数量。所以，你可以理解为什么他们可能没有为所面临的情况接受最佳培训，也没有做好充分准备。\n报道显示，数百名美国公民在移民突袭行动中被错误逮捕，许多人还被错误驱逐——这种事情绝不应该发生在美国公民身上。\n这些激进移民行动的一大原因，是国土安全部和本届政府设立的任意逮捕配额——每天约3,000人，迫使移民执法部门将精力集中在守法、纳税的居民身上，而不是那些真正危害我们社区的惯犯。ICE就在北泽西这里开展过行动——包括蒂内克、帕利塞兹公园、卑尔根菲尔德和哈肯萨克。\n这绝对不可原谅，应该让每一位美国人都感到警觉。\n别忘了，责任最终由领导层承担——在此案中，就是国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆。鉴于在她任期内发生的一切，她必须辞职或被替换。\n但她离任——虽然有必要——并不能单独解决问题。我们实际上需要修复并改进国土安全部的体系。\n这就是为什么今天我要宣布一项新法案《ICE标准法案》，为国土安全部及其ICE移民官员制定明确且可执行的标准——这些标准将保护公众、保护官员，并维护法治。\n这些政策应立即落实，坦率地说，它们本应被纳入我们上周在国会表决通过的国土安全拨款方案中。\n这项立法并不是要削减资金\n移民执法，或让执法人员更难开展工作。我对此完全反对。事实恰恰相反。这项法案旨在让移民执法更加完善、透明且负责任，并对国土安全部及其官员进行正确的投资。同时，也要建立适当的安全护栏，制定保护所有人的行动规则，让我们的社区更加安全。\n首先，这项法案为联邦移民执法官员制定了亟需的培训标准。\n正如我提到的，目前有报道称，一些官员接受的培训短至八周——相比之下，新泽西州警察的培训大约为六个月。这一差距让平民面临风险，也让州和地方执法人员面临风险。\n培训不足以及随之发生的可怕事件，严重损害了那些训练有素、富有效率的移民执法官员的声誉。我们不希望未经训练的暴徒因鲁莽行事而损害这一声誉。\n正如一名前州警察对我所说：“那些戴着头巾、兴高采烈地把美国人从车里拽出来的家伙，让所有佩戴警徽的执法人员都显得很糟糕。”\n我的法案要求国土安全部立即告知国会其官员正在接受何种培训，并规定官员在入职时以及此后每年都必须接受降级处理、符合宪法的搜查与扣押，以及在有抗议者在场时恰当开展行动等方面的培训。\n这一点至关重要——尤其是在移民执法官员越来越多地在社区环境以及他们传统上未接受过培训的场所开展行动之时。\n其次，法案要求在执法行动期间使用随身摄像机和车辆仪表盘摄像机。\n这些摄像机保护公众，也保护执法人员。问问这里泽西州的警察——那些摄像机至关重要。本法案明确保留执法人员查看录像的权利，我们的警察都知道这点非常关键。这些录像也确保公众能够获得充分透明的信息。\n目前，国会的国土安全拨款法案包含了摄像机的资金，但没有强制要求实际使用。本法案弥合了这一差距，确保透明度和问责制。\n第三，法案为制服和身份标识确立了明确标准。\n除非执法人员获得主管书面批准开展卧底行动，否则必须通过适当的制服或身份标识清楚展示所属机构。目标是实现透明，让社区确切知道是谁在他们的街道上开展行动。\n我始终支持保护执法人员，我们必须竭尽全力保护他们免受人肉搜索或其他攻击。但人们也有权知道谁在他们的社区开展行动——谁正在接近他们。两者可以兼顾，我们应该做到。\n第四，法案确立了明确的风险最小化和降级处理标准，要求执法人员尽一切努力降低风险并缓和局势。\n第五——这对我们的宪法权利至关重要，也是关键所在——法案在涉及美国公民时划出了一条明确的界线。\n在将他们逮捕，或随意抓捕并塞进车辆后部之前，必须尽一切合理努力核实其公民身份。美国公民不得被驱逐，美国公民在执法行动期间不得受到骚扰。就这样，毫无例外。\n第六，法案保护敏感地点。\n移民执法将被禁止在学校、医院、礼拜场所等地点进行。\n礼拜场所和投票地点。学校里的孩子不应担心学习以外的任何事情。家庭应当能够进行礼拜。人们应当能够寻求医疗救治，而不必担心自己再也回不了家。\n\n30多年来，联邦政策限制在敏感地点，包括礼拜场所，执行移民法。这应当成为法律。\n\n这是常识，也符合我们的价值观。\n\n最后，我提出的法案要求，在联邦移民执法行动发生在州和地方执法部门辖区内时，向州和地方执法部门发出通知并保持透明。\n\n不应让地方执法部门蒙在鼓里——尤其是在拘留和驱逐活动加速之际。适当的通知和沟通可以提高透明度、保护警员，并让所有人更加安全。也应允许联邦调查局履行职责并展开调查——不应像在明尼苏达州和其他地方那样被排除在外。\n\n这些并不是什么疯狂的想法。它们是常识性的想法——其中许多已经得到两党支持。\n\n令我感到鼓舞的是，两党成员都对近期移民与海关执法局的悲剧表达了严重关切，因为这不应成为党派问题。\n\n我也很高兴看到，国土安全委员会主席安德鲁·加巴里诺将于下个月要求代理移民与海关执法局局长、海关与边境保护局局长以及美国公民及移民服务局局长到委员会作证，并查明全部事实。\n\n事实很重要。宪法很重要。正当程序很重要。法治很重要。人的生命也很重要。\n\n这些都是我们所有人都认同的事情。\n\n我们可以也应当为政府提供资金。我们不应让政府停摆。如果有必要，我准备好本周再次返回，就新的方案再次投票。但对国土安全部的拨款必须附带基本、明智的保障措施，以确保透明度、专业性和问责制。可以是一项修订后的国土安全部法案，也可以单独进行表决。对我来说，两种方式都可以。\n\n但不受制约的权力会破坏公共安全，使警员陷入不可能应对的境地，并侵蚀我们所依赖的机构的公信力。\n\n这项立法关乎法治——并确保国土安全行动体现我们作为美国人的价值观。\n\n最终，我认为，之后还应进行全面的移民改革，这是我们许多人多年来一直在努力推动的事情。然而，我的许多极右翼同事选择在选举中把移民当作政治武器，而不是解决问题。上届国会曾有一项经过审慎考虑的两党法案，却在最后一刻被扼杀，因为总统候选人想利用这一议题进行政治操作。现在看来，这就是自食其果。所以，也许是时候最终解决这些问题了。\n\n我期待着与两党同事合作，推动这项立法向前发展，然后着手处理更大的问题，帮助我们作为一个国家践行我们的价值观。\n\n我们需要降温并共同努力，作出我们所需的改变和改进——这样，我们就能确保最美好的日子还在前方。\n\n谢谢大家。愿上帝保佑你们，愿上帝保佑我们的急救人员，愿上帝保佑美利坚合众国。\n\n###\n分享到","publish_source":"gottheimer.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-01-28T08:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3300","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"特朗普的FBI局长人选呼吁加强网络韧性","title_en":"Trump's FBI Pick Calls for Increased Cyber Resiliency | GovCIO Media & Research","summary_cn":"特朗普提名的联邦调查局（FBI）局长人选卡什·帕特尔强调需要加强国家基础设施以应对外国对手日益增长的网络攻击威胁。他在采访中表达了对电网脆弱性的担忧，认为过时的遗留系统对美国人民的威胁不亚于物理威胁，并呼吁改革相关系统基础设施。文章还提到现任FBI局长克里斯托弗·雷宣布将在拜登政府任期结束时辞职，以及FBI在雷领导下应对外国对手网络攻击的努力。","summary_en":"Kash Patel, President-elect Donald Trump's nominee for FBI director, emphasized the need to strengthen national infrastructure against growing cyber threats from foreign adversaries. In an interview, he expressed concern about the vulnerability of the electrical grid, arguing that outdated legacy systems pose a threat to Americans as serious as physical threats, and called for overhauling related infrastructure. The article also notes that current FBI Director Christopher Wray announced he will resign at the end of the Biden administration and discusses FBI efforts against foreign cyber adversaries under Wray.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:33:47.513024+00:00","url":"https://govciomedia.com/trumps-fbi-pick-calls-for-increased-cyber-resiliency","content":"Cybersecurity\nPeople\nPresidential Transition\nTrump’s FBI Pick Calls for Increased Cyber Resiliency\nTrump’s pick for FBI Director Kash Patel has expressed his plans for bolstering the nation’s cyber resiliency if confirmed by the Senate.\nKash Patel speaking with attendees at the 2022 AmericaFest at the Phoenix Convention Center in Phoenix, Arizona.\nPhoto Credit:\nGage Skidmore\nSilvia Oakland\nStaff Writer\nShare\nFri, 12/13/2024 11:20 AM\n3m read\nKash Patel, president-elect Donald Trump’s nominee for FBI director and former chief of staff to Acting Defense Secretary Christopher Miller, has emphasized the need to strengthen the nation’s infrastructure to counter the growing threat of cyberattacks from foreign adversaries.\nBefore serving as Chief of Staff to Acting Secretary of Defense, Patel was the deputy assistant to the president and senior director for counterterrorism at the National Security Council where he led several of the top Trump’s first administration’s priorities. He also served as principal deputy to the acting director of national intelligence, where he oversaw the operations of all 17 intelligence community agencies.\nPatel highlighted his plans for bolstering the country’s cyber resiliency against foreign adversaries during a September interview on the Shawn Ryan Show. He expressed his concern for threats to the electrical grid, which are increasingly vulnerable to cyberattacks, with the number of susceptible points in electrical networks increasing daily.\nSecuring the power grid from cyberattacks has become evermore critical amid new operating environments that allow for more remote connectivity. Securing the grid means reducing risks for all sectors.\nLast year, the Department of Energy (DOE) and Cybersecurity Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA) released new measures to ensure security and resilience of the nation’s power grid in response to various incidents throughout 2022 that threatened electrical substations throughout the U.S.\nDuring the interview with Shawn Ryan, Patel discussed why the outdated legacy systems pose a threat to the American people just as much as physical threats. He added that the National Intelligence Priorities Framework needs to focus on “intel needed to secure the nation.”\n“The cyber stuff is in a different lane, but could expose us just as much, if not worse. And I think we’re very, very, very vulnerable to that,” said Patel in the interview. “You need to overhaul the infrastructure around these systems to safeguard us from — what I view as — one of the easier threats our adversaries can deploy against America.”\nIf confirmed by the Senate, Patel would succeed current FBI Director Christopher Wray, who announced this week that he will resign from his position at the end of the Biden administration’s term,\n“My goal is to keep the focus on our mission — the indispensable work you’re doing on behalf of the American people every day,” Wray told agency employees during an FBI town hall on Wednesday.\nUnder Wray, the FBI has worked to bolster its cybersecurity against foreign adversaries. Nation-state cyber-attacks and threats have grown especially during the pandemic, like the 2020 SolarWinds incident. During a 2022 congressional hearing, Wray emphasized the importance of meeting milestones to stay ahead.\n“As a country, we’re playing catchup on the threat, and so part of what I’ve got all our people doing is out there beating the bushes, interacting with the business community, the academic community,” Wray said. “I interact with our foreign partners trying to kind of raise awareness of the threat. It’s hard to think in some ways that something that significant could fly that much under the radar for that many people.”\nStay connected via Google News\nFollow us for the latest in federal government IT.\nSilvia Oakland\nStaff Writer\nSilvia Oakland is a staff writer/researcher for GovCIO Media & Research, where she primarily covers the Department of Health and Human Services.\nPrior to joining the team in 2024, Silvia was a communications associate at Briya Public Charter School where she focused on multimedia content creation and student outreach. She also worked as a multimedia reporter in Iowa covering feature stories in Northeast Iowa.\nSilvia earned her Bachelor of…\nread more\nTrending\nThis is a carousel with manually rotating slides.\nUse Next and Previous buttons to navigate\nor jump to a slide with the slide dots\nPrevious\nNext\nInside ASPR’s Efforts to Bolster Healthcare Sector Cyber Resilience12m watchAI Reshapes Critical Infrastructure Cybersecurity38m watchPartner ContentAI Forces a Rethink of Federal Contracting Models5m readDOW Turns to Training, Access to Drive GenAI.mil Adoption2m readFEHRM CTO: TEFCA Could Take Federal Health Data Exchange to ‘Next Evolution’7m watchNew CDM Security Service Aims to Cut Cyber Response Times3m readStreamlining the ATO Process Makes Software Deployments More Efficient, Secure7m watchDOE Opens Applications for $215M Genesis Mission Competition2m readWhite House, CISA Ramp Up Critical Infrastructure Security Efforts3m readContinuous Monitoring Transforms Federal Cyber Risk Management21m watchPartner Content\nRelated Content\nCybersecurity\nPeople\nFederal CIO Tracker: Latest Appointments\nStay up to date on federal CIO and IT leadership changes, including appointments, departures and leadership transitions.\n6m read\nVideo\nArtificial Intelligence\nAI Reshapes Critical Infrastructure Cybersecurity\nAs AI accelerates cyber threats, critical infrastructure operators are embracing zero trust, automation and modernization to bolster their defenses.\n38m watch\nPartner Content\nCloud\nCybersecurity\nNew CDM Security Service Aims to Cut Cyber Response Times\nCISA’s SIEM-as-a-Service platform gives federal agencies automated tools to improve threat hunting, logging and incident response.\n3m read\nHealthCast\nVideo\nInside ASPR’s Efforts to Bolster Healthcare Sector Cyber Resilience\nHHS ASPR’s Bob Bastani details how governance, standards and migration planning can help against emerging threats to medical data and devices.\n12m watch","content_cn":"网络安全\n人物\n总统过渡\n特朗普提名的FBI局长人选呼吁加强网络韧性\n特朗普提名的FBI局长人选卡什·帕特尔表示，如果获得参议院确认，他计划增强国家的网络韧性。\n卡什·帕特尔在亚利桑那州凤凰城凤凰城会议中心参加2022年AmericaFest活动时与出席者交谈。\n图片来源：\nGage Skidmore\nSilvia Oakland\n撰稿人\n分享\n2024年12月13日，星期五，上午11:20\n阅读约需3分钟\n当选总统唐纳德·特朗普提名的FBI局长人选、代理国防部长克里斯托弗·米勒的前幕僚长卡什·帕特尔强调，需要加强国家基础设施，以应对外国对手日益增长的网络攻击威胁。\n在担任代理国防部长的幕僚长之前，帕特尔曾任总统副助理兼国家安全委员会反恐事务高级主任，领导了特朗普第一届政府的若干重点工作。他还曾任代理国家情报总监的首席副手，负责监督情报界全部17个机构的运作。\n帕特尔在9月接受《肖恩·瑞安秀》采访时，谈到了他加强国家抵御外国对手网络攻击韧性的计划。他表达了对电网威胁的担忧；电网正日益容易遭受网络攻击，电力网络中易受攻击的节点数量也在每天增加。\n在允许更多远程连接的新运行环境下，保护电网免受网络攻击变得越来越重要。保护电网意味着降低所有行业面临的风险。\n去年，能源部（DOE）和网络安全与基础设施安全局（CISA）发布了新措施，以确保国家电网的安全与韧性。这些措施是为了应对2022年期间发生的各种事件，当时美国各地的变电站都受到威胁。\n在接受肖恩·瑞安采访时，帕特尔讨论了为什么过时的传统系统对美国民众构成的威胁不亚于实体威胁。他补充说，国家情报优先事项框架需要聚焦于“保护国家所需的情报”。\n帕特尔在采访中说：“网络方面的问题处于另一条轨道，但它对我们的暴露程度可能同样严重，甚至更糟。我认为我们对此极其、极其、极其脆弱。你需要彻底改造围绕这些系统的基础设施，保护我们免受——在我看来——对手能够对美国发动的较为容易实施的威胁之一。”\n如果获得参议院确认，帕特尔将接替现任FBI局长克里斯托弗·雷。雷本周宣布，他将在拜登政府任期结束时辞职，\n雷周三在FBI市政厅会议上对机构员工说：“我的目标是让大家继续专注于我们的使命——你们每天代表美国人民所做的不可或缺的工作。”\n在雷任内，FBI一直致力于加强抵御外国对手的网络安全能力。国家级网络攻击和威胁在疫情期间尤其增加，例如2020年的SolarWinds事件。在2022年的国会听证会上，雷强调了完成各项里程碑、保持领先的重要性。\n“作为一个国家，我们在应对这一威胁方面一直处于追赶状态。因此，我让我们所有人做的一部分工作，就是走出去深入搜寻，与商界、学术界互动\n社区，”Wray说。“我与我们的外国合作伙伴互动，试图提高他们对这一威胁的认识。在某些方面，很难想象如此重大的事情竟能在这么多人毫不知情的情况下躲过雷达探测。”\n通过 Google 新闻保持联系\n关注我们，获取联邦政府 IT 的最新消息。\nSilvia Oakland\n撰稿人\nSilvia Oakland 是 GovCIO Media & Research 的撰稿人兼研究员，主要报道卫生与公众服务部。\n在 2024 年加入团队之前，Silvia 曾是 Briya Public Charter School 的传播助理，负责多媒体内容创作和学生拓展。她还曾在爱荷华州担任多媒体记者，报道爱荷华州东北部的专题故事。\nSilvia 获得了她的学士学位……\n阅读更多\n热门内容\n这是一个手动轮播幻灯片的轮播组件。\n使用“下一页”和“上一页”按钮进行导航\n或点击幻灯片圆点跳转\n上一页\n下一页\nASPR 加强医疗保健行业网络韧性的努力内情12 分钟观看\n人工智能重塑关键基础设施网络安全38 分钟观看\n合作伙伴内容\n人工智能迫使联邦合同模式重新思考5 分钟阅读\nDOW 通过培训和访问权限推动 GenAI.mil 采用2 分钟阅读\nFEHRM CTO：TEFCA 可能将联邦健康数据交换带入“下一阶段”7 分钟观看\n新的 CDM 安全服务旨在缩短网络响应时间3 分钟阅读\n简化 ATO 流程使软件部署更高效、更安全7 分钟观看\n能源部为 2.15 亿美元 Genesis 任务竞赛开放申请2 分钟阅读\n白宫与 CISA 加大关键基础设施安全工作力度3 分钟阅读\n持续监控改变联邦网络风险管理21 分钟观看\n合作伙伴内容\n相关内容\n网络安全\n人物\n联邦 CIO 追踪：最新任命\n及时了解联邦 CIO 和 IT 领导层的变动，包括任命、离任和领导层交接。\n6 分钟阅读\n视频\n人工智能\n人工智能重塑关键基础设施网络安全\n随着人工智能加速网络威胁，关键基础设施运营商正采用零信任、自动化和现代化措施来加强防御。\n38 分钟观看\n合作伙伴内容\n云\n网络安全\n新的 CDM 安全服务旨在缩短网络响应时间\nCISA 的 SIEM 即服务平台为联邦机构提供自动化工具，以改进威胁搜寻、日志记录和事件响应。\n3 分钟阅读\nHealthCast\n视频\nASPR 加强医疗保健行业网络韧性的努力内情\nHHS ASPR 的 Bob Bastani 详细介绍了治理、标准和迁移规划如何帮助应对医疗数据和设备面临的新兴威胁。\n12 分钟观看","publish_source":"govciomedia.com","publish_time":"2024-12-13T15:20:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2504","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"皮伦州长与特朗普总统、国土安全部及移民和海关执法局合作推进国家安全工作","title_en":"Gov. Pillen Partners With President Trump, DHS, ICE On National Security Efforts | Office of Governor Jim Pillen","summary_cn":"内布拉斯加州州长吉姆·皮伦宣布三项州联邦合作举措，以支持特朗普政府的国土安全努力。皮伦下令内布拉斯加国民警卫队为移民和海关执法局官员提供行政与后勤支持，并与国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆达成协议，将麦库克的工作伦理营地用作未来拘留设施，同时州巡逻队拟签署287(g)协议协助逮捕非法移民。","summary_en":"Nebraska Governor Jim Pillen announced three state-federal partnerships supporting the Trump administration's homeland security efforts. Pillen ordered the Nebraska National Guard to provide administrative and logistical support to ICE officials, reached an agreement with DHS Secretary Kristi Noem to use the Work Ethic Camp in McCook as a future detention facility, and directed the State Patrol to sign a 287(g) agreement to help arrest criminal illegal aliens.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:19:15.686116+00:00","url":"https://governor.nebraska.gov/gov-pillen-partners-president-trump-dhs-ice-national-security-efforts","content":"Home\nNews\nPress Releases\nGov. Pillen Partners With President Trump, DHS, ICE On National Security Efforts\nGov. Pillen Partners With President Trump, DHS, ICE On National Security Efforts\nAugust 19, 2025\nCONTACT:\nLaura Strimple, (402) 580-9495\nGov. Pillen Partners With President Trump, DHS, ICE On National Security Efforts\nLINCOLN, NE – Today, Governor Jim Pillen announced three state-federal partnerships to support President Donald Trump’s efforts to promote homeland security and protect Americans from criminal, illegal aliens in the United States.\n“This is about keeping Nebraskans – and Americans across our country – safe,” said Governor Pillen. “We want President Trump to know that Nebraska is supportive and grateful for his ongoing, critical work with Secretary Noem to arrest and deport criminal, illegal aliens.”In conjunction with the U.S. Department of Homeland Security (DHS) and Secretary Kristi Noem, Gov. Pillen ordered the Nebraska National Guard to provide administrative and logistical support to Nebraska-based ICE officials in enforcing immigration laws. Approximately 20 Army National Guard soldiers will participate in this mission, commencing training within the next week.\nAdditionally, Gov. Pillen and Sec. Noem announced an agreement to utilize the Work Ethic Camp (WEC) in McCook as a future detention facility for those awaiting deportation and other immigration proceedings.\nFinally, at Gov. Pillen’s direction, the Nebraska State Patrol announced its intent to sign a 287(g) agreement empowering its Nebraska State troopers to help ICE arrest criminal, illegal aliens.“Earlier this summer, on the streets of Omaha, Nebraska law enforcement agents worked with ICE to arrest a MS-13 drug-trafficking kingpin and murderer,” said Gov. Pillen. “This stuff hits close to home – and hits every corner of this state and country. Government's most important job is to keep us safe, and that’s why the State of Nebraska, under my leadership, is partnering with President Trump and his team to help Make America Safe Again.”","content_cn":"首页\n新闻\n新闻稿\nPillen州长与特朗普总统、国土安全部和ICE合作开展国家安全工作\nPillen州长与特朗普总统、国土安全部和ICE合作开展国家安全工作\n2025年8月19日\n联系人：\nLaura Strimple，(402) 580-9495\nPillen州长与特朗普总统、国土安全部和ICE合作开展国家安全工作\n内布拉斯加州林肯市——今天，州长Jim Pillen宣布建立三项州—联邦合作伙伴关系，以支持总统Donald Trump推动国土安全、保护美国人免受美国境内有犯罪行为的非法外国人侵害的努力。\n“这关乎保障内布拉斯加州民众——以及全国美国人——的安全，”Pillen州长说。“我们希望特朗普总统知道，内布拉斯加州支持并感谢他与Noem部长持续开展的关键工作，以逮捕和驱逐有犯罪行为的非法外国人。”在美国国土安全部（DHS）和部长Kristi Noem的配合下，Pillen州长命令内布拉斯加州国民警卫队为驻内布拉斯加州的ICE官员执行移民法提供行政和后勤支持。大约20名陆军国民警卫队士兵将参与这项任务，并将在未来一周内开始训练。\n此外，Pillen州长和Noem部长宣布达成协议，将麦库克的工作伦理营（WEC）用作未来拘留设施，供等待遣返及其他移民程序的人士使用。\n最后，在Pillen州长的指示下，内布拉斯加州巡警宣布有意签署一项287(g)协议，授权其内布拉斯加州州警协助ICE逮捕有犯罪行为的非法外国人。“今年夏初，在内布拉斯加州奥马哈的街头，内布拉斯加州执法人员与ICE合作，逮捕了一名MS-13贩毒头目兼杀人犯，”Pillen州长说。“这类事情就发生在我们身边——并且影响这个州和这个国家的每一个角落。政府最重要的职责是保障我们的安全，这就是为什么在我的领导下，内布拉斯加州正与特朗普总统及其团队合作，帮助让美国再次安全。”","publish_source":"governor.nebraska.gov","publish_time":"2025-08-19T08:59:52-05:00"}},{"id":"news-13","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"美国国土安全部特工周四在大本德地区活动","title_en":"Homeland Security Agents Operating in Great Bend Area Thursday","summary_cn":"据大本德警察局通报，2026年9月24日上午约9时，巴顿县通信中心接到通知称美国国土安全部特工当日将在大本德地区活动，但未提供活动范围或性质等进一步信息。大本德警察局表示目前未收到协助国土安全部特工的请求，如有更多信息将另行公布。","summary_en":"According to the Great Bend Police Department, at about 9:00 a.m. on 24 September 2026, the Barton County Communications Center was advised that agents of the U.S. Department of Homeland Security would be operating in the Great Bend area that day. No further information on the scope or nature of the activity was provided. The police department said it had not received any requests to assist the agents and will provide additional information if it becomes available.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-25T10:25:16.466469+00:00","url":"https://greatbendpost.com/posts/b1bb0ffd-eda5-4df6-a313-1a1995dbc8ab","content":"From the Great Bend Police Department:On September 24, 2026, at approximately 9:00 a.m., the Barton County Communications Center was contacted and advised that agents of the U.S. Department of Homeland Security would be operating in the Great Bend area today.No further information regarding the scope or nature of their activity was provided.The Great Bend Police Department has not received any requests to assist the U.S. Department of Homeland Security agents at this time.The Police Department will provide additional information if it becomes available.","content_cn":"大本德警察局消息：2026年9月24日上午约9时，巴顿县通信中心接到通知，美国国土安全部的特工今天将在大本德地区开展行动。未提供有关其活动范围或性质的更多信息。截至目前，大本德警察局尚未收到协助美国国土安全部特工的任何请求。如有更多信息，警察局将予以公布。","publish_source":"greatbendpost.com","publish_time":"2026-09-24T20:05:51+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1314","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"格思里第三次投票支持为国土安全部全额拨款，参议院民主党阻挠持续","title_en":"Guthrie Votes for Third Time to Fully Fund Department of Homeland Security as Absurd Democrat Obstruction Continues in Senate | U.S. Congressman Brett Guthrie","summary_cn":"美国众议员布雷特·格思里（肯塔基州第二选区）就众议院通过H.R. 8029《保护国土卫士薪酬法案》发表声明，称这是众议院第三次通过两党拨款方案为国土安全部提供全额资金。他批评参议院民主党人拒绝谈判，导致国土安全部部分停摆已持续40天，TSA机场安检等待时间创历史新高，数千名联邦雇员无薪工作。","summary_en":"U.S. Rep. Brett Guthrie (KY-02) issued a statement after voting for H.R. 8029, the Pay Our Homeland Defenders Act, marking the third time the House passed a bipartisan package to fully fund the Department of Homeland Security. He criticized Senate Democrats for refusing to negotiate, noting the 40-day partial DHS shutdown has produced record TSA airport security wait times and left thousands of federal employees without pay.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:29:58.760529+00:00","url":"https://guthrie.house.gov/news/documentsingle.aspx?DocumentID=390954","content":"Latest News\nGuthrie Votes for Third Time to Fully Fund Department of Homeland Security as Absurd Democrat Obstruction Continues in Senate\nShare on Facebook\nShare on X\nPrint this Page\nShare by Email\nWashington, D.C.,\nMarch 26, 2026\nWashington, D.C. – Congressman Brett Guthrie (KY-02) issued the following statement after voting in favor of H.R. 8029, the Pay Our Homeland Defenders Act. This marks the third time that the House has passed a bipartisan funding package to fully fund the Department of Homeland Security (DHS).\n“The House has taken bipartisan action three times to fully fund the Department of Homeland Security. The same cannot be said for Senate Democrats, who continue to shift the goalpost and refuse to negotiate in good faith with their Republican counterparts to get a bill across the finish line.\n“Democrats in the Senate have been offered reasonable deals to reopen DHS, yet continue to oppose any compromise in an effort to appease their radical, open borders base. Their continued inaction leaves Americans less safe, and thousands of dedicated federal employees working without a paycheck. Ahead of the upcoming busy travel week, Americans are now facing record airport security wait times, all due to the ongoing DHS shutdown.  It’s time Democrats stop playing games and find a solution to end this ridiculous shutdown.”\nBackground:\n– The partial government shutdown for DHS has lasted 40 days, beginning on February 14, 2026. DHS funding supports important federal agencies that ensure the safety and well-being of the American people, including: the U.S. Coast Guard, U.S. Customs and Border Protection (CBP), Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE), Transportation Security Administration (TSA), and Federal Emergency Management Agency (FEMA), and more. DHS has been unfunded and operating under a government shutdown for longer than it has operated funded during fiscal year 2026.\n– As a result of the ongoing DHS shutdown, travelers are experiencing the longest airport security wait times in the history of the TSA, according to the agency.\n– Senate Democrats initiated this partial shutdown in an attempt to defund and reform ICE. Throughout this shutdown, ICE and CBP have continued to operate normally (including agents receiving pay), due to funding allocated to the agencies in the Working Families Tax Cuts.\n– This week, Senate Republicans offered Democrats another deal, which included many Democrat demands, to fully fund DHS. This deal was rejected by Senate Democrats, who counteroffered with additional requests. A rundown on this negotiation can be found HERE.\n– The House passed a bipartisan funding package on three occasions with Congressman Guthrie’s support:\n-On January 28, 2026, the House passed H.R. 7147 by a vote of 220 to 207.\n-On March 5, 2026, the House reasserted its position and voted to pass H.R. 7744 to fund DHS by a vote of 221 to 209.\n-Today, as Senate negotiations continue, the House voted a third time to assert its position on DHS funding by passing H.R. 8029, a bipartisan package, by a vote of 218 to 206.\n– The Senate has repeatedly voted and failed to advance a funding package five times as of March 25, 2026.\nBrowse News\nSearch by News Type\nSelect News Type\nSelect News Type\nLatest News\nSearch by Issue\nIssue\nSelect Issue\nAgriculture\nFiscal Responsibility\nFort Knox\nHealth Care\nJobs and the Economy\nNational Security\nSenior Citizens\nTechnology\nTransportation\nVeterans\nSearch by Month and Year\nSelect a Month\nJanuary\nFebruary\nMarch\nApril\nMay\nJune\nJuly\nAugust\nSeptember\nOctober\nNovember\nDecember\nSelect a Year\n2026\n2025\n2024\n2023\n2022\n2021\n2020\n2019\n2018\n2017\n2016\n2015\n2014\n2013\n2012\n2011\n2010\n2009\nSearch by Phrase\nEnter search term\nStay Up To Date\nEnter email address\nEnter email address to receive updates\nEnter email address to receive updates on how I'm serving you.\nsubscribe","content_cn":"最新消息\n古思里第三次投票支持为国土安全部提供全额资金，荒谬的民主党阻挠仍在参议院持续\n分享到 Facebook\n分享到 X\n打印此页面\n通过电子邮件分享\n华盛顿特区，\n2026年3月26日\n华盛顿特区——众议员布雷特·古思里（肯塔基州第二区）在投票支持 H.R. 8029《支付我们的国土防卫者法案》后发表了以下声明。这是众议院第三次通过两党资金方案，为国土安全部（DHS）提供全额资金。\n“众议院已经三次采取两党行动，为国土安全部提供全额资金。但参议院民主党人却不是这样，他们不断改变目标，并拒绝与共和党同僚本着诚信进行谈判，以推动法案最终通过。\n“参议院民主党人已经获得了重新开放国土安全部的合理方案，但他们仍然反对任何妥协，试图讨好其激进的开放边境支持者。他们持续不作为使美国人更加不安全，也让数千名尽职的联邦雇员在没有薪水的情况下工作。在即将到来的繁忙出行周之前，美国人现在正面临创纪录的机场安检等待时间，而这一切都源于国土安全部持续停摆。民主党人是时候停止玩弄政治游戏，找到解决方案，结束这场荒谬的停摆了。”\n背景：\n– 国土安全部的部分政府停摆已持续40天，始于2026年2月14日。国土安全部资金支持确保美国人民安全与福祉的重要联邦机构，包括美国海岸警卫队、美国海关与边境保护局（CBP）、移民与海关执法局（ICE）、运输安全管理局（TSA）和联邦紧急事务管理局（FEMA）等。国土安全部在2026财年处于无资金并按政府停摆状态运作的时间，已经超过其获得资金运作的时间。\n– 据该机构称，由于国土安全部持续停摆，旅客正经历运输安全管理局历史上最长的机场安检等待时间。\n– 参议院民主党人发起了此次部分停摆，试图削减 ICE 的资金并对其进行改革。在此次停摆期间，ICE 和 CBP 继续正常运作（包括特工领取薪酬），因为《工薪家庭减税法案》已向这些机构拨付资金。\n– 本周，参议院共和党人向民主党人提出了另一项方案，其中包括许多民主党人的要求，以便为国土安全部提供全额资金。参议院民主党人拒绝了该方案，并提出了包括额外要求的反方案。有关此次谈判的概要可在此处找到。\n– 众议院在三次表决中通过了两党资金方案，古思里议员均投了支持票：\n–2026年1月28日，众议院以220票对207票通过 H.R. 7147。\n–2026年3月5日，众议院重申其立场，以221票对209票通过 H.R. 7744，为国土安全部提供资金。\n– 今天，在参议院谈判继续进行之际，众议院第三次重申其在国土安全部资金问题上的立场，以218票对206票通过两党方案 H.R. 8029。\n– 截至2026年3月25日，参议院已五次反复投票，却未能推进资金方案。\n浏览新闻\n按新闻类型搜索\n选择新闻类型\n选择新闻类型\n最新消息\n按议题搜索\n议题\n选择议题\n农业\n财政责任\n诺克斯堡\n医疗保健\n就业与经济\n国家安全\n老年人\n技术\n交通\n退伍军人\n按月份和年份搜索\n选择月份\n一月\n二月\n三月\n四月\n五月\n六月\n七月\n八月\n九月\n十月\n十一月\n十二月\n选择年份\n2026\n2025\n2024\n2023\n2022\n2021\n2020\n2019\n2018\n2017\n2016\n2015\n2014\n2013\n2012\n2011\n2010\n2009\n按短语搜索\n输入搜索词\n获取最新资讯\n输入电子邮件地址\n输入电子邮件地址以接收更新\n输入电子邮件地址以接收有关我如何为您服务的更新\n订阅","publish_source":"guthrie.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-03-26T00:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-338","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"霍楚尔敦促国土安全部撤销对海地人和萨尔瓦多人TPS的终止","title_en":"Hochul urges DHS to reverse TPS termination for Haitians, Salvadorans","summary_cn":"纽约州州长凯西·霍楚尔致信美国国土安全部部长马克韦恩·穆林，重申反对终止海地人的临时保护地位以及即将终止萨尔瓦多人TPS，称此举“鲁莽且不人道”，警告将迫使州和地方政府裁减数百名必要岗位员工，并冲击纽约医疗行业。信中呼吁国土安全部全面恢复对无法安全返回动荡国家者的保护。报道还提及海地TPS持有者面临恐惧、经济困境与心理健康危机，等待法院就保护终止时间作出裁决。","summary_en":"New York Governor Kathy Hochul sent a letter to U.S. Department of Homeland Security Secretary Markwayne Mullin renewing her opposition to the termination of Temporary Protected Status for Haitians and the upcoming termination for Salvadorans, calling it a 'reckless and inhumane act.' She warned the move will force state and local governments to cut hundreds of essential workers and strain New York's health care industry, and urged DHS to fully restore protections for those who cannot safely return to countries facing instability. The report also describes fear, financial upheaval and a mental health crisis among Haitian TPS holders awaiting a court decision on timing.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-25T10:43:49.258526+00:00","url":"https://haitiantimes.com/2026/08/20/hochul-letter-tps-termination-haitians-salvadorans","content":"Posted inImmigration & Migration\nHochul urges DHS to reverse TPS termination\nThe governor warns that ending protections will force New York to cut hundreds of essential workers as soon as next week\nby\nThe Haitian Times\nAug. 20, 2026Aug. 20, 2026\nNew York Governor Kathy Hochul takes part in a press conference to announce action against ICE overreach in New York, Wednesday, Aug. 12, 2026. (AP Photo/Yuki Iwamura)\nOverview:\nGov. Kathy Hochul sent a letter to DHS Secretary Markwayne Mullin renewing her opposition to the termination of Temporary Protected Status for Haitians and the upcoming termination for Salvadorans, warning of imminent job losses for essential workers and strain on New York's healthcare sector. The letter comes as Haitian TPS holders in New York describe mounting fear, financial upheaval and a mental health crisis while awaiting a court decision on when protections will end.\nNew York Gov. Kathy Hochul sent a letter last week to U.S. Department of Homeland Security Secretary Markwayne Mullin renewing her opposition to the end of Temporary Protected Status, warning that the terminations will force state and local governments to cut hundreds of essential employees from payroll.\nThe letter, sent after a conversation Hochul said she had with President Donald Trump, called the recent termination of TPS for Haitians and the upcoming termination for Salvadorans a “reckless and inhumane act.” Hochul said the fallout will extend beyond government payrolls into the private sector, with New York’s health care industry — and the seniors and other vulnerable residents who depend on it — especially exposed.\nSign up for our free newsletters.\nHaitian Times Newsletter and Daily Roundups\nHaitian Excellence\nSign up\nTPS Letter To Mullin\nHochul pointed to her administration’s Office for New Americans, which she said has helped thousands of New Yorkers with TPS applications and legal representation, and said the state “will continue to do everything in our power to prevent harm to the immigrant community.”\nShe called on DHS to fully restore protections for people who cannot safely return to countries facing instability, violence or crisis, arguing TPS exists precisely so people are not sent back into danger.\nThe letter comes as Haitian TPS holders across New York brace for the loss of status amid a pending court decision on timing. At a recent Haitian American Alliance of New York community meeting, attorneys, educators and mental health professionals described families paralyzed by uncertainty — parents losing jobs, children pulled from summer programs and school out of fear of detention, and advocates reporting a rise in suicidal ideation among TPS holders trying to plan for what comes next.\n‘Should I keep paying my mortgage?’ Haitian families confront impossible choices around TPS\nAs Haitian TPS nears an end, families are asking who will care for their children, whether to sell their homes and whether they can survive what comes next\nby Macollvie J. Neel\nJul. 27, 2026Jul. 27, 2026\nOrganizations including Haitian Americans United for Progress have begun offering pro bono wills and estate planning services as families weigh whether to keep paying rent or mortgages, transfer assets to relatives, or arrange care for children in case of sudden separation.\nSupport our work\nAs an independent publication, we rely on contributions from readers like you to fund our journalism.\nOne-time\nMonthly\nAnnually\nOne-time\nDonation amount\n$\nMonthly\nDonation amount per month\n$\nAnnually\nDonation amount per year\n$\nThanks for your contribution!\nContribute Now\nLike this:Like Loading…\nRelated\nTagged: latest news\nLeave a comment\nLeave a ReplyCancel reply\nSearch for:\nSearch","content_cn":"发布于移民与迁徙\nHochul 敦促 DHS 撤销 TPS 终止决定\n州长警告称，终止保护措施最早将于下周迫使纽约裁撤数百名必要岗位工作人员\n作者\nThe Haitian Times\n2026年8月20日2026年8月20日\n纽约州州长 Kathy Hochul 于2026年8月12日星期三在纽约举行的新闻发布会上宣布采取行动应对 ICE 越权行为。（美联社照片/Yuki Iwamura）\n概述：\n州长 Kathy Hochul 致信 DHS 部长 Markwayne Mullin，再次反对终止海地人的临时保护身份以及即将终止萨尔瓦多人的保护身份，并警告必要工作人员将立即失业，纽约医疗保健部门将承受压力。此信发出之际，纽约的海地 TPS 持有人在等待法院就保护措施何时结束作出裁决期间，描述了日益加剧的恐惧、财务动荡和心理健康危机。\n纽约州州长 Kathy Hochul 上周致信美国国土安全部部长 Markwayne Mullin，再次反对结束临时保护身份，并警告这些终止决定将迫使州和地方政府从工资单中裁撤数百名必要岗位雇员。\nHochul 表示，这封信是在她与总统 Donald Trump 交谈之后发出的，信中称近期终止海地人的 TPS 及即将终止萨尔瓦多人的 TPS 是“鲁莽且不人道的行为”。Hochul 表示，其影响将超出政府工资单，蔓延至私营部门；纽约的医疗保健行业——以及依赖该行业的老年人和其他弱势居民——尤其容易受到影响。\n订阅我们的免费新闻通讯。\nHaitian Times 新闻通讯和每日综述\n海地卓越\n注册\n致 Mullin 的 TPS 信函\nHochul 提到其政府的新美国人办公室，她表示该办公室已帮助数千名纽约人申请 TPS 和获得法律代理，并称该州“将继续尽我们所能，防止移民社区受到伤害。”\n她呼吁 DHS 全面恢复对无法安全返回面临不稳定、暴力或危机国家人员的保护，并主张 TPS 的存在正是为了不让人们被遣返回危险之中。\n此信发出之际，纽约各地的海地 TPS 持有人正因一项待决的法院裁决而准备面对身份丧失，该裁决将决定时间安排。在近期举行的纽约海地裔美国人联盟社区会议上，律师、教育工作者和心理健康专业人士描述了被不确定性困住的家庭：父母失去工作，儿童因害怕被拘留而退出暑期项目和学校；倡导者还报告称，试图规划下一步的 TPS 持有人中自杀意念有所上升。\n“我还应该继续还房贷吗？”海地家庭面对 TPS 带来的不可能选择\n随着海地 TPS 接近结束，家庭正在询问谁会照顾他们的孩子、是否应出售房屋，以及他们是否能够撑过接下来的一切\n作者 Macollvie J. Neel\n2026年7月27日2026年7月27日\n包括 Haitian Americans United for Progress 在内的组织已开始提供免费遗嘱和遗产规划服务，家庭正在权衡是否继续支付房租或房贷、将资产转给亲属，或在突然分离的情况下安排儿童照护。\n支持我们的工作\n作为一家独立出版物，我们依靠像您一样的读者捐款来资助新闻报道。\n一次性\n每月\n每年\n一次性\n捐款金额\n$\n每月\n每月捐款金额\n$\n每年\n每年捐款金额\n$\n感谢您的捐款！\n立即捐款\n喜欢这篇：正在加载……\n相关内容\n标签：最新新闻\n发表评论\n留下回复取消回复\n搜索：\n搜索","publish_source":"haitiantimes.com","publish_time":"2026-08-20T16:56:51+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2228","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"国会议员哈马德赞扬FBI局长帕特尔在NBA体育博彩丑闻中的工作","title_en":"Congressman Hamadeh Commends Efforts of FBI Director Patel Amidst NBA Sports Betting Scandal | Congressman Abe Hamadeh","summary_cn":"2025年10月23日，美国国会议员Abe Hamadeh赞扬FBI局长Kash Patel对La Cosa Nostra犯罪家族联邦调查及对波特兰开拓者队主教练Chauncey Billups、迈阿密热火队后卫Terry Rozier和前NBA后卫兼教练Damon Jones的指控。FBI的“Operation Zhen Diagram”行动揭露了一个涉及黑手党犯罪家族、涉嫌诈骗受害者数百万美元的全国性赌博团伙。Hamadeh谴责有组织犯罪和欺诈行为，呼吁依法严惩，并称赞FBI的勤勉工作。","summary_en":"On October 23, 2025, U.S. Congressman Abe Hamadeh commended FBI Director Kash Patel for the federal investigation into La Cosa Nostra crime families and charges against Portland Trail Blazers head coach Chauncey Billups, Miami Heat guard Terry Rozier, and former NBA guard and coach Damon Jones. The FBI's Operation Zhen Diagram uncovered a nationwide gambling ring allegedly involving La Cosa Nostra members accused of defrauding victims of millions of dollars. Hamadeh condemned organized crime and fraud, called for full prosecution, and praised the FBI's diligent work.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:56:31.509539+00:00","url":"https://hamadeh.house.gov/news/documentsingle.aspx?DocumentID=478","content":"Press Releases\nCongressman Hamadeh Commends Efforts of FBI Director Patel Amidst NBA Sports Betting Scandal\nShare on Facebook\nShare on X\nPrint this Page\nShare by Email\nWashington, DC,\nOctober 23, 2025\nTags:\nBack The Blue\n,\nAmerica First\nOn Thursday, Congressman Abe Hamadeh commended FBI Director Kash Patel for the federal investigation into the La Cosa Nostra crime families and charges brought against Portland Trail Blazers head coach Chauncey Billups, Miami Heat guard Terry Rozier and former NBA guard and coach Damon Jones.\nThe FBI’s Operation Zhen Diagram uncovered a “nationwide gambling ring allegedly involving members of the La Cosa Nostra crime families who are accused of defrauding unwitting victims of millions of dollars,\" according to various media reports.\n“Today the FBI successfully dismantled a multi-million-dollar gambling ring tied to the notorious La Cosa Nostra, as well as arrested current and former NBA coaches and players, exposing a long-standing scheme to rig sports betting on the NBA stage,” stated Congressman Hamadeh.\n“This type of scandal is extremely disquieting for a number of reasons when you consider the victims of these egregious crimes, and the damage done to the league and its beloved athletes, who are admired by so many Americans,” stated Congressman Hamadeh, a former Maricopa County prosecutor. “I strongly condemn any and all behavior related to organized crime and fraud. Funding dangerous criminal activity, illegally profiting off rigged systems, and cheating our fellow Americans cannot be tolerated, and those who engaged in this illicit activity should be prosecuted to the fullest extent of the law.”\n“I applaud FBI Director Kash Patel and his team for their exceptional and diligent work in this ongoing investigation. As the FBI remains focused on combatting these despicable crimes, their efforts remind us that we must remain vigilant in fighting against corruption in all forms,” concluded Congressman Hamadeh.\nRelated News\nCongressman Hamadeh Introduces the CATFISH Act to Protect Seniors from Financial Fraudsters\nSeptember 17, 2026 | Posted in Press Releases\nHouse Passes Legislation Targeting Fraud in Federally Funded Programs\nSeptember 16, 2026 | Posted in Press Releases\nVital Information for U.S.Citizens Traveling in Nogales, Sonora, Mexico\nSeptember 6, 2026 | Posted in Press Releases\nConvicted predators face lifetime barrier under GOP lawmaker’s sweeping victim protection bill\nSeptember 3, 2026 | Posted in In the News\nHouse Passes Congressman Hamadeh’s Kayleigh’s Law Bill to Protect Victims of Dangerous Crimes from Their Abusers\nAugust 31, 2026 | Posted in Press Releases\nAbout\nContact\nAccomplishments\nMedia\nServices\nWashington DC Office\n1722 Longworth House Office Building\nWashington, DC 20515\nPhone: (202) 225-4576\nSurprise District Office\n12515 W. Bell Road, Suite 104\nSurprise, AZ 85378\nPhone: (623) 776-7911\nCopyright\nPrivacy Policy\nHouse.gov\nAccessibility","content_cn":"新闻稿\n国会议员哈马德赞扬FBI局长帕特尔在NBA体育博彩丑闻中的努力\n分享到Facebook\n分享到X\n打印此页面\n通过电子邮件分享\n华盛顿特区，\n2025年10月23日\n标签：\n支持警察，\n美国优先\n周四，国会议员阿贝·哈马德赞扬FBI局长卡什·帕特尔对拉科萨诺斯特拉犯罪家族的联邦调查，以及对波特兰开拓者队主教练昌西·比卢普斯、迈阿密热火队后卫特里·罗齐尔和前NBA后卫兼教练达蒙·琼斯提出的指控。\n据多家媒体报道，FBI的“真图行动”揭露了一个“据称涉及拉科萨诺斯特拉犯罪家族成员的全国性赌博团伙，这些成员被指控诈骗毫不知情的受害者数百万美元”。\n“今天，FBI成功捣毁了一个与臭名昭著的拉科萨诺斯特拉有关、涉案金额达数百万美元的赌博团伙，并逮捕了现任和前任NBA教练及球员，揭露了一个长期操纵NBA体育博彩的阴谋，”哈马德议员表示。\n“当你考虑到这些令人发指的罪行的受害者，以及对联盟及其深受众多美国人喜爱的运动员造成的损害时，这类丑闻令人极度不安，原因有很多，”曾任马里科帕县检察官的哈马德议员表示。“我强烈谴责任何与有组织犯罪和欺诈有关的行为。资助危险的犯罪活动、从操纵的系统中非法牟利，以及欺骗我们的同胞美国人，都是不可容忍的；参与这种非法活动的人应依法受到最严厉的起诉。”\n“我赞扬FBI局长卡什·帕特尔及其团队在这项持续调查中的出色和勤勉工作。FBI继续专注于打击这些卑劣罪行，他们的努力提醒我们，必须继续警惕并打击一切形式的腐败，”哈马德议员总结道。\n相关新闻\n哈马德议员提出《CATFISH法案》，保护老年人免受金融诈骗者侵害\n2026年9月17日 | 发布于新闻稿\n众议院通过针对联邦资助项目欺诈行为的立法\n2026年9月16日 | 发布于新闻稿\n美国公民前往墨西哥索诺拉州诺加莱斯的重要信息\n2026年9月6日 | 发布于新闻稿\n根据共和党议员提出的全面受害者保护法案，被定罪的掠夺者将终身受限\n2026年9月3日 | 发布于新闻报道\n众议院通过哈马德议员提出的《凯莉法》，保护危险犯罪受害者免遭施害者伤害\n2026年8月31日 | 发布于新闻稿\n关于\n联系方式\n成就\n媒体\n服务\n华盛顿特区办公室\n朗沃思众议院办公楼1722室\n华盛顿特区20515\n电话：(202) 225-4576\n惊喜市选区办公室\nW.贝尔路12515号，104室\n亚利桑那州惊喜市85378\n电话：(623) 776-7911\n版权\n隐私政策\nHouse.gov\n无障碍功能","publish_source":"hamadeh.house.gov","publish_time":"2025-10-23T00:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2868","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"前FBI局长因一则被视为威胁特朗普生命的帖子受到指责","title_en":"Former FBI Director accused of post seen as potential threat to Trump's life","summary_cn":"美国国土安全部长诺姆称，联邦执法部门正调查前FBI局长詹姆斯·科米在Instagram发布的一张贝壳照片，图中贝壳似构成“86 47”，多名共和党人认为这是呼吁对第47任总统特朗普施暴。科米表示未意识到该数字与暴力相关，已删除帖子并反对任何形式的暴力。现任FBI局长帕特尔称已知悉并与特勤局沟通。科米2013至2017年任FBI局长，2017年被特朗普解职。","summary_en":"Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem said federal law enforcement is investigating a social media post by former FBI Director James Comey showing seashells that appeared to form \"86 47,\" which she and other Republicans suggested was a call for violence against President Donald Trump, the 47th president. Comey said he did not realize the numbers were associated with violence, deleted the post and opposes violence of any kind. Current FBI Director Kash Patel said he was aware and conferring with the Secret Service. Comey led the FBI from 2013 to 2017 and was fired by Trump.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T22:29:28.208539+00:00","url":"https://hayspost.com/posts/f3618bf9-12a0-4769-a0ac-32e2fd1db8c5","content":"WASHINGTON (AP) — Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem said Thursday that federal law enforcement is investigating a social media post made by former FBI Director James Comey that she and other Republicans suggest is a call for violence against President Donald Trump.Image from Comey's Instagram pageIn an Instagram post, Comey wrote “cool shell formation on my beach walk” under a picture of seashells that appeared to form the shapes for “86 47.”Numerous Trump administration officials, including Noem, said Comey was advocating for the assassination of Trump, the 47th president. “DHS and Secret Service is investigating this threat and will respond appropriately,” Noem wrote.Merriam-Webster, the dictionary used by The Associated Press, says 86 is slang meaning “to throw out,” “to get rid of” or “to refuse service to.” It notes: “Among the most recent senses adopted is a logical extension of the previous ones, with the meaning of ‘to kill.’ We do not enter this sense, due to its relative recency and sparseness of use.”The post has since been deleted. Comey subsequently wrote, “I posted earlier a picture of some shells I saw today on a beach walk, which I assumed were a political message. I didn’t realize some folks associate those numbers with violence.“It never occurred to me,” Comey added, “but I oppose violence of any kind so I took the post down.”Comey's original post sparked outrage among conservatives on social media, with Donald Trump Jr. accusing Comey of calling for his father’s killing.Current FBI Director Kash Patel said he was aware of the post and was conferring with the Secret Service and its director.James Blair, White House deputy chief of staff for legislative, political and public affairs, noted that the post came at a delicate time given that Trump is traveling in the Middle East.“This is a Clarion Call from Jim Comey to terrorists & hostile regimes to kill the President of the United States as he travels in the Middle East,” Blair wrote on X.Comey, who was FBI director from 2013 to 2017, was fired by Trump during the president's first term amid the bureau’s probe into allegations of ties between Russian officials and Trump’s 2016 presidential campaign. Comey wrote about his career in the best-selling memoir “A Higher Loyalty.”He is now a crime fiction writer and is promoting his latest book, “FDR Drive,” which is being released on Tuesday.","content_cn":"华盛顿（美联社）——国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆周四表示，联邦执法部门正在调查前联邦调查局局长詹姆斯·科米发布的一则社交媒体帖子；她和其他共和党人认为，这则帖子是在呼吁对总统唐纳德·特朗普实施暴力。\n科米Instagram页面上的图片\n科米在一则Instagram帖子中写道：“在海滩散步时发现了很酷的贝壳排列”，并配有一张贝壳照片；这些贝壳看起来组成了“86 47”的形状。\n包括诺姆在内的多名特朗普政府官员表示，科米是在鼓吹刺杀特朗普这位第47任总统。“国土安全部和特勤局正在调查这一威胁，并将作出适当回应，”诺姆写道。\n美联社使用的词典《韦氏词典》称，86是俚语，意为“扔掉”“摆脱”或“拒绝提供服务”。词典还指出：“最近采用的含义之一，是此前这些含义的逻辑延伸，即‘杀死’。由于这一含义出现时间相对较晚且使用稀少，我们没有收录这一义项。”\n这则帖子后来被删除。科米随后写道：“我早些时候发布了一张今天在海滩散步时看到的一些贝壳的照片，我以为那是一条政治信息。我没有意识到有些人会把这些数字与暴力联系起来。”“我从未想到这一点，”科米补充道，“但我反对任何形式的暴力，所以我删除了这则帖子。”\n科米最初的帖子在社交媒体上激怒了保守派人士，唐纳德·特朗普的儿子小唐纳德·特朗普指责科米是在呼吁杀害他的父亲。\n现任联邦调查局局长卡什·帕特尔表示，他知道这则帖子，并正在与特勤局及其局长协商。\n白宫负责立法、政治和公共事务的副幕僚长詹姆斯·布莱尔指出，鉴于特朗普正在中东出访，这则帖子发布的时机很敏感。\n布莱尔在X上写道：“这是吉姆·科米向恐怖分子和敌对政权发出的号召，呼吁他们在美国总统出访中东期间杀死他。”\n科米于2013年至2017年担任联邦调查局局长，特朗普在其第一任期内解雇了他，当时联邦调查局正在调查有关俄罗斯官员与特朗普2016年总统竞选活动存在联系的指控。科米在畅销回忆录《更高的忠诚》中写述了自己的职业生涯。\n他如今是一名犯罪小说作家，正在宣传自己的新书《FDR大道》，该书将于周二发行。","publish_source":"hayspost.com","publish_time":"2025-05-16T07:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3265","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"2024年CrowdStrike故障对网络风险的启示","title_en":"What the 2024 CrowdStrike Glitch Can Teach Us About Cyber Risk","summary_cn":"2024年7月19日，网络安全公司CrowdStrike的一次内容更新导致全球逾850万台系统崩溃，数千家机构运营中断数日，损失估计超50亿美元，保险公司赔付约15亿美元。达美航空称7000架次航班和130万旅客受影响，索赔逾5亿美元。文章以此为例，分析聚合性网络风险累积的负面影响及企业网络风险管理启示。","summary_en":"On July 19, 2024, a single content update from cybersecurity firm CrowdStrike crashed more than 8.5 million systems, disrupting thousands of organizations worldwide for days, with losses estimated above $5 billion and insurer payouts around $1.5 billion. Delta Air Lines claimed 7,000 flights and 1.3 million customers were affected, seeking over $500 million. The article uses the incident to examine aggregated cyber risk accumulation and lessons for enterprise cyber risk management.","tag":"risk","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:31:53.365627+00:00","url":"https://hbr.org/2025/01/what-the-2024-crowdstrike-glitch-can-teach-us-about-cyber-risk","content":"Cybersecurity and digital privacyWhat the 2024 CrowdStrike Glitch Can Teach Us About Cyber Risk by Raphael YahalomJanuary 10, 2025Giuseppe Cacace/Getty ImagesPostPostShareSaveGet PDFBuy CopiesPrintSummary.   Despite advances in cybersecurity solutions, the number and impact of cyber incidents continue to grow, with the average cost of a data breach in 2024 reaching $4.88 million and the number of...moreLeer en españolLer em portuguêsPostPostShareSaveGet PDFBuy CopiesPrintOn July 19th, 2024, a single content update from CrowdStrike, a cyber security software company, caused more than 8.5 million systems to crash, disrupting operations for days across thousands of organizations worldwide, including hundreds of Fortune 1000 companies. The CrowdStrike “glitch,” as it became known, resulted in losses estimated to be more than $5 billion. The CrowdStrike incident is estimated to cost insurers around $1.5 billion in payouts, under business interruption, cyber, and system failure coverages. It represents one of the biggest examples of the adverse impact of aggregated cyber risk accumulation. In October 2024, Delta, one of the many affected businesses in the incident, filed a lawsuit against CrowdStrike claiming that the outage was “catastrophic.” They claimed it was the result of CrowdStrike’s “forced untested updates to its customers” and led to disruption of 7,000 flights and 1.3 million customers over 5 days. The airline claimed a loss of more than $500 million.Raphael Yahalom is a cybersecurity expert, an affiliated researcher at MIT Sloan School of Management, and a cyber risk strategic advisor.PostPostShareSaveGet PDFBuy CopiesPrintRead more on Cybersecurity and digital privacy or related topics IT security management, Data management, Crisis management, Technology and analytics and Information management","content_cn":"网络安全与数字隐私\n2024年CrowdStrike故障教会我们什么有关网络风险的知识，作者：Raphael Yahalom\n2025年1月10日\nGiuseppe Cacace/Getty Images\n发布\n发布\n分享\n保存\n获取PDF\n购买副本\n打印\n摘要。尽管网络安全解决方案不断进步，网络事件的数量及其影响仍在持续增长，2024年数据泄露的平均成本达到488万美元，且……更多\n阅读西班牙语版\n阅读葡萄牙语版\n发布\n发布\n分享\n保存\n获取PDF\n购买副本\n打印\n\n2024年7月19日，网络安全软件公司CrowdStrike的一次内容更新导致超过850万个系统崩溃，使全球数千家组织的运营中断数日，其中包括数百家《财富》1000强公司。这一后来被称为CrowdStrike“故障”的事件，造成的损失估计超过50亿美元。据估计，CrowdStrike事件将使保险公司在营业中断、网络安全和系统故障保险保障下支付约15亿美元赔款。它是聚合性网络风险累积负面影响最重大的例证之一。2024年10月，Delta是该事件中众多受影响企业之一，其对CrowdStrike提起诉讼，称这次中断是“灾难性的”。其声称，这是CrowdStrike“强制向客户推送未经测试的更新”所致，并在5天内导致7,000个航班和130万名客户受到影响。这家航空公司声称损失超过5亿美元。\n\nRaphael Yahalom是网络安全专家、MIT Sloan School of Management附属研究员，以及网络风险战略顾问。\n\n发布\n发布\n分享\n保存\n获取PDF\n购买副本\n打印\n\n在“网络安全与数字隐私”或相关主题中阅读更多：IT安全管理、数据管理、危机管理、技术与分析以及信息管理","publish_source":"hbr.org","publish_time":"2025-01-10T13:15:03+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3261","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI与DHS警告可能发生恐怖袭击","title_en":"FBI, DHS warn of likely terrorist attacks - Heartlander News","summary_cn":"美国联邦调查局与国土安全部发布公共服务公告，警告在新奥尔良新年袭击后可能出现模仿或报复性恐怖袭击，尤其担忧车辆冲撞战术被极端分子效仿。公告呼吁公众保持警惕，向当地FBI办事处报告可疑活动，并提醒海外美国公民可通过国务院热线或在线表格报告失踪或被劫持人员。文章还提及拜登政府时期恐怖事件增加、国会共和党人要求加强边境安全等背景。","summary_en":"The FBI and the Department of Homeland Security issued a public service announcement warning of possible copycat or retaliatory terrorist attacks following the New Year's Day attack in New Orleans, particularly concerned about vehicle ramming tactics. The PSA urges the public to remain vigilant, report suspicious activity to local FBI field offices, and reminds U.S. citizens overseas to report missing persons or hostages via a State Department hotline or online form. The article also notes increased terrorist incidents under the Biden administration and Republican congressional demands for stronger border security.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:32:07.101367+00:00","url":"https://heartlandernews.com/fbi-dhs-warn-of-likely-terrorist-attacks","content":"Terrorism\nPosted January 14, 2025\nFBI, DHS warn of likely terrorist attacks\n(The Center Square) – The Federal Bureau of Investigation and U.S. Department of Homeland Security are warning that a copycat terrorist attack could occur similar to the New Year’s Day New…\nFBI DHS | terrorist attacks\nBy Bethany Blankley\nShare\n(The Center Square) – The Federal Bureau of Investigation and U.S. Department of Homeland Security are warning that a copycat terrorist attack could occur similar to the New Year’s Day New Orleans attack.\nThe public service announcement urges Americans to remain vigilant and for those living overseas who encounter kidnapping or hostage situations to call a toll-free number or fill out an online form.\n“The FBI and DHS are concerned about possible copycat or retaliatory attacks due to the persistent appeal of vehicle ramming as a tactic for aspiring violent extremist attackers,” the PSA states. “Previous attackers inspired by foreign terrorist organizations who have conducted vehicle attacks in the United States and abroad have used rented, stolen, and personally owned vehicles, which are easy to acquire. Some have used additional weapons, such as firearms and knives, to attack individuals after the vehicle has stopped.\n“Additionally, attackers may attempt to conceal and pre-position improvised explosive devices to supplement a vehicle attack. Targets have included pedestrians, law enforcement or military members, and crowded public venues, including festivals and commercial centers, which generally are accessible from roadways.”\nThe PSA urges members of the public to “remain vigilant” about terrorist attacks, report suspicious activity to local FBI field offices and call 911 to report emergencies.\nFor U.S. citizens living overseas, the PSA encourages them to report “missing persons or individuals taken as hostages” by calling the Department of State’s Overseas Citizens Services toll-free hotline at (888) 407-4747 or complete a Crisis Intake Form.\nBoth agencies were unsuccessful in negotiating the return of American hostages held by Hamas. Hostages who are still alive remain in captivity since Oct. 7, 2023. The Biden administration’s toll-free hotline, and online form did not help them, critics argue.\nPresident-elect Donald Trump has warned Hamas to release all hostages before he’s sworn into office next week or “there will be hell to pay.”\nIslamic terrorist incidents significantly increased under the Biden administration and the greatest number on the U.S. terrorist watch list were apprehended trying to illegally enter the country, The Center Square reported.\nTerrorist incidents increased nationwide, including an Iranian man in Massachusetts linked to murders of U.S. service members and an ISIS-linked Houston man allegedly planning a 9/11 style terrorist attack, among others.\nLast year, FBI Director Christopher Wray warned about an ISIS smuggling ring illegally crossing the border and of increased security risks posed by China and Iran. Prior to the election, hundreds of members of ISIS were confirmed to have illegally entered the U.S., with officials saying vetting wasn’t occurring.\nCongressional Republicans demanded answers about terrorist threats, including the U.S. House Committee on Homeland Security, which published a report citing more than 50 jihadist cases in 29 states under the Biden administration, The Center Square reported.\n“Foreign jihadist networks and homegrown violent extremists” represent a “persistent terror threat to America,” it said, citing the Biden administration’s “chaotic Afghanistan withdrawal and the spillover effects of the October 7 Hamas terrorist attacks against our ally Israel to the vulnerabilities caused by our wide-open borders.”\nU.S. Sen. Ted Cruz, R-Texas, called for greater northern border security due Hamas members entering from Canada and sounded the alarm as Jewish Americans, he and others were targeted by pro-Hamas rioters, The Center Square reported.\nLast year, within a few months, three assassination attempts were foiled against Trump, including by an Iran-linked Pakistani and Iranian assassination plot.\nIn September, Cruz warned, “We are living on borrowed time” in an interview with The Center Square. At the time, he said the U.S. “was at a greater risk for a major terrorist attack than we have been at any point since Sept. 11, 2001” because of Biden administration policies.\nCruz demanded answers on the “incredible lapses in vetting and screening illegal aliens at airports,” adding, “it is only a matter of time before another major terrorist attack is likely to occur.”\nAs Cruz’s demands for increased security went unanswered, DHS, the FBI and the National Counterterrorism Center published resources “to help mitigate potential risks from a variety of threat actors.”\nMonths after Cruz’s warning, and two weeks after the New Orleans attack, the agencies issued the PSA, stating, “Due to the highly personal nature of radicalization to violence and mobilization to violence, it can be difficult to assess specific characteristics indicating the intent of US-based violent extremists to conduct violence.”\nFederal agencies also published a U.S. Violent Extremist Mobilization Indicators resource to help the public identify “all ideologically motivated, US-based violent extremists,” and a “Bystander Awareness eLearning” resource to understand “Targeted Violence Prevention.”\nRelated Posts\nTerrorismCruz targets Hamas, regimes that use human shields in new legislation\nBy Bethany Blankley\nTerrorismWashington, D.C. police to increase police presence after New Orleans attack\nBy Casey Harper\nTerrorismWATCH: Boulder attack suspect said he had no regrets, would ‘do it again’\nBy Elyse Apel","content_cn":"恐怖主义\n发布于2025年1月14日\nFBI、DHS警告可能发生恐怖袭击\n（The Center Square）——联邦调查局和美国国土安全部警告称，可能会发生类似新年元旦新奥尔良袭击的模仿性恐怖袭击……\nFBI DHS | 恐怖袭击\n作者：Bethany Blankley\n分享\n（The Center Square）——联邦调查局和美国国土安全部警告称，可能会发生类似新年元旦新奥尔良袭击的模仿性恐怖袭击。\n这份公共服务公告敦促美国人保持警惕，并建议那些居住在海外、遭遇绑架或人质情况的人拨打免费电话或填写在线表格。\n公告称：“FBI和DHS担心可能发生模仿性或报复性袭击，因为车辆冲撞作为有意实施暴力的极端分子攻击者所采用的策略，持续具有吸引力。此前受外国恐怖组织启发、在美国及海外实施车辆袭击的攻击者，使用过租赁、盗窃和个人所有的车辆，这些车辆很容易获得。有些人在车辆停下后，还使用枪支和刀具等额外武器攻击个人。\n“此外，攻击者可能试图隐藏并预先放置简易爆炸装置，以配合车辆袭击。目标包括行人、执法人员或军人，以及拥挤的公共场所，包括节庆活动和商业中心；这些地点通常可从道路进入。”\n该公告敦促公众对恐怖袭击“保持警惕”，向当地FBI办事处报告可疑活动，并拨打911报告紧急情况。\n对于居住在海外的美国公民，公告鼓励他们拨打国务院海外公民服务免费热线（888）407-4747，或填写危机受理表，报告“失踪人员或被扣为人质的人员”。\n两家机构在谈判让被哈马斯扣押的美国人质获释方面均未成功。仍然活着的人质自2023年10月7日起一直被囚禁。批评人士认为，拜登政府设立的免费热线和在线表格并未帮助他们。\n当选总统唐纳德·特朗普警告哈马斯，必须在他下周宣誓就职前释放所有人质，否则“将有苦头吃”。\n据The Center Square报道，拜登政府执政期间，伊斯兰恐怖事件大幅增加，而美国恐怖分子监视名单中人数最多的一批人是在试图非法进入该国时被捕的。\n全国各地的恐怖事件有所增加，其中包括马萨诸塞州一名与谋杀美国军人有关联的伊朗男子，以及休斯敦一名据称正计划实施类似“9·11”的恐怖袭击、与ISIS有关联的男子等。\n去年，FBI局长克里斯托弗·雷警告称，一个ISIS走私团伙正非法越境，并警告中国和伊朗带来的安全风险增加。大选前，已有数百名ISIS成员被确认非法进入美国，官员称当时并未进行审查。\n国会共和党人要求就恐怖威胁作出答复，其中包括美国众议院国土安全委员会。The Center Square报道，该委员会发布的一份报告援引了拜登政府执政期间29个州发生的50多起圣战分子案件。\n“外国圣战网络和本土暴力极端分子”代表一种“持续的\n“对美国构成的恐怖主义威胁，”报告援引拜登政府“混乱的阿富汗撤军，以及10月7日哈马斯恐怖袭击我们盟友以色列所产生的外溢影响，还有我们几乎不设防的边境所造成的漏洞”称。\n\n据《中心广场》报道，美国得克萨斯州共和党参议员特德·克鲁兹呼吁加强北部边境安全，因为哈马斯成员正从加拿大入境；当他和其他犹太裔美国人成为亲哈马斯骚乱者的目标时，他也发出了警报。\n\n去年，在短短几个月内，针对特朗普的三次刺杀企图被挫败，其中包括一名与伊朗有关联的巴基斯坦人策划的刺杀图谋，以及一项伊朗刺杀阴谋。\n\n9月，克鲁兹在接受《中心广场》采访时警告说：“我们正生活在借来的时间里。”当时，他表示，由于拜登政府的政策，美国“面临重大恐怖袭击的风险高于2001年9月11日以来的任何时候”。\n\n克鲁兹要求就“在机场对非法移民进行审查和筛查时出现的令人难以置信的疏漏”作出解释，并补充说：“另一场重大恐怖袭击很可能发生，这只是时间问题。”\n\n在克鲁兹加强安全措施的要求迟迟未获回应之际，国土安全部、联邦调查局和国家反恐中心发布了相关资源，“以帮助减轻来自各种威胁行为者的潜在风险”。\n\n在克鲁兹发出警告数月后、新奥尔良袭击事件发生两周后，这些机构发布了这份公共服务公告，称：“由于激化暴力和动员实施暴力具有高度个人化的性质，因此很难评估能够表明以美国为基地的暴力极端分子有意实施暴力的具体特征。”\n\n联邦机构还发布了《美国暴力极端分子动员指标》资源，帮助公众识别“所有受意识形态驱动、以美国为基地的暴力极端分子”，并发布“旁观者意识电子学习”资源，以了解“针对性暴力预防”。\n\n相关文章\n恐怖主义：克鲁兹在新法案中将矛头对准哈马斯及使用人体盾牌的政权\n作者：Bethany Blankley\n\n恐怖主义：新奥尔良袭击后，华盛顿特区警方将增加警力部署\n作者：Casey Harper\n\n恐怖主义——观看：博尔德袭击嫌疑人称自己毫不后悔，“还会再做一次”\n作者：Elyse Apel","publish_source":"heartlandernews.com","publish_time":"2025-01-15T02:32:50+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3541","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"照片：委员会成员参观9·11纪念馆和博物馆，23年后会见急救人员","title_en":"PHOTOS: Committee Members Visit September 11 Memorial and Museum, Meet with First Responders 23 Years Later – Committee on Homeland Security","summary_cn":"2024年9月12日，美国众议院国土安全委员会两党代表团在主席马克·格林带领下，于9·11事件23周年之际访问纽约9·11纪念馆和博物馆，敬献花圈并悼念2977名遇难者。成员们与纽约消防局、拿骚县警察局及博物馆负责人举行圆桌会议，随后在零地附近与急救人员共进午餐。声明强调国土安全部自成立以来承担的使命，呼吁美国人民保持团结，铭记反恐教训。","summary_en":"On September 12, 2024, a bipartisan delegation from the House Committee on Homeland Security, led by Chairman Mark Green, visited the September 11 Memorial and Museum in New York City to commemorate the 23rd anniversary of the attacks and honor the 2,977 lives lost. Members held a roundtable with FDNY and Nassau County officials and museum leaders, laid a wreath at the Survivors Tree, and hosted a first responders lunch near Ground Zero. The statement stressed DHS's vital mission and called for national unity.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T22:32:56.677110+00:00","url":"https://homeland.house.gov/2024/09/12/photos-committee-members-visit-september-11-memorial-and-museum-meet-with-first-responders-23-years-later","content":"News\nPHOTOS: Committee Members Visit September 11 Memorial and Museum, Meet with First Responders 23 Years Later\nSeptember 12, 2024\nWASHINGTON, D.C. — This week, a bipartisan delegation of Members from the House Committee on Homeland Security visited the September 11 Memorial and Museum in New York City to commemorate the 23rd anniversary of the September 11, 2001, terrorist attacks on our nation and honor the thousands of lives lost.  Chairman Mark E. Green, MD (R-TN) was joined by Subcommittee on Emergency Management and Technology Chairman Anthony D’Esposito (R-NY), and Representatives Nick LaLota (R-NY), Morgan Luttrell (R-TX), Dan Goldman (D-NY), Rob Menendez (D-NJ), and Tim Kennedy (D-NY). Former House Homeland Security Chairman Peter King (R-NY) also attended. At a roundtable, Members were joined by Fire Department of the City of New York (FDNY) Commissioner Robert Tucker, FDNY Chief Thomas Currao, Nassau County Police Commissioner Patrick Ryder, retired FDNY firefighter Tim Brown, National September 11 Museum & Memorial Executive Vice President Jay Weinkam, and National September 11 Museum & Memorial President Elizabeth Hillman. As our nation continues to mourn the lives taken by enemies of freedom 23 years ago, we must never forget the crucial mission the men and women of the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) were tasked with upon its creation in the wake of the attacks. As we were in the hours and days following September 11, 2001, the American people must remain united––bound together by love of country and clear-eyed about the threats we still face. The Committee on Homeland Security remains dedicated to ensuring DHS can accomplish its vital mission: ensuring our country never faces such a devastating attack on our soil again.\nFollowing a solemn tour of the September 11 Museum, members laid a commemorative wreath at the Survivors Tree.\nTo remember the 2,977 innocent lives lost that day and reflect upon the heroism of the first responders who bravely tried to rescue their fellow Americans, the members placed flowers and American flags at Ground Zero.\nAlong with the president and vice president of the museum, the delegation then hosted a first responders roundtable lunch at O’Hara’s Restaurant and Pub just two blocks from Ground Zero. Michael Keane, the restaurant’s owner, was at O’Hara’s when the attacks occurred. O’Hara’s continues to honor first responders and keep a record of what happened on 9/11 by lining the walls with thousands of patches from firefighters, police officers, and service members around the country.  ###","content_cn":"新闻\n照片：委员会成员参观9月11日纪念馆和博物馆，23年后与急救人员会面\n2024年9月12日\n华盛顿特区——本周，众议院国土安全委员会的两党议员代表团参观了纽约市9月11日纪念馆和博物馆，以纪念2001年9月11日针对我国的恐怖袭击23周年，并缅怀数千名遇难者。委员会主席、医学博士 Mark E. Green（田纳西州共和党人）与紧急事务管理和技术小组委员会主席 Anthony D’Esposito（纽约州共和党人），以及众议员 Nick LaLota（纽约州共和党人）、Morgan Luttrell（得克萨斯州共和党人）、Dan Goldman（纽约州民主党人）、Rob Menendez（新泽西州民主党人）和 Tim Kennedy（纽约州民主党人）一同出席。前众议院国土安全委员会主席 Peter King（纽约州共和党人）也参加了活动。在一场圆桌会议上，议员们与纽约市消防局（FDNY）局长 Robert Tucker、FDNY 局长 Thomas Currao、拿骚县警察局长 Patrick Ryder、已退休的 FDNY 消防员 Tim Brown、国家9月11日博物馆和纪念馆执行副总裁 Jay Weinkam，以及国家9月11日博物馆和纪念馆主席 Elizabeth Hillman 会面。我国仍在哀悼23年前被自由的敌人夺去的生命，我们绝不能忘记国土安全部（DHS）在袭击发生后成立时，其男女工作人员被赋予的关键使命。正如2001年9月11日后的数小时和数天里那样，美国人民必须保持团结——由对祖国的热爱凝聚在一起，并清醒地认识到我们仍面临的威胁。国土安全委员会仍致力于确保 DHS 能够完成其至关重要的使命：确保我们的国家永远不会再次在本土遭遇如此毁灭性的袭击。\n在庄严参观9月11日博物馆后，议员们在“幸存者树”前敬献纪念花圈。\n为缅怀当日失去的2,977名无辜生命，并追思勇敢尝试营救同胞的急救人员所展现的英雄主义，议员们在世贸遗址放置了鲜花和美国国旗。\n随后，代表团与博物馆的主席和副主席一起，在距世贸遗址仅两个街区的 O’Hara’s Restaurant and Pub 举办了急救人员圆桌午餐会。餐厅老板 Michael Keane 在袭击发生时就在 O’Hara’s。O’Hara’s 至今仍通过在墙上陈列来自全国各地消防员、警察和军人的数千枚徽章，向急救人员致敬，并保存9·11事件的记录。###","publish_source":"homeland.house.gov","publish_time":"2024-09-12T00:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3536","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"“损害永远无法弥补”：格林主席就拜登-哈里斯政府灾难性边境记录召开听证会","title_en":"“The Damage Will Never Be Undone”: Chairman Green Opens Hearing on the Biden-Harris Administration’s Catastrophic Border Record – Committee on Homeland Security","summary_cn":"2024年9月18日，美国众议院国土安全委员会主席马克·格林在听证会上发表开场陈述，批评拜登-哈里斯政府及国土安全部长马约卡斯导致美国历史上最严重的边境危机。他引用数据称，自2021年以来边境巡逻队记录超1030万次不可入境外国人遭遇，另有超200万已知逃逸者，并指责大规模假释计划、拘留和遣返数量骤降。格林还批评参议院边境法案，称其只会加剧危机，并呼吁政府结束危机、保障边境安全。","summary_en":"On September 18, 2024, House Homeland Security Committee Chairman Mark Green delivered an opening statement at a hearing examining the Biden-Harris administration's border policies, blaming them and DHS Secretary Mayorkas for the worst border crisis in U.S. history. He cited over 10.3 million inadmissible alien encounters since 2021, more than two million known gotaways, and plummeting detention and removal numbers. Green criticized mass parole programs and the Senate border bill, urging the administration to secure the border.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T22:32:08.610379+00:00","url":"https://homeland.house.gov/2024/09/18/the-damage-will-never-be-undone-chairman-green-opens-hearing-on-the-biden-harris-administrations-catastrophic-border-record","content":"News\n“The Damage Will Never Be Undone”: Chairman Green Opens Hearing on the Biden-Harris Administration’s Catastrophic Border Record\nSeptember 18, 2024\nWASHINGTON, D.C. — Today, House Committee on Homeland Security Chairman Mark E. Green, MD (R-TN) delivered the following opening statement in a hearing to examine how the policies and actions of the Biden-Harris administration sparked the unprecedented border crisis that began in early 2021, how the crisis has undermined the safety and security of communities across our country, and how these unlawful, open-borders, and anti-enforcement policies have impacted DHS law enforcement. Watch his opening statement below and the full hearing live here.\nWatch Chairman Green’s full opening statement.\nAs prepared for delivery:\nPresident Joe Biden, his appointed “border czar”, Vice President Kamala Harris, and Department of Homeland Security Secretary Alejandro Mayorkas have sparked the worst border crisis in American history. Looking back over nearly four years, Americans have witnessed a national security, public safety, and humanitarian disaster at our borders. And every day, we continue to feel its devastating consequences.The flood of inadmissible aliens across our sovereign borders has been unprecedented. Since Biden and Harris’ first full month in office, Customs and Border Protection has recorded more than 10.3 million encounters of inadmissible aliens nationwide, compared to 3.1 million between Fiscal Years 2017-2020. In addition, there have been more than two million known gotaways on their watch—illegal aliens who are at large in our communities, whose intentions and backgrounds are completely unknown.Encounters at our ports of entry have exploded, from roughly one million between Fiscal Years 2017-2020 to more than three million since the start of Fiscal Year 2021.That’s largely because the Biden-Harris administration has devised a host of unlawful, mass-parole programs that encourage otherwise-inadmissible aliens to cross at our land, sea, and airports instead of between them.This solves the terrible optics problem of overcrowded Border Patrol facilities and overwhelmed agents, but the end result is the same—tens of thousands of inadmissible aliens released into the interior every month. It’s just a shell game—a sleight of hand to skew the numbers.It’s like when a parent tells their children to clean their room, only to find the mess simply moved from the floor to the closet. Things might look cleaner, but the underlying problem has not been addressed. So it is with the Biden-Harris administration’s border policies.Other numbers further highlight the crisis. Tragically, more than 200,000 Americans have died from fentanyl that has been smuggled across the Southwest border by criminal cartels. Border Patrol arrests of illegal aliens with criminal backgrounds have more than doubled on Biden and Harris’ watch, from around 22,000 to more than 53,000. Apprehensions of Chinese nationals crossing the Southwest border illegally exceed 36,000 just this fiscal year—more than FY07-20 combined. These are major national security and public safety concerns.This unprecedented surge across our borders was made possible by the Biden-Harris administration. In 2019 and 2020, Biden and Harris both declared they supported decriminalizing border crossings. Biden said that suspected criminal illegal aliens arrested by local law enforcement should not be handed over to ICE. Harris called building more border wall system “a stupid use of money.” Biden encouraged illegal aliens to “surge” to our border to flood our asylum system with illegitimate claims.Their open-borders and anti-enforcement rhetoric soon became reality.Upon assuming office, Biden and Harris worked immediately to end effective border-security policies and to dismantle decades of bipartisan immigration enforcement.For example, Biden and Harris have gutted detention. For example, in Fiscal Year 2013, the Obama administration detained 91 percent of all illegal aliens—82 percent of them from the time they were encountered until their case was resolved. In Biden and Harris’ first year in office, that 82 percent dropped to just 10 percent.Removals have also plummeted, from more than 267,000 in Fiscal Year 2019 to around half that number last year, and as low as 59,000 in Fiscal Year 2021. Even worse, removals of criminal aliens plummeted from around 173,000 in Fiscal Year 2019 to just around 70,000 last fiscal year. And just yesterday, prominent border correspondent Ali Bradley reported exclusive ICE figures showing that since the Biden-Harris administration ended Title 42 in May 2023, the administration has only removed around 23 percent of all inadmissible aliens encountered.Despite the limitations put on them by their leaders, the men and women of CBP and ICE have continued to perform their jobs above and beyond the call of duty, and I commend them for their unwavering service to the nation. Yet they know it is not supposed to be this way.Today, you will no doubt hear more blame-shifting and excuses by my colleagues across the aisle. But all of it is meant to mislead. You’ll probably hear about the recent drop in illegal border crossings between ports of entry along our Southwest border.However, this does not account for the thousands of inadmissible aliens coming in daily through ports of entry, nor does it undo the damage done by the millions that have come in over the past three and a half years.The evidence also suggests no connection between Biden’s recent, loophole-ridden executive order and these new numbers, but rather, stepped-up interior enforcement by Mexico. And as we saw recently, that enforcement is waning, with the Mexican government now busing CBP One appointment holders from southern Mexico to our own Southwest border.Coming almost four years into this self-inflicted crisis, the administration’s action is much too little, and FAR too late. For numerous families across this country, like those of Rachel Morin, Laken Riley, and Jocelyn Nungaray, the damage will never be undone.You certainly won’t hear how the Senate’s border bill, which just a single Republican helped write, would have made the crisis worse.It would have only allowed tough restrictions once encounters passed several thousand per day, mandated mass releases through “noncustodial detention,” improperly expanded the use of parole, and more. It was a terrible bill, one that was roundly criticized by the former heads of CBP, the Border Patrol, and ICE.Today’s hearing is about getting the unvarnished truth from Americans who have been forced to live out the Biden-Harris open-borders nightmare in their own lives.This administration has completely undermined border security, through a host of policies and decisions that have overwhelmed and sidelined the Border Patrol. Biden and Harris have gutted ICE’s ability to conduct immigration enforcement in the interior, making it harder to detain and remove illegal aliens, including criminals. And innocent Americans are suffering as a result. The story you will hear from Patty Morin today is sadly just one of tens of thousands of stories of pain, suffering, and preventable tragedy.What you will hear from Jim Desmond is the account of a major American city that has been overwhelmed and overrun.It does not have to be like this. Later today, my Committee will release a comprehensive report documenting in even more painful, objective detail how Biden, Harris, and their administration have thrown open our borders, and the chaos that has resulted. I encourage all Americans to read it at homeland.house.gov.As we continue to witness Biden and Harris’ resistance to doing anything meaningful about this disaster, we have to ask—why? Why did they let this crisis take place and why have they let it continue? I hope this hearing provides some answers, and inspires President Biden and Vice President Harris to do what they so far have refused to—end this crisis and secure our borders.\n###","content_cn":"新闻\n“损害永远无法挽回”：格林主席就拜登-哈里斯政府灾难性的边境记录开启听证会\n2024年9月18日\n华盛顿特区——今日，众议院国土安全委员会主席马克·E·格林医学博士（田纳西州共和党）在一场听证会上发表了以下开场陈述，以审查拜登-哈里斯政府的政策和行动如何引发始于2021年初、前所未有的边境危机；这场危机如何削弱了全国各地社区的安全与保障；以及这些非法、开放边境和反执法政策如何影响国土安全部执法部门。请观看下方他的开场陈述，并在此观看完整听证会直播。\n观看格林主席的完整开场陈述。\n按准备稿发表：\n乔·拜登总统、他任命的“边境沙皇”、副总统卡玛拉·哈里斯以及国土安全部部长亚历杭德罗·马约卡斯，引发了美国历史上最严重的边境危机。回顾近四年，美国人目睹了边境地区的国家安全、公共安全和人道主义灾难。我们每天仍在承受其毁灭性后果。\n非法入境者洪水般涌过我们主权边界，其规模前所未有。自拜登和哈里斯任职后的第一个完整月份以来，海关与边境保护局在全国记录了超过1030万次不具入境资格的外国人遭遇事件，而2017至2020财年期间为310万次。此外，在他们任内还有超过200万名已知成功逃避查缉者——这些非法外国人目前藏身于我们的社区中，其意图和背景完全不明。\n我们的入境口岸遭遇事件激增：2017至2020财年期间约100万次，而自2021财年开始以来已超过300万次。\n这主要是因为拜登-哈里斯政府制定了一系列非法的大规模假释计划，鼓励原本不具入境资格的外国人从陆路、海路和机场入境，而不是在这些地点之间偷渡。\n这解决了边境巡逻设施人满为患、特工不堪重负这一糟糕的观感问题，但最终结果相同——每月有数万名不具入境资格的外国人被释放到内陆。这只是障眼法——通过偷换概念来扭曲数字。\n这就像父母要求孩子打扫房间，结果却发现只是把地板上的杂物移到了壁橱里。房间看起来可能更干净了，但根本问题并未得到解决。拜登-哈里斯政府的边境政策也是如此。\n其他数字进一步凸显了这场危机。可悲的是，超过20万名美国人死于犯罪集团从西南边境走私入境的芬太尼。拜登和哈里斯任内，边境巡逻队逮捕的有犯罪背景的非法外国人数增加了一倍多，从约2.2万人增至超过5.3万人。仅本财年，非法越过西南边境的中国籍人员就超过3.6万人——超过2007至2020财年的总和。这些都是重大的国家安全和公共安全问题。\n这场前所未有的越境激增是拜登-哈里斯政府促成的。2019年和2020年，拜登和哈里斯都表示支持将越境行为去刑事化。拜登说，地方执法部门逮捕的涉嫌犯罪的非法外国人不应移交给移民与海关执法局。哈里斯称，修建更多边境\n墙系统称为“愚蠢的金钱用法”。拜登鼓励非法移民向我们的边境“蜂拥而来”，用不正当的申请淹没我们的庇护系统。他们开放边境和反执法的言论很快成为现实。上任后，拜登和哈里斯立即着手终结有效的边境安全政策，并拆解数十年来两党共同支持的移民执法措施。\n\n例如，拜登和哈里斯已经大幅削弱了拘留措施。以2013财政年度为例，奥巴马政府拘留了91%的非法移民，其中82%的人从被发现之时一直被拘留到案件得到解决。在拜登和哈里斯上任的第一年，这一比例从82%降至仅10%。遣返数量也大幅下降，从2019财政年度的超过267,000人降至去年的大约一半，2021财政年度甚至低至59,000人。更糟糕的是，刑事非法移民的遣返数量从2019财政年度的大约173,000人骤降至上个财政年度的仅约70,000人。就在昨天，著名边境记者阿里·布拉德利独家报道了ICE的数据，显示自拜登—哈里斯政府于2023年5月终止第42条以来，该政府只遣返了所遇到的所有不符合入境资格的移民中的约23%。\n\n尽管领导层给他们设置了种种限制，CBP和ICE的男女工作人员仍继续超越职责要求履行工作，我赞扬他们对国家始终不渝的服务。然而，他们知道事情本不应该是这样。\n\n今天，你们无疑还会听到我在另一边的同事们继续推卸责任、寻找借口。但这一切都是为了误导。你们可能会听到，最近西南边境各入境口岸之间的非法越境人数有所下降。\n\n然而，这并没有统计每天通过入境口岸进入的数千名不符合入境资格的移民，也无法挽回过去三年半中数百万人进入所造成的损害。\n\n证据还表明，拜登最近那项漏洞百出的行政命令与这些新数字之间没有联系，真正的原因是墨西哥加强了境内执法。正如我们最近看到的那样，这种执法正在减弱，墨西哥政府如今正把持有CBP One预约的人从墨西哥南部用巴士运送到我们自己的西南边境。\n\n这场自残式危机已经持续近四年，政府的行动实在太少，而且远远太晚。对于全国各地许多家庭而言——例如蕾切尔·莫林、莱肯·莱利和乔斯琳·努恩加雷的家人——造成的伤害永远无法挽回。\n\n你们当然不会听到，参议院那项边境法案只由一名共和党人参与起草，实际上会让危机更加恶化。\n\n它只会在每天的遇到人数超过数千人后才允许实施严格限制，强制通过“非羁押拘留”进行大规模释放，不当扩大假释的使用范围，等等。这是一项糟糕的法案，曾受到CBP、边境巡逻队和ICE前任负责人的广泛批评。\n\n今天的听证会旨在从那些被迫亲身经历拜登—哈里斯开放边境噩梦的美国人那里，了解未经修饰的真相。\n\n本届政府通过一系列使边境巡逻队不堪重负并被边缘化的政策和决定，彻底破坏了边境安全。拜登和哈里斯已经削弱了ICE在境内开展移民执法的能力，使拘留和遣返变得更加困难\n非法移民，包括罪犯。因此，无辜的美国人正在遭受苦难。今天你将从帕蒂·莫林那里听到的故事，令人遗憾地只是数以万计关于痛苦、苦难和本可避免的悲剧的故事之一。你将从吉姆·德斯蒙德那里听到的，是一座美国大城市不堪重负、已被压垮的实情。\n事情不必如此。今天晚些时候，我的委员会将发布一份全面报告，以更加令人痛心且客观的细节，记录拜登、哈里斯及其政府如何敞开边境，以及由此造成的混乱。我鼓励所有美国人前往 homeland.house.gov 阅读该报告。\n随着我们继续目睹拜登和哈里斯拒绝采取任何有意义的行动来应对这场灾难，我们必须问——为什么？他们为什么让这场危机发生，又为什么任由危机持续？我希望本次听证会能提供一些答案，并促使拜登总统和哈里斯副总统去做他们迄今一直拒绝做的事——结束这场危机，确保我们的边境安全。\n###","publish_source":"homeland.house.gov","publish_time":"2024-09-18T00:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3122","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"格林主席在“网络PIVOTT法案”及第119届国会委员会监督计划标记会上发表开场声明","title_en":"Chairman Green Delivers Opening Statement in Markup for “Cyber PIVOTT Act,” 119th Congress Committee Oversight Plan – Committee on Homeland Security","summary_cn":"2025年2月26日，美国众议院国土安全委员会主席马克·格林在标记会上发表开场声明，审议第119届国会授权与监督计划、H.R. 1000“网络PIVOTT法案”及两项调查决议。格林表示委员会首要任务是确保边境安全并支持边境巡逻队等国土安全部部门，同时致力于解决网络不安全根源、确保劳动力准备充分，并监督国土安全部结构以提高效率。网络PIVOTT法案旨在培养入门级网络人才，扩大网络专业人才管道。","summary_en":"On February 26, 2025, House Homeland Security Committee Chairman Mark Green delivered an opening statement at a markup considering the 119th Congress authorization and oversight plan, H.R. 1000 the Cyber PIVOTT Act, and two resolutions of inquiry. Green said the committee's top priority is securing borders and supporting Border Patrol and other DHS components, while addressing cyber insecurity, ensuring workforce readiness, and overseeing DHS structure for efficiency. The Cyber PIVOTT Act aims to develop entry-level cyber talent and expand the cyber professional pipeline.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T22:03:03.478963+00:00","url":"https://homeland.house.gov/2025/02/26/chairman-green-delivers-opening-statement-in-markup-for-cyber-pivott-act-119th-congress-committee-oversight-plan","content":"News\nChairman Green Delivers Opening Statement in Markup for “Cyber PIVOTT Act,” 119th Congress Committee Oversight Plan\nFebruary 26, 2025\nWASHINGTON, D.C. –– Today, House Committee on Homeland Security Chairman Mark E. Green, MD (R-TN) delivered the following opening statement during a markup for the 119th Congress Oversight Plan, H.R. 1000, the “Cyber PIVOTT Act,” H. Res. 113, and H. Res. 114.\nAs prepared for delivery:Good morning. Today’s order of business will be consideration of the Committee on Homeland Security’s Authorization and Oversight Plan for the 119th Congress, as well as additional measures. Rule X of the House of Representatives requires each standing Committee to adopt and submit an authorization and oversight plan for the two-year period of the congressional term. The plan under consideration today highlights the Committee’s major priorities for this Congress. First and foremost, we will work to secure America’s borders and support Border Patrol and other DHS components as they carry out their critical mission.  We are committed to addressing the root of many cyber insecurities by ensuring the workforce is prepared, equipped, and placed to face rapidly evolving threats to critical infrastructure and networks from nation-state and criminal actors. We are committed to streamlining regulations to ensure the regime promotes security and rapid, actionable information sharing instead of unnecessary, duplicative paperwork.Cybersecurity is something we must all prioritize––we must work with our companies to ensure they are implementing the best cybersecurity practices possible, while communicating to them that their government is here to help when they face their darkest day: a malicious nation-state sponsored cyberattack.\nAdditionally, the Committee’s plan highlights the need to conduct oversight of the Department of Homeland Security’s structure to examine potential reforms to make DHS more efficient, well-managed, and effective in carrying out the homeland security mission.  This plan will guide the work of this Committee and our Subcommittees during this Congress by focusing on key policy areas, including countering terrorism and foreign nation-state threats such as China, improving emergency preparedness, ensuring the security of our transportation systems, and supporting law enforcement within DHS and our state and local partners. I encourage all members to support adoption of the Committee’s authorization and oversight plan as we do the work that the American people sent us here to do. Our second measure that we will consider is H.R. 1000, the “Cyber PIVOTT Act.” This bill will help us build a skilled cyber workforce and close the cyber workforce gap to meet the evolving threats that the government and American businesses face on a daily basis. The “Cyber PIVOTT Act” seeks to target the development of entry-level cyber talent and expand the pipeline of trained cyber professionals who are ready to work on day one, without requiring a costly four-year college degree. This skill-based approach is a critical step to ensuring that we are able to protect critical networks from cyber threats. For this reason, the “Cyber PIVOTT Act” has earned the support of many leading organizations in the cybersecurity and business communities.  A few months ago in September, we were able to report this bill with unanimous, bipartisan support, and it is my hope that we will be able to do so again today and advance a practical measure to strengthen our cyber workforce. Since its reintroduction in House, it has received widespread industry support, as well as a bipartisan companion bill in the Senate. Finally, we will also be considering two resolutions of inquiry introduced by our Ranking Member. ###","content_cn":"新闻\n格林主席在审议“网络 PIVOTT 法案”及第119届国会委员会监督计划时发表开场声明\n2025年2月26日\n华盛顿特区——今天，众议院国土安全委员会主席马克·E·格林医学博士（田纳西州共和党人）在审议第119届国会监督计划、H.R. 1000号法案《网络 PIVOTT 法案》、H. Res. 113号决议和H. Res. 114号决议期间发表了如下开场声明。\n按准备稿发表：早上好。今天的议程将审议国土安全委员会第119届国会授权与监督计划，以及其他措施。美国众议院规则第十条要求每个常设委员会为国会任期两年期间通过并提交一份授权与监督计划。今天审议的计划突出了本委员会本届国会的主要优先事项。首要的是，我们将努力保障美国边境安全，并支持边境巡逻队和国土安全部其他组成部门履行其关键使命。我们致力于通过确保劳动力已做好准备、配备齐全并得到适当配置，以应对来自国家行为体和犯罪行为体对关键基础设施和网络迅速演变的威胁，从而解决许多网络不安全问题的根源。我们致力于精简监管，确保监管体系促进安全和快速、可行动的信息共享，而不是不必要、重复的文书工作。网络安全是我们所有人都必须优先考虑的事项——我们必须与企业合作，确保它们尽可能实施最佳网络安全实践，同时向它们传达：当它们面临最黑暗的一天——遭受恶意国家支持的网络攻击时，政府会在这里提供帮助。\n此外，委员会的计划强调需要对国土安全部的架构进行监督，以审查潜在改革，使国土安全部在履行国土安全使命时更加高效、管理更善、成效更佳。本计划将通过聚焦关键政策领域，指导本委员会及其各小组委员会在本届国会期间的工作，包括打击恐怖主义和中国等外国国家行为体威胁、提升应急准备、确保运输系统安全，以及支持国土安全部内部执法部门及我们的州和地方合作伙伴。我鼓励所有委员支持通过委员会的授权与监督计划，使我们能够开展美国人民派我们来此从事的工作。\n我们将审议的第二项措施是H.R. 1000号法案《网络 PIVOTT 法案》。该法案将帮助我们建设一支熟练的网络人才队伍，并缩小网络劳动力缺口，以应对政府和美国企业每天面临的不断演变的威胁。《网络 PIVOTT 法案》旨在推动初级网络人才培养，并扩大经过培训、能够从第一天起上岗的网络专业人员输送渠道，而不要求取得昂贵的四年制大学学位。这种以技能为基础的方法，是确保我们能够保护关键网络免受网络威胁的重要一步。因此，《网络 PIVOTT 法案》赢得了网络安全界和商界许多领先组织的支持。几个月前的9月，我们得以在一致、跨党派支持下将该法案提交报告；我希望今天我们能够再次做到这一点，并推进一项加强网络劳动力的务实措施。自该法案在众议院重新提出以来，它获得了广泛的行业支持，并且参议院也提出了一项跨党派配套法案。最后，我们还将审议由我们的少数党领袖委员提出的两项调查决议。###","publish_source":"homeland.house.gov","publish_time":"2025-02-26T00:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3067","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"格林主席欢迎众议院通过委员会法案：打击卡特尔、保护敏感研究、加强生物检测","title_en":"Chairman Green Applauds House Passage of Committee Bills to Counter Cartels, Protect Sensitive Research, Enhance Biodetection – Committee on Homeland Security","summary_cn":"美国众议院国土安全委员会主席马克·格林发表声明，欢迎众议院本周通过H.R.495、H.R.706、H.R.901和H.R.1692四项法案。这些法案旨在加强和简化国土安全部保卫国土的能力，涉及打击卡特尔跨境隧道、改善生物防御能力、保护敏感信息免受对手获取，以及重新授权国土安全部采购尖端技术的权限。格林呼吁参议院尽快推进这些法案。","summary_en":"House Homeland Security Committee Chairman Mark E. Green issued a statement applauding House passage of H.R. 495, H.R. 706, H.R. 901, and H.R. 1692. The bills aim to strengthen and streamline DHS's ability to secure the homeland, addressing cross-border tunnels used by cartels, improving DHS biodefense capabilities, safeguarding sensitive information from adversaries, and reauthorizing DHS authority to purchase cutting-edge technology. Green urged the Senate to advance these mission-critical bills.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:59:41.931503+00:00","url":"https://homeland.house.gov/2025/03/12/chairman-green-applauds-house-passage-of-committee-bills-to-counter-cartels-protect-sensitive-research-enhance-biodetection","content":"News\nChairman Green Applauds House Passage of Committee Bills to Counter Cartels, Protect Sensitive Research, Enhance Biodetection\nMarch 12, 2025\nWASHINGTON D.C. ––House Committee on Homeland Security Chairman Mark E. Green, MD (R-TN) issued the following statement applauding House passage of H.R. 495, H.R. 706, H.R. 901, and H.R. 1692 this week. These bills were previously passed by the House of Representatives in the 118th Congress: “I was glad to work with my colleagues in the House to pass critical legislation that will strengthen and streamline DHS’ ability to secure the homeland,” Chairman Green said. “These bills put forward by the Homeland Security Committee address the deadly threat of cross-border tunnels used by cartels, make necessary improvements to DHS’ biodefense capabilities, safeguard sensitive information from our adversaries, and reauthorize DHS’ authority to purchase cutting-edge technology. I urge my colleagues in the Senate to advance these mission-critical bills to President Trump’s desk.”On the “Subterranean Border Defense Act,” Rep. Eli Crane (R-AZ) said, “Passage of this bill is a massive win for our security. With border crossings thankfully going down since January, it’s safe to assume this will drive threats underneath our border through these tunnels. This legislation will ensure Congress has sufficient knowledge and oversight in regard to this dynamic threat. Effective border security is created by overlapping deterrents, and I’m grateful to Chairman Green, Rep. Correa, and my colleagues for supporting this bill.”On the “DHS Biodetection Improvement Act” and the “Research Security and Accountability in DHS Act,” Rep. Dale Strong (R-AL) said, “The threats we face today are increasingly complex and evolving. We must stay one step ahead of our adversaries. These will improve the effectiveness of DHS’s mission to protect our national security and safeguard our interests.” On the ‘‘PATHS Act,” Rep. Michael Guest (R-MS) said, “From prototypes to help Customs and Border Protection (CBP) detect threats and illicit goods hidden inside vehicles at the border, to research to adapt machine learning practices that can identify supply chain anomalies to prevent the importation of goods that rely on forced labor, to a project conducted by the University of Southern Mississippi to develop sensors for unmanned maritime vehicles for DHS and United States Coast Guard use––the applicability and usefulness of this authority cannot be overstated. The authority expired on September 30, 2024. I am proud to lead this reauthorization effort and am pleased that the House of Representatives has passed this important bill.”Background: H.R. 495, the “Subterranean Border Defense Act,” was introduced by Rep. Eli Crane.\nThis legislation would require U.S. Customs and Border Protection (CBP) to report annually to Congress on the implementation of their strategic plan to identify and remediate illegal cross-border tunnels into the United States.\nH.R. 706, the “DHS Biodetection Improvement Act,” was introduced by Subcommittee on Emergency Management and Technology Chairman Dale Strong.\nThis legislation directs the DHS to assess how it has utilized Department of Energy national laboratories and sites for research and development in carrying out DHS missions and to report to Congress a strategy for how DHS will conduct biodetection research and development in coordination with such laboratories and sites.\nH.R. 901, the “Research Security and Accountability in DHS Act,” was introduced by Chairman Strong.\nThis legislation requires DHS’ Science and Technology Directorate (S&T) to develop a process to safeguard sensitive information in research and development projects across all components of the Department to limit unauthorized access to, and disclosure of, sensitive information.\nH.R. 1692, the “Producing Advanced Technologies for Homeland Security Act,’’ or the ‘‘PATHS Act,” was introduced by Subcommittee on Border Security and Enforcement Chairman Michael Guest.\nThis legislation will reauthorize DHS’ use of Other Transaction Authority (OTA) for three years. This bill requires DHS to provide notification to Congress to explain all uses or extensions of the transaction authority involving artificial intelligence technology. To improve transparency, this legislation will decrease the threshold for what defines a ‘covered contract award’ under the DHS Contract Reporting Act from $4 million to $1 million. This will require DHS to report transactions valued at $1 million or more on its public website.\n###","content_cn":"新闻\n格林主席赞扬众议院通过委员会法案，以打击贩毒集团、保护敏感研究并加强生物检测\n2025年3月12日\n华盛顿特区——国土安全委员会主席马克·E·格林（医学博士）（田纳西州共和党）发表以下声明，赞扬众议院本周通过H.R. 495、H.R. 706、H.R. 901和H.R. 1692。这些法案此前已由第118届国会的众议院通过：“我很高兴与众议院同僚合作，通过关键立法，加强并简化国土安全部保护国土的能力，”格林主席说。“这些由国土安全委员会提出的法案，针对贩毒集团利用的跨境隧道所带来的致命威胁，对国土安全部的生物防御能力作出必要改进，保护敏感信息免遭我们的对手获取，并重新授权国土安全部购买尖端技术。我敦促参议院同僚推进这些对国土安全部使命至关重要的法案，将其送交特朗普总统签署。”\n关于《地下边境防御法》，众议员伊莱·克兰（亚利桑那州共和党）说：“这项法案的通过是我们安全保障的一次巨大胜利。鉴于自1月以来越境人数有幸正在下降，可以合理推断，威胁将通过这些隧道转移到我们边境之下。这项立法将确保国会对这一不断变化的威胁拥有充分了解和监督。有效的边境安全由相互叠加的威慑措施构成，我感谢格林主席、科雷亚众议员以及我的同僚支持这项法案。”\n关于《国土安全部生物检测改进法》和《国土安全部研究安全与问责法》，众议员戴尔·斯特朗（阿拉巴马州共和党）说：“我们今天面临的威胁日益复杂且不断演变。我们必须始终领先对手一步。这些措施将提高国土安全部执行保护国家安全、维护我们利益这一使命的有效性。”\n关于《PATHS法》，众议员迈克尔·格斯特（密西西比州共和党）说：“从帮助海关与边境保护局（CBP）在边境发现藏在车辆内的威胁和违禁品的原型设备，到调整机器学习实践、识别供应链异常以防止进口依赖强迫劳动生产的商品的研究，再到由南密西西比大学开展、为国土安全部和美国海岸警卫队使用而开发无人海上航行器传感器的项目——这项授权的适用性和实用性怎么强调都不为过。该授权已于2024年9月30日到期。我为领导这项重新授权工作感到自豪，也很高兴众议院通过了这项重要法案。”\n背景：H.R. 495，即《地下边境防御法》，由伊莱·克兰众议员提出。\n该立法将要求美国海关与边境保护局（CBP）每年向国会报告其战略计划的实施情况，该计划旨在识别并修复通往美国的非法跨境隧道。\nH.R. 706，即《国土安全部生物检测改进法》，由紧急管理与技术小组委员会主席戴尔·斯特朗提出。\n该立法指示国土安全部评估其在执行国土安全部任务时如何利用能源部国家实验室和场所开展研发，并向国会报告一项战略，说明国土安全部将如何与这些实验室和场所协调开展生物检测研发。\nH.R. 901，即《研究安全与\n《国土安全部问责法》由斯特朗主席提出。\n该法案要求国土安全部科学技术局（S&T）制定流程，保护国土安全部所有组成部门研发项目中的敏感信息，以限制对敏感信息的未经授权访问和披露。\nH.R. 1692，即《国土安全先进技术生产法》（“PATHS法”），由边境安全与执法小组委员会主席迈克尔·盖斯特提出。\n该法案将重新授权国土安全部使用其他交易权限（OTA），为期三年。该法案要求国土安全部向国会提供通知，解释所有涉及人工智能技术的交易权限使用或延长情况。为提高透明度，该法案将根据《国土安全部合同报告法》界定“涵盖合同授予”的门槛从400万美元降至100万美元。这将要求国土安全部在其公共网站上报告价值100万美元或以上的交易。\n###","publish_source":"homeland.house.gov","publish_time":"2025-03-12T00:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2688","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"国土安全共和党人欢迎众议院通过格林议员的“特殊利益外国人报告法案”","title_en":"Homeland Republicans Applaud House Passage of Rep. Greene’s “Special Interest Alien Reporting Act” – Committee on Homeland Security","summary_cn":"2025年6月26日，美国众议院国土安全委员会共和党人欢迎众议院通过众议员玛乔丽·泰勒·格林提出的H.R. 275“2025年特殊利益外国人报告法案”。该法案要求国土安全部每月公布非法越境被查获的特殊利益外国人数量及其国籍，并追溯至2021年1月20日。声明援引格林、主席马克·格林等人言论，称拜登政府隐瞒相关数据，并提及伊朗公民、恐怖分子观察名单等背景。","summary_en":"On June 26, 2025, Republicans on the House Homeland Security Committee applauded House passage of H.R. 275, the Special Interest Alien Reporting Act of 2025, introduced by Rep. Marjorie Taylor Greene. The bill would require the Department of Homeland Security to publish monthly the number and nationalities of Special Interest Aliens encountered crossing the border unlawfully, retroactive to January 20, 2021. The release cites Greene, Chairman Mark Green and others, alleging the Biden administration concealed such data, and references Iranian nationals and the terrorist watchlist.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:33:00.004185+00:00","url":"https://homeland.house.gov/2025/06/26/homeland-republicans-applaud-house-passage-of-rep-greenes-special-interest-alien-reporting-act","content":"News\nHomeland Republicans Applaud House Passage of Rep. Greene’s “Special Interest Alien Reporting Act”\nJune 26, 2025\nLegislation demands transparency on potential national security threats illegally crossing US borders\nWASHINGTON D.C. — Today, House Committee on Homeland Security Republicans applauded the passage of Representative Marjorie Taylor Greene’s (R-GA) legislation, H.R. 275, the “Special Interest Alien Reporting Act of 2025,” by the House of Representatives. The legislation was first introduced and advanced out of the Committee in the 118th Congress, and the bill was re-introduced by Rep. Greene earlier this year. Watch Rep. Greene’s remarks before the House Committee on Rules here. Watch her remarks on the House floor today here.\nH.R. 275 would require the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) to publish every month the number of Special Interest Aliens (SIAs) encountered crossing the border unlawfully, as well as their nationalities. It would also require DHS to publish these statistics retroactive to January 20, 2021. SIAs are non-U.S. persons who, based on an analysis of travel patterns, potentially pose a national security risk to the U.S. or its interests. DHS analysis includes an examination of travel patterns, points of origin, and/or travel segments that are tied to current assessments of national and international threat environments.\nCosponsors of the legislation include Chairman Mark E. Green, MD (R-TN), Representative Clay Higgins (R-LA), Subcommittee on Border Security and Enforcement Chairman Michael Guest (R-MS), Subcommittee on Counterterrorism and Intelligence Chairman August Pfluger (R-TX), Subcommittee on Oversight, Investigations, and Accountability Chairman Josh Brecheen (R-OK), and Representative Eli Crane (R-AZ).\n“For four years, Joe Biden and Kamala Harris kept the American people in the dark and concealed the alarming number of Special Interest Aliens they allowed into our communities. Amid warnings of Iranian ‘sleeper cells’ on U.S. soil, Americans are faced with the terrifying reality of not knowing how many potential public safety threats have entered our country, and where they are coming from. Even worse, it appears Congress often learns this information from the media, rather than regular reports from the executive branch. That is unacceptable,” Rep. Greene said. “Thankfully, President Trump and his administration are working tirelessly to clean up the mess of the last four years and are swiftly removing many of these threats from our communities––but further transparency is essential as threats grow abroad. I’m grateful that the House passed my bill to make this past-due SIA information available to every American, and I urge the Senate to do the same.”“The Biden-Harris administration tried to hide that it released more than 700 Iranian nationals—all Special Interest Aliens—into our communities. At a time of heightened threats to the United States from adversaries like Iran and its proxies, the American people deserve to know how many potential national security threats crossed our borders and their countries of origin,” Chairman Green said.“Representative Greene’s bill demands much-needed transparency from DHS, and I’m proud to help pass this bill in the House. I look forward to seeing this bill on President Trump’s desk, and I urge my Senate colleagues to help us get it there without delay.”“The American people deserve to know the whole truth about who illegally crossed our border under the Biden administration. Representative Greene’s bill delivers transparency and accountability, with mandatory and retroactive reporting on Special Interest Aliens,” Rep. Higgins said. “DHS should absolutely disclose this data. The information is necessary to fully understand the threat environment facing our homeland and to protect the safety and security of America’s citizenry.”“Congress and the American people deserve to know the number and origins of the Special Interest Aliens who are attempting to cross our borders illegally––and how many have done so in the recent past,” Subcommittee Chairman Guest said. “After the complete lack of accountability and transparency from the Biden-Harris administration, we still do not know the full scale of the threats that may have entered the homeland during their historic border crisis. As threats from adversaries like Iran and China grow, the ‘Special Interest Alien Reporting Act’ will send the message that the days of letting foreign adversaries take advantage of our borders—and Democrats trying to hide the truth—are over.”\n“The Biden-Harris administration’s anti-enforcement, open border policies allowed our adversaries to flood our country illegally. This is a massive national security threat that the Trump administration is working to reverse before it’s too late,” Subcommittee Chairman Pfluger said. “Amid a resurgence of foreign terrorist organizations and heightened threats from Iran and its proxies on U.S. soil, the ‘Special Interest Alien Reporting Act’ will bring much-needed transparency following the last four years of failed leadership. It will allow Congress to more effectively work with the Trump administration to combat these threats moving forward.”    “The Biden-Harris administration’s embrace of open-border policies flooded our streets with fentanyl, plagued our communities with criminals, and caused terrorist encounters to skyrocket. Additionally, we saw exponential increases in Special Interest Aliens entering our homeland that now pose a serious long-term risk to our country,” Rep. Crane said. “Many of these foreign nationals operate as military assets, conduct espionage, and present a significant danger to the American people. While we applaud the Trump administration’s all-encompassing approach to remedy the border invasion, Congress needs a steady flow of updated data. Representative Greene’s legislation would directly address information gaps on these potentially dangerous aliens and strengthen congressional oversight. I’m proud to support this sensible measure.”\nBACKGROUND:DHS currently does not publicly publish the number of SIA encounters on its website, despite regularly publishing an even more specific, targeted number—the number of individuals on the terrorist watchlist—among its enforcement statistics. Most of the SIA numbers now public have come from leaks to the press. This bill does nothing to affect operational security or ongoing terrorism investigations. In fact, DHS officials have publicly announced such numbers on occasion.This week, Fox News revealed the threats caused by the Biden-Harris administration’s open-borders policies: “Per senior CBP source, there were 1,504 Iranian nationals caught crossing the border illegally during the Biden administration from FY’21 through FY’24, 729 (48%) of whom were released into the U.S.” The Committee found through documents provided by the Biden-Harris administration that out of 18 appointments made by Iranian nationals using the CBP mass-parole One app from Jan. 12, 2023, and Sept. 30, 2023, 16 were released on parole––a rate of 88 percent.According to DHS, Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) has arrested 130 Iranian national inadmissible aliens this week. Reports indicated that one of the foreign nationals has connections to the Islamic Revolutionary Guard Corps and Hezbollah. In testimony before the Committee in May, DHS Secretary Kristi Noem revealed: “Since President Trump has been in office, in these few short months, we have deported over 250 known terrorists out of the country.”Last Congress, former U.S. Border Patrol Chief Patrol Agent Aaron Heitke testified: “I was told I could not release any information on this increase in [Special Interest Aliens] or mention any of the arrests. The [Biden] administration was trying to convince the public that there was no threat at the border.” In 2023, Subcommittee Chairman Pfluger asked then-DHS Secretary Alejandro Mayorkas if DHS under his leadership had a policy to detain every illegal alien on the terrorist watchlist. He did not give a direct answer. Under the Biden-Harris administration, an unprecedented number of SIAs from outside the Western Hemisphere, including from adversarial nations including China, Iran, and Russia, illegally crossed America’s sovereign borders. For instance, U.S. Border Patrol apprehensions of Chinese nationals nationwide increased from 342 in FY2021 to 37,976 in FY2024 (and more than 60,000 from FY2021-2024). Record migration flows led to increases in SIAs at the Southwest border, with most SIAs using established routes in Central and South America. In just FY2023, Customs and Border Protection (CBP) recorded roughly 75,000 SIA encounters.\n###","content_cn":"新闻\n国土安全委员会共和党人赞扬众议院通过格林议员的《特别利益外国人报告法案》\n2025年6月26日\n立法要求对非法越过美国边境、可能构成国家安全威胁的人员提高透明度\n华盛顿特区——今天，众议院国土安全委员会的共和党议员赞扬众议院通过乔治亚州共和党众议员玛乔丽·泰勒·格林提出的立法，即H.R. 275号《2025年特别利益外国人报告法案》。该立法最初于第118届国会提出并经委员会推进，格林议员于今年早些时候重新提出该法案。点击此处观看格林议员在众议院规则委员会前的讲话。点击此处观看她今天在众议院全院会议上的讲话。\nH.R. 275号法案将要求国土安全部（DHS）每月公布在非法越境时遇到的特别利益外国人（SIA）人数及其国籍。该法案还将要求DHS追溯公布自2021年1月20日起的这些统计数据。特别利益外国人是指非美国人士，根据对旅行模式的分析，他们可能对美国或其利益构成国家安全风险。DHS的分析包括审查旅行模式、出发地和/或与当前国家及国际威胁环境评估相关的旅行路段。\n该法案的共同提案人包括委员会主席马克·E·格林（医学博士，田纳西州共和党）、克莱·希金斯议员（路易斯安那州共和党）、边境安全与执法小组委员会主席迈克尔·盖斯特（密西西比州共和党）、反恐与情报小组委员会主席奥古斯特·普弗卢格（得克萨斯州共和党）、监督、调查与问责小组委员会主席乔什·布雷钦（俄克拉何马州共和党）以及伊莱·克莱恩议员（亚利桑那州共和党）。\n“整整四年，乔·拜登和卡玛拉·哈里斯让美国人民蒙在鼓里，隐瞒了他们允许进入我们社区的特别利益外国人的惊人数目。在有关美国土地上存在伊朗‘潜伏细胞’的警告之际，美国人正面临一个可怕的现实：不知道有多少潜在的公共安全威胁已经进入我们的国家，也不知道他们来自哪里。更糟糕的是，国会似乎经常是从媒体那里得知这些信息，而不是从行政部门获得定期报告。这是不可接受的。”格林议员说。“值得庆幸的是，特朗普总统及其政府正在不懈努力，清理过去四年留下的烂摊子，并迅速将许多此类威胁从我们的社区中清除——但随着海外威胁加剧，进一步提高透明度至关重要。我感谢众议院通过我的法案，让每一位美国人都能获得这项早已逾期的SIA信息，我敦促参议院也这样做。”“拜登—哈里斯政府试图掩盖这样一个事实：它将700多名伊朗国民——全部属于特别利益外国人——释放到我们的社区。在伊朗及其代理人等对手对美国构成威胁加剧之际，美国人民有权知道有多少潜在的国家安全威胁越过了我们的边境，以及他们的原籍国。”格林主席说。“格林议员的法案要求DHS提供亟需的透明度，我很自豪能帮助众议院通过这项法案。我期待看到这项法案送到特朗普总统的办公桌上，并敦促我的参议院同事帮助我们毫不拖延地将其送达。”“美国人民有权知道，在……之下非法越过我们边境的人究竟是谁\n拜登政府。希金斯议员表示：“格林议员的法案通过对特殊利益外国人进行强制性和追溯性报告，带来了透明度和问责制。国土安全部绝对应该披露这些数据。这些信息对于全面了解我们祖国面临的威胁环境以及保护美国公民的安全与保障是必要的。”“国会和美国人民有权知道试图非法越过我们边境的特殊利益外国人的人数和来源，以及最近有多少人这样做过，”小组委员会主席盖斯特表示。“在拜登—哈里斯政府完全缺乏问责和透明度之后，我们仍然不知道在其历史性的边境危机期间可能进入祖国的威胁规模。随着来自伊朗和中国等对手的威胁加剧，《特殊利益外国人报告法》将传达这样的信息：任由外国对手利用我们的边境，以及民主党人试图掩盖真相的日子已经结束。”\n“拜登—哈里斯政府反执法、开放边境的政策让我们的对手得以非法涌入我国。这是一个巨大的国家安全威胁，特朗普政府正在努力在为时已晚之前扭转局面，”小组委员会主席普弗卢格表示。“在外国恐怖组织卷土重来、以及伊朗及其代理人在美国本土构成的威胁加剧之际，《特殊利益外国人报告法》将在过去四年失败的领导之后带来急需的透明度。它将使国会能够更有效地与特朗普政府合作，以应对未来的这些威胁。”\n“拜登—哈里斯政府拥抱开放边境政策，使芬太尼涌入我们的街道，犯罪分子困扰我们的社区，并导致恐怖分子遭遇数量飙升。此外，我们看到进入祖国的特殊利益外国人数量呈指数级增长，他们如今对我国构成严重的长期风险，”克兰议员表示。“其中许多外国国民作为军事资产行动，从事间谍活动，并对美国人民构成重大危险。虽然我们赞赏特朗普政府为解决边境入侵采取的全方位措施，但国会需要持续获得更新的数据。格林议员的立法将直接弥补有关这些潜在危险外国人的信息缺口，并加强国会监督。我很自豪支持这项明智的措施。”\n背景：尽管国土安全部经常在其执法统计数据中公布一个更具体、更有针对性的数字——恐怖分子观察名单上的人数——但目前并未在其网站上公开发布特殊利益外国人遭遇的数量。如今公开的大部分特殊利益外国人数据都来自向媒体泄露的信息。该法案不会影响行动安全或正在进行的恐怖主义调查。事实上，国土安全部官员偶尔会公开宣布此类数字。本周，《福克斯新闻》披露了拜登—哈里斯政府开放边境政策造成的威胁：“据海关与边境保护局一名高级消息人士透露，在拜登政府任期内，即2021财年至2024财年，共有1,504名伊朗国民在非法越境时被捕，其中729人（48%）被释放进入美国。”委员会通过拜登—哈里斯政府提供的文件发现，在伊朗国民提出的18项预约中\n在2023年1月12日至2023年9月30日期间使用CBP mass-parole One应用程序的人员中，有16人获准假释，比例为88%。据国土安全部称，本周，移民与海关执法局（ICE）逮捕了130名不准入境的伊朗籍外籍人员。报道称，其中一名外籍人士与伊斯兰革命卫队和真主党有联系。在5月份向委员会作证时，国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆披露：“自特朗普总统上任以来，在这短短几个月里，我们已经将250多名已知恐怖分子驱逐出境。”上一届国会期间，美国边境巡逻队前首席巡逻特工亚伦·海特克作证说：“有人告诉我，我不能透露特殊利益外国人数量增加的任何信息，也不能提及任何逮捕行动。[拜登]政府试图让公众相信边境不存在威胁。”2023年，委员会小组主席普弗卢格询问当时的国土安全部长亚历杭德罗·马约卡斯，在他的领导下，国土安全部是否制定了拘留恐怖分子观察名单上每一名非法外国人的政策。他没有直接回答。在拜登-哈里斯政府执政期间，来自西半球以外地区、包括中国、伊朗和俄罗斯等敌对国家的特殊利益外国人数量前所未有地增加，他们非法越过了美国的主权边界。例如，美国边境巡逻队在全国范围内拘捕的中国籍人员数量从2021财年的342人增加到2024财年的37,976人（2021至2024财年累计超过60,000人）。创纪录的移民流动导致西南边境的特殊利益外国人数量增加，其中大多数特殊利益外国人利用中美洲和南美洲既有的路线。仅在2023财年，海关与边境保护局（CBP）就记录了大约75,000起特殊利益外国人接触事件。\n###","publish_source":"homeland.house.gov","publish_time":"2025-06-26T00:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-956","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"情报与分析改革立法标记会","title_en":"Markup for I&A Reform Legislation – Committee on Homeland Security","summary_cn":"美国众议院国土安全委员会情报与分析小组委员会发布媒体公告，宣布将于2026年5月14日下午3点在坎农众议院办公楼310室举行标记会，审议多项法案，包括《2026年情报与分析任务重新定位法案》《国家威胁评估与报告计划重新分配与资金改革法案》《特别活动计划调整法案》及《现代化和改进国家恐怖主义咨询系统法案》等。会议将公开直播，记者需提前报名。","summary_en":"The Subcommittee on Counterterrorism and Intelligence of the House Homeland Security Committee issued a media advisory for a markup on May 14, 2026, at 3:00 p.m. in 310 Cannon House Office Building. Bills to be considered include the I&A Mission Reorientation Act of 2026, the National Threat Evaluation and Reporting Program Reassignment and Funding Reform Act, the Special Events Program Alignment Act, and the Modernizing and Improving the National Terrorism Advisory System Act. The markup will be livestreamed and open to the public and press.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:18:40.296408+00:00","url":"https://homeland.house.gov/hearing/media-advisory-subcommittee-chairman-pfluger-to-hold-markup-for-ia-reform-legislation","content":"This event has passed.\nMarkup for I&A Reform Legislation\nMay 14 – 3:00 pm - 5:00 pm\nDETAILS:\nWhat: Legislation that will be considered by the Subcommittee includes:\nH.R. 7443, the “I&A Mission Reorientation Act of 2026,” which was introduced by Subcommittee Chairman August Pfluger and cosponsored by Subcommittee Ranking Member Seth Magaziner (D-RI).\nH.R. 7764, the “National Threat Evaluation and Reporting Program Reassignment and Funding Reform Act of 2026,” which was introduced by Rep. Gabe Evans (R-CO) and cosponsored by Rep. Nellie Pou (D-NJ) and Rep. Matt Van Epps (R-TN).\nH.R. 7574, the “ELO Realignment and Strategic Engagement Reform Act of 2026,” which was introduced by Rep. Evans and cosponsored by Rep. Dan Goldman (D-NY).\nH.R. 8142, the “Special Events Program Alignment Act of 2026,” which was introduced by Rep. Ryan Mackenzie (R-PA) and cosponsored by Rep. Eugene Vindman (D-VA).\nH.R. 7448, the “Modernizing and Improving the National Terrorism Advisory System Act,” which was introduced by Rep. Pou and cosponsored by Rep. Van Epps.\nH.R. 7427, the “Securing Access from Foreign Entities Visiting Internal Sites in the States (SAFE VISITS) Act,” which was introduced by Rep. Goldman and cosponsored by Rep. Evans.\nH.R. 7436, the “Department of Homeland Security Intelligence and Analysis Training Act,” which was introduced by Subcommittee Ranking Member Magaziner and cosponsored by Subcommittee Chairman Pfluger.\nWhen: Thursday, May 14, 2026, at 3:00 p.m. ET\nWhere: 310 Cannon House Office Building\nThe Subcommittee markup will be livestreamed on YouTube and will be open to the public and press. Press must be congressionally credentialed and should RSVP in advance.\nAdd to calendar\nGoogle Calendar\niCalendar\nOutlook 365\nOutlook Live\nHomeland Security Committee | Republican\nU.S. House of Representatives\nH2-176 Ford House Office Building\nWashington, DC 20515\n(202) 226-8417\nMinority Website\nTwitter\nYoutube\nInstagram\nCommittee Activity\nIssues\nHearings\nPress Releases\nLetters\nFact Sheets\nSubcommittees\nBorder Security and Enforcement\nCybersecurity and Infrastructure Protection\nEmergency Management and Technology\nCounterterrorism and Intelligence\nOversight, Investigations, and Accountability\nTransportation and Maritime Security\nTask Force on Enhancing Security for Special Events in the United States\nAbout\nChairman\nMembers\nContact\nBlow The Whistle\nInternships\nName*\nFirst\nLast\nEmail*\naccessibility\ncopyright\nprivacy","content_cn":"本活动已结束。\n情报与分析改革立法标记\n5月14日 – 下午3:00 - 5:00\n详情：\n事项：小组委员会将审议的立法包括：\nH.R. 7443，《2026年情报与分析任务重新定位法案》，由小组委员会主席奥古斯特·普弗卢格提出，并由小组委员会资深成员塞思·马加齐纳（D-RI）共同发起。\nH.R. 7764，《2026年国家威胁评估与报告计划重新分配及经费改革法案》，由众议员加布·埃文斯（R-CO）提出，并由众议员内莉·普（D-NJ）和众议员马特·范·埃普斯（R-TN）共同发起。\nH.R. 7574，《ELO重新调整与战略接触改革法案》，由埃文斯众议员提出，并由众议员丹·戈德曼（D-NY）共同发起。\nH.R. 8142，《特别活动计划协调法案》，由众议员瑞安·麦肯齐（R-PA）提出，并由众议员尤金·温德曼（D-VA）共同发起。\nH.R. 7448，《国家恐怖主义咨询系统现代化与改进法案》，由普众议员提出，并由范·埃普斯众议员共同发起。\nH.R. 7427，《确保外国实体访问美国境内内部地点法案（SAFE VISITS）》，由戈德曼众议员提出，并由埃文斯众议员共同发起。\nH.R. 7436，《国土安全部情报与分析培训法案》，由小组委员会资深成员马加齐纳提出，并由小组委员会主席普弗卢格共同发起。\n时间：2026年5月14日，星期四，美国东部时间下午3:00\n地点：坎农众议院办公楼310室\n小组委员会标记会议将在YouTube上直播，并向公众和媒体开放。媒体必须持有国会证件，并应提前回复确认出席。\n添加到日历\nGoogle日历\niCalendar\nOutlook 365\nOutlook Live\n国土安全委员会 | 共和党\n美国众议院\n福特众议院办公楼H2-176\n华盛顿特区20515\n(202) 226-8417\n少数党网站\nTwitter\nYoutube\nInstagram\n委员会活动\n议题\n听证会\n新闻稿\n信函\n情况说明书\n小组委员会\n边境安全与执法\n网络安全与基础设施保护\n应急管理与技术\n反恐与情报\n监督、调查与问责\n美国特别活动安保强化工作组\n关于\n主席\n成员\n联系\n举报问题\n实习\n姓名*\n名\n姓\n电子邮件*\n无障碍\n版权\n隐私","publish_source":"homeland.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-05-14T07:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3507","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"国土安全部开放网络安全拨款申请期","title_en":"DHS opens application period for cybersecurity grants - Homeland Preparedness News","summary_cn":"美国国土安全部宣布2024财年州和地方网络安全拨款计划提供2.799亿美元资金，用于帮助政府降低网络风险、增强抵御网络威胁的能力。资金可用于网络安全规划与演练、改善居民服务、招聘网络人员等。国土安全部长马约卡斯表示，现代威胁环境下每个社区都可能面临针对医院、学校和电网等关键系统的复杂网络攻击。申请截止日期为12月3日，该计划由网络安全和基础设施安全局与联邦紧急事务管理局联合管理，四年内已向州、地方和领地政府拨款约10亿美元。","summary_en":"The U.S. Department of Homeland Security announced the availability of $279.9 million in State and Local Cybersecurity Grant Program funding for fiscal year 2024. The program helps governments reduce cyber risk and build resilience by detecting, protecting against, and responding to cyber threats. Funds may be used for cybersecurity planning and exercising, improving resident services, hiring cyber personnel, and other capabilities. Secretary Alejandro Mayorkas said every community can face sophisticated cyberattacks on vital systems like hospitals, schools, and electrical grids. The application deadline is December 3. The Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency and FEMA jointly administer the program, which has awarded about $1 billion over four years.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-25T12:03:13.611878+00:00","url":"https://homelandprepnews.com/stories/82354-dhs-opens-application-period-for-cybersecurity-grants","content":"Home » News » DHS opens application period for cybersecurity grants\n« HHS boosts Mpox global vaccine supply through donations\nBipartisan legislation accelerating microchip manufacturing projects passes House »\nDHS opens application period for cybersecurity grants\nWednesday, September 25, 2024\nby Melina Druga\n© Shutterstock\nThe U.S. Department of Homeland Security recently announced the availability of $279.9 million in State and Local Cybersecurity Grant Program grant funding for fiscal year 2024.\nThe program funds projects that help reduce cyber risk and build resilience against evolving cybersecurity threats by allowing governments to detect, protect against, and respond to cyber threats.\nRecipients may use funding for cybersecurity planning and exercising, improving services for residents, hiring cyber personnel, and other cybersecurity improvements and capabilities.\n“In the modern threat landscape, every community can – and too often does – face sophisticated cyberattacks on vital systems like hospitals, schools, and electrical grids,” Secretary of Homeland Security Alejandro N. Mayorkas said. “The Department of Homeland Security’s State and Local Cybersecurity Grant Program empowers key intergovernmental partners with the tools and support necessary to increase resilience and better secure critical infrastructure. Our message to communities everywhere is simple: do not underestimate the reach or ruthlessness of nefarious cyber actors. Through initiatives like the State and Local Cybersecurity Grant Program we can confront these threats together.”\nThe application deadline is Dec. 3.\nThe Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency and the Federal Emergency Management Agency jointly administer the program that has awarded approximately $1 billion in funding over four years to state, local, and territorial governments.\n« HHS boosts Mpox global vaccine supply through donations\nBipartisan legislation accelerating microchip manufacturing projects passes House »","content_cn":"首页 » 新闻 » 国土安全部开放网络安全补助金申请期\n« 卫生与公众服务部通过捐赠增加全球猴痘疫苗供应\n加速微芯片制造项目的两党立法获众议院通过 »\n国土安全部开放网络安全补助金申请期\n2024年9月25日，星期三\n作者：Melina Druga\n© Shutterstock\n美国国土安全部近日宣布，2024财年州和地方网络安全补助计划可提供2.799亿美元的补助资金。\n该计划为有助于降低网络风险并增强应对不断演变的网络安全威胁韧性的项目提供资金，使政府能够发现、防范和应对网络威胁。\n受资助者可将资金用于网络安全规划和演练、改善居民服务、招聘网络安全人员，以及其他网络安全改进和能力建设。\n“在现代威胁形势下，每个社区都可能——而且往往确实会——遭遇针对医院、学校和电网等重要系统的复杂网络攻击，”国土安全部长Alejandro N. Mayorkas说。“国土安全部的州和地方网络安全补助计划为关键的政府间合作伙伴提供必要的工具和支持，以增强韧性并更好地保护关键基础设施。我们向各地社区传达的信息很简单：不要低估恶意网络行为者的触及范围和残酷程度。通过州和地方网络安全补助计划等倡议，我们能够共同应对这些威胁。”\n申请截止日期为12月3日。\n网络安全与基础设施安全局和联邦紧急事务管理局共同管理该计划；过去四年，该计划已向州、地方和领地政府拨款约10亿美元。\n« 卫生与公众服务部通过捐赠增加全球猴痘疫苗供应\n加速微芯片制造项目的两党立法获众议院通过 »","publish_source":"homelandprepnews.com","publish_time":"2024-09-25T12:00:54+00:00"}},{"id":"news-497","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI、DEA、IRS与密歇根州警突袭马斯基根海茨市政厅","title_en":"FBI, DEA, IRS, MSP Raid Muskegon Heights City Hall","summary_cn":"据MIRS.news报道，联邦调查局、缉毒局、国税局及密歇根州警于周四在马斯基根县执行搜查令，作为一项进行中的金融与毒品犯罪调查的一部分。马斯基根县检察官D.J. Hilson证实马斯基根海茨市政厅为搜查地点之一，市检察官Te D. Smith确认搜查令执行并称其办公室人员在场观察。Hilson表示联邦检察官办公室亦参与其中，但未透露具体地点与细节。","summary_en":"According to MIRS.news, officers from the FBI, DEA, IRS and Michigan State Police executed search warrants Thursday in Muskegon County as part of an active financial and drug investigation. Muskegon County Prosecutor D.J. Hilson confirmed Muskegon Heights City Hall was one location, and City Attorney Te D. Smith confirmed the warrant's execution with his office present to observe. Hilson said the U.S. Attorney's Office is also participating, but specific locations and details were not disclosed.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:20:43.055681+00:00","url":"https://home.mirs.news/post/fbi-dea-irs-msp-raid-muskegon-heights-city-hall","content":"All PostsCourtsCyber/TechnologyEconomyElectionsFederalLegislativePolicy IssuesState AgenciesState BudgetEducationEnvironmentGovernorLegislatureInfrastructureFBI, DEA, IRS, MSP Raid Muskegon Heights City Hall Jul 241 min read(Source: MIRS.news, Published 07/23/2026) Officers with at least three federal law enforcement agencies and the Michigan State Police executed search warrants Thursday in Muskegon County as part of an active financial and drug investigation. It is not clear how many or where the raids took place, but WOOD TV 8 reported that Muskegon County Prosecutor D.J. Hilson confirmed that Muskegon Heights City Hall is one location. Te D. Smith, city attorney for Muskegon Heights, confirmed the execution of a search warrant, noting that representatives from his office “were present to observe the process and assist in ensuring that the legal rights and protections afforded to city officials and employees were respected.” Smith said he’s been in contact with Hilson’s office, and those communications represent the city’s “commitment to maintaining appropriate coordination with prosecutorial authorities while protecting the city’s legal interests.” Both Hilson and Smith said investigations of this nature take time. Hilson announced the probe by the Federal Bureau of Investigations, Drug Enforcement Administration and Internal Revenue Service in a post on Facebook that said the U.S. Attorney’s Office also is participating. “This is an active financial and drug crime investigation. Therefore, our ethical duties, as well as protecting the integrity of this investigation, limit our ability at this time to disclose specific details,” Hilson’s letter reads. Hilson’s post didn’t identify locations, but TV 8 also reported that a viewer reported seeing an armored vehicle with DEA markings, one MSP officer and a number of unmarked police vehicles in a neighborhood along Riordan Street near East Hackley Avenue.Tags:FederalFederal Bureau of InvestigationFederal  Recent PostsSee AllPeters: Democrats Were ‘Wrong’ On Border Security   Vance Calls El-Sayed ‘Very, Very Evil’ At Macomb Rally”   Vance Leading Campaign Rally In Sterling Heights","content_cn":"所有文章法院网络/科技经济选举联邦立法政策问题州机构州预算教育环境州长州议会基础设施\n联邦调查局、缉毒局、国税局和密歇根州警察突袭马斯基根海茨市政厅\n7月24日\n阅读1分钟\n（来源：MIRS.news，发表于2026年7月23日）\n周四，至少三个联邦执法机构的警员和密歇根州警察在马斯基根县执行搜查令，这是一起正在进行的金融和毒品调查的一部分。目前尚不清楚突袭行动有多少起或发生在哪里，但WOOD TV 8报道称，马斯基根县检察官D.J.希尔森证实，马斯基根海茨市政厅是其中一个地点。马斯基根海茨市律师特·D·史密斯证实搜查令已被执行，并指出其办公室的代表“在场观察这一过程，并协助确保市政府官员和员工所享有的合法权利和保护得到尊重”。史密斯表示，他一直与希尔森的办公室保持联系，这些沟通体现了该市“在保护城市法律利益的同时，与检察机关保持适当协调的承诺”。希尔森和史密斯都表示，此类调查需要时间。希尔森在脸书的一篇帖子中宣布，联邦调查局、缉毒局和国税局正在进行调查，并称美国检察官办公室也参与其中。希尔森的信中写道：“这是一项正在进行的金融和毒品犯罪调查。因此，我们的道德义务以及保护本次调查的完整性，限制了我们目前披露具体细节的能力。”希尔森的帖子没有说明地点，但TV 8还报道称，一名观众报告称，在东哈克利大道附近里奥丹街沿线的一个社区看到一辆带有缉毒局标志的装甲车、一名密歇根州警察和多辆无标记警车。\n标签：联邦\n联邦调查局\n联邦\n最新文章\n查看全部\n彼得斯：民主党人在边境安全问题上“错了”\n万斯在麦科姆集会上称埃尔-萨耶德“非常、非常邪恶”\n万斯在斯特林海茨带领竞选集会","publish_source":"home.mirs.news","publish_time":"2026-07-24T16:40:04.988000+00:00"}},{"id":"news-756","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"布朗谴责据报特朗普政府FBI突袭克利夫兰选民登记相关机构","title_en":"Brown Blasts Reported Trump FBI Raids Targeting Voter Registration in Cleveland","summary_cn":"美国众议员肖特尔·布朗（俄亥俄州第11选区）就据报FBI突袭俄亥俄组织协作组织发表声明，称该组织支持投票权和选民登记工作。布朗表示已联系FBI要求提供信息，并担忧这是利用联邦执法恐吓和阻止选民登记与组织活动，称其为对民主前所未有的攻击，并强调选民登记、城市社区投票和黑人投票都不是选民欺诈。","summary_en":"US Representative Shontel Brown (OH-11) issued a statement on reported FBI raids targeting the Ohio Organizing Collaborative, an organization supporting voting rights and voter registration efforts in Ohio. Brown said her office has contacted the FBI demanding information and expressed deep concern that this is an effort to use federal law enforcement to intimidate and halt voter registration and organizing. She called it an unprecedented attack on democracy and stressed that voter registration, urban communities voting and Black Americans voting are not voter fraud.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:21:38.804121+00:00","url":"http://shontelbrown.house.gov/media/press-releases/brown-blasts-reported-trump-fbi-raids-targeting-voter-registration-cleveland","content":"Home\nMedia\nPress Releases\nBrown Blasts Reported Trump FBI Raids Targeting Voter Registration in Cleveland\nImage June 12, 2026 Press ReleaseCleveland, OH – Congresswoman Shontel Brown (OH-11) releases the following statement on reported FBI raids targeting the Ohio Organizing Collaborative, an organization supporting voting rights and voter registration efforts in Ohio: “I am alarmed and outraged by reports that the Trump and Kash Patel FBI has raided the Ohio Organizing Collective in Cleveland. “My office has contacted the FBI demanding information, and I am deeply concerned that this is an effort to use federal law enforcement to intimidate and halt voter registration and organizing efforts. This is an unprecedented attack on democracy: these raids must end immediately. “Unfortunately, this appears to be part of a systematic effort by Trump and Kash Patel’s FBI to attack our elections and perpetuate more myths of voter fraud – all to undermine and challenge any election result that Trump does not agree with. It’s an attack on the People. “Let me be very clear: voter registration is not voter fraud. Urban communities voting is not voter fraud. Black Americans voting is not voter fraud. “This appears to be a blatant effort to suppress and deny the vote of people in Northeast Ohio.”###\nIssues:Civil RightsCongress\nMedia Contact\nCommunications Director: Will McDonald\nEmail:  Will.McDonald@mail.house.gov","content_cn":"主页\n媒体\n新闻稿\n布朗抨击有关特朗普 FBI 突袭克利夫兰、针对选民登记工作的报道\n图片 2026年6月12日 新闻稿俄亥俄州克利夫兰——国会女议员肖恩特尔·布朗（俄亥俄州第11选区）就有关 FBI 突袭俄亥俄组织协作社的报道发表以下声明，该组织在俄亥俄州支持投票权和选民登记工作：\n“有关特朗普和卡什·帕特尔领导的 FBI 突袭克利夫兰俄亥俄组织协作社的报道让我感到震惊和愤怒。\n“我的办公室已联系 FBI 要求提供信息，我深切担心这是利用联邦执法部门恐吓并阻止选民登记和组织工作的行动。这是对民主前所未有的攻击：这些突袭必须立即停止。\n“不幸的是，这似乎是特朗普和卡什·帕特尔的 FBI 系统性攻击我们的选举并延续更多选民舞弊谣言的一部分——其目的都是破坏和挑战特朗普不认可的任何选举结果。这是对人民的攻击。\n“让我明确说明：选民登记不是选民舞弊。城市社区投票不是选民舞弊。美国黑人投票不是选民舞弊。\n“这似乎是公然压制并剥夺俄亥俄州东北部民众投票权的行动。”###\n议题：公民权利国会\n媒体联系人\n传播主任：Will McDonald\n电子邮件：  Will.McDonald@mail.house.gov","publish_source":"shontelbrown.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-06-12T08:42:21-04:00"}},{"id":"news-2385","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"休曾加提出立法，确保政府停摆期间ICE、边境巡逻及DHS执法人员照常领薪","title_en":"Huizenga Introduces Legislation to Pay ICE Agents, Border Patrol, and DHS Law Enforcement Officers in the Event of a Shutdown | U.S. House of Representatives","summary_cn":"众议员比尔·休曾加宣布提出《2026年保卫国土者薪酬法案》，确保政府停摆期间国土安全部执法人员仍能获得薪酬。法案仿照《军队薪酬法案》，覆盖ICE、边境巡逻、TSA、特勤局等系列岗位及必要支付人员，适用于2026财年停摆，授权至2027年1月1日。多名共和党议员联署支持。","summary_en":"Congressman Bill Huizenga introduced the Pay Our Homeland Defenders Act of 2026 to ensure DHS law enforcement personnel are paid during a government shutdown. Modeled on the Pay Our Troops Act, it covers ICE, Border Patrol, TSA, Secret Service and related series, applies to any FY26 shutdown, and remains in effect until January 1, 2027 unless Congress acts sooner. Several Republican lawmakers joined in support.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T16:20:55.826722+00:00","url":"https://huizenga.house.gov/news/documentsingle.aspx?DocumentID=404138","content":"Press Releases\nHuizenga Introduces Legislation to Pay ICE Agents, Border Patrol, and DHS Law Enforcement Officers in the Event of a Shutdown\nShare on Facebook\nShare on X\nPrint this Page\nShare by Email\nWashington,\nSeptember 18, 2025\nTags:\nHomeland Security\nToday, Congressman Huizenga announced the introduction of the Pay Our Homeland Defenders Act of 2026. This legislation ensures Department of Homeland Security (DHS) law enforcement personnel defending our borders and interior are actively paid in the event of a government shutdown. Past shutdowns have forced critical homeland security personnel to work without pay, undermining morale and readiness in their mission to secure the border, address illegal immigration, stop the flow of illegal drugs, and protect commerce. The Pay Our Homeland Defenders Act of 2026 is modeled after the Pay Our Troops Act, which Congressman Huizenga cosponsors.\n“We cannot allow the mission-critical and dangerous work of our ICE Agents, Border Patrol Officers, and DHS law enforcement to be held hostage by Washington gridlock driven by partisan politics,” said Congressman Bill Huizenga. “The Pay Our Homeland Defenders Act recognizes that law enforcement personnel at the Department of Homeland Security shouldn’t have to worry about their family’s next paycheck while bravely securing our borders, cracking down on illegal drug trafficking, and keeping communities across America safe.”\nThe Pay Our Homeland Defenders Act of 2026 covers:\nDHS Law Enforcement, including employees classified in series:\n1801: General Inspection, Investigation, Enforcement, and Compliance (e.g., USCIS Immigration Officers, ICE Deportation Officers, TSA Federal Air Marshals).\n1802: Transportation Security Officers\n1811: Criminal Investigators (e.g., HSI Special Agents, ICE Special Agents, U.S. Secret Service Criminal Investigators).\n1881: CBP interdiction\n1895: Customs and Border Protection Officers.\n1896: U.S. Border Patrol Agents.\n2181: DHS Aircraft Operators\n0083: Secret Service Police\nStaff necessary to carry out the payments\nThe U.S. Coast Guard members, civilian personnel, and contractors if not otherwise covered by existing law.\nTime-Limited Coverage:\nApplies to any shutdown in FY26 (and into FY27 if necessary) until authority ends on January 1, 2027, unless Congress acts earlier.\nJoining Congressman Huizenga in support of The Pay Our Homeland Defenders Act are U.S. Representatives: Jennifer Kiggans (R-VA), Brad Finstad (R-MN), Lauren Boebert (R-CO), Aaron Bean (R-FL), Stephanie Bice (R-OK), and Claudia Tenney (R-NY).\nRelated News\nHuizenga Statement Commemorating the 25th Anniversary of 9/11\nSeptember 11, 2026 | Posted in Press Releases\nHuizenga Leads Bipartisan Effort to Strengthen Defense Cooperation with Key Allies Through UNLOCK AUKUS Act\nJuly 2, 2026 | Posted in Press Releases\nHuizenga, Olszewski, Kim, Thompson, and Bilirakis Introduce Bipartisan Legislation to Strengthen American Manufacturing\nJune 4, 2026 | Posted in Press Releases\nHuizenga Introduces Deport the Terrorists Act\nJune 2, 2026 | Posted in Press Releases\nHuizenga Introduces Legislation to Stop China and Russia from Stealing American AI Models\nApril 20, 2026 | Posted in Press Releases","content_cn":"新闻稿\n\nHuizenga提出法案，确保政府停摆期间向ICE特工、边境巡逻人员和国土安全部执法人员支付薪资\n\n在Facebook上分享\n在X上分享\n打印本页\n通过电子邮件分享\n\n华盛顿\n2025年9月18日\n\n标签：\n国土安全\n\n今天，国会议员Huizenga宣布提出《支付我们的国土防卫者法案（2026年）》。该法案确保在政府停摆期间，负责保卫边境和国内安全的国土安全部（DHS）执法人员能够持续获得薪资。过去的政府停摆迫使关键的国土安全人员无薪工作，削弱了他们执行边境安全、应对非法移民、阻止非法毒品流动以及保护商业活动任务时的士气和战备状态。《支付我们的国土防卫者法案（2026年）》以Huizenga议员共同发起的《支付我们的军人法案》为范本。\n\n“我们不能让ICE特工、边境巡逻官员和国土安全部执法人员所从事的关键且危险的工作，成为党派政治驱动的华盛顿僵局的人质，”国会议员Bill Huizenga表示。“《支付我们的国土防卫者法案》承认，国土安全部的执法人员不应在勇敢守卫边境、严厉打击非法毒品贩运并保障全美社区安全的同时，还要担心家人的下一笔薪水。”\n\n《支付我们的国土防卫者法案（2026年）》涵盖：\n\n国土安全部执法人员，包括归入以下系列的雇员：\n1801：一般检查、调查、执法和合规（例如，美国公民及移民服务局移民官员、ICE驱逐官员、运输安全管理局联邦空警）。\n1802：运输安全官员\n1811：刑事调查员（例如，国土安全调查局特别探员、ICE特别探员、美国特勤局刑事调查员）。\n1881：海关与边境保护局拦截执法\n1895：海关与边境保护官员。\n1896：美国边境巡逻特工。\n2181：国土安全部航空器操作员\n0083：特勤局警察\n\n执行支付所必需的工作人员\n\n美国海岸警卫队成员、文职人员和承包商，如未被现行法律涵盖。\n\n有时间限制的保障：\n适用于2026财年内的任何政府停摆（如有必要可延续至2027财年），直至授权于2027年1月1日终止，除非国会更早采取行动。\n\n支持《支付我们的国土防卫者法案》的国会众议员还包括：Jennifer Kiggans（弗吉尼亚州共和党）、Brad Finstad（明尼苏达州共和党）、Lauren Boebert（科罗拉多州共和党）、Aaron Bean（佛罗里达州共和党）、Stephanie Bice（俄克拉何马州共和党）和Claudia Tenney（纽约州共和党）。\n\n相关新闻\n\nHuizenga发表声明纪念“9·11”事件25周年\n2026年9月11日｜发表于新闻稿\n\nHuizenga牵头开展两党努力，通过《解锁澳英美联盟法案》加强与关键盟友的防务合作\n2026年7月2日｜发表于新闻稿\n\nHuizenga、Olszewski、Kim、Thompson和Bilirakis提出两党法案以加强美国制造业\n2026年6月4日｜发表于新闻稿\n\nHuizenga提出《驱逐恐怖分子法案》\n2026年6月2日｜发表于新闻稿\n\nHuizenga提出法案，阻止中国和俄罗斯窃取美国人工智能模型\n2026年4月20日｜发表于新闻稿","publish_source":"huizenga.house.gov","publish_time":"2025-09-18T00:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3594","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"CrowdStrike因大规模中断遭股东起诉","title_en":"CrowdStrike sued by shareholders over mass outage | Information Age | ACS","summary_cn":"CrowdStrike及其CEO乔治·库尔茨、CFO伯特·波德贝雷在得克萨斯州奥斯汀被股东提起集体诉讼，指控其就Falcon软件平台作出误导性陈述，导致7月软件更新缺陷引发全球约850万台Windows电脑崩溃。达美航空据报也寻求赔偿，CrowdStrike表示将积极抗辩。","summary_en":"CrowdStrike, its CEO George Kurtz and CFO Burt Podbere face a class action lawsuit filed in Austin, Texas, accusing them of misleading shareholders about the Falcon platform before a faulty July update crashed about 8.5 million Windows computers worldwide. Delta Air Lines is reportedly seeking damages, and CrowdStrike says it will vigorously defend the case.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:55:37.096977+00:00","url":"https://ia.acs.org.au/article/2024/crowdstrike-sued-by-shareholders-over-mass-outage.html","content":"CrowdStrike sued by shareholders over mass outage\nMajor airline also reportedly seeks damages.\nBy Tom Williams on Aug 01 2024 11:06 AM\nPrint article\nTweet\nCrowdStrike says it will 'vigorously defend' the class action lawsuit. Photo: Shutterstock\nUS cyber security company CrowdStrike, its CEO, and its CFO have been sued by a group of shareholders after a bug in a software update released in July caused more than 8.5 million computers around the world to crash.\nThe outage involving machines running Microsoft’s Windows operating system is believed to be the largest IT outage in history.\nCrowdStrike blamed a faulty software testing program for allowing the bug to get through its quality-control systems, causing the outage which affected numerous businesses and organisations such as banks, airlines, supermarkets and news broadcasters.\nThe class action lawsuit, filed on Tuesday in Austin, Texas, has accused CrowdStrike of misleading shareholders about its Falcon software platform, which was the cause of the recent outage.\nThe complaint cited comments by CrowdStrike CEO George Kurts, who allegedly told a 5 March conference call that the company’s software was “validated, tested, and certified”.\nKurtz and CrowdStrike’s Chief Financial Officer, Burt Podbere, are both defendants in the case.\nThe complaint alleged CrowdStrike had not been properly testing Falcon updates before rolling them out, which led to “a substantial risk” that an update could cause a major outage.\nIt also alleged the resulting outage in July led to “substantial reputational harm and legal risk” to the company.\nCrowdStrike, its CEO George Kurtz, and CFO Burt Podbere are all defendants in the case. Photos: CrowdStrike / Supplied\nThe lawsuit has been brought by New York law firm Labaton Keller Sucharow, on behalf of its client the Plymouth County Retirement Association and anyone who purchased or acquired CrowdStrike stock between 29 November 2023 and 29 July 2024.\nThe firm said it believed “materially false and misleading statements and omissions” by CrowdStrike led to the company’s stock being traded “at artificially high prices” during that period.\nLawyers in the class action said shares of CrowdStrike fell around 11 per cent when the outage occurred on 19 July, before falling another 13.5 per cent on 22 July when CEO Kurtz was asked to testify before US Congress, and CrowdStrike’s stock rating was downgraded by analyst firms.\nThe lawyers said CrowdStrike shares fell 10 per cent on 29 July, when it was reported that major US airline Delta had hired a prominent attorney to seek damages from the company, alleging the outage cost it more than $535 million ($US350 million) due to delays and cancelled flights.\nIn a statement to the Reuters news agency, CrowdStrike said: \"We believe this case lacks merit and we will vigorously defend the company.\"\nCrowdStrike could still face further lawsuits related to its recent outage.\nThe Australian government has not yet provided an estimate of how much the outage may have cost the national economy.\nMicrosoft has already flagged possible security changes in the wake of the outage, including potentially limiting the level of access provided to cyber security and antivirus software within Windows.\nTom Williams\nTom Williams is a senior journalist at Information Age with key interests in consumer technology, artificial intelligence, quantum computing, cybersecurity, and telecommunications. He was previously a digital journalist at ABC News, where he covered technology and breaking news.\nYou can follow Tom on Bluesky, LinkedIn, or Threads, contact him at [email protected], and send tip-offs via secure email to [email protected].\nTags:\ncrowdstrike\nmicrosoft\nwindows\ncyber security\ngeorge kurtz\nburt podbere\ndelta airlines\nclass action lawsuit","content_cn":"CrowdStrike遭股东起诉，涉及大规模宕机\n据报道，一家大型航空公司也寻求赔偿。\nTom Williams，2024年8月1日上午11:06\n打印文章\n推文\nCrowdStrike称将“积极抗辩”这起集体诉讼。图片：Shutterstock\n美国网络安全公司CrowdStrike、其首席执行官和首席财务官遭一群股东起诉，此前该公司7月发布的软件更新中存在一个漏洞，导致全球超过850万台电脑崩溃。\n涉及运行微软Windows操作系统设备的这次宕机被认为是历史上规模最大的IT宕机。\nCrowdStrike将责任归咎于有缺陷的软件测试程序，称该程序使漏洞通过了质量控制系统，造成影响众多企业和组织的宕机，包括银行、航空公司、超市和新闻广播机构。\n这起集体诉讼于周二在得克萨斯州奥斯汀提起，指控CrowdStrike误导股东，涉及其Falcon软件平台，而该平台正是近期宕机的原因。\n诉状引用了CrowdStrike首席执行官George Kurts的言论，据称他在3月5日的一次电话会议上表示，该公司的软件“经过验证、测试和认证”。\nKurtz与CrowdStrike首席财务官Burt Podbere均为本案被告。\n诉状称，CrowdStrike在推出Falcon更新之前没有进行适当测试，因此“一次更新可能造成重大宕机的风险相当大”。\n诉状还称，7月由此造成的宕机给公司带来了“重大的声誉损害和法律风险”。\nCrowdStrike、其首席执行官George Kurtz以及首席财务官Burt Podbere均为本案被告。图片：CrowdStrike/供图\n这起诉讼由纽约律师事务所Labaton Keller Sucharow代表其客户Plymouth County Retirement Association，以及所有在2023年11月29日至2024年7月29日期间购买或取得CrowdStrike股票的人提起。\n该事务所表示，它认为CrowdStrike的“重大虚假和误导性陈述及遗漏”导致公司股票在此期间以“人为抬高的价格”交易。\n集体诉讼律师称，7月19日宕机发生时，CrowdStrike股价下跌约11%；7月22日，当首席执行官Kurtz被要求在美国国会作证且分析机构下调CrowdStrike股票评级时，股价又下跌13.5%。\n律师称，7月29日，在有报道称美国大型航空公司达美航空聘请一名知名律师向该公司索赔后，CrowdStrike股价下跌10%；达美航空指称，由于航班延误和取消，这次宕机使其损失超过5.35亿美元（3.5亿美元）。\nCrowdStrike在向路透社发表的一份声明中称：“我们认为本案缺乏依据，我们将积极为公司抗辩。”\nCrowdStrike仍可能面临与近期宕机有关的更多诉讼。\n澳大利亚政府尚未估算这次宕机可能给国民经济造成的损失。\n微软已经表示，宕机事件后可能进行安全方面的调整，包括可能限制Windows系统中向网络安全和防病毒软件提供的访问权限级别。\nTom Williams\nTom Williams是《Information Age》的资深记者，重点关注消费科技、人工智能、量子计算、网络安全和电信。他此前是ABC News的数字记者，报道科技和突发新闻。\n你可以在Bluesky、LinkedIn或Threads上关注Tom，也可以通过[email protected]联系他，并通过安全电子邮件[email protected]提供线索。\n标签：\ncrowdstrike\nmicrosoft\nwindows\n网络安全\ngeorge kurtz\nburt podbere\ndelta airlines\n集体诉讼","publish_source":"ia.acs.org.au","publish_time":"2024-08-01T07:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-227","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Bing News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"设备制造商在遭网络攻击后重建供应链","title_en":"Device Maker Rebuilds Supply Chain After Breach","summary_cn":"波士顿科学公司2026年8月25日发现网络安全事件，导致部分操作系统和业务应用中断，影响产品制造及订单处理和发货。制造、订单履行和发货现已全面恢复，产品流通达到或高于正常水平。克劳德斯特赖克公司等第三方专家参与调查，独立评估未发现系统或产品技术遭入侵的证据，也未发现持续威胁活动。远程监测激活功能已恢复，积压订单仍在处理中。","summary_en":"Boston Scientific identified a cybersecurity incident on 25 August 2026 that disrupted certain operating systems and business applications, affecting manufacturing and order processing and shipping. Manufacturing, order fulfilment and shipping are now fully restored, with product moving at or above normal levels. CrowdStrike and other third-party experts remain engaged; independent assessments found no evidence of ongoing threat activity or compromise to systems or product technologies. Remote monitoring activation has resumed, while backlog orders are still being worked through.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T19:58:43.063083+00:00","url":"https://idm.net.au/article/0015789-device-maker-rebuilds-supply-chain-after-breach","content":"A cybersecurity incident that stopped a global medical device manufacturer from making or shipping product has ended with operations fully restored. The one clinical workflow it degraded is working again.\nThe supplier of pacemakers, implantable defibrillators, and heart implants, Boston Scientific, identified the incident on 25 August 2026. It has published dated updates since, most recently on 9 September. CrowdStrike and other third-party experts remain engaged.\nThe company reported a network outage affecting certain operating systems and business applications. That included the ability to manufacture products and to process and ship customer orders.\nManufacturing, order fulfilment and shipping are now fully restored. Product is moving through the distribution network at or above normal levels.\nBacklog remains the residual problem. The company is working through orders pending before 25 August alongside those received during the disruption, and says some customers may still see temporary delays.\nOn the security question, independent assessments have come back clean. Since containment began on 25 August, CrowdStrike and other experts have found no evidence of ongoing threat activity. They also found no evidence of compromise to Boston Scientific systems or product technologies.\nThat assessment covers product development systems, product software systems, and manufacturing and medical device maintenance systems. It also covers software and business applications, cloud-based systems, email platforms and external collaboration platforms.\nBusiness applications are still being brought back progressively. Customers experiencing access problems are being notified directly as individual applications return.\nThe remote monitoring gap has closed. Activation capability has been restored, and activations for cardiac device implant communicators and insertable cardiac monitors have resumed.\nWhat was affected while it lasted\nThat workflow was the sharpest edge of the incident. New implants could be placed, but the communicators that send device data to remote patient management systems could not be activated.\nNewly implanted insertable cardiac monitors had to be activated through the company's Clinic Assistant app, and could not pair to the patient's monitoring phone. Recorded episodes had to be retrieved by in-person interrogation.\nImplanted device function itself was never affected. Remote monitoring of devices already being monitored before the disruption continued, and programmer interrogations were unaffected throughout.\nThe company also stated there was no known impact to devices not connected to a Boston Scientific network. It found no evidence the affected environment increased cybersecurity risk to hospital networks.\nOn personal data, the position has not moved. The company says it is still investigating. It will notify affected individuals, regulators and customers in accordance with privacy laws if it determines data has been compromised.\nOrder intake continued throughout via EDI and local applications, with orders queued for later fulfilment.\nRestoration ran shipping first. The company began restoring shipping for most products at major distribution centres on 3 September. It described the network as substantially restored on 5 September, and reported full restoration on 9 September.\nThe disclosure practice is worth noting alongside the recovery. Boston Scientific has run the incident through a single dated page, timestamped to the minute, with eight earlier updates archived beside the current one.\nIt says it will publish further forensic findings from the CrowdStrike investigation as they become available. The incident page is on its newsroom.\nBusiness Solution\nCybersecurity","content_cn":"一起导致一家全球医疗设备制造商无法生产或发运产品的网络安全事件已经结束，运营已全面恢复。其受影响的一项临床工作流程现已恢复运行。\n起搏器、植入式除颤器和心脏植入物供应商波士顿科学于2026年8月25日发现该事件。此后该公司发布了带日期的更新，最近一次是在9月9日。CrowdStrike 和其他第三方专家仍在参与处理。\n该公司报告称，网络中断影响了某些操作系统和业务应用程序。其中包括生产产品以及处理和发运客户订单的能力。\n制造、订单履行和发运现已全面恢复。产品正以正常水平或高于正常水平的速度通过配送网络流转。\n积压订单仍是残留问题。该公司正在处理8月25日前待处理的订单以及在中断期间收到的订单，并称部分客户可能仍会遇到暂时延误。\n在安全问题上，独立评估结果未发现问题。自8月25日开始遏制以来，CrowdStrike 和其他专家未发现持续威胁活动的证据。他们也未发现波士顿科学系统或产品技术遭到入侵的证据。\n该评估涵盖产品开发系统、产品软件系统，以及制造和医疗设备维护系统。它还涵盖软件和业务应用程序、基于云的系统、电子邮件平台和外部协作平台。\n业务应用程序仍在逐步恢复。遇到访问问题的客户会在各应用程序恢复时被直接通知。\n远程监测缺口已经消除。激活功能已经恢复，心脏设备植入通信器和植入式心脏监测器的激活工作已恢复。\n受影响的情况\n这是该事件影响最明显的工作流程。可以进行新的植入手术，但无法激活将设备数据发送至远程患者管理系统的通信器。\n新植入的植入式心脏监测器必须通过该公司的 Clinic Assistant 应用程序激活，且无法与患者的监测手机配对。记录的事件必须通过现场询问获取。\n植入设备本身的功能从未受到影响。对在中断前已处于远程监测状态的设备的远程监测持续进行，编程器询问在整个过程中也未受影响。\n该公司还表示，已知未连接到波士顿科学网络的设备没有受到影响。该公司未发现受影响环境增加医院网络网络安全风险的证据。\n关于个人数据，其立场没有变化。该公司称仍在调查中。如果确定数据已泄露，将根据隐私法律通知受影响个人、监管机构和客户。\n订单接收通过 EDI 和本地应用程序持续进行，订单排队等待后续履行。\n恢复工作首先进行发运。该公司于9月3日开始在主要配送中心恢复大多数产品的发运。其于9月5日称网络已基本恢复，并于9月9日报告已全面恢复。\n除恢复情况外，其披露做法也值得注意。波士顿科学通过一个带日期的单独页面公布该事件，页面精确标注至分钟，当前更新旁还归档了此前八次更新。\n该公司称，将在 CrowdStrike 调查的进一步取证结果可用时公布。事件页面位于其新闻编辑室。\n业务解决方案\n网络安全","publish_source":"idm.net.au","publish_time":"2026-09-11T11:03:01+10:00"}},{"id":"news-127","ktid":1000490,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000490","source":"Bing News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"分析称中国升级吉布提基地监视系统","title_en":"Apps","summary_cn":"战略与国际研究中心于2026年9月17日发布对商业卫星图像的分析，显示中国在吉布提的军事基地自2024年中期以来新建了两处通信设施，配备新天线、卫星通信设备等系统。该基地2017年启用，是中国唯一正式承认的海外军事基地。报告称新设备的类型和朝向多样，可覆盖广泛信号和频率，或使中国更全面掌握该地区作战环境，但仅凭图像无法确定基地是否正在主动拦截通信。","summary_en":"The Center for Strategic and International Studies released an analysis of commercial satellite imagery on 17 September 2026 showing upgrades at China's military base in Djibouti. Two new communications compounds have been built since mid-2024, with new antennas and satellite communications equipment. The base, opened in 2017, is China's only formally acknowledged overseas military base. CSIS says the varied type and orientation of the new equipment could enable transmission and detection across a wide range of signals, giving China a more robust picture of the regional operating environment, though it cannot determine from images alone whether the base is actively intercepting communications.","tag":"geopolitics","founddate":"2026-09-24T19:51:35.340370+00:00","url":"https://ijr.com/discover/china-reportedly-upgrades-djibouti-base-for-regional-surveillance-55d9684f","content":"Analysis Details China Upgrades to Djibouti Base Surveillance SystemsShareWorldAnalysis Details China Upgrades to Djibouti Base Surveillance Systems6 sources·Updated Sep 18, 2026Photo: Magda Ehlers / Wikimedia Commons (Pexels)SponsoredCSIS released an analysis of commercial satellite imagery on September 17, 2026 showing upgrades at China's military base in Djibouti. Two new communications compounds have been built since mid-2024, with new antennas, satellite communications equipment and other systems. The base opened in 2017 near the Bab al-Mandeb Strait. It is China's only formally acknowledged overseas military base and supports Chinese naval operations in the Gulf of Aden and Red Sea. The United States, France, Italy and Japan operate bases less than 10 miles (16 km) from China's. Conflicts involving the Houthis, Iran, Israel and the United States are cited as increasing regional military activity. China's Washington embassy did not respond to Reuters by the time of publication.\nCONTESTED\nCSIS says the type and orientation of the base's new equipment is varied, enabling transmission and detection across a wide range of signals and frequencies. The facilities would provide China with a much more robust picture of the operating environment in the region, the report said. CSIS says China could draw valuable insights into U.S. and other militaries' operations by observing the direction, origin, frequency, and pace of their signals. CSIS states it cannot determine from images alone whether the base is actively intercepting communications.","content_cn":"分析详述中国升级吉布提基地监视系统\n分享\n世界\n分析详述中国升级吉布提基地监视系统\n6个来源 · 更新于2026年9月18日\n照片：Magda Ehlers / Wikimedia Commons（Pexels）\n赞助内容\nCSIS于2026年9月17日发布了对商业卫星图像的分析，显示中国在吉布提的军事基地进行了升级。自2024年年中以来，已建成两处新的通信设施区，配备新天线、卫星通信设备及其他系统。该基地于2017年在曼德海峡附近启用。这是中国唯一正式承认的海外军事基地，并为中国海军在亚丁湾和红海的行动提供支持。美国、法国、意大利和日本运营的基地距中国基地不足10英里（16公里）。涉及胡塞武装、伊朗、以色列和美国的冲突被认为加剧了地区军事活动。截至发稿时，中国驻华盛顿大使馆未回应路透社的置评请求。\n存在争议\nCSIS称，基地新设备的类型和朝向多样，可在广泛的信号与频率范围内实现传输和探测。报告称，这些设施将使中国能够对该地区的运行环境形成更为全面的认识。CSIS表示，中国可以通过观察美国及其他国家军队信号的方向、来源、频率和节奏，获得有关其行动的宝贵洞见。CSIS称，仅凭图像无法确定该基地是否正在积极截获通信。","publish_source":"ijr.com","publish_time":"2026-09-17T22:34:21+00:00"}},{"id":"news-197","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Bing News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI局长帕特尔在参议院审查中作证","title_en":"Apps","summary_cn":"美国联邦调查局局长卡什·帕特尔于2026年9月15日出席参议院司法委员会听证会，这是他自2025年9月以来首次作证。报道称已有超过1100名FBI特工离职。参议员迪克·德宾批评帕特尔是史上最不合格、最具党派色彩的FBI局长，并指控其将执法权力用于对特朗普政治对手的报复。帕特尔则就个人出行次数、航班费用及装甲车辆成本等作出说明。","summary_en":"FBI Director Kash Patel testified before the Senate Judiciary Committee on 15 September 2026, his first appearance since September 2025. More than 1,100 FBI special agents have departed the bureau. Sen. Dick Durbin called Patel the least qualified and most partisan FBI director in the nation's history and accused him of using law enforcement powers for retribution against Trump's political opponents. Patel addressed his personal travel, flight costs and armored vehicle expenses during the hearing.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:02:05.002347+00:00","url":"https://ijr.com/discover/fbi-director-patel-testifies-amid-senate-scrutiny-5cbafef4","content":"FBI Director Patel Testifies Amid Senate ScrutinySharePoliticsFBI Director Patel Testifies Amid Senate Scrutiny15 sources·Updated Sep 15, 2026Photo: Federal Bureau of Investigation / Wikimedia Commons (Public domain)SponsoredFBI Director Kash Patel testified before the Senate Judiciary Committee on September 15, 2026, his first appearance since September 2025. More than 1,100 FBI special agents have departed the bureau. A wire summary reported an 18.1 percent drop in the murder rate in 2025. Sen. Dick Durbin called Patel the least qualified and most partisan FBI director in the nation's history and accused him of using law enforcement powers for retribution against Trump's political opponents. Durbin said Patel opens positions to applicants with significant misconduct histories; Democrats alleged the FBI admits applicants with histories of employee theft, paying for sex, or bestiality. Patel told Sen. Chuck Grassley he made 11 personal residence trips in 2025, a 41.3 percent reduction versus Wray and 38.9 percent versus Comey, and that Andrews flights could have saved $3.5 million. He said two armored BMWs saved over $1 million each versus Suburbans. In the 2025 hearing Patel called Schiff a political buffoon and Booker an embarrassment. Patel filed a $420 million defamation lawsuit against The Atlantic. The FBI assigned hundreds of analysts to Fulton County election records and raided a warehouse there in January.","content_cn":"FBI 局长 Patel 在参议院审查中作证\n分享\n政治\nFBI 局长 Patel 在参议院审查中作证\n15个来源·更新于 2026年9月15日\n图片：Federal Bureau of Investigation / Wikimedia Commons（公共领域）\n赞助内容\nFBI 局长 Kash Patel 于2026年9月15日在参议院司法委员会作证，这是他自2025年9月以来首次出席。超过1,100名 FBI 特工已离开该局。一份通讯摘要报告称，2025年谋杀率下降18.1%。参议员 Dick Durbin 称 Patel 是美国历史上资历最不足、党派色彩最浓的 FBI 局长，并指控他利用执法权力报复 Trump 的政治对手。Durbin 表示，Patel 向有严重不当行为记录的申请人开放职位；民主党人指称 FBI 录取具有员工盗窃、付费性交易或兽交史的申请人。Patel 告诉参议员 Chuck Grassley，他在2025年进行了11次私人住所出行，比 Wray 少41.3%、比 Comey 少38.9%，且从 Andrews 起飞的航班本可节省350万美元。他表示，两辆装甲 BMW 相比 Suburban 每辆节省超过100万美元。在2025年的听证会上，Patel 称 Schiff 是政治小丑，Booker 是一种耻辱。Patel 对《大西洋月刊》提起4.2亿美元诽谤诉讼。FBI 指派数百名分析师审查 Fulton County 的选举记录，并于1月突袭了当地一处仓库。","publish_source":"ijr.com","publish_time":"2026-09-15T14:12:40+00:00"}},{"id":"news-203","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Bing News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"举报人称国土安全部非法访问选民记录","title_en":"Apps","summary_cn":"2026年9月14日，参议员舒默和帕迪利亚发布近30页举报人报告，指控国土安全部通过“非法选民倡议”非法访问州选民系统。报告称USCIS员工被抽调，接受不到两小时培训后以每人约12分钟的速度核查名单。DHS首席法律顾问称该访问方式合规。白宫一份文件称四州有超25万非公民登记。新泽西州长称软件错误导致约6600例自动登记，实际投票不足400张。DHS与白宫尚未公开回应。","summary_en":"On Sept. 14, 2026, Senators Schumer and Padilla released a nearly 30-page whistleblower report alleging DHS illegally accessed state voter systems via an 'Unlawful Voter Initiative.' USCIS employees were reportedly pulled from duties, given under two hours of training, and ran DHS lists at about 12 minutes per person. DHS's chief counsel said the access technique was permissible. A White House document claimed over 250,000 non-citizens registered in four states. New Jersey's governor cited a software error causing about 6,600 automatic registrations with fewer than 400 ballots cast. DHS and the White House had not publicly responded.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T05:45:36.099075+00:00","url":"https://ijr.com/discover/politics-2026-09-14-whistleblower-alleges-dhs-illegally-accessed-voter-records-491adfc2","content":"Whistleblower Alleges DHS Illegally Accessed Voter RecordsSharePoliticsWhistleblower Alleges DHS Illegally Accessed Voter Records15 sources·Updated Sep 15, 2026© IJRSponsoredIn late August 2026, USCIS employees were pulled off regular duties, given under two hours of training, and set to run DHS lists through state voter systems at about 12 minutes per person. On September 14, Senators Chuck Schumer and Alex Padilla released a nearly 30-page Democracy Defenders Fund whistleblower report on the Unlawful Voter Initiative and held a news conference after a letter to DHS Secretary Markwayne Mullin demanding a halt.\nWhat is contested: The whistleblower report states \"the current process is knowingly sweeping known U.S. citizens in as potentially 'unlawful voters,'\" citing alien identification numbers that remain after naturalization. DHS chief counsel told agents the access technique was permissible; officials said agents are not personally liable if searches are official and documented. A White House DHS document tied to Trump's July 16 speech claimed more than 250,000 non-citizens registered in California, Nevada, New Jersey, and Pennsylvania. New Jersey Gov. Mikie Sherrill said a \"serious software error\" produced about 6,600 automatic non-citizen registrations from June 2023 to June 2024, with fewer than 400 ballots cast.\nSchumer said, \"We just got more proof of Trump's vile schemes to rig our elections,\" and called it how far Trump will go to interfere. DHS told the New York Times, \"Our message to aliens who vote in American elections is clear: we will find you, arrest you, and you will face the consequences — including criminal charges and deportation.\" A DHS spokesperson earlier told AP the department cross-referenced publicly available voter-roll data with known illegal aliens. DHS and the White House had not publicly responded in the reports provided.SponsoredIn this story:👤Alex Padilla👤Donald John TrumpTagWhere do you stand?Alex PadillaSupportOpposeDonald John TrumpSupportOpposeCoverage detailsL 64%C 36%More on this storyBack to NewsBusinessKelce Named Fraud Victim; Operator Sentenced 11 YearsSiddharth Jawahar got 11 years for a $35 million fraud scheme; prosecutors named Travis Kelce a victim at the St. Louis sentencing.108 sourcesPolitics12 Charged in Alleged $10M San Diego Childcare Fraud12 charged with allegedly collecting more than $10M in San Diego childcare subsidies for daycares prosecutors say had no children.","content_cn":"举报人指称 DHS 非法访问选民记录\n分享\n政治\n举报人指称 DHS 非法访问选民记录\n15 个来源·更新于 2026年9月15日\n© IJR\n赞助内容\n2026年8月下旬，USCIS 员工被从日常职责中抽调出来，接受了不足两小时的培训，并被安排以每人约12分钟的速度，通过州选民系统核查 DHS 名单。9月14日，参议员 Chuck Schumer 和 Alex Padilla 发布了一份近30页、由 Democracy Defenders Fund 出具的关于“非法选民倡议”的举报人报告；此前他们曾致函 DHS 部长 Markwayne Mullin，要求停止该倡议，随后又举行了新闻发布会。\n\n存在争议之处：举报人报告称，“当前流程明知会将已知的美国公民一并纳入可能的‘非法选民’之列”，理由是归化入籍后仍保留的外国人识别号码。DHS 首席法律顾问告诉特工，该访问技术是被允许的；官员称，若搜索属于公务且有记录，特工不承担个人责任。一份与 Trump 7月16日演讲相关的白宫 DHS 文件称，加利福尼亚州、内华达州、新泽西州和宾夕法尼亚州有超过250,000名非公民已登记。新泽西州州长 Mikie Sherrill 表示，一项“严重的软件错误”导致从2023年6月至2024年6月约6,600名非公民被自动登记，其中投出的选票不足400张。\n\nSchumer 表示：“我们刚刚获得更多证据，证明 Trump 企图操纵我们选举的卑劣阴谋，”并称这显示了 Trump 为干预所能走多远。DHS 告诉《纽约时报》：“我们对在美国选举中投票的外国人的信息很明确：我们会找到你们、逮捕你们，而你们将面临后果——包括刑事指控和驱逐出境。”DHS 一位发言人早前告诉 AP，该部门将公开可得的选民名册数据与已知非法外国人进行交叉比对。在所提供的报道中，DHS 和白宫尚未公开回应。\n赞助内容\n本报道涉及：\n👤Alex Padilla\n👤Donald John Trump\n标签\n你的立场是什么？\nAlex Padilla\n支持\n反对\nDonald John Trump\n支持\n反对\n报道详情\nL 64%\nC 36%\n更多相关报道\n返回新闻\n商业\nKelce 被列为欺诈受害者；运营者被判11年\nSiddharth Jawahar 因一项3,500万美元的欺诈计划被判11年；检方在圣路易斯的宣判中将 Travis Kelce 列为受害者。\n108 个来源\n政治\n12 人因涉嫌圣迭戈1,000万美元儿童保育欺诈案被起诉\n12 人被指控从检方称没有儿童的日托机构中骗取超过1,000万美元的圣迭戈儿童保育补贴。","publish_source":"ijr.com","publish_time":"2026-09-14T22:55:19+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2151","ktid":1001270,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001270","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"印度基金会与CNAS代表团举行互动会议","title_en":"Interactive Session with Center for a New American Security (CNAS) Delegation – India Foundation","summary_cn":"2025年11月6日，印度基金会接待了来自华盛顿智库新美国安全中心（CNAS）的代表团，由CNAS主席理查德·方丹率领。会议为闭门讨论，参与者包括印度学者、前外交官、战略分析师和政策实践者。核心议题是美印关系的历史演变，探讨关键转折点、共同障碍及推动两国关系升级为“全面全球战略伙伴关系”的因素，并分析当前共同关切问题，旨在增进相互理解、寻找未来合作路径。","summary_en":"On November 6, 2025, the India Foundation hosted an interactive session with a visiting delegation from the Center for a New American Security (CNAS), a Washington, D.C.-based think tank, led by CNAS President Richard Fontaine. The closed-door discussion brought together Indian academics, former diplomats, strategic analysts and policy practitioners. The core focus was the evolution of US-India relations, covering historical turning points, shared obstacles and factors elevating ties to a Comprehensive Global Strategic Partnership, along with current issues of mutual significance, aiming to foster mutual understanding and identify pathways for future collaboration.","tag":"geopolitics","founddate":"2026-09-24T13:48:44.363133+00:00","url":"https://indiafoundation.in/event-reports/interactive-session-with-center-for-a-new-american-security-cnas-delegation/","content":"India FoundationPosts PageEvent ReportsInteractive Session with Center for a New American Security (CNAS) Delegation\nEvent Reports |\nNovember 6, 2025Interactive Session with Center for a New American Security (CNAS) Delegation\nListen to this article now\n1.0x\n00:00\n--:--On November 6, 2025, India Foundation had hosted an interactive session with a visiting delegation from the Center for a New American Security (CNAS), a prominent think tank based in Washington, D.C. The delegation was notably led by Mr. Richard Fontaine, the President of CNAS.The gathering was structured as a closed-door discussion, ensuring a candid and focused exchange of perspectives. The participants included a select group of subject experts from India—academics, former diplomats, strategic analysts, and policy practitioners—who possess deep insights into international relations, security, and strategic affairs.The core focus of the session was a comprehensive and nuanced exploration of the evolution of US-India relations over the years. The discussions focused on the historical development of the partnership, exploring key turning points, shared obstacles, and the elements that have been instrumental in elevating the relationship from a historically distant one to a “Comprehensive Global Strategic Partnership,” alongside an analysis of current issues of mutual significance. The dialogue aimed to foster mutual understanding and identify pathways for future collaboration in an increasingly complex global order.\nPosted byIndia FoundationNov 6, 2025Nov 17, 2025Posted inEvent ReportsLatest News\nANNUAL REPORT 2025\nSeptember 16, 2026\nNavigating Chokepoints: The Indo-Mediterranean Corridor and India’s Vision 2047\nSeptember 1, 2026\nReimagining India’s Western Theatre in an Age of Strategic Disruption and Transition to a New World Order\nSeptember 1, 2026Post navigationPrevious Post Previous post: Charting a Circular Battery Future in IndiaNext Post Next post: Fudan University Delegation Visit to Bengaluru and New Delhi from 10-15 November 2025\nLeave a comment Cancel replyYour email address will not be published. Required fields are marked *Comment *Name * Email * Website Please enter an answer in digits:five × two =","content_cn":"印度基金会文章页面活动报告与新美国安全中心（CNAS）代表团的互动会议\n活动报告 |\n2025年11月6日与新美国安全中心（CNAS）代表团的互动会议\n立即收听本文\n1.0倍速\n00:00\n--:--2025年11月6日，印度基金会举办了一场与来访的新美国安全中心（CNAS）代表团的互动会议。CNAS是总部位于华盛顿特区的知名智库。该代表团由CNAS主席理查德·方丹先生领衔。\n此次会议采用闭门讨论形式，以确保坦诚且聚焦的观点交流。与会者包括来自印度的精选领域专家——学者、前外交官、战略分析人士和政策从业者——他们对国际关系、安全和战略事务具有深刻见解。\n会议的核心重点是全面且细致地探讨多年来美印关系的演变。讨论聚焦于伙伴关系的历史发展，探究关键转折点、共同障碍，以及促使两国关系从历史上较为疏远的关系提升为“全面全球战略伙伴关系”的关键要素，同时分析当前具有共同重要性的议题。对话旨在促进相互理解，并在日益复杂的全球秩序中寻找未来合作的路径。\n发布者：印度基金会 2025年11月6日 2025年11月17日 发布于活动报告 最新新闻\n2025年年度报告\n2026年9月16日\n驾驭关键瓶颈：印地中海走廊与印度的2047愿景\n2026年9月1日\n在战略扰动与向新世界秩序过渡时代重新构想印度西部战区\n2026年9月1日文章导航上一篇文章：规划印度循环电池的未来 下一篇文章：复旦大学代表团于2025年11月10日至15日访问班加罗尔和新德里\n发表评论 取消回复您的电子邮件地址不会被公开。必填字段标有 *评论 *姓名 *电子邮件 *网站 请用数字输入答案：五 × 二 =","publish_source":"indiafoundation.in","publish_time":"2025-11-06T16:59:59+05:30"}},{"id":"news-2949","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI局长卡什·帕特尔赞扬哈普里特·辛格被捕","title_en":"FBI DIrector Kash Patel Hails Arrest Of Harpreet Singh","summary_cn":"美国联邦调查局（FBI）局长卡什·帕特尔4月21日表示，涉嫌在印度和美国策划多起袭击的哈普里特·辛格被捕后“正义将得到伸张”。帕特尔赞扬FBI萨克拉门托团队与印度当局合作。辛格与两个国际恐怖组织有关联，非法入境美国并使用一次性手机躲避追捕，于4月18日在萨克拉门托被捕。旁遮普警察总监称这是打击恐怖网络的重要里程碑。","summary_en":"FBI Director Kash Patel said on April 21 that \"justice will be done\" following the arrest of Harpreet Singh, who is accused of planning multiple attacks in India and the United States. Patel praised the FBI Sacramento team for collaborating with Indian authorities. Singh, linked to two international terrorist groups, entered the U.S. illegally and used burner phones to evade capture; he was arrested on April 18 in Sacramento. Punjab's police chief called the arrest a major milestone against terror networks.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:15:15.247024+00:00","url":"https://indiawest.com/fbi-director-kash-patel-hails-arrest-of-harpreet-singh","content":"0 Comments\nApril 22, 2025\nFBI DIrector Kash Patel Hails Arrest Of Harpreet Singh\nSACRAMENTO, CA (ANI)– FBI Director Kash Patel declared on April 21 that “justice will be done” following the arrest of Harpreet Singh, a terrorist involved in attacks in Punjab.\nPatel commended the FBI Sacramento team for their collaboration with Indian authorities in the investigation. “CAPTURED: HARPREET SINGH, part of an alleged foreign terrorist gang illegally in the United States, who we believe was involved in planning multiple attacks on police stations both in India and the United States,” Patel posted on X. He added, “The FBI will continue finding those who perpetrate violence—no matter where they are.”\nSingh, linked to two international terrorist groups, entered the U.S. illegally and used burner phones to avoid capture. He was arrested on April 18 by the FBI and Enforcement and Removal Operations in Sacramento.\nThe Punjab Director General of Police, Gaurav Yadav, praised the arrest of Singh, also known as Happy Passia, as a “major milestone” in the fight against ISI-backed terror networks. Yadav, in a post on X, emphasized that Singh, a key operative of Babbar Khalsa International (BKI), was responsible for orchestrating targeted killings, grenade attacks on police stations, and extortion.\nShare With:","content_cn":"0条评论\n\n2025年4月22日\n\nFBI局长卡什·帕特尔称赞逮捕哈普里特·辛格\n\n加利福尼亚州萨克拉门托（ANI）——FBI局长卡什·帕特尔4月21日宣布，在逮捕参与旁遮普邦袭击事件的恐怖分子哈普里特·辛格后，“正义将得到伸张”。\n\n帕特尔赞扬FBI萨克拉门托团队在调查中与印度当局的合作。“已抓获：哈普里特·辛格，一名属于涉嫌在美国非法滞留的外国恐怖主义团伙成员。我们认为，他参与策划了针对印度和美国警察局的多起袭击，”帕特尔在X上发文称。他补充道：“FBI将继续追查实施暴力行为的人——无论他们身在何处。”\n\n辛格与两个国际恐怖组织有关联，他非法进入美国，并使用一次性手机躲避抓捕。他于4月18日在萨克拉门托被FBI和执法与遣返行动部门逮捕。\n\n旁遮普邦警察总长高拉夫·亚达夫称赞逮捕辛格——又名“哈皮·帕西亚”——是打击由ISI支持的恐怖网络的“重要里程碑”。亚达夫在X上发文强调，作为巴巴尔·卡尔萨国际组织（BKI）的关键行动人员，辛格负责策划定点杀人、针对警察局的手榴弹袭击和敲诈勒索。\n\n分享至：","publish_source":"indiawest.com","publish_time":"2025-04-22T17:50:27+00:00"}},{"id":"news-121","ktid":1056587,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1056587","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"苹果内存供应商SK海力士探讨与英特尔在美合作生产，AI需求推动","title_en":"Apple memory supplier explores U.S. manufacturing with Intel as AI demand grows","summary_cn":"据路透社报道并经MacRumors转述，苹果内存供应商SK海力士正与英特尔探讨在美国制造的可能方案：一是租用英特尔计划中的俄亥俄州制造园区部分设施，二是与英特尔及大型云服务商组建合资企业。报道强调相关讨论尚未达成协议，也未作出决定，其他安排仍有可能。此举背景是云企业大举投资AI基础设施，推高高带宽内存需求，挤压其他内存产品产能，或间接影响智能手机和电脑的供应与成本。英特尔俄亥俄厂址为讨论增添了美国制造角度，但任何设施安排仍需投资、设备、认证和客户承诺。","summary_en":"According to Reuters reporting summarized by MacRumors, Apple memory supplier SK Hynix is exploring U.S. manufacturing options with Intel: one possibility would lease part of Intel's planned Ohio complex, another would involve a joint venture with Intel and large cloud providers. The report stresses no agreement or decision has been made and other arrangements remain possible. The talks come as cloud companies spend heavily on AI infrastructure, boosting demand for high-bandwidth memory and pressuring other memory products, potentially tightening supply or raising component costs for smartphones and computers. Intel's planned Ohio site adds a U.S. manufacturing angle, but any facility arrangement would still require investment, equipment, qualification work and customer commitments.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:26:12.689625+00:00","url":"https://inews.zoombangla.com/apple-memory-supplier-explores-us-manufacturing-with-intel-as-ai-demand-grows/","content":"<p>Apple memory supplier SK Hynix is exploring U.S. manufacturing options with Intel, according to Reuters reporting summarized by MacRumors. One possibility would lease part of Intel’s planned Ohio manufacturing complex, while another would involve a joint venture with Intel and large cloud providers.</p><p>The discussions are not a completed agreement. The report says no decision has been made and that other arrangements remain possible. That distinction matters because a discussion about capacity is not the same as a confirmed factory plan or a production schedule.</p><p>SK Hynix supplies memory to Apple alongside Samsung and Micron. The conversations come as cloud companies spend heavily on AI infrastructure, increasing demand for high-bandwidth memory used with AI processors and placing pressure on other memory products.</p><p>The consumer impact is indirect. If memory makers direct more capacity toward higher-margin AI products, smartphone and computer manufacturers may face tighter supply or higher component costs. The report does not say that any particular Apple product will be delayed by the talks.</p><p>Intel’s planned Ohio site gives the discussion a U.S. manufacturing angle. A facility arrangement would still require investment, equipment, qualification work and customer commitments before it could change the supply of finished memory chips.</p><p>The report also shows why memory supply has become a technology-business story rather than a narrow component issue. AI servers, cloud contracts, smartphones and personal computers now compete for manufacturing capacity in the same broad industry.</p><p>MacRumors cited Reuters for the exploratory talks and identified Apple’s relationship with SK Hynix. This article reports the status as discussions, not as a signed partnership or a guarantee of domestic memory production.</p><p>The immediate news is the possible U.S. manufacturing path and the supply pressure behind it. Any effect on Apple devices, Intel’s factory or cloud customers will depend on the negotiations and the investment decisions that follow.</p><p>Neither SK Hynix nor Intel has announced a final structure, so the report remains an early supply-chain discussion.</p>fXinmwalink@tg\nAI Infrastructure Intel Memory chips semiconductor supply SK Hynix","content_cn":"<p>据 MacRumors 对路透社报道的总结，苹果内存供应商 SK Hynix 正在与英特尔探索美国制造方案。一种可能性是租赁英特尔计划建设的俄亥俄州制造园区的一部分；另一种则涉及 SK Hynix 与英特尔及大型云服务商成立合资企业。</p><p>这些讨论尚未达成协议。报道称尚未作出决定，其他安排仍有可能。这一区别很重要，因为有关产能的讨论并不等同于已经确认的工厂计划或生产时间表。</p><p>SK Hynix 与三星和美光一起向苹果供应内存。此次对话发生之际，云服务公司正大举投资 AI 基础设施，推动了用于 AI 处理器的高带宽内存需求，并对其他内存产品造成压力。</p><p>对消费者的影响是间接的。如果内存制造商将更多产能投向利润率更高的 AI 产品，智能手机和电脑制造商可能面临更紧张的供应或更高的组件成本。报道并未称任何特定苹果产品会因这些谈判而延迟。</p><p>英特尔计划中的俄亥俄州厂址为此次讨论增添了美国制造的维度。任何设施安排仍需投资、设备、认证工作和客户承诺，之后才可能改变成品内存芯片的供应。</p><p>该报道还显示，内存供应为何已成为一项科技商业议题，而不再是狭义的组件问题。AI 服务器、云服务合同、智能手机和个人电脑如今都在同一广泛行业中竞争制造产能。</p><p>MacRumors 援引路透社报道这些探索性谈判，并指出苹果与 SK Hynix 的关系。本文将其状态描述为讨论，而非已签署的合作关系或国内内存生产的保证。</p><p>即时新闻是潜在的美国制造路径及其背后的供应压力。对苹果设备、英特尔工厂或云服务客户的任何影响，都将取决于后续谈判和投资决定。</p><p>SK Hynix 与英特尔均未公布最终架构，因此该报道仍是一场早期的供应链讨论。</p>fXinmwalink@tg\nAI 基础设施 英特尔 内存芯片 半导体供应 SK Hynix","publish_source":"inews.zoombangla.com","publish_time":"2026-09-18T08:15:31+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2379","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"美国国土安全部2025年终止叙利亚临时保护地位","title_en":"DHS Ends TPS for Syria in 2025","summary_cn":"美国国土安全部（DHS）于2025年9月19日宣布终止对叙利亚国民的临时保护地位（TPS），称叙利亚状况已不再需要继续保护。DHS助理部长表示TPS本应是临时性的。受影响的叙利亚人须在60天内自愿离境，否则将面临逮捕和驱逐，并永久禁止返美。DHS提供免费机票和1000美元奖励鼓励自行遣返。此举在移民和人道主义领域引发广泛争议，可能面临法律挑战。","summary_en":"The U.S. Department of Homeland Security (DHS) announced on September 19, 2025, that it is terminating Temporary Protected Status (TPS) for Syrian nationals, saying conditions in Syria no longer justify continued protection. A DHS assistant secretary said TPS is meant to be temporary. Affected Syrians must depart voluntarily within 60 days or face arrest, deportation and a permanent ban on returning. DHS offers a free plane ticket and a $1,000 bonus for self-deportation. The decision has sparked debate in immigration and humanitarian circles and may face legal challenges.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:43:16.372333+00:00","url":"https://inmigracionyvisas.com/a6420-tps-syria-termination-2025.html","content":"DHS Terminates Temporary Protected Status for Syrian Nationals\nDHS Terminates TPS for Syrian\nThe Department of Homeland Security (DHS) has announced a major policy shift that will affect thousands of Syrian nationals currently residing in the United States. On September 19, 2025, DHS Secretary Kristi Noem officially ended the Temporary Protected Status (TPS) designation for Syria, stating that conditions in the country no longer justify continued protection.\nThis decision has generated significant debate in immigration and humanitarian circles, as it impacts Syrians who fled conflict, terrorism, and political instability.\nTabla de Contenido\nWhat you should know\nDHS Justification for Ending TPS for Syria\nDeadlines for Syrian Nationals Under TPS\nImpact on the Syrian Community in the U.S.\nWhat Happens Next?\nFrequently Asked Questions (FAQs)\nSummary\nWhat you should know\nThe U.S. Department of Homeland Security (DHS) has officially terminated Temporary Protected Status (TPS) for Syria, a decision that impacts thousands of Syrian nationals currently residing in the United States. Syrians under TPS now have 60 days to leave voluntarily or face deportation, with DHS offering incentives such as a free plane ticket and a $1,000 bonus for those who self-deport. This announcement marks a significant turning point in U.S. immigration policy, raising urgent questions about the future of affected families and the humanitarian implications of sending people back to a country still facing instability. ↑\nDHS Justification for Ending TPS for Syria\nAccording to DHS Assistant Secretary Tricia McLaughlin, the decision is intended to restore \"sanity\" to America’s immigration system. McLaughlin emphasized:\n“Conditions in Syria no longer prevent their nationals from returning home. Syria has been a hotbed of terrorism and extremism for nearly two decades, and it is contrary to our national interest to allow Syrians to remain in our country. TPS is meant to be temporary.”\nWith this statement, DHS is reinforcing that TPS protections are not permanent and must reflect changing conditions in the designated country. ↑\nDeadlines for Syrian Nationals Under TPS\nSyrian TPS holders will now face strict timelines to comply with the new policy:\n60 Days to Depart Voluntarily: Syrian nationals must leave the United States within 60 days.\nSelf-Deportation Incentives: DHS has encouraged departures through the CBP Home app, which allows individuals to report their exit securely. Benefits include:\nA complimentary plane ticket\nA $1,000 exit bonus\nConsideration for future legal immigration opportunities\nAfter 60 Days: Those who remain without initiating voluntary removal will face arrest and deportation. Anyone forcibly removed will be permanently barred from returning to the U.S. ↑\nImpact on the Syrian Community in the U.S.\nThe cancellation of TPS for Syria places thousands of families in a precarious situation. Many Syrian nationals have lived, worked, and raised children in the U.S. for years. Immigration advocates argue that returning to Syria is unsafe due to ongoing instability, while DHS maintains that conditions have improved enough to end protections.\nThis conflict of perspectives will likely lead to legal challenges, community protests, and calls for congressional action. ↑\nWhat Happens Next?\nThe DHS announcement signals a tougher stance on temporary immigration programs. Syrian nationals under TPS now have limited options:\n1. Depart voluntarily using DHS procedures.\n2. Seek other forms of legal immigration relief (such as asylum, work visas, or family petitions).\n3. Face deportation if they remain after the 60-day grace period.\nImmigration attorneys strongly recommend that affected individuals consult with a licensed immigration lawyer immediately to understand their rights and explore legal alternatives. ↑\nFrequently Asked Questions (FAQs)\n❓ What is Temporary Protected Status (TPS)?\nTPS is a humanitarian program that allows nationals of certain countries to remain in the U.S. if their homeland is experiencing armed conflict, natural disaster, or extraordinary conditions.\n❓ When does TPS for Syria officially end?\nSyrian TPS holders have 60 days from the DHS announcement on September 19, 2025, to depart the United States.\n❓ What happens if Syrians do not leave within 60 days?\nFailure to depart voluntarily will result in arrest, deportation, and a permanent ban from returning to the United States.\n❓ What is the CBP Home app?\nThe CBP Home app is a DHS tool that allows foreign nationals to securely report their voluntary departure. Incentives include a free flight, $1,000 cash bonus, and possible eligibility for future visas. ↑\nSummary\nThe DHS decision to end TPS for Syria marks a turning point in U.S. immigration policy. While the government frames it as a return to normalcy, many Syrians face uncertain futures. With just 60 days to act, legal guidance and prompt decisions will be crucial for those affected. ↑\nConsulta un Experto\nBaja el App!Recibe la Revista Digital\nOtros artículos importantes visitados por nuestros lectores:\nTribunal permite a Trump avanzar con la revocación del TPS para Honduras, Nicaragua y Nepal\nEl 20 de agosto de 2025, el Noveno Circuito permitió a la administración Trump revocar el Estatus de Protección Temporal (TPS) para Honduras, Nicaragua y Nepal...\nUS cancels Temporary Protected Status (TPS) for Nepal and Cameroon\nDHS Terminates Temporary Protected Status for Nepal and Cameroon The U.S. Department of Homeland Security (DHS) ...","content_cn":"DHS终止叙利亚国民的临时保护身份\nDHS终止叙利亚TPS\n国土安全部（DHS）宣布了一项重大政策转变，将影响目前居住在美国的数千名叙利亚国民。2025年9月19日，DHS部长克里斯蒂·诺姆正式终止了叙利亚的临时保护身份（TPS）指定，称该国的状况已不再证明继续提供保护是合理的。\n这一决定在移民和人道主义领域引发了重大争议，因为它影响到逃离冲突、恐怖主义和政治不稳定的叙利亚人。\n目录\n您应了解的内容\nDHS终止叙利亚TPS的理由\nTPS下叙利亚国民的期限\n对美国叙利亚社区的影响\n接下来会发生什么？\n常见问题（FAQs）\n摘要\n您应了解的内容\n美国国土安全部（DHS）已正式终止叙利亚的临时保护身份（TPS），这一决定影响到目前居住在美国的数千名叙利亚国民。持有TPS的叙利亚人现在有60天时间自愿离境，否则将面临遣返；DHS为自行离境者提供免费机票和1,000美元奖金等奖励。这一公告标志着美国移民政策的重大转折点，并对受影响家庭的未来以及将人们送回仍面临不稳定局势的国家所带来的人道主义影响提出了紧迫问题。↑\nDHS终止叙利亚TPS的理由\n据DHS助理部长特里西亚·麦克劳克林称，该决定旨在恢复美国移民制度的“理智”。麦克劳克林强调：\n“叙利亚的状况已不再阻止其国民返乡。近二十年来，叙利亚一直是恐怖主义和极端主义的温床，允许叙利亚人留在我国不符合我们的国家利益。TPS本应是临时性的。”\n通过这一声明，DHS强调TPS保护并非永久性，且必须反映被指定国家不断变化的状况。↑\nTPS下叙利亚国民的期限\n叙利亚TPS持有人现在将面临严格的期限，以遵守新政策：\n60天内自愿离境：叙利亚国民必须在60天内离开美国。\n自行遣返奖励：DHS通过CBP Home应用程序鼓励离境，该应用程序允许个人安全地申报离境。福利包括：\n一张免费机票\n1,000美元离境奖金\n对未来合法移民机会的考量\n60天后：未启动自愿离境程序而继续逗留者将面临逮捕和遣返。任何被强制遣返者将被永久禁止返回美国。↑\n对美国叙利亚社区的影响\n取消叙利亚TPS使数千个家庭陷入岌岌可危的处境。许多叙利亚国民已在美国生活、工作并抚养子女多年。移民倡导者认为，由于持续的不稳定局势，返回叙利亚并不安全；而DHS则坚持认为，状况已改善到足以终止保护。\n这种观点冲突很可能会导致法律挑战、社区抗议以及要求国会采取行动的呼声。↑\n接下来会发生什么？\nDHS的公告表明其对临时移民项目采取了更强硬的立场。持有TPS的叙利亚国民现在选择有限：\n1. 使用DHS程序自愿离境。\n2.\n寻求其他形式的合法移民救济（例如庇护、工作签证或家庭申请）。\n3. 如果他们在60天宽限期后仍然逗留，将面临被驱逐出境。\n移民律师强烈建议受影响人士立即咨询持牌移民律师，以了解其权利并探索合法替代方案。 ↑\n常见问题（FAQs）\n❓ 什么是临时保护身份（TPS）？\nTPS是一项人道主义项目，允许某些国家的国民在其祖国正经历武装冲突、自然灾害或特殊情况时留在美国。\n❓ 叙利亚TPS何时正式结束？\n叙利亚TPS持有人自国土安全部于2025年9月19日发布公告之日起有60天时间离开美国。\n❓ 如果叙利亚人未在60天内离开，会发生什么？\n未能自愿离境将导致被逮捕、驱逐出境，并被永久禁止返回美国。\n❓ 什么是CBP Home应用程序？\nCBP Home应用程序是国土安全部的一项工具，允许外国国民安全报告其自愿离境。激励措施包括免费机票、1,000美元现金奖金，以及未来可能有资格获得签证。 ↑\n总结\n国土安全部终止叙利亚TPS的决定标志着美国移民政策的一个转折点。虽然政府将其描述为回归常态，但许多叙利亚人面临着不确定的未来。仅有60天时间采取行动，法律指导和迅速作出决定对受影响人士至关重要。 ↑\n咨询专家\n下载应用程序！获取数字杂志\n我们的读者访问过的其他重要文章：\n法院允许特朗普推进撤销洪都拉斯、尼加拉瓜和尼泊尔TPS\n2025年8月20日，第九巡回法院允许特朗普政府撤销洪都拉斯、尼加拉瓜和尼泊尔的临时保护身份（TPS）……\n美国取消尼泊尔和喀麦隆的临时保护身份（TPS）\n国土安全部终止尼泊尔和喀麦隆的临时保护身份 美国国土安全部（DHS）……","publish_source":"inmigracionyvisas.com","publish_time":"2025-09-20T08:19:00+01:00"}},{"id":"news-240","ktid":1000490,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000490","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"CSIS：伊朗皮克山设施建设活动激增","title_en":"Iran's Pickaxe Mountain sees surge in construction: CSIS","summary_cn":"印媒Inshorts援引战略与国际研究中心（CSIS）分析的卫星图像报道，2026年伊朗纳坦兹附近皮克山设施建设活动明显增加。分析人士称，该地下设施可能被用作核安全庇护所，目前正从开挖阶段转向内部加固。报道还提到特朗普总统发出打击威胁，美军在White Sands测试深层穿透能力。","summary_en":"Inshorts, citing satellite imagery analysed by the Center for Strategic and International Studies (CSIS), reports a sharp rise in construction at Iran's Pickaxe Mountain facility near Natanz in 2026. Analysts say the underground site, likely intended as a nuclear safe haven, is shifting from excavation to internal reinforcement. The report also notes President Trump's strike threats and U.S. military deep-penetration tests at White Sands.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T13:26:58.080065+00:00","url":"https://inshorts.com/en/news/iran-s-pickaxe-mountain-sees-surge-in-construction--csis-1788970128068","content":"Iran's Pickaxe Mountain sees surge in construction: CSISshort by / 04:08 pm on Wednesday, 9 September, 2026Satellite imagery analysed by CSIS shows a sharp rise in construction at Iran's Pickaxe Mountain facility near Natanz in 2026. Analysts say the underground site, likely intended as a nuclear safe haven, is shifting from excavation to internal reinforcement. President Trump has threatened strikes, while the US military tests deep-penetration capabilities at White Sands.read more at Timesnownews","content_cn":"伊朗“镐山”建设激增：CSIS\n短讯 / 2026年9月9日星期三下午4:08\nCSIS分析的卫星图像显示，2026年伊朗纳坦兹附近的“镐山”设施建设大幅增加。分析人士称，这处地下地点可能意在作为核安全避难所，正从挖掘阶段转向内部加固。特朗普总统曾威胁发动打击，而美军正在白沙测试深层穿透能力。\n在Timesnownews阅读更多","publish_source":"inshorts.com","publish_time":"2026-09-09T16:08:48+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1217","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"CrowdStrike宣布将股票回购计划规模增加5亿美元","title_en":"CrowdStrike Announces $500 Million Increase to Share Repurchase Program","summary_cn":"CrowdStrike Holdings宣布，其董事会已批准在现有股票回购计划基础上追加最多5亿美元A类普通股回购授权，使该计划总授权规模达到15亿美元。公司此前已以每股364.57美元均价回购413,130股，合计约1.506亿美元。CFO表示，此举旨在把握AI带来的增长动能与当前估值之间的脱节，机会性地回馈股东。回购计划无固定到期日，不承诺回购具体数量。","summary_en":"CrowdStrike Holdings announced that its Board of Directors authorized the repurchase of up to an additional $500 million of its Class A common stock, bringing the total authorization under its existing share repurchase program to $1.5 billion. The company has already repurchased 413,130 shares at an average price of $364.57 per share, for an aggregate of $150.6 million. CFO Burt Podbere said the move aims to opportunistically return value to shareholders amid a disconnect between AI-driven momentum and current valuation. The program has no fixed expiration date.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:22:17.991700+00:00","url":"https://investingnews.com/crowdstrike-announces-500-million-increase-to-share-repurchase-program","content":"Investing News NetworkApril 06, 2026 CrowdStrike Holdings, Inc. (Nasdaq: CRWD) today announced that CrowdStrike's Board of Directors has authorized the repurchase of up to an additional $500 million of CrowdStrike's Class A common stock to its existing stock repurchase program, bringing the total authorization under the program to $1.5 billion. Under its existing share repurchase program, CrowdStrike has repurchased 413,130 shares of its outstanding Class A common stock at an average price of $364.57 per share, for an aggregate purchase price of $150.6 million. \"We repurchased $150.6 million of shares following our record Q4 FY26, as we see a growing disconnect between our improving momentum fueled by AI tailwinds and our current valuation,\" said Burt Podbere, CrowdStrike's CFO. \"We have increased our share repurchase authorization to $1.5 billion to opportunistically return value to shareholders as we progress toward our goal of reaching $20 billion in ending ARR by FY36.\" The share repurchase program does not have a fixed expiration date and does not obligate CrowdStrike to acquire any specific number of shares. Repurchases may be made from time to time using a variety of methods, including open market purchases, privately negotiated transactions, Rule 10b5-1 trading plans and other means. The timing, manner, price and amount of any repurchases will be determined by CrowdStrike in its discretion and will depend on a variety of factors, including legal requirements, price and economic and market conditions. CrowdStrike currently expects to use the share repurchase program opportunistically depending on the market price of the common stock and other factors, and there can be no assurance that any shares will be repurchased under the share repurchase program. Forward-Looking Statements This press release contains forward-looking statements that involve risks and uncertainties, including statements regarding CrowdStrike's future growth and future financial and operating performance, the share repurchase program and the factors that will impact the amount and timing of purchases, if any, thereunder. A number of factors could cause outcomes to differ materially from our statements, including the risks and uncertainties included in our filings with the Securities and Exchange Commission, particularly under the caption \"Risk Factors\" and \"Management's Discussion and Analysis of Financial Condition and Results of Operations\" in our most recently filed Annual Report on Form 10-K. Accordingly, you should not place undue reliance on these forward-looking statements. All forward-looking statements are based on information currently available to us, and we do not assume any obligation to update any statement to reflect changes in circumstances or our expectations. About CrowdStrike Holdings CrowdStrike (NASDAQ: CRWD), a global cybersecurity leader, has redefined modern security with the world's most advanced cloud-native platform for protecting critical areas of enterprise risk – endpoints and cloud workloads, identity and data. Powered by the CrowdStrike Security Cloud and world-class AI, the CrowdStrike Falcon® platform leverages real-time indicators of attack, threat intelligence, evolving adversary tradecraft and enriched telemetry from across the enterprise to deliver hyper-accurate detections, automated protection and remediation, elite threat hunting and prioritized observability of vulnerabilities. Purpose-built in the cloud with a single lightweight-agent architecture, the Falcon platform delivers rapid and scalable deployment, superior protection and performance, reduced complexity and immediate time-to-value. CrowdStrike: We stop breaches. For more information, please visit: ir.crowdstrike.com © 2026 CrowdStrike, Inc. All rights reserved. CrowdStrike and CrowdStrike Falcon are marks owned by CrowdStrike, Inc. and are registered in the United States and other countries. CrowdStrike owns other trademarks and service marks and may use the brands of third parties to identify their products and services. View source version on businesswire.com: https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20260406095554/en/ Investor Relations Contact CrowdStrike Holdings, Inc. Andrew Nowinski investors@crowdstrike.com 669-721-0742 News Provided by Business Wire via QuoteMediaCrowdStrike HoldingsCRWDnasdaq:crwdCRWD","content_cn":"Investing News Network2026年4月6日，CrowdStrike Holdings, Inc.（纳斯达克代码：CRWD）今天宣布，CrowdStrike董事会已批准在现有股票回购计划基础上额外回购最多5亿美元的CrowdStrike A类普通股，使该计划下的总授权额度达到15亿美元。在现有股票回购计划下，CrowdStrike已回购413,130股已发行A类普通股，每股平均价格为364.57美元，总购买价为1.506亿美元。“继创纪录的FY26第四季度之后，我们回购了1.506亿美元的股票，因为我们看到，由人工智能顺风推动的势头不断改善与当前估值之间的脱节日益扩大，”CrowdStrike首席财务官Burt Podbere表示。“我们已将股票回购授权额度提高至15亿美元，以便在朝着FY36年末年度经常性收入达到200亿美元的目标迈进过程中，抓住机会向股东回馈价值。”该股票回购计划没有固定的到期日，也不要求CrowdStrike收购任何特定数量的股票。回购可能不时通过多种方式进行，包括公开市场购买、私下协商交易、规则10b5-1交易计划及其他方式。任何回购的时间、方式、价格和金额将由CrowdStrike自行决定，并将取决于多种因素，包括法律要求、价格以及经济和市场状况。CrowdStrike目前预计将根据普通股市场价格及其他因素，择机使用股票回购计划，但无法保证会根据该股票回购计划回购任何股票。前瞻性声明本新闻稿包含涉及风险和不确定性的前瞻性声明，包括有关CrowdStrike未来增长及未来财务和经营业绩、股票回购计划以及将影响回购金额和时间（如有）的因素的声明。许多因素可能导致实际结果与我们的声明存在重大差异，包括我们向美国证券交易委员会提交的文件中所列的风险和不确定性，特别是我们最近提交的10-K表格年度报告中“风险因素”和“管理层对财务状况和经营业绩的讨论与分析”部分所述的风险和不确定性。因此，您不应过度依赖这些前瞻性声明。所有前瞻性声明均基于我们目前掌握的信息，我们不承担更新任何声明以反映情况或预期变化的义务。关于CrowdStrike HoldingsCrowdStrike（纳斯达克代码：CRWD）是全球网络安全领导者，凭借全球最先进的云原生平台，重新定义了现代安全，用于保护企业风险的关键领域——终端和云工作负载、身份及数据。CrowdStrike Falcon®平台由CrowdStrike Security Cloud和世界一流的人工智能驱动，利用实时攻击指标、威胁情报、不断演变的对手技战术以及来自整个企业的丰富遥测数据，提供极其准确的检测、自动化防护与修复、顶级威胁搜寻以及按优先级排列的漏洞可观测性。该平台专为云而建，采用单一\n凭借轻量级代理架构，Falcon 平台实现快速且可扩展的部署、卓越的防护与性能、更低的复杂性以及即时价值实现。CrowdStrike：我们阻止入侵。如需更多信息，请访问：ir.crowdstrike.com © 2026 CrowdStrike, Inc. 保留所有权利。CrowdStrike 和 CrowdStrike Falcon 是 CrowdStrike, Inc. 拥有的商标，并已在美国及其他国家注册。CrowdStrike 还拥有其他商标和服务标志，并可能使用第三方品牌来标识其产品和服务。在 businesswire.com 查看源版本：https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20260406095554/en/ 投资者关系联系人 CrowdStrike Holdings, Inc. Andrew Nowinski investors@crowdstrike.com 669-721-0742 新闻由 Business Wire 通过 QuoteMedia 提供 CrowdStrike HoldingsCRWD纳斯达克:crwdCRWD","publish_source":"investingnews.com","publish_time":"2026-04-06T10:30:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1666","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"CrowdStrike宣布第四季度及2026财年财务业绩电话会议日期","title_en":"CrowdStrike Announces Date of Fourth Quarter and Fiscal Year 2026 Financial Results Conference Call","summary_cn":"CrowdStrike Holdings宣布，将于2026年3月3日美国股市收盘后发布截至2026年1月31日的第四季度及2026财年财务业绩。公司将于当天太平洋时间下午2点（东部时间下午5点）召开电话会议讨论业绩。电话会议网络直播及财报新闻稿可通过公司投资者关系网站获取，音频回放将在该网站保留一年。","summary_en":"CrowdStrike Holdings announced it will release financial results for its fourth quarter and fiscal year 2026, ended January 31, 2026, after the U.S. market close on Tuesday, March 3, 2026. The company will host a conference call that day at 2:00 p.m. Pacific time (5:00 p.m. Eastern time) to discuss the results. A live webcast and the financial results press release will be accessible from CrowdStrike's investor relations website, with an audio replay available for one year.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:32:45.210913+00:00","url":"https://investingnews.com/crowdstrike-announces-date-of-fourth-quarter-and-fiscal-year-2026-financial-results-conference-call","content":"Investing News NetworkFebruary 03, 2026 CrowdStrike Holdings, Inc. (Nasdaq: CRWD), today announced that it will release financial results for its fourth quarter and fiscal year 2026 ended January 31, 2026 after the U.S. market close on Tuesday, March 3, 2026. CrowdStrike will host a conference call that day at 2:00 p.m. Pacific time (5:00 p.m. Eastern time) to discuss the results. To register for the live event please visit https://crowdstrike-fiscal-fourth-quarter-2026-results-conference-call.open-exchange.net/ A live webcast of the conference call and the financial results press release will be accessible from the CrowdStrike investor relations website at ir.crowdstrike.com . An audio webcast replay of the conference call will be available on the investor relations website for one year. About CrowdStrike Holdings CrowdStrike (Nasdaq: CRWD), a global cybersecurity leader, has redefined modern security with the world's most advanced cloud-native platform for protecting critical areas of enterprise risk endpoints and cloud workloads, identity, and data. Powered by the CrowdStrike Security Cloud and world-class AI, the CrowdStrike Falcon® platform leverages real-time indicators of attack, threat intelligence, evolving adversary tradecraft, and enriched telemetry from across the enterprise to deliver hyper-accurate detections, automated protection and remediation, elite threat hunting, and prioritized observability of vulnerabilities. Purpose-built in the cloud with a single lightweight-agent architecture, the Falcon platform delivers rapid and scalable deployment, superior protection and performance, reduced complexity, and immediate time-to-value. CrowdStrike: We stop breaches. For more information, please visit: ir.crowdstrike.com © 2026 CrowdStrike, Inc. All rights reserved. CrowdStrike and CrowdStrike Falcon are marks owned by CrowdStrike, Inc. and are registered in the United States and other countries. CrowdStrike owns other trademarks and service marks and may use the brands of third parties to identify their products and services. View source version on businesswire.com: https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20260203552979/en/ Investor Relations Contact CrowdStrike Holdings, Inc. Andrew Nowinski investors@crowdstrike.com 669-721-0742 News Provided by Business Wire via QuoteMediaCrowdStrike HoldingsCRWDnasdaq:crwdCRWD","content_cn":"投资新闻网络\n2026年2月3日\nCrowdStrike Holdings, Inc.（纳斯达克：CRWD）今日宣布，将于2026年3月3日（星期二）美国市场收盘后发布截至2026年1月31日的2026财年第四季度及全年财务业绩。CrowdStrike将于当天太平洋时间下午2:00（东部时间下午5:00）举行电话会议，讨论业绩。\n\n如需注册参加直播活动，请访问 https://crowdstrike-fiscal-fourth-quarter-2026-results-conference-call.open-exchange.net/\n\n电话会议的实时网络直播及财务业绩新闻稿将可通过CrowdStrike投资者关系网站 ir.crowdstrike.com 获取。电话会议的音频网络直播回放将在投资者关系网站保留一年。\n\n关于CrowdStrike Holdings\n\nCrowdStrike（纳斯达克：CRWD）是全球网络安全领导者，通过全球最先进的云原生平台，保护企业风险的关键领域——端点和云工作负载、身份及数据——重新定义了现代安全。由CrowdStrike Security Cloud和世界级人工智能驱动，CrowdStrike Falcon®平台利用实时攻击指标、威胁情报、不断演进的对手攻击手法，以及来自整个企业的丰富遥测数据，提供极高准确度的检测、自动化防护和修复、精英威胁搜寻以及按优先级排列的漏洞可观测性。\n\nFalcon平台专为云端打造，采用单一轻量级代理架构，可实现快速且可扩展的部署、卓越的防护与性能、降低复杂性，以及即时实现价值。\n\nCrowdStrike：我们阻止入侵。\n\n欲了解更多信息，请访问：ir.crowdstrike.com\n\n© 2026 CrowdStrike, Inc. 保留所有权利。CrowdStrike和CrowdStrike Falcon是CrowdStrike, Inc.拥有的商标，已在美国及其他国家注册。CrowdStrike拥有其他商标和服务标志，并可能使用第三方品牌来识别其产品和服务。\n\n在businesswire.com查看源版本：https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20260203552979/en/\n\n投资者关系联系人\nCrowdStrike Holdings, Inc.\nAndrew Nowinski\ninvestors@crowdstrike.com\n669-721-0742\n\n新闻由Business Wire通过QuoteMedia提供\nCrowdStrike Holdings\nCRWD\nnasdaq:crwd\nCRWD","publish_source":"investingnews.com","publish_time":"2026-02-03T11:30:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-281","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"CrowdStrike成立网络超级智能实验室，首次将前沿AI研究引入网络防御","title_en":"CrowdStrike Establishes Cyber Superintelligence Lab, Bringing Frontier AI Research to Cyber Defense for the First Time","summary_cn":"CrowdStrike宣布成立Cyber Superintelligence Lab，称其为首个专为网络防御与AI安全而建的前沿AI研究机构，由首席AI与自主系统官Bartley Richardson领导。实验室依托Falcon平台背后的数据、对手情报与高保真环境，整合AI研究人员、攻击性操作人员与事件响应人员。CEO George Kurtz表示，安全是AI规模化的前提，该实验室将数据优势与顶尖AI人才结合以增强防御方能力。","summary_en":"CrowdStrike announced its Cyber Superintelligence Lab, described as the first frontier AI research organization built for cyberdefense and AI safety, led by Dr. Bartley Richardson, chief AI and autonomous systems officer. The Lab unites AI researchers, offensive operators, and incident responders, drawing on the data, adversary intelligence, and high-fidelity environments behind the Falcon platform. CEO George Kurtz said security is how AI scales, and the Lab combines CrowdStrike's data advantage with top applied AI talent to strengthen defenders.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:03:44.189119+00:00","url":"https://investingnews.com/crowdstrike-establishes-cyber-superintelligence-lab-bringing-frontier-ai-research-to-cyber-defense-for-the-first-time","content":"Investing News NetworkSeptember 01, 2026 The talent, the data, and the environments to build AI for defense, solving the industry's defining problem: AI safety CrowdStrike (NASDAQ: CRWD) today announced its Cyber Superintelligence Lab the first frontier AI research organization built for cyberdefense and AI safety. The Lab unites the expertise of CrowdStrike's AI researchers, offensive operators, and incident responders into one mission-focused charter. Built on the data, the adversary intelligence, and the high-fidelity environments behind the CrowdStrike Falcon® platform , the Lab paves the way for the next-generation of defense technology built for the agentic era. Dr. Bartley Richardson, chief AI and autonomous systems officer, leads the Lab. CrowdStrike's Data Advantage Compounds The Lab's primary input is CrowdStrike's unmatched security data corpus. Every signal is mapped and labeled by front-line analysts, with verdicts attached, establishing cybersecurity's ontology. The Falcon sensor reports from endpoints, identity systems, cloud workloads, data stores, and Falcon Next-Gen SIEM into a single architecture, producing trillions of events every day. That footprint spans environments diverse enough to capture the edge cases that matter, which is where adversaries operate. Inside those signals sit 15 years of CrowdStrike threat intelligence and incident response: expert-verified accounts of what an attack was, how it worked, and what stopped it. Volume alone does not teach defense to be right. A confirmed outcome does, and CrowdStrike produces more of them, every day the platform runs. \"Security is how AI scales,\" said George Kurtz, CEO and founder of CrowdStrike. \"The Cyber Superintelligence Lab concentrates the PhDs, AI researchers, and the threat hunters who stop real attacks every day on the Falcon platform. That depth of applied AI talent belongs on the platform where breaches are stopped. The synthesis of our data moat and cybersecurity's very best AI talent advantages defenders like never before.\" \"The real test for AI in security is whether it can stop breaches,\" said Dr. Richardson. \"To accomplish this today, we need intelligence that operates at machine speed, continuously learning and improving. It is the standard the whole industry will need to move towards in the face of AI-empowered adversaries.\" About CrowdStrike CrowdStrike (NASDAQ: CRWD), a global cybersecurity leader, has redefined modern security with the world's most advanced cloud-native platform for protecting critical areas of enterprise risk – endpoints and cloud workloads, identity and data. Powered by the CrowdStrike Security Cloud and world-class AI, the CrowdStrike Falcon® platform leverages real-time indicators of attack, threat intelligence, evolving adversary tradecraft, and enriched telemetry from across the enterprise to deliver hyper-accurate detections, automated protection and remediation, elite threat hunting, and prioritized observability of vulnerabilities. Purpose-built in the cloud with a single lightweight-agent architecture, the Falcon platform delivers rapid and scalable deployment, superior protection and performance, reduced complexity, and immediate time-to-value. CrowdStrike: We stop breaches. Learn more: https://www.crowdstrike.com/ Follow us: Blog | X | LinkedIn | Instagram Start a free trial today: https://www.crowdstrike.com/trial © 2026 CrowdStrike, Inc. All rights reserved. CrowdStrike and CrowdStrike Falcon are marks owned by CrowdStrike, Inc. and are registered in the United States and other countries. CrowdStrike owns other trademarks and service marks and may use the brands of third parties to identify their products and services. View source version on businesswire.com: https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20260901071017/en/ Media Contact Jake Schuster CrowdStrike Corporate Communications press@crowdstrike.com News Provided by Business Wire via QuoteMediaCrowdStrike HoldingsCRWDnasdaq:crwdCRWD","content_cn":"投资新闻网络\n2026年9月1日\n构建国防人工智能所需的人才、数据和环境，解决该行业的核心问题：人工智能安全。CrowdStrike（纳斯达克：CRWD）今日宣布成立其网络超级智能实验室，这是首个专为网络防御和人工智能安全而建立的前沿人工智能研究机构。该实验室将CrowdStrike人工智能研究人员、进攻性行动人员和事件响应人员的专业知识 объедин合为一项以使命为导向的章程。\n该实验室建立在CrowdStrike Falcon®平台背后的数据、对手情报和高保真环境之上，为智能代理时代打造下一代防御技术铺平道路。首席人工智能与自主系统官巴特利·理查森博士领导该实验室。\n\nCrowdStrike的数据优势不断累积\n该实验室的主要输入是CrowdStrike无与伦比的安全数据集。每条信号都由一线分析师进行映射和标注，并附加判定结果，从而建立网络安全本体。Falcon传感器从终端、身份系统、云工作负载、数据存储以及Falcon下一代SIEM报告数据，并汇入单一架构，每天生成数万亿个事件。其覆盖范围足够多样，能够捕捉重要的边缘案例，而对手正是在这些地方开展行动。\n这些信号中包含CrowdStrike长达15年的威胁情报和事件响应记录：由专家验证的攻击经过，包括攻击是什么、如何运作以及是什么阻止了它。仅有数量并不能教会防御系统做出正确判断；经过确认的结果才能做到这一点，而CrowdStrike每天都会在平台运行时产生更多此类结果。\n\n“安全是人工智能实现规模化的方式，”CrowdStrike首席执行官兼创始人乔治·库尔茨表示。“网络超级智能实验室汇聚了博士、人工智能研究人员以及每天在Falcon平台上阻止真实攻击的威胁猎手。这种深厚的应用人工智能人才应当归属于那个能够阻止入侵的平台。我们的数据护城河与网络安全领域最优秀人工智能人才的融合，将以前所未有的方式赋能防御者。”\n\n“人工智能在安全领域的真正考验，是它能否阻止入侵，”理查森博士表示。“要在今天实现这一点，我们需要以机器速度运行、持续学习和改进的情报。这是整个行业在面对人工智能赋能的对手时需要努力达到的标准。”\n\n关于CrowdStrike\nCrowdStrike（纳斯达克：CRWD）是全球网络安全领导者，凭借全球最先进的云原生平台，重新定义了现代安全，用于保护企业风险的关键领域——终端、云工作负载、身份和数据。CrowdStrike Falcon®平台由CrowdStrike安全云和世界级人工智能提供支持，利用实时攻击指标、威胁情报、不断演变的对手战术以及来自整个企业的丰富遥测数据，提供高度准确的检测、自动化防护与修复、顶级威胁猎杀，以及对漏洞的优先级化可观测性。\nFalcon平台专为云环境构建，采用单一轻量级代理架构，可实现快速且可扩展的部署、卓越的防护与性能、更低的复杂性，以及即时的价值实现。\nCrowdStrike：我们阻止入侵。\n了解更多：https://www.crowdstrike.com/\n关注我们：博客 | X | LinkedIn | Instagram\n立即开始免费试用：https://www.crowdstrike.com/trial\n© 2026 CrowdStrike, Inc. 保留所有权利。CrowdStrike和CrowdStrike Falcon是CrowdStrike, Inc.拥有的商标，并已在美国及其他国家注册。CrowdStrike还拥有其他商标和服务标志，并可能使用第三方品牌来识别其产品和服务。\n在businesswire.com查看源版本：https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20260901071017/en/\n媒体联系人\n杰克·舒斯特\nCrowdStrike企业传播\npress@crowdstrike.com\n新闻由Business Wire通过QuoteMedia提供\nCrowdStrike Holdings\nCRWD\n纳斯达克：crwd\nCRWD","publish_source":"investingnews.com","publish_time":"2026-09-01T14:36:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-312","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"CrowdStrike将网络直播投资者简报会","title_en":"CrowdStrike to Webcast Investor Briefing","summary_cn":"CrowdStrike Holdings, Inc.（NASDAQ: CRWD）宣布将于2026年9月2日在Fal.Con 2026大会期间举办投资者简报会，地点为拉斯维加斯，演讲时间为太平洋夏令时上午11:30。活动名额有限，需提前注册，有意出席的分析师和投资者可通过investors@crowdstrike.com联系投资者关系部门。简报会将在公司投资者关系网站ir.crowdstrike.com提供直播和回放。","summary_en":"CrowdStrike Holdings, Inc. (NASDAQ: CRWD) announced it will host an investor briefing on September 2, 2026, during its Fal.Con 2026 conference in Las Vegas, with the presentation at 11:30 a.m. PDT. Space is limited and pre-registration is required; analysts and investors interested in attending are encouraged to contact Investor Relations at investors@crowdstrike.com. A live webcast and replay will be accessible from the investor relations section of CrowdStrike's website at ir.crowdstrike.com.","tag":"other","founddate":"2026-09-25T10:40:41.177772+00:00","url":"https://investingnews.com/crowdstrike-to-webcast-investor-briefing","content":"Investing News NetworkAugust 26, 2026 CrowdStrike Holdings, Inc. (NASDAQ: CRWD) today announced that it will host a briefing for investors on September 2, 2026 during its Fal.Con 2026 conference. Event: CrowdStrike Investor Briefing Location: Las Vegas Date: Wednesday, September 2, 2026 Presentation time: 11:30 a.m. PDT Space for the event is limited and pre-registration is required. Analysts and investors interested in attending are encouraged to contact Investor Relations at investors@crowdstrike.com . A live webcast and replay of the briefing will be accessible from the investor relations section of CrowdStrike's website at ir.crowdstrike.com . About CrowdStrike Holdings CrowdStrike (NASDAQ: CRWD), a global cybersecurity leader, has redefined modern security with the world's most advanced cloud-native platform for protecting critical areas of enterprise risk – endpoints and cloud workloads, identity and data. Powered by the CrowdStrike Security Cloud and world-class AI, the CrowdStrike Falcon® platform leverages real-time indicators of attack, threat intelligence, evolving adversary tradecraft, and enriched telemetry from across the enterprise to deliver hyper-accurate detections, automated protection and remediation, elite threat hunting and prioritized observability of vulnerabilities. Purpose-built in the cloud with a single lightweight-agent architecture, the Falcon platform delivers rapid and scalable deployment, superior protection and performance, reduced complexity and immediate time-to-value. CrowdStrike: We stop breaches. For more information, please visit: ir.crowdstrike.com © 2026 CrowdStrike, Inc. All rights reserved. CrowdStrike and CrowdStrike Falcon are marks owned by CrowdStrike, Inc. and are registered in the United States and other countries. CrowdStrike owns other trademarks and service marks and may use the brands of third parties to identify their products and services. View source version on businesswire.com: https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20260826840128/en/ Investor Relations Contact CrowdStrike Holdings, Inc. Andrew Nowinski investors@crowdstrike.com News Provided by Business Wire via QuoteMediaCrowdStrike HoldingsCRWDnasdaq:crwdCRWD","content_cn":"投资新闻网\n2026年8月26日 CrowdStrike Holdings, Inc.（纳斯达克：CRWD）今日宣布，将于2026年9月2日在其Fal.Con 2026大会期间为投资者举办简报会。\n活动：CrowdStrike投资者简报会\n地点：拉斯维加斯\n日期：2026年9月2日，星期三\n演示时间：太平洋夏令时间上午11:30\n活动名额有限，必须提前注册。有意参加的分析师和投资者请联系投资者关系部门：investors@crowdstrike.com 。简报会的网络直播及回放将在CrowdStrike网站的投资者关系部分提供，网址为 ir.crowdstrike.com 。\n关于CrowdStrike Holdings\nCrowdStrike（纳斯达克：CRWD）是全球网络安全领导者，通过全球最先进的云原生平台保护企业风险的关键领域——终端、云工作负载、身份和数据，重新定义了现代安全。CrowdStrike Falcon®平台由CrowdStrike Security Cloud和世界级人工智能驱动，利用实时攻击指标、威胁情报、不断演变的对手技战术以及来自整个企业的丰富遥测数据，提供高度精准的检测、自动化防护与修复、顶尖的威胁搜寻，以及按优先级呈现的漏洞可观察性。Falcon平台基于云构建，采用单一轻量级代理架构，能够快速、规模化部署，提供卓越的防护和性能，降低复杂性并立即实现价值。\nCrowdStrike：我们阻止入侵。\n如需更多信息，请访问：ir.crowdstrike.com\n© 2026 CrowdStrike, Inc. 版权所有。CrowdStrike和CrowdStrike Falcon是CrowdStrike, Inc.拥有的商标，并已在美国及其他国家注册。CrowdStrike拥有其他商标和服务标志，也可能使用第三方品牌来标识其产品和服务。\n请在 businesswire.com 查看源版本：https://www.businesswire.com/news/home/20260826840128/en/\n投资者关系联系人\nCrowdStrike Holdings, Inc.\nAndrew Nowinski\ninvestors@crowdstrike.com\n新闻由Business Wire通过QuoteMedia提供\nCrowdStrike Holdings\nCRWD\n纳斯达克：crwd\nCRWD","publish_source":"investingnews.com","publish_time":"2026-08-26T18:10:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-975","ktid":1056587,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1056587","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"回归“宿敌”：英特尔会成为苹果处理器的下一个代工厂吗？","title_en":"Return to the \"Arch-Nemesis\": Will Intel Become the Next Manufacturer of Apple Processors? | Phonegram","summary_cn":"据《华尔街日报》报道，苹果与英特尔已达成初步协议，英特尔将为苹果代工其设计的处理器，角色类似台积电。报道称苹果可能先从较简单的M系列芯片入手，逐步推进。文章分析苹果回归英特尔的原因包括：英特尔在陈立武领导下重振代工业务，押注14A（1.4纳米）和18A（1.8纳米）制程；苹果希望分散对台积电的单一依赖，降低地缘政治风险，并缓解A19芯片产能受限问题。","summary_en":"According to a Wall Street Journal report, Apple and Intel have reached a preliminary agreement under which Intel will manufacture processors designed by Apple, playing a role similar to TSMC. Leaks suggest Apple may start with less complex chips such as basic M-series processors before moving to flagship ones. The article attributes Apple's return to Intel to several factors: Intel's efforts under new CEO Lip-Bu Tan to revive its foundry business, betting on 14A (1.4nm) and 18A (1.8nm) process technologies; Apple's desire to diversify its exclusive reliance on TSMC amid geopolitical tensions around Taiwan; and constraints on A19 chip supply.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-24T16:25:08.284007+00:00","url":"https://iphoneislam.com/language/en/2026/05/return-to-the-arch-nemesis-will-intel-become-the-next-manufacturer-for-apple-processors/166337","content":"Return to the “Arch-Nemesis”: Will Intel Become the Next Manufacturer of Apple Processors?\nNews\nذكي AI\n5 months ago\n0 Comments\nWho would have imagined that the tables would turn and Apple would return to Intel’s embrace once again? After years of the famous technical “divorce” in which Apple announced its independence with its own processors (Apple Silicon), moving away from Intel’s problems and delays, it seems that the winds of interest have begun to blow in a completely different direction. Recent reports indicate that Apple and Intel have signed a preliminary agreement that paves the way for Intel’s return as a key player in Apple devices, but this time not as a processor designer, but as a manufacturer.\nA Preliminary Agreement for a New Marriage of Convenience\nAccording to a report published by The Wall Street Journal, Apple and Intel have reached a preliminary agreement under which Intel will manufacture processors designed by Apple. The idea here is that Intel will play a role similar to the one currently performed by the Taiwanese company TSMC; it will take the brilliant designs of Apple’s engineers and turn them into actual silicon chips inside its advanced factories.\nLeaks suggest that Apple may start with less complex chips at first, such as the basic M-series processors used in iPads and some low-cost Mac models. This gradual approach is very logical, as Apple does not want to risk its flagship processors (such as Pro and Max) before ensuring the quality and efficiency of Intel’s new production lines.\nWhy is Apple returning to Intel now?\nHistorically, Apple abandoned Intel because the latter suffered from constant delays in improving manufacturing precision, which hindered Apple’s plans to update its devices. But the scene has now changed with Lip-Bu Tan taking over as head of Intel, succeeding Pat Gelsinger; Tan is leading massive efforts to revive Intel’s manufacturing sector and attract major clients the size of Apple.\nIntel is currently betting on 1.4nm manufacturing technology (known as 14A), which is supposed to begin production in 2028, in addition to 18A technology (1.8nm). These technologies are what Apple needs to stay at the forefront of the performance race, and it seems that Intel has finally begun to catch up with the pack that TSMC and Samsung have led for years.\nThe TSMC Crisis and the Search for an Alternative\nThe most important reason for this collaboration is Apple’s urgent desire to diversify its supply chains. Currently, Apple relies entirely and exclusively on TSMC to manufacture every “Apple Silicon” chip in the world. This total reliance represents a major risk, especially with the geopolitical tensions surrounding Taiwan.\nFurthermore, Tim Cook noted in the latest earnings call that iPhone 17 models faced some availability constraints due to TSMC’s inability to provide sufficient quantities of A19 and A19 Pro chips. With the AI craze, major companies like Nvidia have been devouring a large share of TSMC’s production capacity, which has weakened Apple’s influence and its ability to push for absolute priority.\nSecuring the Future of Silicon\nEntering Intel as a second manufacturing option will give Apple tremendous flexibility and make it less affected by any production pressures in Taiwan. It is Apple’s usual strategy: do not put all your eggs in one basket, even if that basket is currently the best in the world. As for Intel, having Apple as a client for its foundry business is the greatest testament to success it could receive on its journey back to the top.\nDo you accept the idea that your “next iPhone” could contain a processor manufactured in Intel’s factories?\nSource:\nmacrumors.com\nShare this:\nShare on Facebook (Opens in new window)\nFacebook\nShare on X (Opens in new window)\nX\nMore\nShare on WhatsApp (Opens in new window)\nWhatsApp\nShare on Telegram (Opens in new window)\nTelegram\nEmail a link to a friend (Opens in new window)\nEmail\nPrevious post\nDo you nod in agreement when hearing AI terms? It’s time we explained them to you\nNext post\nApple’s 2026 Roadmap: 18 New Products from the Foldable iPhone to Augmented Reality Glasses\nمقالات ذات صلة\nذكي AI\n0\n5 Tools and Features on the iPhone Lock Screen in iOS 27 You Should Try Immediately\n8 hours ago\nذكي AI\n0\niPhone 18 Pro Reviews: Superb performance and advanced photography capabilities, but is it worth the upgrade?\n23 hours ago\nذكي AI\n0\nThe iPhone camera gets smarter: Your guide to using Visual Intelligence and “Siri mode” in the iOS 27 update\n1 day ago\nLeave a ReplyCancel reply","content_cn":"重返“宿敌”：英特尔会成为下一家苹果处理器制造商吗？\n新闻\nذكي AI\n5个月前\n0条评论\n谁能想到局势会发生逆转，苹果竟会再次回到英特尔的怀抱？多年来，苹果宣布凭借自有处理器（Apple Silicon）实现独立，与英特尔的问题和延误渐行渐远，这场著名的技术“离婚”之后，利益的风向似乎开始朝着完全不同的方向转变。近期报道称，苹果和英特尔已签署初步协议，为英特尔重返苹果设备、成为关键参与者铺平道路，但这一次英特尔不再是处理器设计商，而是制造商。\n一段新便利婚姻的初步协议\n据《华尔街日报》报道，苹果和英特尔已达成一项初步协议，英特尔将制造由苹果设计的处理器。这里的设想是，英特尔将扮演类似于目前台湾公司台积电（TSMC）所扮演的角色；它将接过苹果工程师的出色设计，并在其先进工厂中将其转化为实际的硅芯片。\n有消息称，苹果起初可能会从复杂度较低的芯片开始，例如用于iPad和部分低价Mac机型的基础M系列处理器。这种循序渐进的方式非常合理，因为苹果不想在确认英特尔新生产线的质量和效率之前，就拿旗舰处理器（如Pro和Max）冒险。\n苹果为何现在重返英特尔？\n从历史上看，苹果放弃英特尔，是因为后者在提升制造精度方面不断延误，阻碍了苹果更新设备的计划。但如今局面已经改变，Lip-Bu Tan接任英特尔掌门人，取代Pat Gelsinger；Tan正领导大规模努力，试图振兴英特尔的制造业务，并吸引苹果这样规模的大客户。\n英特尔目前押注1.4纳米制造技术（称为14A），预计将于2028年开始生产，此外还有18A技术（1.8纳米）。这些技术正是苹果保持性能竞赛领先地位所需要的，而英特尔似乎终于开始追上台积电和三星多年来引领的队伍。\n台积电危机与寻找替代方案\n这次合作最重要的原因，是苹果迫切希望实现供应链多元化。目前，苹果完全且唯一依赖台积电制造全球每一枚“Apple Silicon”芯片。这种完全依赖构成了重大风险，尤其是在围绕台湾的地缘政治紧张局势下。\n此外，蒂姆·库克在最近一次财报电话会议中指出，由于台积电无法提供足够数量的A19和A19 Pro芯片，iPhone 17系列面临一定的供应限制。随着人工智能热潮席卷，英伟达等大型公司正在吞噬台积电生产能力的很大一部分，这削弱了苹果的影响力，也削弱了其争取绝对优先权的能力。\n确保硅芯片的未来\n将英特尔引入为第二制造选项，将赋予苹果巨大的灵活性，使其不易受到台湾任何生产压力的影响。这正是苹果一贯的策略：不要把所有鸡蛋放在一个篮子里，即使那个篮子目前是世界上最好的。至于英特尔，让苹果成为其晶圆代工业务的客户，是对其最大的证明\n它在重返巅峰的旅程中可能获得的成功。\n你是否接受这样一种可能：你的“下一部 iPhone”可能搭载在英特尔工厂生产的处理器？\n来源：\nmacrumors.com\n分享：\n分享到 Facebook（在新窗口中打开）\nFacebook\n分享到 X（在新窗口中打开）\nX\n更多\n分享到 WhatsApp（在新窗口中打开）\nWhatsApp\n分享到 Telegram（在新窗口中打开）\nTelegram\n通过电子邮件将链接发送给朋友（在新窗口中打开）\n电子邮件\n上一篇文章\n听到 AI 术语时，你会点头表示同意吗？是时候向你解释这些术语了\n下一篇文章\n苹果 2026 年路线图：从折叠屏 iPhone 到增强现实眼镜的 18 款新品\n相关文章\n智能 AI\n0\niOS 27 中 iPhone 锁定屏幕上的 5 个工具和功能，你应该立即尝试\n8 小时前\n智能 AI\n0\niPhone 18 Pro 评测：性能卓越、摄影能力先进，但值得升级吗？\n23 小时前\n智能 AI\n0\niPhone 相机变得更智能：iOS 27 更新中视觉智能和“ Siri 模式”使用指南\n1 天前\n发表评论取消回复","publish_source":"iphoneislam.com","publish_time":"2026-05-11T13:35:08+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1078","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"斯普林菲尔德FBI在丹维尔展开行动，称与移民无关","title_en":"Springfield FBI starts sweep in Danville, says it is not immigration-related - IPM Newsroom","summary_cn":"美国联邦调查局斯普林菲尔德办公室周三上午在伊利诺伊州丹维尔启动大规模行动，包括逮捕和搜查。代理公共事务专家Jake Griffin表示，该行动与移民无关，是打击暴力犯罪和毒品活动的协调行动一部分，由FBI及地方、州和联邦执法伙伴共同参与。此前联邦探员抵达香槟市曾引发移民执法担忧，FBI已澄清未进行移民执法。","summary_en":"The FBI's Springfield office launched a major operation Wednesday morning in Danville, Illinois, including arrests and searches. Acting Public Affairs Specialist Jake Griffin said it is not immigration-related but part of a coordinated effort against violent crime and drug activity with local, state, and federal partners. The arrival of federal agents in Champaign had fueled immigration crackdown fears, which the FBI clarified were unfounded.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:41:50.016815+00:00","url":"https://ipmnewsroom.org/springfield-fbi-starts-sweep-in-danville-says-it-is-not-immigration-related","content":"Springfield FBI starts sweep in Danville, says it is not immigration-related\nBy Emily Hays\nApril 29, 2026\nTiktok\nInstagram\nFacebook-f\nThe presence of federal agents in town has fueled fears of an immigration crackdown. The Springfield FBI office says it launched a major sweep Wednesday morning and that the sweep is not immigration-related.\nPhoto: Emily Hays/IPM News\nhttps://ipmnewsroom.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/FBISweep.mp3\nDANVILLE —The FBI is starting a major operation Wednesday morning in Danville.\nSpringfield FBI Acting Public Affairs Specialist Jake Griffin says it is not immigration related.\n“FBI Springfield Field Office as well as local, state, and federal law enforcement partners are conducting court authorized activity in the Danville, Illinois area, to include arrests and searches. This event is part of a coordinated effort to combat violent crime and drug activity,” Griffin said in a statement Wednesday morning.\nGriffin said the office would provide more details later in the week.\n“Due to the operation size and requirements, there will be no further comment at this time,” Griffin said.The arrival of federal agents in Champaign this weekend fueled fears of a major immigration crackdown. The Springfield FBI clarified Monday that there are agents in town, along with federal drug and law enforcement agencies, and that they are not doing immigration enforcement.\nTAGS: Champaign, Danville, FBI, immigration, Immigration and Customs Enforcement\nWILL and the Illinois Newsroom are committed to bringing you in-depth, relevant coverage that keeps you informed and engages you with our community and state. Join with thousands of others to keep this important public media-based resource available to all. Donate today >>\nEmily Hays\nEmily Hays started at WILL in October 2021 after three-plus years in local newsrooms in Virginia and Connecticut. She has won state awards for her housing coverage at Charlottesville Tomorrow and her education reporting at the New Haven Independent. Emily graduated from Yale University where she majored in History and South Asian Studies.","content_cn":"斯普林菲尔德FBI在丹维尔展开大规模行动，称与移民事务无关\n作者：Emily Hays\n2026年4月29日\nTiktok\nInstagram\nFacebook-f\n联邦特工在该镇出现，引发了人们对移民执法行动的担忧。斯普林菲尔德FBI办公室表示，其于周三上午启动了一项大规模行动，且该行动与移民事务无关。\n照片：Emily Hays/IPM News\nhttps://ipmnewsroom.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/04/FBISweep.mp3\n丹维尔——FBI于周三上午在丹维尔启动一项重大行动。\n斯普林菲尔德FBI代理公共事务专员Jake Griffin表示，该行动与移民事务无关。\n“FBI斯普林菲尔德外地办事处以及地方、州和联邦执法合作伙伴正在伊利诺伊州丹维尔地区开展经法院授权的活动，包括逮捕和搜查。此事件是打击暴力犯罪和毒品活动的协调行动的一部分，”Griffin在周三上午的一份声明中说。\nGriffin表示，该办公室将在本周晚些时候提供更多细节。\n“由于行动规模和要求，目前不会进一步置评，”Griffin说。联邦特工于本周末抵达香槟市，引发了人们对大规模移民执法行动的担忧。斯普林菲尔德FBI于周一澄清，特工以及联邦缉毒和执法机构均在该市，但并未开展移民执法。\n标签：香槟、丹维尔、FBI、移民、移民与海关执法局\nWILL和Illinois Newsroom致力于为您带来深入、相关的报道，让您及时了解信息，并与我们的社区和州保持互动。与数千名其他人一起，确保这一重要的公共媒体资源能够继续向所有人提供。立即捐款 >>\nEmily Hays\nEmily Hays于2021年10月加入WILL，此前曾在弗吉尼亚州和康涅狄格州的地方新闻编辑部工作三年多。她因在Charlottesville Tomorrow进行的住房报道和在New Haven Independent进行的教育报道获得州级奖项。Emily毕业于耶鲁大学，主修历史和南亚研究。","publish_source":"ipmnewsroom.org","publish_time":"2026-04-29T06:45:00-05:00"}},{"id":"news-3007","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"英迈拉美区荣获2025年CrowdStrike美洲增长分销商年度大奖","title_en":"Ingram Micro LATAM Wins 2025 CrowdStrike AMS Growth Distributor of the Year Award :: Ingram Micro Holding Corporation (INGM)","summary_cn":"英迈（Ingram Micro）宣布在CrowdStrike美洲合作伙伴峰会上被评为“美洲增长分销商年度大奖”。作为CrowdStrike在拉美地区分销商的第一年，英迈扩大了合作伙伴生态、提升了市场势头，并推出面向中小企业与MSP的项目及赋能培训。英迈高管表示该认可体现其运营能力与拉美市场认知，CrowdStrike方面则强调合作伙伴生态对其增长的重要性。","summary_en":"Ingram Micro announced it was named AMS Growth Distributor of the Year at CrowdStrike's Americas Partner Symposium. In its first year as a CrowdStrike distributor in LATAM, Ingram Micro expanded its partner ecosystem, increased market momentum, and launched programs for SMB and MSP sectors along with partner enablement training. An Ingram Micro executive said the recognition reflects its operational excellence and LATAM market knowledge, while CrowdStrike emphasized the importance of its partner ecosystem to growth.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-24T21:26:49.987976+00:00","url":"https://ir.ingrammicro.com/in-the-news/detail/23105/ingram-micro-latam-wins-2025-crowdstrike-ams-growth-distributor-of-the-year-award","content":"Ingram Micro LATAM Wins 2025 CrowdStrike AMS Growth Distributor of the Year Award\nApr 04, 2025\nIngram Micro is proud to share that we’ve been named the “AMS Growth Distributor of the Year” at CrowdStrike’s Americas Partner Symposium.\nIn our first year as a CrowdStrike distributor in LATAM, we’ve grown our partner ecosystem, increased market momentum and introduced impactful programs for the SMB and MSP sectors. We’ve also established enablement programs to train and empower our partners.\n“This recognition highlights our operational excellence, deep knowledge of the LATAM market and our strong partner network,” said Daniela Rosa, VP, CCE LATAM Export Division. “In our first year as a distributor for CrowdStrike, we’ve demonstrated that we have the right sales and presales teams in place to support its business.”\nCrowdStrike’s Americas Partner Symposium brings together industry-leading partners to unlock new opportunities, accelerate growth and help customers consolidate security investments on the Falcon platform. The awards program recognizes partners that deliver innovation and business outcomes with the Falcon platform, exceed revenue expectations and build successful customer relationships.\n\"We proudly congratulate all the winners of the 2025 Americas Partner Awards,\" said Amanda Adams, VP of Americas Alliances at CrowdStrike. \"As a partner-first company, our ecosystem is how we win and is in hypergrowth, fueled by the breadth and depth of the Falcon platform. This year we recognize ecosystem growth, innovation and partner-led services as we keep driving our shared mission forward—stopping breaches together with the Falcon platform.\"\nWe’re excited to continue building on this success and look forward to achieving more together with CrowdStrike.","content_cn":"Ingram Micro拉美荣获2025年度CrowdStrike AMS增长分销商奖\n2025年4月4日\nIngram Micro很自豪地宣布，我们在CrowdStrike美洲合作伙伴研讨会上被评为“年度AMS增长分销商”。\n作为CrowdStrike在拉丁美洲的首年分销商，我们扩大了合作伙伴生态系统，增强了市场势头，并为中小企业（SMB）和托管服务提供商（MSP）领域推出了富有影响力的计划。我们还建立了赋能计划，以培训和支持合作伙伴。\n“这一认可凸显了我们的卓越运营能力、对拉美市场的深刻了解以及强大的合作伙伴网络，”CCE拉美出口部门副总裁Daniela Rosa表示。“作为CrowdStrike的首年分销商，我们已经证明，我们配备了合适的销售和售前团队来支持其业务。”\nCrowdStrike美洲合作伙伴研讨会汇聚行业领先的合作伙伴，以发掘新机遇、加速增长，并帮助客户在Falcon平台上整合安全投资。该奖项计划表彰那些通过Falcon平台实现创新和业务成果、超出收入预期并建立成功客户关系的合作伙伴。\n“我们谨向2025年美洲合作伙伴奖的所有获奖者表示祝贺，”CrowdStrike美洲联盟副总裁Amanda Adams表示。“作为一家合作伙伴优先的公司，我们的生态系统是我们取胜的方式，并且正处于高速增长之中，这得益于Falcon平台的广度和深度。今年，我们表彰生态系统增长、创新和由合作伙伴主导的服务，同时继续推动我们的共同使命——借助Falcon平台共同阻止安全漏洞。”\n我们很高兴继续巩固这一成功，并期待与CrowdStrike携手取得更多成果。","publish_source":"ir.ingrammicro.com","publish_time":"2025-04-04T00:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3042","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"守护民主：CISA在保护选举中的角色","title_en":"Safeguarding Democracy: CISA’s Role in Protecting Elections - Issue One","summary_cn":"Issue One举办线上活动，讨论网络安全和基础设施安全局（CISA）在识别和缓解网络威胁、加强选举安全方面的作用。文章回顾2016年外国干预后，国会与特朗普首届政府推动将选举系统列为关键基础设施并成立CISA。文章称当前CISA被大幅缩减，关键网络安全项目资金被叫停，使选举面临风险。前官员与现任选举官员参与对话。","summary_en":"Issue One hosted a virtual event on CISA's role in identifying and mitigating cyber threats and enhancing election security. The article recalls that after 2016 foreign interference, Congress and Trump's first administration designated election systems as critical infrastructure and created CISA under DHS. It says CISA has since been dramatically downsized and funding for key cybersecurity initiatives halted, leaving elections vulnerable. Former and current election officials took part in the discussion.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:57:02.834324+00:00","url":"https://issueone.org/events/cisas-role-in-protecting-elections","content":"Mar 21, 2025\nSafeguarding Democracy: CISA’s Role in Protecting Elections\nVirtual Event\nWatch Recording\nShare\nTwitter\nFacebook\nLinkedin\nEmail\nFollowing unprecedented levels of foreign interference operations during the 2016 presidential election, members of Congress and President Trump’s first administration recognized the urgent need to bolster election security. That collective effort resulted in the Department of Homeland Security designating election systems as critical infrastructure, and President Trump signing into law and establishing the Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA).\nToday, and despite a history of broad bipartisan support since its inception, CISA has been dramatically downsized by the new Trump administration and funding for key cybersecurity initiatives, including the Elections Infrastructure Information Sharing and Analysis Center (EI-ISAC) and the Multi-State Information Sharing and Analysis Center (MS-ISAC), has been halted. This dismantling of CISA leaves our elections vulnerable and impairs a critical partnership between the federal government and state and local election officials that keeps our elections secure and safe.\nWe hosted an important discussion about the role that CISA plays in identifying and mitigating cyber threats and enhancing election security. “Safeguarding Democracy: CISA’s Role in Protecting Elections,” featured Kim Wyman, former Washington Secretary of State and CISA Senior Election Security Advisor, in conversation with current election officials Rob Rock, Rhode Island Deputy Secretary of State, Wesley Wilcox, Supervisor of Elections in Marion County, Florida, and Julie Wise, Director of Elections in King County, Washington.\nThe event was presented by Issue One and Issue One’s Faces of Democracy initiative.\nWatch the event recording.","content_cn":"2025年3月21日\n保护民主：CISA在保护选举中的作用\n线上活动\n观看录像\n分享\nTwitter\nFacebook\nLinkedIn\n电子邮件\n在2016年总统选举期间发生前所未有的大规模外国干预行动后，国会议员和特朗普总统的第一届政府认识到加强选举安全的迫切需要。这一共同努力促成国土安全部将选举系统指定为关键基础设施，并促成特朗普总统签署立法，设立网络安全与基础设施安全局（CISA）。\n如今，尽管CISA自成立以来一直得到广泛的两党支持，但新特朗普政府已大幅缩减CISA规模，并停止了包括选举基础设施信息共享与分析中心（EI-ISAC）和多州信息共享与分析中心（MS-ISAC）在内的关键网络安全倡议的资金。这种拆解CISA的做法使我们的选举处于脆弱状态，并损害了联邦政府与州及地方选举官员之间的关键伙伴关系，而正是这种伙伴关系保障我们的选举安全可靠。\n我们举办了一场重要讨论，探讨CISA在识别和缓解网络威胁、提升选举安全方面所发挥的作用。“保护民主：CISA在保护选举中的作用”邀请了前华盛顿州务卿兼CISA高级选举安全顾问Kim Wyman，并与现任选举官员进行对谈：罗德岛州副州务卿Rob Rock、佛罗里达州马里恩县选举监督官Wesley Wilcox，以及华盛顿州金县选举主任Julie Wise。\n本次活动由Issue One及其“民主面孔”倡议主办。\n观看活动录像。","publish_source":"issueone.org","publish_time":"2025-03-21T00:00:00"}},{"id":"news-2277","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"Westcon-Comstor与CrowdStrike在新加坡扩展Falcon平台","title_en":"Westcon-Comstor & CrowdStrike expand Falcon platform in Singapore","summary_cn":"Westcon-Comstor与CrowdStrike签署分销协议，将CrowdStrike Falcon平台引入新加坡合作伙伴与客户，扩展此前在印尼、马来西亚和泰国的合作。Westcon-Comstor将提供端点安全、云安全、身份安全和下一代SIEM等方案，并通过AWS Marketplace私有报价简化部署，同时提供技术赋能与数据洞察支持。","summary_en":"Westcon-Comstor and CrowdStrike have entered a distribution agreement to bring the CrowdStrike Falcon platform to partners and customers in Singapore, extending an existing collaboration in Indonesia, Malaysia and Thailand. Westcon-Comstor will offer Endpoint Security, Falcon Cloud Security, Falcon Next-Gen Identity Security and Falcon Next-Gen SIEM, with deployment streamlined via Channel Partner Private Offers and private listings on AWS Marketplace, plus technical enablement and data-driven insights.","tag":"technology","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:32:15.797680+00:00","url":"https://itbrief.asia/story/westcon-comstor-crowdstrike-expand-falcon-platform-in-singapore","content":"Cloud Security\nAdvanced Persistent Threat Protection\nPartner Programmes\nWestcon-Comstor & CrowdStrike expand Falcon platform in Singapore\nWed, 8th Oct 2025\nCATHERINE KNOWLES\nNews Editor\nWestcon-Comstor and CrowdStrike have entered into a distribution agreement to bring the CrowdStrike Falcon platform to partners and customers in Singapore.\nThe agreement marks an expansion of Westcon-Comstor's partnership with CrowdStrike, extending an existing collaboration already in place in Indonesia, Malaysia, and Thailand. The aim is to meet the growing demand in Singapore for cybersecurity consolidation and cloud-native security solutions, driven by increasingly sophisticated and AI-driven security threats.\nSingapore market opportunity\nWestcon-Comstor will offer its partner network access to the suite of CrowdStrike solutions, including Endpoint Security, Falcon Cloud Security, Falcon Next-Gen Identity Security, and Falcon Next-Gen SIEM. These products are designed to address modern cybersecurity challenges, particularly those posed by the rise in targeted attacks on critical infrastructure and organisations grappling with digital complexity.\nThe company intends to support a range of existing and new customers, from enterprise and corporate clients to small and medium businesses. To further streamline deployment, Westcon-Comstor will make the Falcon platform available via Channel Partner Private Offers and private listings on the AWS Marketplace, leveraging its status as an AWS Designated Seller of Record.\nWestcon-Comstor, a specialist distributor and technology provider, plans to deliver additional value-added services in conjunction with the Falcon platform. This includes technical enablement, upskilling support, and data-driven insights tailored to strengthen CrowdStrike's channel ecosystem in the region.\nLeadership comments\n\"Singapore's digitalisation drive has raised the bar for infrastructure and cybersecurity, putting pressure on businesses to modernise quickly. By providing a streamlined route with hands-on support, we aim to unlock significant new growth opportunities for both CrowdStrike and channel partners. Our role is crucial in helping businesses consolidate their security and stay secure without getting overwhelmed, driving adoption of CrowdStrike solutions while creating revenue opportunities for channel partners in the process,\" said Jacquie Young, Managing Director, Cloud, APAC, at Westcon-Comstor.\n\"Expanding our partnership with Westcon-Comstor to Singapore strengthens our channel reach and partner-first strategy in the region, while providing Westcon-Comstor's partners and customers with cybersecurity's platform of choice for the agentic era. Together, we will accelerate adoption of the AI-native Falcon platform, enabling our partners to drive vendor consolidation, reduce security complexity and costs, and stop breaches with a truly agentic security platform,\" said Girsih Gargeshwari, Senior Director, Distribution and Alliances, CrowdStrike Asia Pacific and Japan.\nRecognition and expansion\nWestcon-Comstor received the title of 2024 CrowdStrike Global Distributor Partner of the Year, an acknowledgement of its performance in promoting adoption of the Falcon platform across its network of over 12,000 channel partners in EMEA and APAC.\nThe expanded agreement between Westcon-Comstor and CrowdStrike in Singapore is expected to help organisations in the country respond to the increasing demands of digitalisation, and the need for consolidated, cloud-native cybersecurity solutions.\nExplore with AI\nChatGPT\nKey takeaways\nExplain why it matters\nCreate action plan\nFuture watch\nClaude\nKey takeaways\nExplain why it matters\nCreate action plan\nFuture watch\nPerplexity\nKey takeaways\nExplain why it matters\nCreate action plan\nFuture watch\nGrok\nKey takeaways\nExplain why it matters\nCreate action plan\nFuture watch\nShare\nShare\nAdd us as a preferred source on Google\nRelated stories\nOkta appoints Sunil Kedaraji as APJ Partner Vice President\nKobalt.io signs security partnerships across North America\nTrendAI tops USD $1 billion in AWS Marketplace sales\nSysdig launches Secure AI for cloud security teams\nProofpoint launches OEM programme for security vendors\nTop stories\nGoogle Cloud expands session controls with 16-hour default\nGoogle warns AI is reshaping cyber attacks & defences\nCohere launches North Small Translate in translation push\nCFOs focus on cash flow as AI use rises in finance\nWealthAi appoints Lynn Räbsamen as Chief Markets Officer","content_cn":"云安全\n高级持续性威胁防护\n合作伙伴计划\nWestcon-Comstor 与 CrowdStrike 在新加坡扩展 Falcon 平台\n2025年10月8日，星期三\nCATHERINE KNOWLES\n新闻编辑\nWestcon-Comstor 与 CrowdStrike 已达成分销协议，将 CrowdStrike Falcon 平台带给新加坡的合作伙伴和客户。\n该协议标志着 Westcon-Comstor 与 CrowdStrike 的合作进一步扩大，延伸了双方已在印度尼西亚、马来西亚和泰国开展的现有合作。此举旨在满足新加坡对网络安全整合和云原生安全解决方案日益增长的需求，这一需求受到日益复杂且由人工智能驱动的安全威胁推动。\n新加坡市场机遇\nWestcon-Comstor 将为其合作伙伴网络提供访问 CrowdStrike 解决方案套件的权限，包括终端安全、Falcon 云安全、Falcon 下一代身份安全和 Falcon 下一代 SIEM。这些产品旨在应对现代网络安全挑战，尤其是关键基础设施遭受定向攻击增加，以及各组织努力应对数字复杂性所带来的挑战。\n该公司计划支持各种现有和新客户，从企业和公司客户到中小型企业。为进一步简化部署，Westcon-Comstor 将通过渠道合作伙伴专属优惠以及 AWS Marketplace 上的私人上架提供 Falcon 平台，并利用其作为 AWS 指定记录销售商的地位。\nWestcon-Comstor 是一家专业分销商和技术提供商，计划配合 Falcon 平台提供额外的增值服务。这包括技术赋能、技能提升支持以及数据驱动的洞察，旨在强化 CrowdStrike 在该地区的渠道生态系统。\n领导层评论\n“新加坡的数字化进程提高了基础设施和网络安全的要求，给企业迅速实现现代化带来了压力。通过提供一条简化的路径和实操支持，我们旨在为 CrowdStrike 和渠道合作伙伴释放重要的新增长机遇。我们的作用对于帮助企业整合安全防护、在不堪重负的情况下保持安全至关重要；在推动采用 CrowdStrike 解决方案的同时，也为渠道合作伙伴创造收入机会，”Westcon-Comstor 亚太区云业务董事总经理 Jacquie Young 表示。\n“将我们与 Westcon-Comstor 的合作扩展到新加坡，强化了我们在该地区的渠道覆盖和伙伴优先战略，同时为 Westcon-Comstor 的合作伙伴和客户提供了代理式时代的首选网络安全平台。双方将共同加速采用 AI 原生 Falcon 平台，使我们的合作伙伴能够推动供应商整合、降低安全复杂性和成本，并借助真正的代理式安全平台阻止入侵，”CrowdStrike 亚太及日本地区分销与联盟高级总监 Girsih Gargeshwari 表示。\n认可与扩张\nWestcon-Comstor 获得了“2024 年 CrowdStrike 全球年度分销合作伙伴”称号，这是对其在 EMEA 和 APAC 超过 12,000 家渠道合作伙伴网络中推动 Falcon 平台采用表现的认可。\nWestcon-Comstor 与 CrowdStrike 在新加坡扩大的协议预计将帮助该国组织应对日益增长的数字化需求，以及对\n整合的云原生网络安全解决方案。\n使用 AI 探索\nChatGPT\n关键要点\n解释其重要性\n创建行动计划\n未来展望\nClaude\n关键要点\n解释其重要性\n创建行动计划\n未来展望\nPerplexity\n关键要点\n解释其重要性\n创建行动计划\n未来展望\nGrok\n关键要点\n解释其重要性\n创建行动计划\n未来展望\n分享\n分享\n在 Google 上将我们添加为首选来源\n相关新闻\nOkta 任命 Sunil Kedaraji 为亚太及日本地区合作伙伴副总裁\nKobalt.io 在北美签署安全合作协议\nTrendAI 在 AWS Marketplace 的销售额突破 10 亿美元\nSysdig 为云安全团队推出 Secure AI\nProofpoint 为安全厂商推出 OEM 计划\n头条新闻\nGoogle Cloud 将会话控制的默认时长扩展至 16 小时\nGoogle 警告 AI 正在重塑网络攻击与防御\nCohere 推出 North Small Translate，发力翻译领域\n随着 AI 在金融领域的应用增加，CFO 们聚焦现金流\nWealthAi 任命 Lynn Räbsamen 为首席市场官","publish_source":"itbrief.asia","publish_time":"2025-10-08T21:03:00+13:00"}},{"id":"news-1995","ktid":1000580,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000580","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"CrowdStrike警告AI将在2026年前重新定义网络威胁","title_en":"CrowdStrike warns AI will redefine cyber threats by 2026","summary_cn":"CrowdStrike预计人工智能将在2026年重塑网络威胁格局，预测提示注入攻击激增、AI驱动的零日漏洞发现以及企业非人类身份快速扩张。CTO Elia Zaitsev表示，提示注入正在定义AI时代，AI系统本身将成为主要攻击面，AI检测与响应（AIDR）将像EDR一样成为必需。他还预计安全运营中心将转向代理化SOC，身份管理将从以人为中心转向机器与代理身份主导。SVP Adam Meyers预计AI将加速零日漏洞的发现与利用。","summary_en":"CrowdStrike expects artificial intelligence to reshape the cyber threat landscape in 2026, predicting a surge in prompt-injection attacks, AI-driven zero-day discovery and rapid expansion of non-human identities. CTO Elia Zaitsev said prompt injection is defining the AI era, with AI systems becoming a primary attack surface and AI Detection and Response becoming as essential as EDR. He also expects a shift toward agentic SOCs and machine-dominated identity management. SVP Adam Meyers expects AI to accelerate zero-day discovery and exploitation.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:38:54.256503+00:00","url":"https://itbrief.com.au/story/crowdstrike-warns-ai-will-redefine-cyber-threats-by-2026","content":"Digital Transformation\nPAM\nAdvanced Persistent Threat Protection\nCrowdStrike warns AI will redefine cyber threats by 2026\nWed, 10th Dec 2025\nKALEAH SALMON\nHead of Growth\nCrowdStrike expects artificial intelligence to reshape the cyber threat landscape in 2026, predicting a surge in prompt-injection attacks, AI-driven zero-day discovery, and a rapid expansion of non-human identities across enterprises.\nSenior leaders at the security company say that security operations teams will need to re-architect how they monitor, orchestrate and control both human and machine activity if they are to keep pace with adversaries using AI at scale.\nElia Zaitsev, Chief Technology Officer, CrowdStrike, said, \"Just as phishing defined the email era, prompt injection is defining the AI era. Adversaries are embedding hidden instructions to override safeguards, hijack agents, steal data, and manipulate models - turning the AI interaction layer into the new attack surface and prompts into the new malware.\"\nPrompt injection\nZaitsev said organisations should prepare for AI systems themselves to become a primary attack surface, as businesses embed models and agents into workflows, customer interfaces and internal tools.\nHe expects dedicated monitoring and control to emerge as a core security requirement for AI deployments, much as endpoint detection and response (EDR) became standard for laptops and servers.\n\"In 2026, AI Detection and Response (AIDR) will become as essential as EDR, with organisations requiring real-time visibility into prompts, responses, agent actions, and tool calls to contain AI abuse before it spreads, ensuring AI drives innovation, not risk,\" said Zaitsev.\nAgentic SOCs\nCrowdStrike forecasts that AI agents will be used not only by attackers but also inside security operations centres (SOCs) to speed up detection, investigation and response.\n\"Adversaries are already using AI to move faster than humanly possible - and legacy SOCs can't keep up. In 2026, defenders will evolve from alert handlers to orchestrators of the agentic SOC: intelligent agents that reason, decide, and act across the security lifecycle at machine speed, always under human command. This is the model that will reshape the balance between adversaries and defenders, accelerating outcomes and giving humans the time and clarity to focus on strategy, judgment, and impact,\" said Zaitsev.\nHe set out several conditions that he believes must be in place before this model can function reliably at scale.\n\"The success of this evolution will be dependant on the following prerequisites: Providing both agents and analysts complete environmental context with the ability to action any signal immediately. An agentic workforce of mission-ready agents trained on years of expert SOC decisions to automate high-friction tasks with speed and precision. Benchmarks and validation to prove the effectiveness of agents. The ability for organisations to build and customise their own agents to satisfy unique needs.Orchestrating agent-to-agent and analyst-to-agent collaboration within one coordinated system guided by human expertise. Security analysts are not going away - they're being elevated by a fleet of agents that work at machine speed,\" said Zaitsev.\nNon-human identities\nZaitsev also expects identity management to shift from a primarily human-centric discipline to one dominated by machine and agent identities with wide-ranging access rights.\n\"In 2026, AI agents and non-human identities will explode across the enterprise, expanding exponentially and dwarfing human identities. Each agent will operate as a privileged super-human with OAuth tokens, API keys, and continuous access to previously siloed data sets, making them the most powerful and most dangerous entities in your environment.\"\nHe said this change would require security teams to track and control machine actions at a granular level and to maintain clear lines of accountability back to specific staff and teams.\n\"Identity security built for humans won't survive this shift. Security teams will need real-time visibility, instant containment, and the ability to trace every agent action back to the human who created it. When an AI agent wires money to the wrong account or leaks intellectual property, \"the AI did it\" won't be an acceptable answer. This is the era where identity security means protecting entities that don't have a pulse,\" said Zaitsev.\nZero-day surge\nAdam Meyers, Senior Vice President of Counter Adversary Operations at CrowdStrike, expects AI to accelerate both software creation and vulnerability discovery, leading to more zero-day flaws being identified and exploited.\n\"In 2026, we'll likely see an explosion of zero-day vulnerabilities driven by AI. As AI accelerates code generation and software development, it's also becoming ideally suited to finding flaws in software. There are two primary ways to identify these vulnerabilities: targeted analysis, which is resource-intensive and typically requires a human in the loop. The other is commonly called fuzzing and involves automation to identify flaws. GenAI is a game-changer for the latter. AI can optimise fuzzing methodologies and analyse crash reports at scale, rapidly surfacing exploitable flaws.\"\nMeyers said early activity suggests that better-resourced attackers are already experimenting with AI-assisted methods to locate and weaponise vulnerabilities more cheaply and at greater speed.\n\"Early indicators suggest advanced adversaries are already investing in this research, driving down the cost of discovering and weaponising vulnerabilities. These exploits are the keys that adversaries use to gain initial access to their targets. The defenders who succeed will be those using AI with the same speed and precision: detecting, patching, and proactively hunting for zero-days as fast as they're found,\" said Meyers.\nExplore with AI\nChatGPT\nKey takeaways\nExplain why it matters\nCreate action plan\nFuture watch\nClaude\nKey takeaways\nExplain why it matters\nCreate action plan\nFuture watch\nPerplexity\nKey takeaways\nExplain why it matters\nCreate action plan\nFuture watch\nGrok\nKey takeaways\nExplain why it matters\nCreate action plan\nFuture watch\nShare\nShare\nAdd us as a preferred source on Google\nRelated stories\nThreatDown adds shadow AI & identity tracking tools\nKnowBe4 adds Claude oversight to Agent Risk Manager\nCrowdStrike launches AI security challenge with AWS\nCyera launches tools to secure enterprise AI agents\nAI security incidents expose new criminal tradeoffs\nTop stories\nCFOs focus on cash flow as AI use rises in finance\nGSMA warns rising handset costs could widen AI divide\nDayforce named leader in Gartner workforce management\nAirwallex adds AUD $4.6 billion to Australia economy\nMacquarie law school installs Sennheiser audio systems","content_cn":"数字化转型\nPAM\n高级持续性威胁防护\nCrowdStrike警告称，到2026年人工智能将重新定义网络威胁\n2025年12月10日，星期三\nKALEAH SALMON\n增长负责人\nCrowdStrike预计，人工智能将在2026年重塑网络威胁格局，并预测提示词注入攻击、人工智能驱动的零日漏洞发现将激增，以及企业中的非人类身份将迅速扩张。\n这家安全公司的高级领导者表示，如果安全运营团队要跟上大规模使用人工智能的对手，就需要重新设计监控、编排和控制人类与机器活动的方式。\nCrowdStrike首席技术官Elia Zaitsev表示：“正如网络钓鱼定义了电子邮件时代，提示词注入正在定义人工智能时代。对手正嵌入隐藏指令，以绕过安全防护、劫持代理、窃取数据并操纵模型——将人工智能交互层变成新的攻击面，将提示词变成新的恶意软件。”\n提示词注入\nZaitsev表示，随着企业将模型和代理嵌入工作流程、客户界面和内部工具，组织应准备好应对人工智能系统本身成为主要攻击面。\n他预计，专门的监控和控制将成为人工智能部署的核心安全要求，就像端点检测与响应（EDR）已成为笔记本电脑和服务器的标准配置一样。\nZaitsev表示：“到2026年，人工智能检测与响应（AIDR）将与EDR同样不可或缺。组织将需要实时了解提示词、响应、代理行动和工具调用，以便在人工智能滥用扩散之前加以遏制，确保人工智能推动创新，而非带来风险。”\n代理型SOC\nCrowdStrike预测，人工智能代理不仅会被攻击者使用，也会进入安全运营中心（SOC），以加快检测、调查和响应。\nZaitsev表示：“对手已经在利用人工智能，以超越人类可能达到的速度行动——而传统SOC跟不上。到2026年，防御者将从警报处理者转变为代理型SOC的编排者：这些智能代理能够在整个安全生命周期中以机器速度进行推理、决策和行动，并始终处于人类指挥之下。这一模式将重塑对手与防御者之间的平衡，加快成果产出，让人类拥有时间和清晰度，专注于战略、判断和影响。”\n他列出了若干他认为这一模式要在大规模环境中可靠运行前必须具备的条件。\nZaitsev表示：“这一演进的成功将取决于以下先决条件：为代理和分析师提供完整的环境背景，并能够立即对任何信号采取行动。一支由随时可执行任务的代理组成的代理型劳动力，这些代理接受多年SOC专家决策的训练，能够快速而精准地自动化高摩擦任务。用于证明代理有效性的基准和验证。组织能够构建和定制自己的代理，以满足独特需求。在一个由人类专业知识指导的协调系统内，编排代理对代理以及分析师对代理的协作。安全分析师不会消失——他们正由一支以机器速度工作的代理队伍提升能力。”\n非人类身份\nZaitsev还预计，身份管理将从以人为中心的学科，转变为主要由拥有广泛访问权限的机器和代理身份主导的领域。\n“到2026年，人工智能代理和非人类身份将\n在整个企业中爆发式扩散，以指数级增长，令人的身份相形见绌。每个代理都将以拥有 OAuth 令牌、API 密钥以及持续访问此前彼此隔离的数据集的特权超人身份运行，使其成为你环境中最强大、也最危险的实体。”\n他说，这一变化将要求安全团队以细粒度跟踪和控制机器行为，并保持明确的问责链，追溯到具体员工和团队。\n“为人类打造的身份安全将无法适应这一转变。安全团队需要实时可见性、即时遏制能力，以及将代理的每项行动追溯到创建它的人类的能力。当 AI 代理把钱汇入错误账户或泄露知识产权时，‘是 AI 干的’不会是可接受的答案。这是一个身份安全意味着保护没有脉搏的实体的时代，”Zaitsev 说。\n零日漏洞激增\nCrowdStrike 负责反对手行动的高级副总裁 Adam Meyers 预计，AI 将加速软件创建和漏洞发现，从而导致更多零日漏洞被识别和利用。\n“2026 年，我们很可能会看到由 AI 驱动的零日漏洞爆发。随着 AI 加速代码生成和软件开发，它也越来越适合发现软件中的缺陷。识别这些漏洞主要有两种方式：有针对性的分析，这种方式资源消耗大，通常需要人工参与。另一种通常称为模糊测试，依靠自动化来识别缺陷。生成式 AI 将改变后者的游戏规则。AI 可以优化模糊测试方法，并大规模分析崩溃报告，快速发现可被利用的缺陷。”\nMeyers 表示，早期活动表明，资源更充足的攻击者已经在尝试借助 AI 的方法，以更低成本、更快速度定位并武器化漏洞。\n“早期迹象表明，先进的对手已经在这项研究上投入资金，降低发现和武器化漏洞的成本。这些漏洞利用工具是对手用来获得目标初始访问权限的钥匙。能够成功的防御者，将是那些以同样速度和精确度使用 AI 的人：在发现零日漏洞后，以最快速度进行检测、修补并主动搜寻，”Meyers 说。\n借助 AI 探索\nChatGPT\n主要要点\n解释其重要性\n制定行动计划\n未来展望\nClaude\n主要要点\n解释其重要性\n制定行动计划\n未来展望\nPerplexity\n主要要点\n解释其重要性\n制定行动计划\n未来展望\nGrok\n主要要点\n解释其重要性\n制定行动计划\n未来展望\n分享\n分享\n在 Google 上将我们添加为首选来源\n相关文章\nThreatDown 增加影子 AI 和身份跟踪工具\nKnowBe4 为 Agent Risk Manager 增加 Claude 监管功能\nCrowdStrike 与 AWS 推出 AI 安全挑战赛\nCyera 推出保障企业 AI 代理安全的工具\nAI 安全事件暴露新的犯罪权衡\n热门报道\n随着 AI 在金融领域的应用增加，CFO 关注现金流\nGSMA 警告，手机成本上涨可能扩大 AI 鸿沟\nDayforce 被 Gartner 评为劳动力管理领域领导者\nAirwallex 为澳大利亚经济增加 46 亿澳元\nMacquarie 法学院安装森海塞尔音频系统","publish_source":"itbrief.com.au","publish_time":"2025-12-10T12:57:00+13:00"}},{"id":"news-955","ktid":1001190,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001190","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"巴库如何看待大西洋理事会的美国-阿塞拜疆“大交易”提议？","title_en":"Proposed US-Azerbaijan deal/JAMnews","summary_cn":"美国智库大西洋理事会5月10日发文，呼吁特朗普政府以解除对阿塞拜疆武器销售限制，换取巴库释放被当地及国际人权组织视为政治犯的在押活动人士和记者，包括经济学家伊巴多格鲁、记者梅赫拉利扎达等。文章建议废除《自由支持法》第907条，并称风险低、政治收益大。文章梳理了阿塞拜疆分析人士的分歧看法及该提议面临的现实障碍。","summary_en":"The US think tank Atlantic Council published an article on 10 May urging the Trump administration to lift restrictions on arms sales to Azerbaijan in exchange for Baku releasing jailed civil society activists and journalists regarded by local and international rights groups as political prisoners, including economist Gubad Ibadoghlu and journalist Farid Mehralizada. It proposed repealing Section 907 of the Freedom Support Act, arguing risks are low and political gains substantial. The piece surveys divided views among Azerbaijani analysts and the practical obstacles the proposal faces.","tag":"geopolitics","founddate":"2026-09-18T13:29:00.973678+00:00","url":"https://jam-news.net/how-does-baku-view-atlantic-councils-us-azerbaijan-grand-bargain-proposal","content":"Azerbaijan-USA\nՀայերեն\nAzərbaycanca\nქართული\nРусский\nAzerbaijan-USA\n14.05.2026\nHow does Baku view Atlantic Council’s US-Azerbaijan ‘grand bargain’ proposal?\nJAMnews\nBaku\nShare\nShare\nProposed US-Azerbaijan deal\nThe US think tank Atlantic Council has urged President Donald Trump’s administration to lift restrictions on arms sales to Azerbaijan in exchange for the release of jailed civil society activists and journalists whom local and international rights groups regard as political prisoners.\nIn an article titled “It’s time for a US-Azerbaijan grand bargain”, published on 10 May, authors Andrew D’Anieri and Mercedes Sapuppo proposed the following framework.\nThe US Congress would repeal Section 907 of the Freedom Support Act, which restricts US government assistance to Azerbaijan, while Baku would release what the authors described as “wrongfully imprisoned” detainees.\nAmong those named were economist Gubad Ibadoghlu, who is under house arrest; Radio Free Europe/Radio Liberty journalist Farid Mehralizada, who was sentenced to nine years in prison; former Voice of America correspondent Ulviya Ali; and lawyer Alasgar Mammadli, whose cases are still ongoing.\nAll have officially been charged with financial crimes, but they deny the accusations and say they are being persecuted for criticism of the authorities.\nThe article also suggested that some Armenian detainees held in Baku could be released as part of the arrangement.\nThe authors compared the proposal to a model previously used by the White House in dealings with Belarus, which they said resulted in the release and exile of more than 500 political prisoners.\nThey argued that shifting US policy in the South Caucasus, upcoming parliamentary elections in Armenia and the importance of signing a final peace agreement between Azerbaijan and Armenia increased the relevance of such a “grand bargain” between Washington and Baku.\nAccording to the authors, the risks of the approach would be minimal, while the political gains could be substantial: deepening US-Azerbaijan relations, giving new momentum to the Armenia-Azerbaijan peace process and delivering a major foreign policy success for the White House.\nYerevan vox pops: what residents say on peace with Azerbaijan\nThe Armenian-Azerbaijani border has been calm for two years, with no exchange of fire. Both governments say peace has been established. But what do Yerevan residents think?\nThe Atlantic Council largely frames Section 907 as a restriction on arms sales, although formally it limits all direct US government assistance to Azerbaijan, including military aid.\nSince 2001, US presidents have routinely waived the restriction, and in August 2025 Donald Trump once again suspended its application.\nA memorandum signed by Trump in 2025 stated that the decision was intended to support joint counterterrorism efforts and avoid harming the peace process between Azerbaijan and Armenia.\nIn practice, this means that under the proposed “grand bargain”, the US would be giving up one of its key remaining sources of leverage over Azerbaijan.\nHowever, Andrew D’Anieri and Mercedes Sapuppo argue that, compared with the model previously used in Belarus, the strategic benefits in Azerbaijan’s case are greater while the risks are lower.\nThe timing of the proposal also appears deliberate.\nThe Atlantic Council noted that Vice-President JD Vance’s visits to Armenia and Azerbaijan in February reflected an unprecedented level of US engagement in the region.\nVance’s trip to Baku was accompanied by the signing of a strategic partnership charter and expanded cooperation in defence and infrastructure projects.\nThe article also stressed that the outcome of Armenia’s parliamentary elections on 7 June could either accelerate or slow the peace process.\nThe Atlantic Council further argued that releasing some Armenian detainees held in Baku before the elections could strengthen Prime Minister Nikol Pashinyan’s position and help keep the path towards a peace agreement open.\nWhat's next for Armenians imprisoned in Azerbaijan — and could Ilham Aliyev release them?\nArmenian parliament speaker Alen Simonyan has said that “negotiations will not stop until the last Armenian detainee is returned”, a position that differs sharply from that of Azerbaijani President Ilham Aliyev.\nViews from Azerbaijani analysts\nPolitical analysts Arastun Orujlu and Rauf Mirqadirov argue that energy cooperation, the Middle Corridor transit route and security issues remain the key drivers of Azerbaijan’s relations with the West, while concerns over human rights and political prisoners are pushed into the background.\nIn that context, the Atlantic Council’s proposed “grand bargain” is seen in independent circles in Baku as a familiar formula: the West once again prioritising strategic interests while attaching the release of prisoners to the deal.\nFor some rights advocates, this represents an opportunity. For others, it risks turning human rights into a bargaining chip.\nIn one of his earlier statements, rights activist Arif Yunus said Armenian prisoners — including those sentenced to life imprisonment — could potentially be released in exchange for major political concessions.\nAt the same time, analyst Elkhan Shahinoglu, who is widely seen as close to the authorities, has argued the opposite. In his view, the continued detention of former Nagorno-Karabakh “state minister” Ruben Vardanyan may be politically advantageous primarily for Yerevan.\nAs a result, even within Azerbaijan’s expert community there is no single consensus. Independent analysts tend to see detainees as leverage in negotiations, while pro-government commentators view the issue through the prism of Armenia’s elections and Azerbaijan’s domestic politics.\nAlthough pro-government media outlets have not directly responded to the Atlantic Council article, they have openly supported repealing Section 907 in recent months.\nPresident Ilham Aliyev described the measure in January as “absolutely absurd”, while pro-government media portrayed it as the main obstacle in bilateral relations.\nThe overall message has remained unchanged: Section 907 should be repealed because both Baku and Washington increasingly see it as an outdated political burden.\nAt the same time, pro-government media support repealing Section 907 but show little willingness to tie the issue to demands involving political prisoners or Armenian detainees.\nUS vice-president’s visit to Baku: strategic partnership and new pledges\nTrip marked by high-level talks and strategic partnership charter\nExpert commentary also reflects these divisions.\n● Former US ambassador to Azerbaijan Matthew Bryza has described Section 907 as a “political anachronism” and sees its continued existence largely as a symbolic source of tension.\n● Commentator Andrew Korybko argues that the process of repealing the amendment is already under way, although Armenian lobbying groups in Congress remain an obstacle.\n● According to analyst Eldeniz Amirov, the amendment’s economic impact is limited, while its significance is mainly symbolic and political.\n● Political analyst Matin Mammadli believes repealing the amendment would strengthen US influence in the South Caucasus.\nAt the same time, sources close to Azerbaijan’s human rights and media circles see the issue differently.\nIf the release of political prisoners becomes tied to a broader geopolitical package, would that legitimise a new form of transactional diplomacy in the future?\nThe practical side of the proposal is also not so simple.\nMany political prisoners and ethnic Armenian detainees held in Azerbaijan face “serious” or “especially serious” charges, meaning they were excluded from the amnesty announced in 2025.\nIn such cases, release would generally require either a presidential pardon or a separate political decision.\nThat is an important detail for the Atlantic Council’s proposal: its implementation depends less on legal procedures than on political will.\nAs a result, the issue is not only whether the US Congress would agree to such a step, but whether Baku itself would be prepared to make a serious domestic political decision.\nSo far, the Atlantic Council’s proposed “grand bargain” has not sparked a major public debate in Azerbaijan. However, the main lines of reaction are already becoming clear.\nIf Washington does attempt to push forward with such a model, the central debate is likely to focus not on closer US-Azerbaijan ties themselves, but on their moral and political price.\nUS vice-president’s visit to Armenia hailed as ‘historic’ – what it delivered\nArmenia’s prime minister and the US vice-president signed a joint statement on the peaceful use of nuclear energy and discussed new areas of strategic partnership.\nProposed US-Azerbaijan deal\nMore on JAMnews\nArmenia’s anti-corruption campaign: law on confiscating illicit assets takes effect\nPoll: Do Abkhazia residents consider voting in Russia’s State Duma elections important? Video\nInvestigation launched into dozens of children falling ill at Tbilisi nurseries\nCouncil of Europe Committee of Ministers urges Russia to withdraw troops from Georgia's occupied territories\nOpinion: Abolition of Georgia's state grants agency contradicts pledges to 'support good causes'\nLIVE: Key morning headlines from Armenia, Azerbaijan and Georgia\nArmenians to be able to fund media directly through their income tax payments\n'NGOs are artificial phenomenon' — Georgia to shut down grants management agency\nUS court orders Georgia to pay $350m over halted Namakhvani HPP project\nMost read\n1\nEPRC: Wildberries expansion poses significant risks for Georgia\n2\nTrump Tower project unveiled in Tbilisi\n3\nWall Street Journal: New Trump Tower to be built in Georgia as country draws closer to Russia\n4\nLIVE: Key morning headlines from Armenia, Azerbaijan and Georgia\n5\n'Helping Baku justify ethnic cleansing': Yerevan views on diplomats’ trip to Karabakh\n6\nArmenian citizenship to become harder and five times more expensive under Interior Ministry draft","content_cn":"阿塞拜疆-美国\nՀայերեն\nAzərbaycanca\nქართული\nРусский\n阿塞拜疆-美国\n14.05.2026\n巴库如何看待大西洋理事会提出的美阿“重大交易”建议？\nJAMnews\n巴库\n分享\n分享\n拟议中的美阿协议\n美国智库大西洋理事会敦促唐纳德·特朗普政府解除对阿塞拜疆武器销售的限制，以换取释放被监禁的公民社会活动人士和记者；当地及国际人权组织认为这些人是政治犯。\n在5月10日发表、题为《是时候达成美阿重大交易了》的文章中，作者安德鲁·达涅里和梅赛德斯·萨普波提出了以下框架。\n美国国会将废除《自由支持法》第907条，该条限制美国政府向阿塞拜疆提供援助；与此同时，巴库将释放作者所称的“被错误监禁”的被拘押者。\n被点名者包括正在软禁中的经济学家古巴德·伊巴多格鲁；被判处九年监禁的自由欧洲电台/自由电台记者法里德·梅赫拉利扎德；美国之音前记者乌尔维娅·阿里；以及律师阿拉斯加尔·马马德利，他们的案件目前仍在审理中。\n所有人都被正式指控犯有金融犯罪，但他们否认这些指控，并称自己因批评当局而受到迫害。\n文章还建议，作为该安排的一部分，可以释放一些被关押在巴库的亚美尼亚被拘押者。\n作者将这一建议比作白宫此前与白俄罗斯打交道时采用的一种模式；他们说，该模式促成了500多名政治犯获释并被流放。\n他们认为，美国对南高加索政策的调整、亚美尼亚即将举行的议会选举，以及签署阿塞拜疆与亚美尼亚最终和平协议的重要性，都提高了华盛顿与巴库达成这种“重大交易”的相关性。\n作者称，这一做法的风险将极小，而政治收益可能十分可观：深化美阿关系，为亚美尼亚—阿塞拜疆和平进程注入新动力，并为白宫带来一项重大的外交政策成功。\n埃里温街头采访：居民如何看待与阿塞拜疆的和平\n亚美尼亚—阿塞拜疆边境已平静两年，没有发生交火。两国政府都表示和平已经建立。但埃里温居民怎么看？\n大西洋理事会在很大程度上将第907条描述为对武器销售的限制，尽管从正式定义看，该条限制美国政府向阿塞拜疆提供一切直接援助，包括军事援助。\n自2001年以来，美国总统一直例行豁免这项限制；2025年8月，唐纳德·特朗普再次暂停了其实施。\n特朗普于2025年签署的一份备忘录称，这一决定旨在支持联合反恐努力，并避免损害阿塞拜疆与亚美尼亚之间的和平进程。\n实际上，这意味着按照拟议的“重大交易”，美国将放弃其对阿塞拜疆所剩不多的关键施压手段之一。\n然而，安德鲁·达涅里和梅赛德斯·萨普波认为，与此前在白俄罗斯采用的模式相比，在阿塞拜疆的案例中，战略收益更大，而风险更低。\n该建议提出的时机似乎也是经过刻意安排的。\n大西洋理事会指出，副总统J·D·万斯于2月访问亚美尼亚和阿塞拜疆，反映出美国对该地区前所未有的参与程度。\n万斯此行前往\n巴库之行还伴随着签署战略伙伴关系宪章，以及扩大在国防和基础设施项目方面的合作。\n文章还强调，6月7日亚美尼亚议会选举的结果可能加快或拖慢和平进程。\n大西洋理事会进一步主张，在选举前释放一些被关押在巴库的亚美尼亚被拘留者，可能会巩固总理 Nikol Pashinyan 的地位，并有助于保持通往和平协议的道路畅通。\n被关押在阿塞拜疆的亚美尼亚人接下来会怎样——Ilham Aliyev 会释放他们吗？\n亚美尼亚议会议长 Alen Simonyan 表示，“在最后一名亚美尼亚被拘留者获释之前，谈判不会停止”，这一立场与阿塞拜疆总统 Ilham Aliyev 的立场截然不同。\n阿塞拜疆分析人士的看法\n政治分析人士 Arastun Orujlu 和 Rauf Mirqadirov 认为，能源合作、中间走廊运输路线和安全问题仍是阿塞拜疆与西方关系的主要驱动因素，而对人权和政治犯的担忧则被置于次要位置。\n在这一背景下，大西洋理事会提出的“宏大交易”在巴库独立圈子看来是一种熟悉的公式：西方再次优先考虑战略利益，同时把释放囚犯作为协议的一部分。\n对一些权利倡导者而言，这代表着一个机会。对另一些人而言，这有将人权变成讨价还价筹码的风险。\n权利活动人士 Arif Yunus 在早先的一份声明中表示，亚美尼亚囚犯——包括被判处终身监禁者——有可能以换取重大政治让步为条件获释。\n与此同时，被广泛认为与当局关系密切的分析人士 Elkhan Shahinoglu 则提出了相反的观点。在他看来，继续拘押纳戈尔诺-卡拉巴赫前“国务部长” Ruben Vardanyan，主要可能对埃里温具有政治上的好处。\n因此，即便在阿塞拜疆专家界内部，也没有形成单一共识。独立分析人士倾向于将被拘留者视为谈判中的筹码，而亲政府评论人士则透过亚美尼亚选举和阿塞拜疆国内政治的棱镜看待这一问题。\n尽管亲政府媒体没有直接回应大西洋理事会的文章，但近几个月来一直公开支持废除第907条款。\n总统 Ilham Aliyev 在1月将该措施称为“绝对荒谬”，而亲政府媒体则将其描述为双边关系中的主要障碍。\n总体信息始终未变：第907条款应被废除，因为巴库和华盛顿都越来越认为它是一项过时的政治负担。\n与此同时，亲政府媒体支持废除第907条款，但几乎没有意愿将这一问题与涉及政治犯或亚美尼亚被拘留者的要求挂钩。\n美国副总统访问巴库：战略伙伴关系与新的承诺\n此次访问以高层会谈和战略伙伴关系宪章为特色\n专家评论也反映了这些分歧。\n● 美国前驻阿塞拜疆大使 Matthew Bryza 将第907条款称为“政治时代错误”，并认为其继续存在主要是象征性的紧张来源。\n● 评论员 Andrew Korybko 认为，废除该修正案的进程已经开始，尽管国会中的亚美尼亚游说团体仍然构成障碍。\n● 据分析人士 Eldeniz Amirov 称，\n该修正案的经济影响有限，其意义主要在于象征性和政治性。\n● 政治分析人士马丁·马马德利认为，废除该修正案将加强美国在南高加索地区的影响力。\n与此同时，接近阿塞拜疆人权和媒体圈的消息人士对此问题有不同看法。\n如果政治犯获释与更广泛的地缘政治方案挂钩，这是否会在未来使一种新形式的交易型外交获得合法性？\n该提案的实际操作层面也并不简单。\n许多被关押在阿塞拜疆的政治犯和亚美尼亚族被拘押者面临“严重”或“特别严重”的指控，这意味着他们被排除在2025年宣布的大赦之外。\n在这种情况下，释放通常需要总统赦免或单独的政治决定。\n这是大西洋理事会提案中的一个重要细节：其落实与其说取决于法律程序，不如说取决于政治意愿。\n因此，问题不仅在于美国国会是否会同意采取这一步骤，还在于巴库自身是否准备作出重大的国内政治决定。\n到目前为止，大西洋理事会提出的“重大交易”尚未在阿塞拜疆引发大规模公共辩论。不过，反应的主要脉络已经逐渐清晰。\n如果华盛顿确实试图推动这种模式，核心争论可能不会集中在美阿关系本身是否更加密切，而会集中在这种关系的道德和政治代价上。\n美国副总统访问亚美尼亚被誉为“历史性”——带来了什么\n亚美尼亚总理与美国副总统签署了关于和平利用核能的联合声明，并讨论了战略伙伴关系的新领域。\n拟议中的美阿协议\nJAMnews更多内容\n亚美尼亚反腐行动：没收非法资产的法律生效\n民调：阿布哈兹居民是否认为参加俄罗斯国家杜马选举很重要？视频\n第比利斯托儿所数十名儿童患病事件展开调查\n欧洲委员会部长委员会敦促俄罗斯从格鲁吉亚被占领土撤军\n观点：废除格鲁吉亚国家拨款机构与“支持公益事业”的承诺相矛盾\n直播：亚美尼亚、阿塞拜疆和格鲁吉亚晨间要闻\n亚美尼亚人将能够通过缴纳所得税直接资助媒体\n“非政府组织是人为现象”——格鲁吉亚将关闭拨款管理机构\n美国法院裁定格鲁吉亚因叫停纳马赫瓦尼水电站项目支付3.5亿美元\n阅读最多\n1\nEPRC：Wildberries扩张给格鲁吉亚带来重大风险\n2\n第比利斯特朗普大厦项目公布\n3\n《华尔街日报》：随着格鲁吉亚日益靠近俄罗斯，新的特朗普大厦将在该国建成\n4\n直播：亚美尼亚、阿塞拜疆和格鲁吉亚晨间要闻\n5\n“帮助巴库为种族清洗辩护”：埃里温对外交官前往卡拉巴赫的看法\n6\n根据内政部草案，亚美尼亚公民身份申请将变得更加困难，费用将提高至五倍","publish_source":"jam-news.net","publish_time":"2026-05-14T08:49:56+00:00"}},{"id":"news-3556","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"贾亚帕尔敦促国土安全部停止使用私营营利性移民监狱","title_en":"Jayapal Urges DHS to Stop Use of Private, For-Profit Immigration Prisons - Congresswoman Pramila Jayapal","summary_cn":"美国众议员普拉米拉·贾亚帕尔在视察西北移民处理中心后致信国土安全部部长马约卡斯，敦促逐步淘汰移民和海关执法局对私营营利性移民拘留设施的使用，并在明年9月合同到期时终止该中心与GEO集团的合同。信中列举了该中心的人权侵犯、单独监禁超期及被拘留者死亡等记录。","summary_en":"U.S. Representative Pramila Jayapal sent a letter to DHS Secretary Alejandro Mayorkas after inspecting the Northwest Immigrant Processing Center, urging a phase-out of private for-profit immigration detention facilities used by ICE and ending the center's GEO Group contract when it expires next September. The letter cites reports of human rights abuses, prolonged solitary confinement and a detainee's death.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T22:34:39.917421+00:00","url":"https://jayapal.house.gov/2024/08/26/jayapal-urges-dhs-to-stop-use-of-private-for-profit-immigration-prisons","content":"08.26.2024\n|\nNews\nJayapal Urges DHS to Stop Use of Private, For-Profit Immigration Prisons\nSEATTLE, WA – U.S. Representative Pramila Jayapal (WA-07), Ranking Member of the Immigration Integrity, Security, and Enforcement Subcommittee, sent a letter to Department of Homeland Security (DHS) Secretary Alejandro Mayorkas following her inspection of the Northwest Immigrant Processing Center (NWIPC), formerly the Northwest Detention Center, earlier this month. She urged Secretary Mayorkas to phase out the use of private, for-profit immigration detention facilities by Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) and to end NWIPC’s contract with GEO Group when it expires next September.\n“I have long found the use of for-profit prisons concerning—a concern shared by many of my colleagues in Congress,” Jayapal said. “As President Biden himself said in 2023, ‘There should be no private prisons, no private detention centers.’ Unfortunately […] the use of private prisons in the immigration system has grown: as of July 2023, 90.8 percent of individuals in immigration detention were held in detention facilities owned or operated by private prison companies, up from 81 percent in 2020. The two largest for-profit companies GEO and CoreCivic […] raked in $1 billion and $552 million respectively from ICE in just 2022.”\nThe NWIPC has a history of troubling allegations including:\nAn August 2023 report detailing human rights abuses at the center;\nA February 2024 report finding that the NWIPC and other immigration detention facilities regularly detain immigrants in solitary confinement beyond the United Nation’s 15-day threshold for considering such confinement to be torture;\nAn April 2024 report showing that there were 41 calls made to 911 from the center in a ten week period this year;\nThe tragic death of Charles Leo Daniel in March 2024, after he was kept in solitary confinement for a total of 1,418 days; and\nAn August 2024 lawsuit filed by the Washington Department of Health requesting access to the facility after they received over 700 complaints from detainees since April 2024.\nJayapal further stated, “We have a responsibility to treat all human beings with dignity and fairness. All facilities operated by or in connection with the United States government, funded by taxpayers should reflect that. Unfortunately, it is clear facilities operated by private prison companies are falling far short of our obligations. It is time for us to transition away from using these for-profit companies.”\nJayapal has been a leader in the effort to end the use of private, for-profit detention centers and to instead substantially reduce our reliance on detention and use humane community-based alternatives to detention. She has led calls to DHS to urge the closure of facilities with records of abuse and has also worked to push accountability and transparency at these facilities. She has conducted significant oversight over the Northwest Detention Center.\nJayapal is the sponsor of the Dignity for Detained Immigrants Act, transformative legislation that would overhaul the immigration detention system by ending the use of for-profit, private detention facilities, repealing mandatory detention, and protecting the civil and human rights of immigrants.\nThe full text of the letter can be read here.\nIssues: Immigration\nShare:\nFacebook\nTwitter\nMail","content_cn":"2024年8月26日\n|\n新闻\n贾亚帕尔敦促国土安全部停止使用私营营利性移民监狱\n华盛顿州西雅图——美国众议员普拉米拉·贾亚帕尔（华盛顿州第7选区）、移民诚信、安全与执法小组委员会首席成员，在本月早些时候检查西北移民处理中心（NWIPC，原名西北拘留中心）后致信国土安全部（DHS）部长亚历杭德罗·马约卡斯。她敦促马约卡斯部长逐步停止移民与海关执法局（ICE）使用私营营利性移民拘留设施，并在明年9月合同到期时终止NWIPC与GEO集团的合同。\n贾亚帕尔说：“我长期以来一直对使用营利性监狱感到担忧——国会中的许多同僚也有同样的担忧。正如拜登总统本人在2023年所说，‘不应有私营监狱，也不应有私营拘留中心。’遗憾的是……移民系统中私营监狱的使用已经扩大：截至2023年7月，90.8%的移民拘留人员被关押在由私营监狱公司拥有或运营的拘留设施中，高于2020年的81%。两家最大的营利性公司GEO和CoreCivic仅在2022年就分别从ICE获得了10亿美元和5.52亿美元。”\nNWIPC曾被提出多项令人不安的指控，包括：\n2023年8月的一份报告，详细说明了该中心发生的人权侵害；\n2024年2月的一份报告，发现NWIPC及其他移民拘留设施经常将移民单独监禁超过联合国认定构成酷刑的15天门槛；\n2024年4月的一份报告显示，今年十周期间该中心拨打了41次911；\n查尔斯·利奥·丹尼尔于2024年3月悲惨死亡，此前他总计被单独监禁1,418天；以及\n华盛顿州卫生部于2024年8月提起的一起诉讼，要求进入该设施，此前该部门自2024年4月以来收到被拘留者提出的700多起投诉。\n贾亚帕尔进一步表示：“我们有责任以尊严和公平对待所有人。所有由美国政府运营或与其有关联、由纳税人资助的设施都应体现这一点。遗憾的是，很明显，私营监狱公司运营的设施远未履行我们的义务。现在是我们停止使用这些营利性公司的时候了。”\n贾亚帕尔一直是结束使用私营营利性拘留中心、实质性减少对拘留的依赖并采用人道社区替代方案的倡导者。她曾带头呼吁DHS关闭有虐待记录的设施，也推动这些设施加强问责和透明度。她还对西北拘留中心开展了大量监督工作。\n贾亚帕尔是《被拘留移民尊严法》的发起人。该变革性立法将通过结束使用营利性私营拘留设施、废除强制拘留并保护移民的公民权利和人权，彻底改革移民拘留制度。\n信函全文可在此处阅读。\n议题：移民\n分享：\nFacebook\nTwitter\n邮件","publish_source":"jayapal.house.gov","publish_time":"2024-08-26T16:06:12+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2289","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"国土安全委员会与司法委员会就芝加哥暴力移民突袭展开调查","title_en":"Homeland Security and Judiciary Committees Launch Investigation into Violent Chicago Immigration Raid - Congresswoman Pramila Jayapal","summary_cn":"美国众议院国土安全委员会与司法委员会就2025年9月30日芝加哥南岸公寓楼移民突袭展开调查。议员致信国土安全部长诺姆和司法部长邦迪，要求说明海关与边境保护局、联邦调查局及烟酒火器管理局的行动细节，包括搜查令依据、被拘留美国公民和儿童人数、使用闪光弹和扎带等战术的理由，以及国土安全部关于 Tren de Aragua 帮派成员说法的证据。","summary_en":"The House Homeland Security and Judiciary Committees launched an investigation into the September 30, 2025 immigration raid on a South Shore apartment building in Chicago. Ranking Members sent a letter to DHS Secretary Noem and Attorney General Bondi demanding details on the operation and the actions of CBP, the FBI and the ATF, including warrants used, the number of U.S. citizens and children detained, and justification for tactics such as flashbang grenades and zip-tying children, as well as evidence for DHS claims about Tren de Aragua.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:40:53.709063+00:00","url":"https://jayapal.house.gov/2025/10/07/homeland-security-and-judiciary-committees-launch-investigation-into-violent-chicago-immigration-raid","content":"10.07.2025\n|\nNews\nHomeland Security and Judiciary Committees Launch Investigation into Violent Chicago Immigration Raid\nWASHINGTON – The House Committees on Homeland Security and the Judiciary launched an investigation into the September 30th immigration raid in Chicago that terrorized residents of a South Shore apartment building.\nRanking Members Bennie G. Thompson (D-MS) and Jamie Raskin (D-MD), Immigration Integrity, Security & Enforcement Subcommittee Ranking Member Pramila Jayapal (D-WA), Border Security & Enforcement Subcommittee Ranking Member Lou Correa (D-CA), Oversight, Investigations & Accountability Subcommittee Ranking Member Shri Thanedar, Constitution & Limited Government Subcommittee Ranking Member Mary Gay Scanlon (D-PA), and Chicago area Representatives Delia C. Ramirez (D-IL) and Chuy García (D-IL) sent a letter to Department of Homeland Security (DHS) Secretary Kristi Noem and Attorney General Pamela Bondi demanding details on the operation and answers on the actions of Customs and Border Protection (CBP), the Federal Bureau of Investigation (FBI) and the Bureau of Alcohol, Tobacco, Firearms and Explosives (ATF) under their control.\n“According to media reports, armed federal agents in military fatigues approached or entered nearly every apartment in the five-story, 130-unit apartment building, using flashbang grenades, busting down doors, and pulling men, women and children from their beds. Agents put residents in zip ties and led them to unmarked vans to wait for hours while handcuffed, with children separated from their parents,” the Members wrote.\n“Reporting indicates that there were U.S. citizens and military veterans among those dragged out of their apartments in zip ties and detained for hours,” the Members added. “They were not told why they were detained, and they were not allowed to contact attorneys. Residents report significant property damage and having their units ransacked. Doors were blown off hinges and holes left in walls. When returning to their apartments, some residents found their items stolen after federal agents left apartments open.”\nAfter making 37 arrests during the operation, DHS claimed, without providing any evidence, that neighborhood was a location frequented by Tren de Aragua members. However, law enforcement authorities have not confirmed that any of the people arrested in this raid were members of Tren de Aragua.\n“It is unacceptable that this violent, heavy-handed immigration enforcement operation put families and children at risk and detained U.S. citizens, while traumatizing an entire community.”\nThe letter presses DHS and DOJ to provide details on warrants used, the number of U.S. citizens and children detained, evidence supporting DHS’s claims of criminality, and explanations for tactics including the use of flashbang grenades, helicopters, and the zip-tying of children.\nClick here to read the full letter.\nIssues: Government Reform & Ethics, Immigration\nShare:\nFacebook\nTwitter\nMail","content_cn":"2025年10月7日\n|\n新闻\n国土安全委员会和司法委员会就芝加哥暴力移民突袭行动启动调查\n华盛顿——众议院国土安全委员会和司法委员会已就9月30日发生在芝加哥、令南岸一栋公寓楼居民感到恐惧的移民突袭行动启动调查。\n资深成员 Bennie G. Thompson（密西西比州民主党）、Jamie Raskin（马里兰州民主党）、移民完整性、安全与执法小组委员会资深成员 Pramila Jayapal（华盛顿州民主党）、边境安全与执法小组委员会资深成员 Lou Correa（加利福尼亚州民主党）、监督、调查与问责小组委员会资深成员 Shri Thanedar、宪法与有限政府小组委员会资深成员 Mary Gay Scanlon（宾夕法尼亚州民主党），以及芝加哥地区众议员 Delia C. Ramirez（伊利诺伊州民主党）和 Chuy García（伊利诺伊州民主党）致函国土安全部（DHS）部长 Kristi Noem 和司法部长 Pamela Bondi，要求提供此次行动的细节，并就其管辖下的海关与边境保护局（CBP）、联邦调查局（FBI）和烟酒枪炮及爆炸物管理局（ATF）的行动作出答复。\n议员们写道：“据媒体报道，身穿军用迷彩服、携带武器的联邦特工接近或进入了这栋五层、130个单元的公寓楼中几乎每一套公寓，使用震爆弹、破门而入，并将男性、女性和儿童从床上拉出。特工用扎带捆住居民，将他们带到无标识面包车旁，在手被铐住的情况下等待数小时，儿童则与父母分离。”\n议员们补充说：“报道表明，被用扎带从公寓中拖出并拘留数小时的人中，有美国公民和退伍军人。他们没有被告知遭拘留的原因，也不被允许联系律师。居民报告称财产受到严重损坏，住所被翻得一片狼藉。门被从铰链上炸脱，墙上留下洞孔。一些居民返回公寓时发现，由于联邦特工离开时让公寓敞开，他们的物品被盗。”\n国土安全部称，此次行动共逮捕37人，并在未提供任何证据的情况下声称该社区是阿拉瓜火车帮成员经常出没的地点。然而，执法部门尚未确认此次突袭中被捕者中有任何人是阿拉瓜火车帮成员。\n“这场暴力、强硬的移民执法行动让家庭和儿童面临风险，并拘留了美国公民，同时给整个社区造成创伤，这是不可接受的。”\n该信函敦促国土安全部和司法部提供所使用搜查令的细节、被拘留的美国公民和儿童人数、支持国土安全部犯罪指控的证据，以及对使用震爆弹、直升机和用扎带捆绑儿童等战术的解释。\n点击此处阅读完整信函。\n议题：政府改革与道德规范、移民\n分享：\nFacebook\nTwitter\n邮件","publish_source":"jayapal.house.gov","publish_time":"2025-10-07T18:30:41+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2233","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"众议员拉斯金、贾亚帕尔再次要求国土安全部与ICE就错误拘留美国公民作出答复","title_en":"Ranking Members Raskin, Jayapal Renew Demand for Answers from DHS, ICE on Wrongful Detainment of U.S. Citizens - Congresswoman Pramila Jayapal","summary_cn":"2025年10月21日，众议院司法委员会资深成员拉斯金与移民小组委员会资深成员贾亚帕尔致信美国国土安全部及移民和海关执法局，再次要求其就持续错误逮捕和拘留美国公民作出答复。信中批评此前回复敷衍，未回应具体问题，并列举芝加哥67岁公民约翰逊被破门拘押近三小时、阿拉巴马州公民加西亚·贝内加斯出示真实身份证仍被拘留等案例，要求提供每起事件详情及防范政策。","summary_en":"On October 21, 2025, Ranking Members Raskin and Jayapal sent a letter renewing demands for answers from the Department of Homeland Security and ICE regarding the wrongful arrest and detention of U.S. citizens. The letter criticizes the Administration's flippant prior response and cites cases including Rodrick Johnson, a 67-year-old U.S. citizen detained in Chicago, and Leonardo Garcia Venegas, detained twice in Alabama despite showing his REAL ID. They seek details on each incident and ICE's preventive policies.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:54:21.113498+00:00","url":"https://jayapal.house.gov/2025/10/21/ranking-members-raskin-jayapal-renew-demand-for-answers-from-dhs-ice-on-wrongful-detainment-of-u-s-citizens","content":"10.21.2025\n|\nNews\nRanking Members Raskin, Jayapal Renew Demand for Answers from DHS, ICE on Wrongful Detainment of U.S. Citizens\nWashington, D.C. (October 21, 2025)—Rep. Jamie Raskin, Ranking Member of the House Judiciary Committee, and Rep. Pramila Jayapal, Ranking Member of the Subcommittee on Immigration Integrity, Security, and Enforcement, sent a letter renewing their demand for answers from the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) and Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) regarding their continuing and escalating wrongful arrest and detainment of U.S. citizens. The Administration has failed to address the Committee’s concerns, even in light of worsening abuses.\n“Why do you continue unlawfully detaining U.S. citizens? In February 2025, we wrote to express our serious concerns that U.S. citizens were being wrongfully detained during immigration enforcement operations. Unfortunately, your response was flippant and unserious. Rather than address the specific questions we posed, you simply reiterated existing policy—without providing any assurance that Department of Homeland Security (DHS) and Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) personnel are actually following that policy. DHS and ICE are doing nothing to acknowledge or protect the fundamental rights of U.S. citizens during immigration raids,” wrote the Ranking Members.\nICE policy explicitly prohibits the detainment of U.S. citizens when conducting immigration enforcement and requires that any U.S. citizenship claims by detainees be promptly and carefully investigated. Yet, DHS and ICE continue to wrongfully detain U.S. citizens—sometimes with violent force—while failing to investigate these cases with the urgency and care required.\nSince the Administration’s response to Judiciary Democrats’ February letter, which contained empty assurances that “ICE has significant protections in place to ensure U.S. citizens are not mistakenly arrested, detained, or removed,” the Administration has wrongfully detained a growing number of U.S. citizens. For example, in Chicago, Rodrick Johnson, a 67-year-old U.S. citizen, was detained during an immigration raid on an apartment building. His door was broken down, and he was dragged out in zip ties and left tied up outside the building for nearly three hours. Another U.S. citizen, Leonardo Garcia Venegas, was detained by ICE twice during worksite raids in Alabama. Agents refused to release him even after he produced his REAL ID.\nIn the wake of these unlawful detainments, the Ranking Members renewed their demand for details on each incident where a U.S. citizen was detained during immigration enforcement activities since the start of the Trump Administration, as well as information on the policies ICE currently has in place to prevent the wrongful detention of U.S. citizens.\nClick here to read the letter.\n###\nIssues: Civil Rights, Immigration\nShare:\nFacebook\nTwitter\nMail","content_cn":"2025年10月21日\n|\n新闻\n众议院司法委员会首席成员拉斯金、杰亚帕尔再次要求国土安全部和移民及海关执法局就错误拘押美国公民作出答复\n\n华盛顿特区（2025年10月21日）——众议院司法委员会首席成员杰米·拉斯金众议员和移民诚信、安全与执法小组委员会首席成员普拉米拉·杰亚帕尔众议员致函，再次要求国土安全部（DHS）和移民及海关执法局（ICE）就其持续且不断升级的错误逮捕和拘押美国公民问题作出答复。即使在虐待行为日益恶化的情况下，政府仍未解决委员会的担忧。\n\n“你们为什么继续非法拘押美国公民？2025年2月，我们致函表达了严重关切：美国公民在移民执法行动中遭到错误拘押。遗憾的是，你们的回复轻率且不严肃。你们没有回答我们提出的具体问题，只是重申现行政策——却没有保证国土安全部（DHS）和移民及海关执法局（ICE）人员确实遵守该政策。在移民突袭行动中，DHS和ICE没有采取任何措施承认或保护美国公民的基本权利。”首席成员们写道。\n\nICE政策明确禁止在执行移民执法时拘押美国公民，并要求对被拘押者提出的任何美国公民身份主张迅速、认真地进行调查。然而，DHS和ICE仍在错误拘押美国公民，有时还使用暴力，同时未能以所要求的紧迫性和谨慎程度调查这些案件。\n\n自政府回应司法委员会民主党议员2月来函以来——该回应空洞地保证“ICE已采取重要保护措施，确保美国公民不会被错误逮捕、拘押或驱逐”——政府错误拘押的美国公民人数却不断增加。例如，在芝加哥，67岁的美国公民罗德里克·约翰逊在一次针对公寓楼的移民突袭行动中被拘押。他的房门被撞破，他被拖出后戴上束带，并被捆在楼外近三个小时。另一名美国公民莱昂纳多·加西亚·韦内加斯在阿拉巴马州的工作场所突袭行动中两次被ICE拘押。即使他出示了REAL ID，特工仍拒绝释放他。\n\n在这些非法拘押发生后，首席成员们再次要求提供自特朗普政府开始以来每一起美国公民在移民执法活动中被拘押事件的详细信息，以及ICE目前为防止错误拘押美国公民而采取的政策信息。\n\n点击此处阅读信函。\n###\n议题：公民权利、移民\n分享：\nFacebook\nTwitter\n邮件","publish_source":"jayapal.house.gov","publish_time":"2025-10-21T13:15:44+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1930","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"国会两院移民事务领袖抨击特朗普政府国土安全部提案：惩罚合法获取医疗与食品援助的移民家庭","title_en":"House and Senate Immigration Leaders Rebuke Trump DHS Proposal That Would Punish Immigrant Families for Lawfully Accessing Health Care and Food Assistance - Congresswoman Pramila Jayapal","summary_cn":"2025年12月22日，国会两院移民事务领袖向美国国土安全部提交正式监管意见，反对特朗普政府拟议的“公共负担不可入境理由”规则。意见指出该提案绕过国会，改写沿用135年的“公共负担”定义，将使用医疗、营养和住房等补充性福利的移民家庭纳入惩罚范围，可能引发移民社区恐慌，导致家庭放弃应得援助，并造成健康恶化、贫困加剧等后果。签署人包括拉斯金、贾亚帕尔、斯科特、德宾、帕迪利亚、桑德斯和怀登，要求国土安全部放弃该规则并维持2022年法规。","summary_en":"On December 22, 2025, House and Senate immigration leaders submitted a formal regulatory comment to the Department of Homeland Security opposing the Trump Administration's proposed 'Public Charge Ground of Inadmissibility' rule. They argue it unlawfully rewrites the 135-year-old meaning of 'public charge' by penalizing immigrants for using supplemental health, nutrition, and housing benefits Congress made available. Signatories include Raskin, Jayapal, Scott, Durbin, Padilla, Sanders, and Wyden, urging DHS to abandon the rule and maintain 2022 regulations.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:44:35.135853+00:00","url":"https://jayapal.house.gov/2025/12/22/house-and-senate-immigration-leaders-rebuke-trump-dhs-proposal-that-would-punish-immigrant-families-for-lawfully-accessing-health-care-and-food-assistance","content":"12.22.2025\n|\nNews\nHouse and Senate Immigration Leaders Rebuke Trump DHS Proposal That Would Punish Immigrant Families for Lawfully Accessing Health Care and Food Assistance\nWashington, D.C. — House and Senate immigration leaders submitted a formal regulatory comment to the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) opposing the Trump Administration’s proposed “Public Charge Ground of Inadmissibility” rule, warning that the proposal unlawfully rewrites longstanding immigration law and would deter immigrant families from accessing basic health, nutrition, and housing assistance they are legally entitled to receive.\nThe proposed rule would circumvent Congress to alter the meaning of “public charge,” a term that for more than 135 years has applied only to individuals who are primarily dependent on the government for subsistence. If an immigrant is determined likely to become a public charge, it can affect their eligibility to enter the U.S. The Trump Administration’s proposal would penalize immigrants for using supplemental benefits like health care, nutrition, or housing assistance that Congress deliberately made available to immigrant populations to support working families.\n“DHS is seeking to circumvent Congress by administratively altering the 135-year-old meaning of the term ‘public charge’ in violation of congressional intent. […] Congress has deliberately rejected the very changes that DHS now seeks to implement administratively in complete defiance of our will and intent,” the Members wrote.\nCongress has repeatedly revisited immigration law without ever redefining “public charge” to include the use of non-cash benefits. Federal agencies have long recognized that programs such as Medicaid, Supplemental Nutrition Assistance Program (SNAP), and housing assistance are supplemental benefits that promote public health, food security, and housing stability to help working families remain self-sufficient.\nDHS’s proposal would ignite widespread fear and confusion in immigrant communities, leading families to forgo medical care, nutrition assistance, and housing support even when they qualify under federal law. DHS itself expressly concedes in the proposed rule that the policy could lead to worse health outcomes, increased poverty, housing instability, and greater use of emergency rooms for basic care—harms that would extend well beyond immigrant households to communities nationwide.\nCongress has consistently made decisions about immigrants’ access to public benefits through eligibility rules, not by barring people from adjusting their immigration status for using those benefits. Recent legislation, including the 2025 reconciliation law, deliberately preserved access to key programs for certain immigrant populations.\nFor these reasons, the Members urge DHS to abandon the rule and maintain the 2022 regulations that reflect congressional intent, protect public health, and ensure that families are not punished for using lawful, life-sustaining assistance.\nThe comment was submitted by Rep. Jamie Raskin, Ranking Member of the House Judiciary Committee; Rep. Pramila Jayapal, Ranking Member of the Subcommittee on Immigration Integrity, Security, and Enforcement; Rep. Robert C. “Bobby” Scott, Ranking Member of the House Committee on Education and the Workforce; Sen. Dick Durbin, Ranking Member of the Senate Judiciary Committee; Sen. Alex Padilla, Ranking Member of the Subcommittee on Border Security and Immigration; Sen. Bernie Sanders; and Sen. Ron Wyden.\nClick here to read the comment.\nIssues: Health Care, Immigration\nShare:\nFacebook\nTwitter\nMail","content_cn":"2025年12月22日\n|\n新闻\n众议院和参议院移民事务领袖严厉批评特朗普国土安全部提案：该提案将因移民家庭依法获取医疗保健和食品援助而惩罚他们\n华盛顿特区——众议院和参议院移民事务领袖向国土安全部（DHS）提交了正式监管意见，反对特朗普政府提出的“不可入境的公共负担理由”规则，并警告称，该提案非法改写长期以来的移民法，将阻止移民家庭获取依法有权享受的基本医疗、营养和住房援助。\n拟议规则将绕过国会，改变“公共负担”的含义。135多年来，该术语仅适用于主要依赖政府维持生计的个人。如果一名移民被认定可能成为公共负担，可能会影响其进入美国的资格。特朗普政府的提案将因移民使用医疗保健、营养或住房援助等补充福利而惩罚他们，而这些福利正是国会有意向移民群体提供、以支持工薪家庭的。\n“DHS试图绕过国会，以行政方式改变‘公共负担’这一已有135年历史的术语含义，违反国会意图。[…]国会一再明确拒绝DHS如今试图以行政方式实施的这些改变，完全无视我们的意愿和意图。”议员们写道。\n国会曾多次重新审视移民法，但从未重新定义“公共负担”以纳入非现金福利的使用。联邦机构长期以来都承认，医疗补助（Medicaid）、补充营养援助计划（SNAP）和住房援助等项目属于补充福利，能够促进公共卫生、食品安全和住房稳定，帮助工薪家庭保持自给自足。\nDHS的提案将​​在移民社区引发广泛恐慌和混乱，导致即使符合联邦法律资格，家庭也放弃医疗护理、营养援助和住房支持。DHS在拟议规则中明确承认，这项政策可能导致更差的健康结果、贫困加剧、住房不稳定，以及为基本护理更多使用急诊室——这些危害将远远超出移民家庭，波及全国各地社区。\n国会一贯通过资格规则决定移民获得公共福利的机会，而不是因为人们使用这些福利就禁止其调整移民身份。包括2025年和解法案在内的近期立法，特意保留了某些移民群体获得关键项目的机会。\n基于这些原因，议员们敦促DHS放弃该规则，维持反映国会意图、保护公共卫生并确保家庭不会因使用合法且维系生活的援助而受到惩罚的2022年法规。\n该意见由以下人士提交：众议院司法委员会首席少数党议员杰米·拉斯金（Jamie Raskin）；移民诚信、安全与执法小组委员会首席少数党议员普拉米拉·贾亚帕尔（Pramila Jayapal）；众议院教育与劳动力委员会首席少数党议员罗伯特·C·“鲍比”·斯科特（Robert C. “Bobby” Scott）；参议院司法委员会首席少数党议员迪克·德宾（Dick Durbin）；边境安全与移民小组委员会首席少数党议员亚历克斯·帕迪利亚（Alex Padilla）；参议员伯尼·桑德斯（Bernie Sanders）；以及参议员罗恩·怀登（Ron Wyden）。\n点击此处阅读该意见。\n议题：医疗保健、移民\n分享：\nFacebook\nTwitter\n邮件","publish_source":"jayapal.house.gov","publish_time":"2025-12-22T21:02:57+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1793","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"众议员贾亚帕尔就国土安全部拨款发表声明","title_en":"Ranking Member Jayapal Statement on DHS Funding - Congresswoman Pramila Jayapal","summary_cn":"美国众议员普拉米拉·贾亚帕尔就包含国土安全部拨款的拨款方案发表声明，表示尽管法案含少量报告要求和执法记录仪及检查资金，但因缺乏对ICE和CBP的问责与约束，她无法支持该法案。她批评ICE和CBP的执法行为，并呼吁在提供司法令状、终止蒙面执法、停止使用私营营利性监狱等保障措施到位前不再拨款。","summary_en":"U.S. Representative Pramila Jayapal released a statement on the appropriations package including Department of Homeland Security funding, saying that despite some reporting requirements and funding for body cameras and inspections, she cannot support the bill without real accountability and guardrails for ICE and CBP. She criticized enforcement actions and called for judicial warrants, an end to masked agents and private for-profit prisons before further funding.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:42:04.325814+00:00","url":"https://jayapal.house.gov/2026/01/20/ranking-member-jayapal-statement-on-dhs-funding","content":"01.20.2026\n|\nNews\nRanking Member Jayapal Statement on DHS Funding\nWASHINGTON, DC — U.S. Representative Pramila Jayapal, Ranking Member of the Immigration, Integrity, Security, and Enforcement Subcommittee, released the following statement regarding the appropriations package, including funding for the Department of Homeland Security (DHS), which will likely come to the House Floor for a vote this week.\n“While this DHS spending bill includes a handful of reporting requirements to the Appropriations Committee, as well as some funding for body cameras and inspections, it simply does not meet the moment we face in this country with the lawlessness of Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) and Customs and Border Protection (CBP) agents. I understand that this is due to the complete refusal of Republicans to hold this Administration accountable. However, without real accountability and guardrails, I simply cannot support this bill.\n“We have seen ICE and DHS descending on cities across this country, racially profiling, and rounding up immigrants and US citizens alike — many of whom have committed no crimes. We have watched in horror as they have dragged people out into the snow and as they have shot and killed US citizens. As they foment this terror and chaos on our streets, 37 people have died in ICE custody since Trump came back to office. Meanwhile, across the country, over 70,000 people are being incarcerated in immigration jails run by private, for-profit prison contractors and being denied due process and bond hearings in Trump’s mass detention effort that dozens of judges have said is not lawful. All of this is dangerous — not just for immigrants but for every single American worried about the erosion of Constitutional rights.\n“As I have said over and over again, I simply cannot vote to give another cent to ICE and CBP until we have real, enforceable guardrails in place to end lawless enforcement, including requiring DHS to get a warrant and end the use of masked agents, to end detention abuses by ending the use of private, for-profit prisons, and to rein in DHS by ensuring that independent investigations can be conducted and meaningful consequences put into place for those who violate constitutional rights. Continuing to fund this agency without these guardrails is an affront to the Constitutional rights of US citizens and immigrants alike, and we must not be complicit in this.”\nIssues: Immigration\nShare:\nFacebook\nTwitter\nMail","content_cn":"2026年1月20日\n|\n新闻\nJayapal谈国土安全部拨款的声明\n华盛顿特区——美国众议员普拉米拉·贾亚帕尔、移民、诚信、安全与执法小组委员会的少数党首席成员，就拨款方案（包括为国土安全部（DHS）提供资金的部分）发表了以下声明。该方案可能于本周提交众议院表决。\n“尽管这项DHS支出法案包含一些向拨款委员会提交报告的要求，以及为执法记录仪和检查提供的部分资金，但它根本无法应对我们国家当前面临的局面：移民与海关执法局（ICE）和海关与边境保护局（CBP）人员肆意违法。我明白，这是因为共和党人完全拒绝追究本届政府的责任。然而，如果没有真正的问责和约束措施，我就无法支持这项法案。\n“我们看到ICE和DHS席卷全国各城市，进行种族画像，并围捕移民和美国公民——其中许多人根本没有犯罪。我们惊恐地看着他们把人拖到雪地里，还枪杀美国公民。在他们煽动街头恐怖与混乱之际，自特朗普重返白宫以来，已有37人死于ICE羁押。与此同时，全国有超过7万人被关押在由私人营利性监狱承包商运营的移民监狱中，并在特朗普的大规模拘留行动中被剥夺正当程序和保释听证；数十名法官已经表示这一做法不合法。所有这一切都很危险——不仅对移民如此，对每一位担心宪法权利遭到侵蚀的美国人也是如此。\n“正如我一再所说，在建立真正可执行的约束措施、结束无法无天的执法之前，我绝不会投票再给ICE和CBP一分钱。这些措施包括要求DHS取得搜查令、结束蒙面特工的使用，通过停止使用私人营利性监狱来结束拘留虐待，并通过确保能够开展独立调查、对侵犯宪法权利者施加有意义的后果来约束DHS。在没有这些约束措施的情况下继续资助该机构，是对美国公民和移民宪法权利的侮辱，我们绝不能成为共犯。”\n议题：移民\n分享：\nFacebook\nTwitter\n邮件","publish_source":"jayapal.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-01-20T22:53:49+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1787","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"众议员贾亚帕尔提出修正案要求ICE停止针对美国公民","title_en":"Ranking Member Jayapal Introduces Amendment to DHS Spending Bill Requiring ICE to End Targeting of US Citizens - Congresswoman Pramila Jayapal","summary_cn":"美国众议员普拉米拉·贾亚帕尔向国土安全部拨款法案提交修正案，拟正式禁止ICE在民事移民执法中拘留或驱逐美国公民。她引用ICE内部指引称其无权逮捕或拘留美国公民，并批评ICE在多地拘留美国公民的行为，呼吁在法案中加入实质性约束措施以问责国土安全部。","summary_en":"U.S. Representative Pramila Jayapal is submitting an amendment to the Department of Homeland Security appropriations bill to formally block ICE from detaining or deporting U.S. citizens during civil immigration enforcement. Citing ICE's own internal guidance that it cannot arrest or detain U.S. citizens, she criticized detentions of citizens and urged meaningful guardrails to hold DHS accountable.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:42:04.551470+00:00","url":"https://jayapal.house.gov/2026/01/21/ranking-member-jayapal-introduces-amendment-to-dhs-spending-bill-requiring-ice-to-end-targeting-of-us-citizens","content":"01.21.2026\n|\nNews\nRanking Member Jayapal Introduces Amendment to DHS Spending Bill Requiring ICE to End Targeting of US Citizens\nWASHINGTON, DC — U.S. Representative Pramila Jayapal, Ranking Member of the Subcommittee on Immigration, Integrity, Security, and Enforcement, is submitting an amendment to the Department of Homeland Security (DHS) appropriations bill to add language that would formally block Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE) from detaining or deporting U.S. citizens while conducting civil immigration enforcement.\n“ICE has been terrorizing communities across this country, kidnapping and detaining immigrants and US citizens alike,” said Jayapal. “In the last few days, we have seen stark examples of this, including an elderly man being walked in the freezing cold without clothes on. At my field hearing in Minnesota, we heard from a woman who was detained and taken to a designated ‘US citizens’ cell in ICE detention. We also heard from a man who stated repeatedly that he was a US citizen as ICE arrested him and agents told him, ‘that don’t matter.’ All of this is illegal and outside the scope of ICE’s jurisdiction. We cannot pass the DHS funding bill without significant and meaningful guardrails to hold DHS accountable and stop their reckless and lawless actions. I hope to see this amendment seriously considered to protect Americans and further work done to overhaul this bill to rein in DHS.”\nReporting shows that ICE has detained hundreds of US citizens, as detention and death in detention have both skyrocketed to all-time highs.\nICE has no authority to arrest, detain, or deport U.S. citizens. Their own internal guidance states, “As a matter of law, ICE cannot assert its civil immigration enforcement authority to arrest and/or detain a U.S. citizen.” U.S. citizens also cannot be deported under U.S. law.\nIssues: Civil Rights, Immigration\nShare:\nFacebook\nTwitter\nMail","content_cn":"2026年1月21日\n|\n新闻\n排名成员贾亚帕尔提出国土安全部支出法案修正案，要求移民与海关执法局停止针对美国公民\n华盛顿特区——众议院移民、诚信、安全与执法小组委员会排名成员普拉米拉·贾亚帕尔（Pramila Jayapal）正在向国土安全部（DHS）拨款法案提交一项修正案，加入相关措辞，正式阻止移民与海关执法局（ICE）在开展民事移民执法时拘留或驱逐美国公民。\n“ICE一直在恐吓全国各地的社区，绑架并拘留移民和美国公民，”贾亚帕尔说。“在过去几天里，我们看到了这方面的鲜明例子，包括一名老人没穿衣服、在严寒中被带走。在我于明尼苏达州举行的现场听证会上，我们听到一名妇女讲述，她被拘留并带到ICE拘留设施内一个指定的‘美国公民’牢房。我们还听到一名男子反复声明自己是美国公民，但ICE逮捕他时，探员告诉他：‘那不重要。’这一切都是非法的，超出了ICE的管辖范围。除非设置重大且有实质意义的护栏，以追究DHS责任并制止其鲁莽且无法无天的行为，否则我们不能通过DHS拨款法案。我希望这项修正案能得到认真考虑，以保护美国人，并进一步开展工作，彻底改革该法案，约束DHS。”\n报道称，ICE已经拘留了数百名美国公民，因为拘留人数和拘留期间死亡人数都飙升至历史最高水平。\nICE无权逮捕、拘留或驱逐美国公民。其内部指引明确写道：“根据法律，ICE不能主张其民事移民执法权来逮捕和/或拘留美国公民。”根据美国法律，美国公民也不能被驱逐。\n议题：公民权利、移民\n分享：\nFacebook\nTwitter\n邮件","publish_source":"jayapal.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-01-21T19:20:36+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1718","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"司法委员会民主党人敦促乔丹主席就明尼阿波利斯国土安全部致命枪击事件举行听证会","title_en":"Judiciary Democrats Press Chairman Jordan for Hearing with Secretary Noem Following Fatal Shootings of American Citizens by DHS in Minneapolis - Congresswoman Pramila Jayapal","summary_cn":"众议院司法委员会民主党人要求主席吉姆·乔丹就明尼阿波利斯两名美国公民被联邦探员枪杀一事举行听证会，并邀请国土安全部长诺姆出席。议员指出，亚历克斯·杰弗里·普雷蒂和蕾妮·妮可·古德在行使宪法权利时被枪杀，而诺姆在无证据情况下将两人称为“国内恐怖分子”，视频证据与国土安全部说法相矛盾。议员认为国土安全部试图掩盖真相，需由委员会调查。","summary_en":"House Judiciary Committee Democrats demanded Chairman Jim Jordan hold a hearing with DHS Secretary Kristi Noem following the fatal shootings of two U.S. citizens in Minneapolis by federal agents. The lawmakers said Alex Jeffrey Pretti and Renée Nicole Good were killed while exercising their constitutional rights, and that Noem labeled both victims 'domestic terrorists' without evidence, while video footage contradicts DHS claims. They argued the alleged DHS cover-up requires committee inquiry.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:20:51.561218+00:00","url":"https://jayapal.house.gov/2026/01/27/judiciary-democrats-press-chairman-jordan-for-hearing-with-secretary-noem-following-fatal-shootings-of-american-citizens-by-dhs-in-minneapolis","content":"01.27.2026\n|\nNews\nJudiciary Democrats Press Chairman Jordan for Hearing with Secretary Noem Following Fatal Shootings of American Citizens by DHS in Minneapolis\nWashington, D.C. (January 27, 2026)—Today, House Judiciary Committee Democrats demanded Chairman Jim Jordan hold a House Judiciary Committee hearing with Department of Homeland Security (DHS) Secretary Kristi Noem following the fatal federal agent shootings of two U.S. citizens in Minneapolis who were peacefully exercising their First and Second Amendment rights.\nThe House Judiciary Committee Majority’s own website says that “the Committee’s oversight responsibility for the Departments of Justice and Homeland Security” is “[p]articularly important in our time.”  Yet not a single witness from DHS has appeared before the Judiciary Committee during this Congress.“This Committee has devoted years of oversight to alleged First Amendment violations by social media companies and has subpoenaed foreign companies over censorship concerns abroad. Mr. Chairman: look what’s happening right in front of our eyes. Federal agents have shot dead two American citizens in the past two weeks for doing no more than exercising their fully protected rights to protest, observe, and record law enforcement in public,” wrote the Members.\nThe lawmakers want answers regarding the killings of Alex Jeffrey Pretti, an ICU nurse and lawful gun owner who was filming law enforcement activity, and Renée Nicole Good, an unarmed mother of three who was observing an ICE operation from her vehicle.\nImmediately following the shootings, Secretary Noem publicly labeled both victims “domestic terrorists” without evidence. But video footage viewed nationwide and verified by multiple news outlets contradicts DHS’s claims and all but proves that the shootings were without any legal justification.\nFootage shows Mr. Pretti holding a cell phone when he was tackled by multiple agents and shot repeatedly in the back. Video also appears to show agents removing a firearm from his possession before another agent fired ten shots. Minneapolis Police have confirmed that Mr. Pretti had a valid permit to carry under Minnesota law and no criminal record.\nSimilarly, video evidence shows that Ms. Good was shot while seated in her car observing an ICE operation. Although DHS claimed she attempted to run over agents, footage shows her steering her car away from the agent who fired three shots into her vehicle.\n“The attempted cover-up by DHS requires an inquiry by the House Judiciary Committee. Mr. Chairman, if your commitment to the First and Second Amendments—not to mention the Fifth Amendment’s guarantee of due process—is genuine, as we have always believed it to be, then this Committee cannot look away when federal agents gun down Americans for peacefully exercising their constitutional rights,” wrote the Members.\nThe lawmakers’ demand comes amid reports that Secretary Noem will testify before the Senate Judiciary Committee on March 3.\nClick here to read the letter to Chairman Jordan.\nIssues: Civil Rights, Immigration\nShare:\nFacebook\nTwitter\nMail","content_cn":"01.27.2026\n|\n新闻\n司法委员会民主党议员敦促主席乔丹在国土安全部长诺姆之后就明尼阿波利斯发生的国土安全部枪杀美国公民事件举行听证会\n华盛顿特区（2026年1月27日）——今天，众议院司法委员会民主党议员要求主席吉姆·乔丹在国土安全部（DHS）部长克里斯蒂·诺姆就明尼阿波利斯两名美国公民遭联邦特工致命枪击一事举行众议院司法委员会听证会。这两名公民当时正在和平行使其《第一修正案》和《第二修正案》权利。\n众议院司法委员会多数党方面自己的网站称，“委员会对司法部和国土安全部的监督责任”在“我们这个时代尤为重要”。然而，在本届国会期间，国土安全部没有一名证人出席司法委员会。“本委员会多年来一直对社交媒体公司涉嫌违反《第一修正案》的行为进行监督，并因海外审查问题而传唤外国公司。主席先生：看看正在我们眼前发生的一切。过去两周内，联邦特工枪杀了两名美国公民，仅仅因为他们行使了受到充分保护的抗议、观察和在公共场所记录执法活动的权利，”议员们写道。\n这些议员希望就以下两起杀人事件得到答复：亚历克斯·杰弗里·普雷蒂是一名重症监护室护士和合法持枪者，当时正在拍摄执法活动；勒妮·妮可·古德是一名未携带武器的三孩母亲，当时正从车内观察一场移民及海关执法局（ICE）行动。\n枪击发生后，部长诺姆立即在没有证据的情况下公开将两名受害者都称为“国内恐怖分子”。但在全国范围内播出并经多家新闻机构核实的视频画面与国土安全部的说法相矛盾，几乎证明这些枪击没有任何法律依据。\n画面显示，普雷蒂先生手持手机时被多名特工扑倒，并被从背后反复射击。视频似乎还显示，特工从他身上取走了一把枪，随后另一名特工开了十枪。明尼阿波利斯警方已确认，普雷蒂先生持有根据明尼苏达州法律颁发的有效携枪许可证，且没有犯罪记录。\n同样，视频证据显示，古德女士坐在车内观察ICE行动时遭到枪击。尽管国土安全部声称她试图驾车撞向特工，但画面显示，她正将车辆驶离向她开出三枪的那名特工。\n“国土安全部企图掩盖事实，要求众议院司法委员会展开调查。主席先生，如果您对《第一修正案》和《第二修正案》的承诺——更不用说《第五修正案》关于正当程序的保障——如我们一直相信的那样是真诚的，那么当联邦特工枪杀和平行使宪法权利的美国人时，本委员会就不能视而不见，”议员们写道。\n议员们提出这一要求之际，有报道称部长诺姆将于3月3日在参议院司法委员会作证。\n点击此处阅读致主席乔丹的信。\n议题：公民权利、移民\n分享：\nFacebook\nTwitter\n邮件","publish_source":"jayapal.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-01-27T21:48:13+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1661","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"贾亚帕尔就国土安全部拨款投反对票发表声明","title_en":"Jayapal Statement on DHS Funding “No” Vote - Congresswoman Pramila Jayapal","summary_cn":"美国众议员普拉米拉·贾亚帕尔就其对重新开放国土安全部的持续决议投反对票发表声明，称在缺乏可执行约束的情况下不会支持继续向国土安全部拨款。她呼吁立即撤出相关执法人员，要求正当程序、司法令状和保释听证、强制使用执法记录仪、取消蒙面执法，并对不当行为进行独立调查。","summary_en":"U.S. Representative Pramila Jayapal released a statement on her 'no' vote on the continuing resolution to reopen the Department of Homeland Security, saying she will not support further funding without enforceable guardrails. She called for removing agents from cities, due process, judicial warrants and bond hearings, mandatory body cameras, an end to masks, and independent investigations into misconduct.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:35:16.720257+00:00","url":"https://jayapal.house.gov/2026/02/03/jayapal-statement-on-dhs-funding-no-vote","content":"02.03.2026\n|\nNews\nJayapal Statement on DHS Funding “No” Vote\nWASHINGTON, DC — U.S. Representative Pramila Jayapal, Ranking Member of the Immigration, Integrity, Security, and Enforcement Committee, released the following statement regarding her “no” vote on the continuing resolution to reopen the Department of Homeland Security (DHS).\n“I have been clear since the beginning of this funding fight: I will not be complicit in sending another dime to DHS as they continue their reign of terror on the Twin Cities and communities across this country.\n“There is nothing that I am calling for today that I will not continue to call for over the next 10 days while Congress negotiates. We must immediately get these agents out of our cities. There must be due process, a requirement for judicial warrants and bond hearings, every agent must not only have a bodycam but be required to use it, take off their masks, and in cases of misconduct, there must be immediate, independent investigations. We cannot fold on our demands — our very democracy and people’s Constitutional rights are at risk.\n“We cannot trust this DHS, which already has received an unprecedented funding spike for Immigration and Customs Enforcement (ICE), to operate within the bounds of our Constitution or our laws. And for that reason, we cannot continue to fund them without significant and enforceable guardrails.”\nIssues: Immigration\nShare:\nFacebook\nTwitter\nMail","content_cn":"2026年2月3日\n|\n新闻\nJayapal就国土安全部拨款“反对”票发表声明\n华盛顿特区——移民、诚信、安全与执法委员会首席少数党委员、美国众议员普拉米拉·贾亚帕尔就她对重新开放国土安全部（DHS）的持续决议投下“反对”票发表了以下声明。\n“自这场拨款斗争开始以来，我一直明确表示：在国土安全部继续对双子城和全国各地社区实施恐怖统治之际，我不会同谋向DHS再提供一分钱。\n“今天我所要求的一切，在国会进行谈判的未来10天里，我都不会停止要求。我们必须立即让这些特工撤出我们的城市。必须提供正当程序，要求获得司法搜查令并举行保释听证；每名特工不仅必须配备随身摄像机，还必须被要求使用；摘下他们的面具；在发生不当行为的情况下，必须立即展开独立调查。我们不能放弃要求——我们整个民主制度和人民的宪法权利都处于危险之中。\n“我们不能信任这个DHS。它已经为移民及海关执法局（ICE）获得了前所未有的资金激增，却无法保证在宪法或法律的范围内运作。因此，在没有重大且可执行的保障措施之前，我们不能继续为其提供资金。”\n议题：移民\n分享：\nFacebook\nTwitter\n邮件","publish_source":"jayapal.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-02-03T19:29:58+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1271","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"贾亚帕尔就反对国土安全部拨款法案投票发表声明","title_en":"Jayapal Statement on DHS Funding NO Vote - Congresswoman Pramila Jayapal","summary_cn":"美国众议员普拉米拉·贾亚帕尔就众议院共和党提出的国土安全部持续决议投下反对票并发表声明。她表示，在ICE和CBP未进行重大改革前不会为其提供资金，并批评共和党拒绝通过参议院一致同意、为TSA、FEMA和海岸警卫队等机构拨款的法案，反而以程序手段推动一项无望在参议院通过、将危机再拖延60天的提案。她呼吁众议院共和党人将参议院法案付诸表决。","summary_en":"US Representative Pramila Jayapal released a statement after voting NO on House Republicans' Department of Homeland Security continuing resolution. She said she will not fund ICE or CBP without major reforms, and criticized Republicans for refusing to pass the Senate's unanimous-consent bill funding TSA, FEMA and the Coast Guard, instead using procedural tricks to advance a proposal with no hope of passing the Senate that extends the crisis another 60 days. She urged House Republicans to bring the Senate bill to a vote.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:38:54.369203+00:00","url":"https://jayapal.house.gov/2026/03/27/jayapal-statement-on-dhs-funding-no-vote-2","content":"03.27.2026\n|\nNews\nJayapal Statement on DHS Funding NO Vote\nWASHINGTON, DC — U.S. Representative Pramila Jayapal (WA-07), Ranking Member of the Subcommittee on Immigration, Integrity, Security, and Enforcement, released the following statement after voting NO on House Republicans’ Department of Homeland Security (DHS) continuing resolution.\n“I have been clear since the start of the appropriations process: I will not vote to give Trump’s ICE or CBP another cent without major reforms. ICE and CBP agents have killed American citizens on the streets, terrorized communities, and forever traumatized families and children. Republicans in the House and Senate continue to refuse to implement any meaningful reforms — it appears they want ICE and CBP to continue their lawless reign of terror against American families and communities.\n“In the face of this Republican refusal, Democrats have called for weeks to pass funding for everything except ICE and CBP so that TSA agents, FEMA, and the Coast Guard, among other agencies, can get funded. Finally, Senate Republicans saw the light and did just that last night in a unanimous consent vote. However, House Republicans know just how to snatch defeat from the jaws of victory and refused to pass the unanimous Senate bill, instead passing a ridiculous proposal to kick the can down the road for another 60 days with a bill that has absolutely no hope of passing the Senate. Late on a Friday night, Republicans are using procedural tricks to pass their proposal that stalls any progress and leaves TSA unfunded, without any debate before the American people. This will only extend this crisis and create yet more chaos and cruelty for the American people.\n“It is time for House Republicans to get to work and bring the Senate bill to a vote so we can pass it and fund TSA, FEMA, and the Coast Guard.”\nIssues: Foreign Affairs & National Security, Immigration, Public Safety & Criminal Justice\nShare:\nFacebook\nTwitter\nMail","content_cn":"2026年3月27日\n|\n新闻\n贾亚帕尔就DHS拨款投反对票发表声明\n华盛顿特区——美国众议员普拉米拉·贾亚帕尔（华盛顿州第07选区），移民、诚信、安全与执法小组委员会首席少数党成员，在投票反对众议院共和党提出的国土安全部（DHS）持续决议后发表以下声明。\n“自拨款程序开始以来，我一直明确表示：在没有重大改革的情况下，我不会投票再给特朗普的ICE或CBP一分钱。ICE和CBP特工在街头杀害美国公民，恐吓社区，并给家庭和儿童造成永久创伤。众议院和参议院的共和党人继续拒绝实施任何有意义的改革——看来他们希望ICE和CBP继续对美国家庭和社区进行无法无天的恐怖统治。\n“面对共和党的这种拒绝，民主党人已呼吁数周，通过除ICE和CBP以外一切事项的拨款，让TSA特工、FEMA和海岸警卫队等机构能够获得资金。最终，参议院共和党人昨晚看清了形势，并通过一致同意表决做到了这一点。然而，众议院共和党人深谙如何在胜利边缘攫取失败之道，拒绝通过参议院一致通过的法案，转而通过一项荒谬提案，以一项绝无可能在参议院获得通过的法案再将问题拖延60天。周五深夜，共和党人正利用程序手段通过他们的提案；该提案阻碍任何进展，使TSA得不到拨款，而且未在美国人民面前进行任何辩论。这只会延长这场危机，并为美国人民制造更多混乱与残酷。\n“现在是众议院共和党人开始工作、将参议院法案付诸表决的时候了，这样我们才能通过它并为TSA、FEMA和海岸警卫队提供资金。”\n议题：外交与国家安全、移民、公共安全与刑事司法\n分享：\nFacebook\nTwitter\n邮件","publish_source":"jayapal.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-03-28T03:44:01+00:00"}},{"id":"news-825","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"贾亚帕尔就揭露温恩惩教中心状况的国土安全部监察长报告发表声明","title_en":"Jayapal Statement on Damning DHS OIG Report Detailing Conditions at Winn Correctional Center - Congresswoman Pramila Jayapal","summary_cn":"美国众议员普拉米拉·贾亚帕尔就国土安全部监察长办公室发布的报告发表声明。该报告详述了温恩惩教中心在食品安全、医疗护理和武力使用等方面严重违反标准的情况，包括厨房天花板破洞漏水、食品储存温度超标、医疗文件未及时更新以及武力使用未按规定上报等。贾亚帕尔呼吁国土安全部立即撤资不合格拘留中心，并要求国会通过其《被拘留移民尊严法案》。","summary_en":"US Representative Pramila Jayapal released a statement on a Department of Homeland Security Office of Inspector General report detailing serious violations of standards for food safety, medical care and use of force at the Winn Correctional Center. The report cited a hole in the kitchen ceiling, leaking vents, food stored above safe temperatures, improperly updated medical documents and unreported use-of-force incidents. Jayapal called on DHS to withdraw funding from substandard detention centers and urged Congress to pass her Dignity for Detained Immigrants Act.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:22:44.549953+00:00","url":"https://jayapal.house.gov/2026/06/04/jayapal-statement-on-damning-dhs-oig-report-detailing-conditions-at-winn-correctional-center","content":"06.04.2026\n|\nNews\nJayapal Statement on Damning DHS OIG Report Detailing Conditions at Winn Correctional Center\nWASHINGTON, D.C. — U.S. Representative Pramila Jayapal (WA-07), Ranking Member of the Subcommittee on Immigration Integrity, Security, and Enforcement, released the following statement regarding a report released by the Department of Homeland Security Office of Inspector General (DHS OIG) that detailed serious violations of standards for food safety, medical care, and use of force, among other breaches at the Winn Correctional Center.\n“This DHS OIG report details what we have heard from detained immigrants across the country — that these detention centers have violated numerous required standards and are putting people’s health and safety at serious risk.\n“Among other major issues, the report details serious safety and sanitation issues, including a massive hole in the ceiling and leaking vents that left pools of water in the kitchen, risking food safety; it showed that food was stored above safe temperatures, with both freezers and refrigerators running too hot; it showed that medical documents were not properly updated; and in a major breach of protocol, use of force instances were not being properly reported — with incidents including a banned choke hold being used on a detained person and the use of a pen to stab a detained person’s hand.\n“An unprecedented forty-nine people have died in immigration detention since Trump returned to office. And this report verifies what many immigrants have stated is happening at these private, for-profit detention centers across the country. DHS must immediately withdraw funding from the numerous detention centers that consistently do not meet the minimum required standards for housing immigrant detainees. For those that remain, DHS must require facilities to take immediate corrective action and engage in serious oversight of these for-profit prison operators who are prioritizing their cash coffers over meeting basic health and safety standards.\n“Congress must immediately step in and pass my Dignity for Detained Immigrants Act to end the use of private, for-profit detention centers, end the use of mandatory detention, update and implement robust minimum requirements for care, and conduct urgent oversight at other facilities across the country.”\nInformation from other facilities includes reports that detained people are being held in inhumane living conditions, with reports of overcrowding forcing 35 men to share one toilet and sleep head to toe on concrete floors, of people being served only a cup of rice a day or rotting food, and of people having their medications withheld or being denied necessary medical care. Further, the Trump Administration has restarted the practice of detaining families and children, which has long been criticized as unsafe and inflicting irreversible harm on children.\nJayapal leads the Dignity for Detained Immigrants Act to enact guardrails and oversight on immigration detention, and to ensure civil and human rights are protected. She also held an accountability hearing on Trump’s Detention Abuses in December of 2025.\nIssues: Immigration\nShare:\nFacebook\nTwitter\nMail","content_cn":"2026年06月04日\n|\n新闻\nJayapal就国土安全部监察长办公室详述温恩惩教中心状况的严厉报告发表声明\n华盛顿特区——美国众议员Pramila Jayapal（华盛顿州第07选区）、移民诚信、安全与执法小组委员会少数党首席成员，就国土安全部监察长办公室（DHS OIG）发布的一份报告发表以下声明。该报告详述了温恩惩教中心在食品安全、医疗照护和使用武力标准等方面的严重违规，以及其他违规情况。\n“这份DHS OIG报告详述了我们从全国各地被拘留移民那里听到的情况——这些拘留中心违反了众多强制性标准，正使人们的健康与安全面临严重风险。\n“除其他重大问题外，报告还详述了严重的安全和卫生问题，包括天花板上的一个巨大破洞和漏水的通风口，使厨房内积起水洼，危及食品安全；报告显示，食物储存在不安全的温度下，冷冻柜和冰箱的运行温度都过高；报告显示，医疗文件未得到妥善更新；而且，作为对程序的重大违反，使用武力的事件没有得到妥善报告——事件包括对一名被拘留者使用被禁止的锁喉动作，以及用笔刺伤一名被拘留者的手。\n“自特朗普重返执政以来，已有前所未有的49人在移民拘留期间死亡。这份报告证实了许多移民所称的、正在全国各地这些私营营利性拘留中心发生的情况。DHS必须立即撤回对众多持续未达到安置移民被拘留者最低强制标准的拘留中心的资金。对于仍保留的中心，DHS必须要求设施立即采取纠正措施，并对这些将充实自身金库置于满足基本健康与安全标准之上的营利性监狱运营商进行严肃监督。\n“国会必须立即介入，通过我的《被拘留移民尊严法案》，终止使用私营营利性拘留中心，终止强制拘留，更新并落实有力的最低照护要求，并对全国其他设施进行紧急监督。”\n其他设施的信息包括报告称，被拘留者被置于不人道的生活条件中；有报告称，拥挤迫使35名男子共用一个厕所，并在水泥地板上头脚相对地睡觉；有人每天只得到一杯米饭或腐烂的食物；还有人的药物被扣留，或被拒绝提供必要的医疗照护。此外，特朗普政府已重启拘留家庭和儿童的做法，该做法长期以来一直因不安全并对儿童造成不可逆转的伤害而受到批评。\nJayapal牵头推动《被拘留移民尊严法案》，以对移民拘留建立保障措施和监督，并确保公民权利和人权得到保护。她还于2025年12月举行了一场关于特朗普拘留虐待行为的问责听证会。\n议题：移民\n分享：\nFacebook\nTwitter\n邮件","publish_source":"jayapal.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-06-04T13:58:28+00:00"}},{"id":"news-805","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"FBI公布新的头号欺诈通缉犯名单","title_en":"FBI's new list of most wanted fraudsters","summary_cn":"美国联邦调查局周四宣布启动“头号欺诈通缉犯名单”，这是一份新的通缉名单，专门用于公开识别被控欺诈美国民众的个人。报道称，任何掌握这些逃犯下落信息的人可通过tips.fbi.gov网站、拨打1-800-CALL-FBI电话或联系最近的FBI外地办事处提交线索。","summary_en":"The Federal Bureau of Investigation on Thursday announced the launch of its Most Wanted Fraudsters List, a new wanted list dedicated to publicly identifying individuals charged with defrauding the American people. Anyone with information about the whereabouts of these fugitives can submit tips at tips.fbi.gov, by calling 1-800-CALL-FBI, or by contacting the nearest FBI field office.","tag":"security","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:23:44.715385+00:00","url":"https://jcpost.com/posts/887e287b-899c-49cd-bc7d-80159b129983","content":"The Federal Bureau of Investigation on Thursday announced the launch of its Most Wanted Fraudsters List, a new wanted list dedicated to publicly identifying individuals charged with defrauding the American people.FBI\nAnyone with information about the whereabouts of these fugitives can submit tips at http://tips.fbi.gov, by calling 1-800-CALL-FBI, or by contacting the nearest FBI field office: Click here for additional information on the list.","content_cn":"联邦调查局周四宣布推出“最受通缉诈骗犯名单”，这是一个新的通缉名单，专门公开确认被控欺诈美国民众的个人。FBI\n\n任何掌握这些逃犯下落信息的人，都可以通过http://tips.fbi.gov提交线索，拨打1-800-CALL-FBI，或联系最近的FBI外勤办公室：点击此处获取该名单的更多信息。","publish_source":"jcpost.com","publish_time":"2026-06-06T07:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-2869","ktid":1000110,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1000110","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"前FBI局长科米就“8647”帖文接受特勤局问询","title_en":"Ex-FBI Director meets with Secret Service over '8647' post","summary_cn":"据美联社报道，前美国联邦调查局（FBI）局长詹姆斯·科米因在Instagram发布贝壳排列成“86 47”的照片，于周五接受特勤局问询。共和党人认为该帖是对总统特朗普的暴力暗示，科米否认并删除帖文，称未意识到数字与暴力相关。FBI局长帕特尔表示该局也在支持调查。特朗普称科米清楚其含义，是否起诉将由司法部长邦迪决定。报道回顾了特朗普与科米自2017年解职以来的紧张关系。","summary_en":"Former FBI Director James Comey was interviewed by the Secret Service on Friday over an Instagram post showing seashells forming '86 47,' which Republicans called a call for violence against President Trump. Comey denied intent and deleted the post. FBI Director Kash Patel said the bureau is supporting the investigation. Trump said Comey knew what it meant, with any charging decision left to Attorney General Bondi. The report recounts the fraught Trump-Comey relationship since Comey's 2017 firing.","tag":"risk","founddate":"2026-09-24T22:29:24.067655+00:00","url":"https://jcpost.com/posts/ac090267-8836-49f5-8e23-f0413eaed56e","content":"From Comey's now deleted InstagramBy  REBECCA SANTANA and ERIC TUCKERWASHINGTON (AP) — Former FBI Director James Comey was being interviewed by the Secret Service on Friday about a social media post that Republicans insisted was a call for violence against President Donald Trump, according to a law enforcement official.The interview is part of an ongoing Trump administration investigation and is expected to help investigators assess the purpose and intent of the post and whether Comey intended to communicate a threat to the president, which he flatly denied. Any decision on whether charges should be filed would be up to Attorney General Pam Bondi, Trump said Friday, though there’s a high bar in proving that comments or posts amount to direct threats of violence.The official who confirmed the interview, which is standard for the Secret Service while investigating comments perceived as potentially threatening, was not authorized to discuss the matter by name and spoke on condition of anonymity to The Associated Press.At issue is an Instagram post from Thursday in which Comey wrote “cool shell formation on my beach walk” under a picture of seashells that appeared to form the shapes for “86 47.”Merriam-Webster, the dictionary used by The Associated Press, says 86 is slang meaning “to throw out,” “to get rid of” or “to refuse service to.” It notes: “Among the most recent senses adopted is a logical extension of the previous ones, with the meaning of ‘to kill.’ We do not enter this sense, due to its relative recency and sparseness of use.”Numerous Trump administration officials, including Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem, asserted that Comey was advocating the assassination of Trump, the 47th president. FBI Director Kash Patel said the bureau was also supporting the investigation.Asked about it Friday during a Fox News interview, Trump said: “He knew exactly what that meant. A child knows what that meant. If you’re the FBI director and you don’t know what that meant, that meant assassination. And it says it loud and clear.”He deflected a question on what he thought should happen, saying the decision would be up to Bondi.The post was deleted Thursday after it was made, with Comey subsequently writing: “I posted earlier a picture of some shells I saw today on a beach walk, which I assumed were a political message. I didn’t realize some folks associate those numbers with violence.Trump and Comey have had a fraught dynamic dating back nearly a decade.Comey was the FBI director when Trump took office in 2017, having been appointed four years earlier by then-President Barack Obama and serving before that as a senior Justice Department official in President George W. Bush’s administration.But the relationship was strained from the start, including after Comey resisted a request by Trump at a private dinner to pledge his personal loyalty to the president -- an overture that so unnerved the FBI director that he documented it in a contemporaneous memorandum.Trump fired Comey in May 2017 amid an FBI investigation into potential ties between Russia and Trump’s presidential campaign. That inquiry, later taken over by special counsel Robert Mueller, would ultimately find that while Russia interfered in the 2016 election and the Trump team welcomed the help, there was insufficient evidence to prove a criminal collaboration.","content_cn":"来自科米现已删除的 Instagram\n作者：REBECCA SANTANA 和 ERIC TUCKER\n华盛顿（美联社）——据一名执法官员称，前 FBI 局长詹姆斯·科米周五正接受特勤局问询，事由是一则社交媒体帖子；共和党人坚称该帖是在呼吁对总统唐纳德·特朗普实施暴力。\n\n该问询是特朗普政府持续调查的一部分，预计将帮助调查人员评估该帖的目的和意图，以及科米是否意图向总统传达威胁；科米对此予以断然否认。特朗普周五表示，是否应提出指控将由司法部长帕姆·邦迪决定，不过要证明评论或帖子构成直接暴力威胁，门槛很高。\n\n确认了该问询的这名官员未获授权以姓名讨论此事，并在匿名条件下向美联社发表谈话。特勤局在调查被视为可能构成威胁的评论时进行问询，属于标准程序。\n\n争议焦点是一则周四的 Instagram 帖子。科米在一张看起来由贝壳排列成“86 47”形状的照片下写道：“我在海滩散步时看到很酷的贝壳造型。”\n\n美联社使用的《韦氏词典》称，86 是俚语，意为“扔掉”“除掉”或“拒绝提供服务”。词典指出：“最近被采用的含义中，有一种是此前含义的逻辑延伸，即‘杀死’之意。由于这一含义出现相对较晚且使用稀少，我们未将其收录。”\n\n包括国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆在内的多名特朗普政府官员宣称，科米是在鼓吹暗杀第47任总统特朗普。FBI 局长卡什·帕特尔表示，该局也在支持这项调查。\n\n周五在接受福克斯新闻采访时被问及此事，特朗普说：“他完全知道那是什么意思。一个孩子都知道那是什么意思。如果你是 FBI 局长，却不知道那是什么意思，那意思就是暗杀。而且它说得响亮又清楚。”\n\n他回避了有关他认为应如何处理的问题，称决定将由邦迪作出。\n\n该帖子在周四发布后被删除，科米随后写道：“我早些时候发布了一张今天在海滩散步时看到的一些贝壳的照片，我以为那是一则政治信息。我没有意识到有些人把那些数字与暴力联系在一起。\n\n特朗普与科米之间紧张的关系可追溯至近十年前。\n\n科米在特朗普于2017年上任时担任 FBI 局长。他四年前由时任总统巴拉克·奥巴马任命，此前曾在乔治·W·布什总统任内担任司法部高级官员。\n\n但两人的关系从一开始就很紧张，包括科米在一次私人晚宴上拒绝特朗普要求其宣誓对总统个人效忠之后——这一提议令 FBI 局长十分不安，以至于他在当时的一份备忘录中记录了此事。\n\n2017年5月，特朗普在 FBI 调查俄罗斯与特朗普总统竞选团队之间可能存在的联系期间解雇了科米。这项调查后来由特别检察官罗伯特·穆勒接手，最终认定，尽管俄罗斯干预了2016年选举，且特朗普团队欢迎这种帮助，但证据不足以证明存在犯罪性的合作。","publish_source":"jcpost.com","publish_time":"2025-05-16T07:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1693","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS discovery","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"杰弗里斯领袖：“特朗普和共和党人承诺降低美国生活成本，共和党的国土安全部却在冷血地杀害美国人”","title_en":"LEADER JEFFRIES: “DONALD TRUMP AND REPUBLICANS PROMISED TO CUT COSTS IN AMERICA. INSTEAD, THE REPUBLICAN DEPARTMENT OF HOMELAND SECURITY IS CUTTING DOWN AMERICAN LIVESIN COLD BLOOD.” – Congressman Hakeem Jeffries","summary_cn":"2026年1月29日，美国众议院民主党领袖哈基姆·杰弗里斯举行新闻发布会，批评特朗普政府执政一年来美国生活成本全面失控，包括住房、食品、电力和医疗费用上涨，并指责共和党通过的法案削减了医疗补助。他特别抨击由克里斯蒂·诺姆领导的国土安全部行为失控，称其“冷血地杀害美国人”，并呼吁在涉及移民和海关执法局及海关与边境保护局的拨款法案推进前，对国土安全部进行重大改革。","summary_en":"On January 29, 2026, House Democratic Leader Hakeem Jeffries held a press conference criticizing the Trump administration after one year in office, saying the cost of living is out of control, including housing, groceries, electricity and healthcare, and accusing Republicans of enacting the largest Medicaid cut in history. He specifically attacked the Department of Homeland Security under Kristi Noem as out of control, saying it is 'cutting down American lives in cold blood,' and called for dramatic change at DHS before any appropriations bill related to ICE or CBP proceeds.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-24T20:40:11.757674+00:00","url":"https://jeffries.house.gov/2026/01/29/leader-jeffries-donald-trump-and-republicans-promised-to-cut-costs-in-america-instead-the-republican-department-of-homeland-security-is-cutting-down-american-livesin-cold-blood","content":"January 29th, 2026\n|\nPress Release\nLEADER JEFFRIES: “DONALD TRUMP AND REPUBLICANS PROMISED TO CUT COSTS IN AMERICA. INSTEAD, THE REPUBLICAN DEPARTMENT OF HOMELAND SECURITY IS CUTTING DOWN AMERICAN LIVESIN COLD BLOOD.”\nToday, House Democratic Leader Hakeem Jeffries a held a press conference where he highlighted how Donald Trump and Kristi Noem’s Department of Homeland Security are behaving in an out-of-control manner while Republicans continue to abdicate their responsibility to lower costs and deliver an economy that makes life better for hardworking American taxpayers.\nLEADER JEFFRIES: One year into the Trump administration, the situation here in America is a complete and total disaster. Donald Trump and Republicans have failed the American people in every possible way. Cost of living is completely and totally out of control. Housing costs, out of control. Grocery costs, out of control. Electricity bills, out of control. Healthcare costs, out of control. Child care costs, out of control. America is way too expensive and Donald Trump and the Republican Party has done nothing about it. Under Republican policies, costs haven’t gone down in America, costs have gone up, including for reasons that relate directly to Trump’s tariffs, which have increased costs by thousands of dollars per year on everyday Americans.\nWe have a broken healthcare system and a Republican healthcare crisis. Republicans have enacted the largest cut to Medicaid in American history. Hospitals, nursing homes and community-based health clinics have closed because of toxic Republican policies in the One Big Ugly Bill. And Republicans in the Senate refuse to extend the Affordable Care Act tax credits, which is going to skyrocket healthcare costs for tens of millions of Americans who will be unable to afford to go see a doctor when they need one.\nDonald Trump and Republicans promised to cut costs in America. Instead, the Republican Department of Homeland Security is cutting down American lives in cold blood. It’s completely and totally unacceptable. Taxpayer dollars should be used to make life more affordable for the American people, not brutalize everyday Americans or kill American citizens. But that’s exactly what’s happening right now in the United States of America, which is why dramatic change is needed with the Department of Homeland Security before any appropriations bill related to ICE or CBP proceeds. That’s the Democratic position, because that’s the position of the American people. Full press conference can be watched here.\n###\nBack to News\nShare:\nFacebook\nTwitter","content_cn":"2026年1月29日\n|\n新闻稿\n杰弗里斯领袖：“唐纳德·特朗普和共和党人承诺降低美国的成本。相反，共和党领导的国土安全部正在冷血地夺走美国人的生命。”\n今天，众议院民主党领袖 Hakeem Jeffries 举行了新闻发布会，指出唐纳德·特朗普和 Kristi Noem 领导的国土安全部正以失控的方式行事，而共和党人继续逃避降低成本、提供一个让辛勤工作的美国纳税人生活更美好之经济的责任。\n杰弗里斯领袖：特朗普政府执政一年后，美国的局势是一场彻头彻尾的灾难。唐纳德·特朗普和共和党人在所有可能的方面都辜负了美国人民。生活成本完全失控。住房成本失控。食品杂货成本失控。电费失控。医疗保健成本失控。托儿成本失控。美国太过昂贵，而唐纳德·特朗普和共和党什么都没做。在共和党的政策下，美国的成本没有下降，反而上升了，其中包括与特朗普关税直接相关的原因；这些关税使普通美国人每年增加数千美元的成本。\n我们的医疗保健体系已经破碎，并且正面临共和党制造的医疗保健危机。共和党实施了美国历史上最大规模的医疗补助削减。医院、疗养院和社区医疗诊所因共和党在《一项又大又丑陋的法案》中的有毒政策而关闭。参议院共和党人拒绝延长《平价医疗法案》税收抵免，这将使数千万美国人的医疗保健成本飙升，他们将无力在需要时去看医生。\n唐纳德·特朗普和共和党人承诺降低美国的成本。相反，共和党领导的国土安全部正在冷血地夺走美国人的生命。这完全不可接受。纳税人的钱应当用于让美国人民的生活更加负担得起，而不是虐待普通美国人或杀害美国公民。但这正是目前在美利坚合众国发生的事情，这也是为什么在任何涉及 ICE 或 CBP 的拨款法案推进之前，国土安全部都需要发生重大改变。这是民主党的立场，因为这也是美国人民的立场。完整新闻发布会可在此处观看。\n###\n返回新闻\n分享：\nFacebook\nTwitter","publish_source":"jeffries.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-01-29T08:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1103","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS (deep pilot)","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"杰弗里斯领袖：“今天就把参议院两党通过的国土安全部法案提交众议院表决”","title_en":"LEADER JEFFRIES: “BRING THE BIPARTISAN SENATE-PASSED DHS BILL TO THE HOUSE FLOOR TODAY” – Congressman Hakeem Jeffries","summary_cn":"众议院民主党领袖哈基姆·杰弗里斯举行记者会，批评共和党人宁愿迎合特朗普的极端大规模驱逐议程，也不愿为国土安全部员工薪资和项目拨款。他称国土安全部已被关闭超过70天，参议院两党一致通过的法案在众议院搁置，该法案可全额资助特勤局、运输安全管理局、联邦应急管理局、海岸警卫队及网络安全人员，呼吁议长约翰逊立即将其提交表决。","summary_en":"House Democratic Leader Hakeem Jeffries held a press availability criticizing Republicans for refusing to fund DHS programs and pay employees while pursuing Trump's extreme mass deportation agenda. He said DHS has been shut down for more than 70 days and that a bipartisan Senate-passed bill is languishing in the House. The bill would fully fund the Secret Service, TSA, FEMA, the Coast Guard and DHS cybersecurity professionals, and he urged Speaker Johnson to bring it to the floor today.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-25T11:04:35.703862+00:00","url":"https://jeffries.house.gov/2026/04/27/leader-jeffries-bring-the-bipartisan-senate-passed-dhs-bill-to-the-house-floor-today","content":"April 27th, 2026\n|\nPress Release\nLEADER JEFFRIES: “BRING THE BIPARTISAN SENATE-PASSED DHS BILL TO THE HOUSE FLOOR TODAY”\nToday, House Democratic Leader Hakeem Jeffries held a press availability, where he emphasized that Republican sycophants would rather bend the knee to Trump’s extreme mass deportation agenda than fund the programs that pay our Department of Homeland Security employees and keep Americans safe.\nLEADER JEFFRIES: Donald Trump and House Republicans have now shut down the Department of Homeland Security for more than 70 days because Donald Trump and Republicans want to continue to drive their extreme immigration agenda and violent mass deportation machine led by ICE down the throats of the American people. Several weeks ago, a bill was sent over from the United States Senate that was supported by every single Republican and every single Democrat in the Senate. It’s a bipartisan bill that has been languishing in the House of Representatives. We can bring that bill to the Floor today, and it would fully fund the United State Secret Service. Why is Mike Johnson and House Republicans continuing to refuse to bring that bipartisan bill to the Floor that would fund TSA, it would fund the Secret Service, it would fund FEMA, it would fund the Coast Guard and it would fund the cybersecurity professionals at the Department of Homeland Security who are working hard to keep us safe? Instead, it’s House Republicans that continue to play partisan political games. If they really do believe we need to act swiftly, there’s a vehicle to do it. Bring the bipartisan Senate-passed bill to the House Floor today and it would fund the Department of Homeland Security in its entirety with the exception of ICE and the violent Republican mass deportation machine.\nFull availability can be watched here.\n###\nBack to News\nShare:\nFacebook\nTwitter","content_cn":"2026年4月27日\n|\n新闻稿\n杰弗里斯领袖：“今天就将参议院通过的两党国土安全部法案提交众议院全院表决”\n今天，众议院民主党领袖哈基姆·杰弗里斯举行媒体见面会。他强调，共和党阿谀奉承者宁愿向特朗普极端的大规模驱逐议程屈膝，也不愿为支付国土安全部员工薪资、保障美国人安全的项目提供资金。\n杰弗里斯领袖：唐纳德·特朗普和众议院共和党人如今已经让国土安全部停摆超过70天，因为唐纳德·特朗普和共和党人想继续把由ICE领导的极端移民议程和暴力大规模驱逐机器强行灌输给美国人民。几周前，美国参议院通过了一项法案，并获得参议院每一位共和党人和每一位民主党人的支持。这是一项两党法案，一直滞留在众议院。我们今天可以将该法案提交全院表决，它将为美国特勤局提供全部资金。为什么迈克·约翰逊和众议院共和党人仍然拒绝将这项两党法案提交全院表决？该法案将为运输安全管理局（TSA）提供资金，为特勤局提供资金，为联邦紧急事务管理局（FEMA）提供资金，为海岸警卫队提供资金，也将为国土安全部负责网络安全、努力保障我们安全的专业人员提供资金？相反，正是众议院共和党人继续玩弄党派政治游戏。如果他们真的认为我们需要迅速行动，就有现成途径。今天就把参议院通过的两党法案提交众议院全院表决，它将为国土安全部提供全部资金，但ICE以及共和党暴力大规模驱逐机器除外。\n完整的媒体见面会可在此观看。\n###\n返回新闻\n分享：\nFacebook\nTwitter","publish_source":"jeffries.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-04-27T07:00:00+00:00"}},{"id":"news-1807","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"布朗利就支持针对国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆的弹劾条款发表声明","title_en":"Brownley Statement in Support of Articles of Impeachment Against DHS Secretary Kristi Noem - Congresswoman Julia Brownley","summary_cn":"美国众议员朱莉娅·布朗利（加州第26选区）发表声明，支持针对国土安全部长克里斯蒂·诺姆的弹劾条款。条款由众议员罗宾·凯利提出，已获80余名议员联署。布朗利指责诺姆拒绝正当程序、无视法治，称ICE拘留期间死亡人数创纪录，并批评其阻碍国会监督、延误FEMA救灾援助、滥用纳税人资金，认为诺姆不适合任职。","summary_en":"U.S. Rep. Julia Brownley (CA-26) released a statement supporting Articles of Impeachment against Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem, introduced by Rep. Robin Kelly and co-sponsored by over 80 members. Brownley accused Noem of denying due process, disregarding the rule of law, and overseeing record ICE detention deaths. She also cited obstruction of congressional oversight, delayed FEMA disaster aid, and misuse of taxpayer funds, calling Noem unfit to serve.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T15:42:16.695822+00:00","url":"https://juliabrownley.house.gov/brownley-statement-in-support-of-articles-of-impeachment-against-dhs-secretary-kristi-noem","content":"Home > Press Releases > Brownley Statement in Support of Articles of Impeachment Against DHS Secretary Kristi Noem\nBrownley Statement in Support of Articles of Impeachment Against DHS Secretary Kristi Noem\nJanuary 16, 2026\n| Press Releases\nWashington, DC – Today, Congresswoman Julia Brownley (CA-26) released the following statement in support of Articles of Impeachment filed against U.S. Department of Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem. The articles of impeachment were introduced earlier this week by Congresswoman Robin Kelly (IL-02) and have been co-sponsored by more than 80 Members of Congress.\n“Kristi Noem has repeatedly violated her oath of office by denying due process, disregarding the rule of law, and placing both citizens and immigrants in grave danger. Rather than enforcing the law responsibly, DHS has weaponized immigration enforcement to sow chaos, intimidate families, and terrorize entire neighborhoods — all with Secretary Noem’s full knowledge and approval.\n“Last year marked the deadliest year on record for ICE detention, with 32 individuals dying in custody. More recently, Renee Good, a mother of three and beloved community member, was murdered by an ICE agent whose excessive use of force resulted in the most horrific outcome. These are not isolated incidents. They are the predictable result of a Department operating without meaningful oversight, transparency, or accountability.\n“Kristi Noem oversees this lawlessness with blatant disregard for the Constitution and for the basic rights of the people she is sworn to protect. ICE agents have been emboldened to use excessive force, forcibly separate children from their families, deport veterans who served our nation in uniform, and detain people — including pregnant women and other vulnerable populations — under deplorable conditions. These actions undermine constitutional protections, erode public trust in law enforcement, and make our communities unsafe.\n“To make matters worse, Noem has refused to condemn ICE’s misconduct or take steps to restore order and accountability. Instead, she has doubled down on false and inflammatory rhetoric that fuels fear, escalates tensions, and perpetuates violence nationwide.\n“Noem has also obstructed congressional oversight by preventing Members of Congress, including myself, from carrying out our constitutional duty to investigate abuses within the Department of Homeland Security. She has repeatedly failed to answer for DHS’s misconduct, delayed lifesaving FEMA assistance to communities devastated by natural disasters, and abused taxpayer dollars.\n“Kristi Noem’s reckless leadership has hollowed out DHS, normalized lawlessness, and placed lives at risk. She is wholly unfit to serve, which is why I will continue working with my colleagues to advance these Articles of Impeachment and demand accountability, transparency, and adherence to the rule of law.”\n###\nIssues: 119th Congress, Disaster Relief, Immigration\nBack to News\nFacebook\nBluesky\nMail","content_cn":"首页 > 新闻稿 > 布朗利支持弹劾国土安全部部长克里斯蒂·诺姆的声明\n布朗利支持弹劾国土安全部部长克里斯蒂·诺姆的声明\n2026年1月16日\n| 新闻稿\n华盛顿特区——今天，联邦众议员朱莉娅·布朗利（加利福尼亚州第26选区）就针对美国国土安全部部长克里斯蒂·诺姆提出的弹劾条款发布以下支持声明。该弹劾条款由联邦众议员罗宾·凯利（伊利诺伊州第02选区）于本周早些时候提出，已有80多名国会议员共同提案。\n“克里斯蒂·诺姆一再拒绝给予正当程序、无视法治，并将公民和移民都置于严重危险之中，从而违反了她的就职誓言。国土安全部并未负责任地执法，反而将移民执法武器化，以制造混乱、恐吓家庭并恐怖威胁整个社区——这一切都得到诺姆部长的充分知情和批准。\n“去年是ICE拘留死亡人数创纪录最多的一年，32人在羁押期间死亡。最近，三个孩子的母亲、备受社区爱戴的成员蕾妮·古德，被一名过度使用武力并造成最可怕结果的ICE特工杀害。这些并非孤立事件，而是一个缺乏有意义监督、透明度和问责制的部门运作所带来的可预见结果。\n“克里斯蒂·诺姆监管着这种无法无天的行为，公然无视宪法以及她宣誓保护的人民的基本权利。ICE特工受到鼓励使用过度武力，强行将儿童与家人分离，驱逐曾身着制服为国家服役的退伍军人，并在恶劣条件下拘留人员——其中包括孕妇和其他脆弱群体。这些行为破坏宪法保障，侵蚀公众对执法部门的信任，并使我们的社区变得不安全。\n“更糟糕的是，诺姆拒绝谴责ICE的不当行为，也拒绝采取措施恢复秩序和问责。相反，她变本加厉地使用虚假且煽动性的言辞，加剧恐惧、升级紧张局势，并使全国范围内的暴力持续存在。\n“诺姆还阻碍国会监督，阻止包括我本人在内的国会议员履行调查国土安全部内部滥权行为的宪法职责。她一再未能就国土安全部的不当行为作出交代，延误向遭受自然灾害重创的社区提供救命的联邦紧急事务管理署援助，并滥用纳税人资金。\n“克里斯蒂·诺姆鲁莽的领导已经掏空国土安全部，使无法无天常态化，并将生命置于风险之中。她完全不适合任职，因此我将继续与同事合作推进这些弹劾条款，并要求问责、透明度以及遵守法治。”\n###\n议题：第119届国会、灾害救援、移民\n返回新闻\nFacebook\nBluesky\n邮件","publish_source":"juliabrownley.house.gov","publish_time":"2026-01-16T22:22:30+00:00"}},{"id":"news-640","ktid":1001140,"fields":{"id":"","kt_id":"1001140","source":"Google News RSS","create_time":"","update_time":"","title_cn":"塞勒姆市就与救灾资金挂钩的DEI条件起诉国土安全部和FEMA","title_en":"City of Salem sues DHS, FEMA over DEI conditions tied to disaster relief funding","summary_cn":"美国俄勒冈州塞勒姆市6月30日在尤金联邦地区法院起诉国土安全部和联邦应急管理局（FEMA），指控特朗普政府将DEI、移民执法、性别认同及行政命令合规等政治条件附加于救灾拨款，超出国会授权。诉讼称这些条件危及2025年12月风暴后基础设施修复资金，包括逾100万美元的涵洞更换和泵站修复项目。国土安全部回应称受助方须遵守反歧视法律，并否认相关指控。","summary_en":"The City of Salem, Oregon, filed a federal lawsuit on 30 June in the US District Court in Eugene against the Department of Homeland Security and FEMA, arguing the Trump administration unlawfully attached political conditions involving DEI, immigration enforcement, gender identity and executive-order compliance to disaster relief grants beyond congressional authorization. The suit says the conditions jeopardize funding for infrastructure repairs after December 2025 storms, including over $1 million for culvert replacement and pump station restoration. DHS defended its policies and declined to address the allegations.","tag":"policy","founddate":"2026-09-18T14:12:25.291236+00:00","url":"https://katu.com/news/local/city-of-salem-sues-dhs-fema-over-dei-conditions-tied-to-disaster-relief-funding-oregon-diversity-inclusion-equity-equality-race-federal-management-homeland-security-donald-trump-eugene-district-court-law-legal-congress-lawsuit","content":"City of Salem sues DHS, FEMA over DEI conditions tied to disaster relief fundingby Vasili VarlamosMon, July 6, 2026 at 11:46 AMUpdated Mon, July 6, 2026 at 11:15 PM3VIEW ALL PHOTOSFILE - The Federal Emergency Management Agency (FEMA) building is seen on May 15, 2025, in Washington, D.C. (Photo by Kayla Bartkowski/Getty Images)24CommentSharetopics: SalemFEMADHSDisaster reliefDEIExecutive ordersImmigration enforcementFederal lawsuitSALEM, Ore. (KATU) — The City of Salem has filed a federal lawsuit against the U.S. Department of Homeland Security and the Federal Emergency Management Agency (FEMA), arguing the Trump administration is unlawfully attaching political conditions to disaster relief grants.The lawsuit was filed June 30 in the U.S. District Court in Eugene. The city declined further comment on the pending litigation. According to the 71-page complaint, the city of Salem argues DHS and FEMA grant requirements go beyond what Congress authorized by tying disaster funding to policies involving diversity, equity, and inclusion (DEI), immigration enforcement, gender identity, and compliance with executive orders unrelated to disaster recovery.SEE ALSO | Supreme Court ruling preserves Oregon law protecting late-arriving mail ballotsThe lawsuit points to FEMA grant agreements that require recipients to comply with executive orders addressing DEI and what the administration calls the \"promotion\" of gender ideology. The city of Salem argues that those requirements have nothing to do with disaster recovery and should not determine whether communities receive federal emergency funding.\"By imposing conditions that Congress has not authorized and that even Congress could not constitutionally enact, DHS and FEMA have exceeded their lawful authority and encroached upon Congress's power of the purse,\" the lawsuit states.Salem says those conditions jeopardize funding for infrastructure projects damaged during the December 2025 storms, including more than $1 million approved to replace damaged culverts and restore access to the West Salem Pump Station, which carries wastewater from West Salem beneath the Willamette River to the city's primary wastewater treatment facility. Temporary access has been restored, but the city says a permanent replacement is needed before future severe weather.Read the lawsuit below: SALEM V DHSPDF previewPreview PDFView PDFThe Department of Homeland Security defended the administration's policies but declined to address the allegations in the lawsuit.\"While FEMA does not comment on pending litigation, this lawsuit is another attempt to obstruct President Trump's agenda and the will of the American people,\" a DHS spokesperson said.The department said recipients of federal funding must comply with anti-discrimination laws and argued that taxpayer dollars should not be used for DEI initiatives, climate activism, or other activities it considers unrelated to the grants' purpose.DHS also said jurisdictions that impede federal immigration enforcement should not receive federal funding and that FEMA has implemented additional controls to ensure grant money is used lawfully.\"FEMA has implemented strict controls to ensure grant activity is transparent, lawful, and free from past fraud, waste, or abuse,\" said the spokesperson in a statement.Separately, FEMA's Region 10 External Affairs office told KATU only that the agency \"does not comment on pending litigation.\"NEWS IN PHOTOS:\"Local\"7NEWMan shot by Border Patrol in Portland gets time served, faces deportation3Police identify man killed in late-August shooting in Portland's Buckman neighborhood8Portland International Airport ranks No. 2 in JD Power’s 2026 large airport survey4Multnomah County DA: Death of 6th woman linked to Jesse Calhoun","content_cn":"塞勒姆市就与灾害救援资金挂钩的DEI条件起诉国土安全部和联邦紧急事务管理署\n作者：Vasili Varlamos\n2026年7月6日，星期一，上午11:46\n更新于2026年7月6日，星期一，晚上11:15\n\n文件——2025年5月15日，华盛顿特区，联邦紧急事务管理署（FEMA）大楼。（Kayla Bartkowski/Getty Images摄）\n\n俄勒冈州塞勒姆（KATU）——塞勒姆市已对美国国土安全部和联邦紧急事务管理署（FEMA）提起联邦诉讼，称特朗普政府非法为灾害救援拨款附加政治条件。\n\n该诉讼于6月30日在尤金的美国地区法院提起。该市拒绝就未决诉讼进一步置评。根据这份长达71页的诉状，塞勒姆市认为，国土安全部和FEMA的拨款要求超出了国会授权范围，因为其将灾害资金与涉及多元化、公平与包容（DEI）、移民执法、性别认同，以及遵守与灾后恢复无关的行政命令等政策挂钩。\n\n另见｜最高法院裁决维持俄勒冈州保护迟到邮寄选票的法律\n\n诉讼指出，FEMA拨款协议要求受款方遵守涉及DEI以及政府所谓“宣传”性别意识形态的行政命令。塞勒姆市认为，这些要求与灾后恢复毫无关系，不应决定社区是否获得联邦紧急资金。\n\n诉状称：“通过施加国会未授权、且即便国会也无法合宪制定的条件，国土安全部和FEMA已超越其合法权限，并侵蚀了国会的财政拨款权。”\n\n塞勒姆表示，这些条件危及2025年12月风暴期间受损的基础设施项目资金，包括获批逾100万美元用于更换受损涵洞、恢复通往西塞勒姆泵站的通道。该泵站将西塞勒姆的污水从威拉米特河下方输送至该市主要污水处理设施。临时通道已恢复，但该市称，未来严峻天气到来前需要永久替换设施。\n\n请在下方阅读诉状：SALEM诉DHS\n\n国土安全部为政府政策辩护，但拒绝回应诉讼中的指控。\n\n一名国土安全部发言人表示：“尽管FEMA不评论未决诉讼，但这起诉讼是又一次试图阻挠特朗普总统议程和美国人民意愿的行为。”\n\n该部门称，联邦资金受款方必须遵守反歧视法律，并认为纳税人的资金不应被用于DEI倡议、气候活动或其认为与拨款目的无关的其他活动。\n\n国土安全部还称，妨碍联邦移民执法的辖区不应获得联邦资金，且FEMA已实施额外管控，以确保拨款资金被合法使用。\n\n该发言人在一份声明中表示：“FEMA已实施严格管控，以确保拨款活动透明、合法，并且不存在过去的欺诈、浪费或滥用问题。”\n\n此外，FEMA第10区对外事务办公室仅向KATU表示，该机构“不会评论未决诉讼”。","publish_source":"katu.com","publish_time":"2026-07-06T18:46:05+00:00"}}];
